hadiths[2195]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11963","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: If a slave girl among the people of al-Madinah took the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she would go with him for her need."
"11964","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"11965","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, consummated marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh, he gave a feast. He said: He fed us bread and meat."
"11966","Hushaym narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, raising the hadith, he said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away, ignorance appears, men decrease and women increase, until one man is in charge of fifty women."
"11967","Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a Hibarah cloak. He said: I think he tied its two ends together."
"11968","Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit all his wives in one night with a single ghusl."
"11969","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered the lavatory, said, he says: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female impurities."
"11970","Hushaym narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas informed us, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."
"11971","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Anas, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Help your brother, wronging or wronged. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this one I help wronged, so how do I help him if he is wronging. He said: You restrain him, you prevent him, for that is helping him."
"11972","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz and Ismail informed us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take sahur, for in sahur there is blessing."
"11973","Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I saw the ring of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made of silver."
"11974","Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took Safiyyah, he stayed with her three nights, and she was previously married."
"11975","Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard him narrating, he said: I attended two wedding feasts of the wives of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He did not feed us in them bread nor meat. I said: What then. He said: Hays, meaning dates and dried yogurt with ghee."
"11976","Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, al-Azhar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not seek light from the fire of the polytheists, and do not engrave your rings in Arabic."
"11977","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and heard a rustling before me, and behold it was al-Ghumaysa bint Milhan, the mother of Anas ibn Malik."
"11978","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had his front tooth broken on the day of Uhud, and was wounded in his forehead until blood flowed over his face. He said: How can a people prosper who did this to their prophet while he calls them to their Lord. Then this verse was revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"11979","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed Safiyyah bint Huyayy and made her freedom her dowry."
"11980","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that they heard him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, calling the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together, saying: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj, here I am for Umrah and Hajj."
"11981","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: And I am Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, and I think I heard from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man driving a sacrificial animal, and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, two or three times."
"11982","Hushaym narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, and he would mention the name and magnify Allah, and I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot on their sides."
"11983","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, calling the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together. So I told Ibn Umar of that, and he said: He called the talbiyah for Hajj alone. Then I met Anas and told him the saying of Ibn Umar, and he said: Do you count us except as children. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj."
"11984","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, I think he said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he responded to one of them, or he said: blessed him, and left the other. It was said: Two men, one sneezed and you responded to him, and you did not respond to the other. He said: This one praised Allah Almighty."
"11985","Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, liked the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be next to him in prayer."
"11986","Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and wipe off what is on it of harm, and let him not leave it for Satan."
"11987","Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: There were not in the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor his beard, twenty white hairs. And Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and Umar dyed with henna."
"11988","Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: Abu Taybah cupped the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gave him a sa of food, and spoke to his masters, and they lightened his burden."
"11989","Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among the most complete of people in prayer and the briefest."
"11990","Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan, from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold a cup and a mat to whoever bids more."
"11991","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu al-Akhdar, he said: And Waki narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, meaning the companion of Shubah, from al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan, from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"11992","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We used to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in intense heat, and when one of us could not place his face firmly on the ground, he spread his garment and prostrated on it."
"11993","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When supper is placed and the prayer is called, begin with supper."
"11994","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you dozes in his prayer, let him leave and sleep."
"11995","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, and Yazid ibn Harun, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is only that he pray it when he remembers it. Yazid said: So its expiation is that."
"11996","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Blessed and Almighty, is surely pleased with the servant that he eats a meal and praises Allah Almighty for it, or drinks a drink."
"11997","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I served the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nine years, and I never knew him to say to me at all: Why did you not do such and such, nor did he ever criticize anything of mine at all."
"11998","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, I said: Inform me of something you learned from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Where did he pray Zuhr on the day of Tarwiyah. He said: At Mina. And where did he pray Asr on the day of departure. He said: At al-Abtah. He said: Then he said: Do as your rulers do."
"11999","Abbad ibn Abbad and Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah, he said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in his sandals. He said: Yes."
"12000","Ziyad ibn al-Rabi Abu Khidash al-Yuhmadi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Imran al-Jawni saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I do not recognize anything today of what we were upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: We said to him: Where is prayer. He said: Did you not do with prayer what you have known."
"12001","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to perfume himself with saffron."
"12002","Ismail narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him, but if he must wish for death then let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me in death when death is good for me."
"12003","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you supplicates, let him be firm in supplication and let him not say: O Allah, if You will then give me, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has none to compel Him."
"12004","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Qatada asked Anas which supplication the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to make most often. He said: The supplication the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to make most often was: O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. And when Anas wanted to make a supplication he would make it with this, and when he wanted to make a supplication he would include it in it."
"12005","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, and once he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb informed us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Muadh used to lead his people in prayer, then Haram came in while wanting to water his palm trees, so he entered the mosque to pray with the people, but when he saw that Muadh was prolonging, he shortened his own prayer and caught up with his palm trees to water them, then when Muadh finished his prayer it was said to him that Haram had entered the mosque."
"12006","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas who said: When the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the lavatory he would say: I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils."
"12007","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sacrifice two rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice two rams."
"12008","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wears silk in this world will never wear it in the Hereafter."
"12009","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the mosque while a rope was stretched between two pillars, so he said: What is this. They said: It belongs to Zaynab; she prays, and when she grows lazy or weary she holds on to it. He said: Untie it. Then he said: Let each one of you pray with energy, and when he grows lazy or weary let him sit down."
"12010","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer was called while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in private conversation with a man in the mosque, so he did not rise for prayer until the people stood up."
"12011","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina, Abu Talha took my hand and set out with me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas is a clever boy, so let him serve you. He said: So I served him on journeys and at home. By Allah, he never said to me about something I did: Why did you do this like this, nor about something I did not do: Why did you not do this like this."
"12012","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a ring made and said: We have had a ring made and have engraved an inscription in it, so let no one engrave upon it."
"12013","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to shorten the prayer and complete it."
"12014","Ismail narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"12015","Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raided Khaybar, and we prayed the dawn prayer with him there in the darkness. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted, and Abu Talha mounted, and I rode behind Abu Talha. Then the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made his mount run through the lanes of Khaybar, and my knees were touching the thighs of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the lower garment was uncovered from the thighs of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I could see the whiteness of the thighs of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When he entered the town he said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned. He said it three times. He said: The people had gone out to their work and said: Muhammad. Abd al-Aziz said: And some of our companions said: The fifth army. He said: So we seized it by force, and the captives were gathered. He said: Then Dihya came and said: O Prophet of Allah, give me a slave girl from the captives. He said: Go and take a slave girl. He said: So he took Safiyya bint Huyayy. Then a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have given Dihya Safiyya bint Huyayy, the mistress of Qurayza and Nadir; by Allah, she is fit for none but you. He said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Call him to bring her. So he brought her, and when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at her he said: Take a slave girl from the captives other than her. Then the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed her and married her. Thabit said to him: O Abu Hamza, what did he give her as dowry. He said: Herself; he freed her and married her. Then when he was on the road, Umm Sulaym prepared her and presented her to him at night, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke as a bridegroom and said: Whoever has anything with him, let him bring it. And he spread a leather mat, and one man would bring dried yogurt, and one man would bring dates, and one man would bring clarified butter. He said: And I think he mentioned barley meal. He said: So they mixed a porridge, and that was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12016","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Amash informed us, from Anas who said: The coat of mail of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was pawned, and he could find nothing to redeem it with until he died."
"12017","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise which my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, promised me."
"12018","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Most High said to me: Your community will keep questioning among themselves until they say: This is Allah who created mankind, so who created Allah."
"12019","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mukhtar ibn Fulful who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dozed off briefly, then raised his head smiling. Either he said to them or they said to him: Why did you laugh. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A surah has just been sent down to me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: Indeed We have given you al-Kawthar, until he completed it. He said: Do you know what al-Kawthar is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It is a river which my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has given me in Paradise, upon it much good; my community will come to it on the Day of Resurrection, its vessels as many as the stars; a servant among them will be pulled away, so I will say: O Lord, he is from my community. Then it will be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"12020","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said one day after finishing the prayer, turning to us: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, nor in sitting, nor in leaving, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you see. He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire."
"12021","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yunus ibn Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him and removes ten sins from him."
"12022","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: I and a man of the Ansar visited Anas ibn Malik after we had prayed noon, and he called a slave girl for ablution water. We said to him: Which prayer are you going to pray. He said: The afternoon prayer. He said: We said: We have just now prayed noon. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: That is the prayer of the hypocrite; he leaves the prayer until when it is between the two horns of Satan, or in the two horns of Satan, he prays, remembering Allah in it only a little."
"12023","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit Umm Sulaym, and she would spread a leather mat for him and he would nap on it, and she would take some of his sweat and put it in her perfume, and she would spread a palm mat for him and he would pray on it."
"12024","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Bilal was ordered to make the call to prayer even and to make the call to commence odd."
"12025","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three things, whoever has them in him finds through them the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be dearer to him than all else, and that he love a man loving him only for Allah, and that he hate to return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, just as he hates to be kindled a fire and thrown into it."
"12026","Amr ibn Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: There is none who enters Paradise who loves to leave it, even if he had all that is on earth, except the martyr; he loves to leave and be killed because of the honor he sees, or with its meaning."
"12027","Amr ibn Haytham narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No prophet was sent but warned his community of the one-eyed liar. Behold, he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is: Disbeliever."
"12028","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying one night in his chamber, then some people came and prayed with his prayer, so he shortened. Then he entered the house, then came out and repeated it several times, each time praying. In the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed while we love you to prolong your prayer. He said: I knew your place, and I did that deliberately."
"12029","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Medina while they had two days in which they played during the ignorance, so he said: Allah, Blessed and Most High, has replaced them for you with better than them: the Day of Breaking the Fast and the Day of Sacrifice."
"12030","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a garden of the gardens of Banu Najjar and heard a sound from a grave, so he asked about it: When was this one buried. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one was buried during the ignorance. That impressed him, and he said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have called upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"12031","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and there I was before a river whose banks were tents of pearl. So I struck with my hand into what flowed in it of water, and behold it was strongly scented musk. I said: What is this, O Jibril. He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you."
"12032","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned from the raid of Tabuk and drew near Medina, he said: In Medina there are people: you traveled no march nor crossed a valley but they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, while they are in Medina. He said: While they are in Medina; an excuse detained them."
"12033","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was called Adba, and she was never beaten. Then a Bedouin came on a young camel and beat her, and that was hard on the Muslims. When he saw what was in their faces they said: O Messenger of Allah, Adba has been beaten. He said: It is a right upon Allah that He raises nothing of this world but He lowers it."
"12034","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The prayer was called, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and turned to us with his face and said: Straighten your rows and draw close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"12035","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd who said: Anas was asked about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: We never wished to see him at night praying but we saw him, and we never wished to see him sleeping but we saw him. And he used to fast part of the month until we would say: He does not break any of it, and he would break fast until we would say: He does not fast any of it."
"12036","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: We liked that a man from the desert folk would come and ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the establishment of the Hour. And the prayer was called, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed. When he finished his prayer he said: Where is the one asking about the Hour. He said: It is I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And what have you prepared for it. He said: I have not prepared for it much deed, neither prayer nor fasting, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man is with whom he loves. Anas said: I never saw the Muslims rejoice after Islam with anything as they rejoiced with this."
"12037","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The prayer was called while there was something between the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his wives, so he kept turning some of them away from others. Then Abu Bakr came and said: Throw dust in their mouths, O Messenger of Allah, and go out to prayer."
"12038","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him, but let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me in death when death is good for me."
"12039","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: Abu Talha used to fast much in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died he would not break fast except on a journey or in sickness."
"12040","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was resident he would seclude himself in the last ten of Ramadan, and when he traveled he would seclude himself the next year for twenty. My father said: I heard this hadith only from Ibn Abi Adi, from Humayd, from Anas."
"12041","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed among a group of his companions while a boy was on the road. When his mother saw the people she feared for her child that he would be trampled, so she came running, saying: My son, my son, and she hastened and took him. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, this one would never throw her son into the Fire. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, calmed them and said: No, by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He does not throw His beloved into the Fire."
"12042","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd who said: Anas was asked: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raise his hands. He said: It was said to him on Friday: O Messenger of Allah, rain has been withheld, the land is barren, and wealth has perished. He said: So he raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and he sought rain. And he raised his hands and sought rain, while we saw no cloud in the sky. When we finished the prayer, even a youth near his house would be concerned about returning to his family. He said: When the next Friday came they said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and caravans have been detained. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled at the hasty weariness of the son of Adam and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. Then it was cleared away from Medina."
"12043","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Muslims heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, calling over the well of Badr: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Utba ibn Rabia, O Shayba ibn Rabia, O Umayya ibn Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true, for I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, are you calling a people who have decayed. He said: You do not hear what I say better than they do, but they cannot answer."
"12044","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O company of the Ansar, did I not come to you astray and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guided you through me; did I not come to you divided and Allah joined you through me; did I not come to you as enemies and Allah reconciled your hearts through me. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Will you not say: You came to us fearful and we gave you security, and expelled and we sheltered you, and forsaken and we aided you. They said: Rather to Allah, Blessed and Most High, belongs the favor through it upon us, and to His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12045","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out for Badr he went out and consulted the people. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, advised him, then he consulted them and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, advised him, then he fell silent. Then a man of the Ansar said: He means you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, we will not be as the Children of Israel said to Musa, peace be upon him: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we are sitting here. But by Allah, if you struck the livers of camels until you reached Barq al-Ghimad, we would be with you."
"12046","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: I invited the Muslims to the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the morning after he consummated with Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he filled the Muslims with bread and meat. He said: Then he returned as he used to do, visiting the chambers of his wives and greeting them, and they prayed for him. He said: Then he returned to his house, and I was with him. When he reached the house, there were two men conversing in a corner of the house. When he saw them he turned back, and when the two men saw that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had turned away from his house, they rose hastening. I do not know whether I informed him or he was informed of it. Then he returned to his dwelling and lowered the curtain between me and him, and the verse of the veil was sent down."
"12047","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: Abu Talha used to shoot before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raise his head from behind him to look at the spots where his arrows landed. He said: So Abu Talha stretched his chest to shield the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with it, saying: O Messenger of Allah, my throat before your throat."
"12048","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not tell you of the best quarters of the Ansar: the quarter of Banu Najjar, then the quarter of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the quarter of Banu Harith ibn Khazraj, then the quarter of Banu Saida. And in all the quarters of the Ansar there is good."
"12049","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come to you peoples whose hearts are softer than yours. He said: Then the Asharis came, among them Abu Musa al-Ashari. When they drew near Medina they were chanting, saying: Tomorrow we meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party."
"12050","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, and Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was with one of his wives, I think it was Aisha, when one of the Mothers of the Believers sent with her servant a bowl containing food. He said: Then the other struck the hand of the servant and the bowl broke in two. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept saying: Your mother is jealous. He said: And he took the two pieces and joined one to the other and put the food in it. Then he said: Eat. So they ate, and he detained the messenger and the bowl until they finished. Then he handed to the messenger another bowl and left the broken one in its place."
"12051","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: A son of Abu Talha fell ill. Abu Talha went out to the mosque, and the boy died. Umm Sulaym prepared the dead and said to her family: Let none of you inform Abu Talha of the death of his son. He returned to his family with some people of the mosque among his companions. He said: How is the boy. She said: Better than he was. So she brought their supper near to them and they ate supper, and the people left, and the woman rose to what a woman rises to. When it was the end of the night she said: O Abu Talha, have you not seen the family of so-and-so: they borrowed a loan, enjoyed it, then when it was asked back it was as if they disliked that. He said: They were not fair. She said: Then your son was a loan from Allah, Blessed and Most High, and Allah has taken him. So he uttered the retrieval and praised Allah. In the morning he went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he saw him he said: May Allah bless you both in your night. Then she conceived Abdullah, and gave birth to him at night, and she disliked to rub his palate until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would rub his palate. So I carried him in the morning with some Ajwa dates, and found him tarring his camels or branding them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym gave birth last night, and she disliked to rub his palate until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would rub his palate. He said: Is there anything with you. I said: Some Ajwa dates. So he took some of them and chewed them, then gathered his saliva and fed it to him. He began to smack his lips, and he said: The love of the Ansar is dates. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, name him. He said: He is Abdullah."
"12052","Bundar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us some of this hadith. He said: So I came to him while he wore a cloak."
"12053","Bundar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas: So I came to him while he wore a striped woolen garment of his, in the garden branding the charity camels that had come to him. He said: Wait a little until I finish for you. Ibn Abi Adi said at the beginning of the hadith: Abu Talha went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You spent as two bridegrooms. He said: So may Allah bless you both in your wedding. And Abu Talha said to Umm Sulaym: How is that boy. She said: He is calmer than he was."
"12054","Musa ibn Hilal narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Abu Talha married Umm Sulaym, she being the mother of Anas and Bara, and she bore him a boy whom he loved. Then he mentioned the hadith. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So you spent as two bridegrooms while he is beside you both. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: May Allah bless you both in your night."
"12055","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, and Yazid informed us, Humayd informed us with the meaning, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer was called, so everyone near the mosque rose, while those whose families were far from the mosque remained. Then a stone basin was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, too small for him to spread his palms in it. He said: So he joined his fingers. He said: So the rest of them performed ablution. Humayd said: And Anas was asked: How many were they. He said: Eighty or more."
"12056","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Banu Salima wanted to move from their dwellings and live near the mosque. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he disliked that Medina be emptied. He said: O Banu Salima, will you not count your traces to the mosque. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they stayed."
"12057","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Suhayl ibn Yusuf with the meaning, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The prayer was called, then a man came hurrying and finished out of breath, or winded. When he reached the row he said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his prayer he said: Which of you is the speaker. The people fell silent. He said: Which of you is the speaker, for he said good, or he said no harm. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I hastened walking and reached the row and said what I said. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it. Then he said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk gently, pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"12058","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and heard before me a movement. And there I was before Ghumaysa bint Milhan."
"12059","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah wants good for a servant He employs him. They said: And how does He employ him. He said: He guides him to a righteous deed before his death."
"12060","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The vision of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"12061","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man supported between his two sons. He said: What is this. They said: He vowed to walk. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is surely rich beyond tormenting this one himself. So he ordered him and he rode."
"12062","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man supported between his two sons and mentioned the like of it."
"12063","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man driving a sacrificial camel while walking had exhausted him. He said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, even if it is a sacrificial camel."
"12064","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: A man called Anjasha used to drive the Mothers of the Believers, and he drove hard. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Anjasha, gently, driving the glass vessels."
"12065","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: Some people of Urayna embraced Islam but found Medina unhealthy. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: If you went out to some milch camels of ours and drank from their milk. Humayd said: And Qatada said, from Anas: And their urine. So they did. When they recovered they disbelieved after their Islam, killed the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a believer, or a Muslim, drove away the milch camels of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and fled as warriors. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent after them, and they were seized. Then he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the lava field until they died."
"12066","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come until none is said on earth: Allah, Allah."
"12067","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not ask me about anything until the Day of Resurrection but I will tell you. He said: Then Abdullah ibn Hudhafa said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father. He said: Your father is Hudhafa. Then his mother said: What did you mean by this. He said: I meant to rest. And it was said about him. Humayd said: And I think this is from Anas. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry, so Umar said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as prophet. We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger."
"12068","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best you treat yourselves with is cupping and sea costus. And do not torture your children by squeezing."
"12069","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and there I was before a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this palace. They said: A young man of Quraysh. I said: Who. They said: Umar ibn Khattab. He said: Were it not for what I know of your jealousy I would have entered it. Then Umar said: Over you, O Messenger of Allah, should I be jealous."
"12070","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we all hate death. He said: It is not that hatred of death, but when the believer is attended, the bearer of glad tidings comes to him from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with what he is heading to, so nothing is dearer to him than meeting Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so Allah loves meeting him. And when the wicked, or the disbeliever, is attended, there comes to him what he is heading to of evil, or what he will meet of evil, so he hates meeting Allah and Allah hates meeting him."
"12071","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd who said: Anas ibn Malik said: I never touched anything, silk brocade nor silk, softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor did I smell a scent sweeter than the scent of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12072","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, and Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited a sick man of the Muslims who had become like a chick. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did you supplicate with anything or ask Him for it. He said: Yes, I used to say: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Glory be to Allah, you cannot bear it nor are you able to. Why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. He said: So he supplicated Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, healed him."
"12073","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: A man would come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and embrace Islam for something of this world given to him, then evening would not come before Islam was dearer to him and mightier to him than this world and all in it."
"12074","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never asked anything for Islam but he gave it. He said: A man came to him and asked him, so he ordered for him many sheep between two mountains, from the sheep of charity. He said: So he returned to his people and said: O my people, embrace Islam, for Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gives a giving fearing no poverty."
"12075","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: Umm Sulaym sent with me a basket containing fresh dates to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I did not find him, and he had gone out nearby to a freedman of his who had invited him and made food for him. He said: So I came to him while he was eating, and he invited me to eat with him. He said: And he had made for him tharid with meat and pumpkin. He said: And he liked pumpkin. He said: So I gathered it and brought it near to him. He said: When he had tasted, he returned to his dwelling. He said: And I placed the basket before him. He said: So he ate and divided until he finished the last of it."
"12076","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter, while he was fasting. He said: Return your dates to their container and your clarified butter to its skin. Then he stood to a corner of the house and prayed two cycles, and we prayed with him. Then he prayed for Umm Sulaym and her family for good. Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a little special one. He said: And what is she. She said: Your servant Anas. He said: He left no good of the Hereafter nor of this world but he prayed for me with it, saying: O Allah, grant him wealth and children and bless him in it. He said: There is no man of the Ansar wealthier than me. And he mentioned that he owns neither gold nor silver except his ring. He said: And he mentioned that his eldest daughter Umayna told him that over one hundred and twenty of his loins were buried by the advent of Hajjaj."
"12077","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd who said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dye his hair. He said: He saw only about seventeen or twenty white hairs at the front of his beard. And he said: He was not disfigured by grayness. It was said to Anas: Is grayness a defect. He said: You all dislike it. But Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and Umar dyed with henna."
"12078","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in his house when a man peeped at him, so he motioned toward him with an arrowhead he had with him, and the man withdrew."
"12079","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abu Musa sought a mount from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but met him busy, so he said: By Allah, I will not carry you. When he turned his back he called him and carried him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore not to carry me. He said: So I swear I will surely carry you."
"12080","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon his arrival in Medina and said: O Messenger of Allah, I will ask you about three traits which none knows but a prophet. He said: Ask. He said: What is the first sign of the Hour, and what is the first that the people of Paradise eat from, and from where does the child resemble his father and his mother. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, has just informed me of them. He said: That is the enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: As for the first sign of the Hour, it is a fire that comes out from the east and gathers the people to the west. As for the first that the people of Paradise eat from, it is the extra lobe of the liver of the whale. As for the resemblance of the child to his father and his mother, when the water of the man precedes the water of the woman the child inclines to him, and when the water of the woman precedes the water of the man it inclines to her. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. And he said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people, and if they know of my Islam they will slander me before you. So send for them and ask them about me: What kind of man is Ibn Salam among you. He said: So he sent for them and said: What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you. They said: Our best and the son of our best, our scholar and the son of our scholar, our most understanding and the son of our most understanding. He said: What do you think, if he embraces Islam will you embrace Islam. They said: May Allah protect him from that. He said: Then Ibn Salam came out and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Our worst and the son of our worst, our ignorant and the son of our ignorant. Then Ibn Salam said: This is what I feared."
"12081","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: When the Muslims were defeated on the day of Hunayn, Umm Sulaym called out: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us who fled. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Umm Sulaym, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sufficed. He said: Then Abu Talha came to her while she had a pickaxe with her, and said: What is this, O Umm Sulaym. She said: If one of the polytheists draws near me I will rip him open with it. He said: Then Abu Talha said: O Messenger of Allah, see what Umm Sulaym says."
"12082","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: When I wanted to embrace Islam I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I will ask you. He said: Ask about whatever occurs to you. He said: I said: What is the first that the people of Paradise eat. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"12083","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, and Yazid said: Humayd informed us, from Anas who said: I was playing with the boys when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and greeted. Yazid said in his hadith: Upon us. And he took my hand and sent me on an errand, and sat in the shade of a garden wall or a wall until I returned to him. So I delivered the message he had sent me with. When I came to Umm Sulaym she said: What detained you. I said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand of his. She said: And what is it. I said: It is a secret. She said: Guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And I never told it to anyone after."
"12084","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a man: Embrace Islam. He said: I find myself averse. He said: Embrace Islam, even if you are averse."
"12085","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar said: Said informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is its burial."
"12086","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is in prayer he is conversing with his Lord, so let none of you spit to his right. Ibn Jafar said: So let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left or under his feet."
"12087","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar, Said narrated to us with the meaning, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, upon him prayer and peace, was approached by Ril and Dhakwan and Usayya and Banu Lihyan, claiming they had embraced Islam, and they sought his aid against their people. So the Prophet of Allah, upon him prayer and peace, aided them on that day with seventy of the Ansar. Anas said: We used to call them in their time the Reciters; they would gather firewood by day and pray by night. They set out with them until when they reached the well of Mauna they betrayed them and killed them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated in قنوت for a month in the dawn prayer, praying against these tribes: Ril and Dhakwan and Usayya and Banu Lihyan. He said: Qatada said: And Anas told us that they recited about them a Quran. And Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: We recited about them a Quran: Convey from us to our people that we have met our Lord, He is pleased with us and has made us pleased. Then that was lifted after. And Ibn Jafar said: Then that was abrogated, or lifted."
"12088","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar, Said narrated to us, and Khaffaf, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is the matter with peoples who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer. And his speech about that was stern, until he said: They will surely desist from that, or their eyes will surely be snatched away."
"12089","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf, from Humayd, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, upon him prayer and peace, said: Be straight in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like the dog."
"12090","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, and Ibn Jafar, and Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, upon him prayer and peace, said: I enter the prayer wanting to prolong it, then I hear the crying of the boy and shorten my prayer, because of what I know of the distress of his mother from his crying."
"12091","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Mecca on the day of the Conquest wearing a helmet. It was said to him that Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kaba. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill him."
"12092","Abd al-Rahman said: And in what I recited to him, meaning Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not in pilgrim sanctity that day, and Allah knows best."
"12093","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: What did you use to do on this day, meaning the day of Arafa. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; one of us would utter the declaration of unity and none objected to him, and one of us would utter the magnification and none objected to him."
"12094","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it. He said: So I told it to my father. He said: I heard Abu Hurayra narrating it."
"12095","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourds and varnished vessels, and that date-drink be made in them."
"12096","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri, from Anas who said: The last look I looked at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on Monday. He lifted the curtain while the people were behind Abu Bakr. I looked at his face as if it were a leaf of a mushaf. The people wanted to move, so he gestured to them to stay, and he let down the curtain, and he died at the end of that day, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12097","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri who heard it from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Do not break ties, nor hate one another, nor turn your backs on one another, nor envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers. And it is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three."
"12098","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri who heard it from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell from a horse and his right side was abraded. We visited him to console him. The prayer came and he prayed sitting while we prayed sitting. When he finished the prayer he said: The imam is only to be followed. When he declares greatness, declare greatness, and when he bows, bow. And Sufyan once said: When he prostrates, prostrate. And when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise. And if he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"12099","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the Hour. He said: What have you prepared for it. He said: I have prepared nothing for it. And Sufyan once said: I have not prepared much for it. But I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: A man is with whom he loves. And Sufyan another time said: You are with whom you loved."
"12100","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When supper is placed and the prayer is called, begin with supper."
"12101","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri, he heard it from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah and I was ten years old, and he died and I was twenty years old, and my mothers used to urge me to serve him. He entered upon us and we milked for him from a tame sheep, and water from a well in the house was mixed for him, and a Bedouin was on his right and Abu Bakr on his left and Umar to the side. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank, then Umar said: Give Abu Bakr. So he handed to the Bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost. And Sufyan once said: Al-Zuhri: Anas informed us."
"12102","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave a wedding feast for Safiyyah with dates and sawiq."
"12103","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, I heard them both saying: We heard Anas saying: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Madinah four, and in Dhu al-Hulayfah two."
"12104","Sufyan narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, he heard Anas narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Three follow the dead: his family, his wealth, and his deeds. Two return and one remains: his family and his wealth, and his deeds remain."
"12105","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdallah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me from his uncle Anas, he said: I prayed, I and an orphan who was with us in the house, and Sufyan once said: in our house, behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to them in their house, and Umm Sulaym prayed behind us."
"12106","Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya from Anas, he said: A Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pour over it a bucket or a vessel of water."
"12107","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Zuhr in Madinah four, and Asr in Dhu al-Hulayfah two rakahs."
"12108","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ayyub from Qatadah from Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, and they used to open with Alhamdu."
"12109","Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya, it was said to Sufyan meaning he heard from Anas, saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, summoned the Ansar to grant them Bahrain, so they said: No, until you grant our brothers among the Muhajirun like us. So he said: You will meet after me selfishness, so be patient until you meet me."
"12110","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Khaybar in the morning early, and they had gone out with spades. When they looked at him they said: Muhammad and the army, Muhammad and the army. Then they turned running to the fortress, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hands, then said the takbir three times, then said: Khaybar is ruined, indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. We found donkeys outside the village and cooked them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger forbid you from domestic donkeys, for it is filth of the work of Satan. Sufyan said: Muhammad and the army, meaning: and the army."
"12111","Sufyan narrated to us from Asim from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not grieve over a detachment as he grieved over them; they were called the Qurra. Sufyan said: There was revealed concerning them: Convey to our people from us that we are pleased and He is pleased with us. It was said to Sufyan: Concerning whom was it revealed? He said: Concerning the people of Bir Maunah."
"12112","He said: It was recited to Sufyan: I heard Asim, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not grieve like what he felt over the seventy who were struck at Bir Maunah."
"12113","He said: It was recited to Sufyan: I heard Asim from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made an alliance between the Muhajirun and the Ansar in our house. Sufyan said: As if he says: He made them brothers."
"12114","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Taymi from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey, and he had a driver called Anjashah, and the mother of Anas was with them, so he said: O Anjashah, gently with the glass vessels."
"12115","Sufyan narrated to us from Humayd from Anas: He heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying the talbiyah at al-Bayda: Labbayk with Umrah and Hajj together."
"12116","Sufyan narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Anas, and Ibn Sirin said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah and sacrificed his sacrificial animals, he had cupping done and gave the cupper, and Sufyan once said: and gave the barber his right side, so he shaved it, and he gave it to Abu Talhah, then he shaved the left and gave it to the people."
"12117","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Judan from Anas, he said: Ukaydir of Dumah gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, meaning a cloak, so the people were impressed by its beauty, so he said: The handkerchiefs of Sad in Paradise are better, or more beautiful, than it."
"12118","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Judan, he said: Thabit said to Anas: O Anas, you touched the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with your hand? He said: Yes. He said: Show me, I kiss it."
"12119","He said: It was recited to Sufyan: I heard from Ibn Judan from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group."
"12120","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Qasim the traveler heard Anas saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a ruin belonging to Banu al-Najjar, and he was relieving himself in it, then he came out to us alarmed or frightened, and said: If it were not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah, Blessed and Exalted, to let you hear of the torment of the people of the graves what He let me hear."
"12121","Sufyan narrated to us, Mamar narrated to me from Thabit from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to go around his wives in one night with one washing."
"12122","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Maysarah and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir saying: We heard Anas saying: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Madinah four, and in Dhu al-Hulayfah two rakahs."
"12123","Abdallah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about drinking in vessels, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the muzaffatah, and said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. He said: I said: What is the muzaffatah? He said: The coated with pitch. He said: I said: Then lead and gourd? He said: No harm in them. He said: I said: Then people dislike them. He said: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt, for every intoxicant is forbidden. He said: I said to him: You spoke truthfully, intoxication is forbidden, but a drink or two drinks with our food? He said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden. And he said: Wine is from grapes, dates, honey, wheat, barley, and corn, so whatever you ferment of that, it is wine."
"12124","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to relieve himself for his need, I would bring him water, and he would wash with it."
"12125","He said: It was recited to Sufyan: I heard Ibn Judan from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group."
"12126","Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Amr ibn Said from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I did not see anyone more merciful to children than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ibrahim was being suckled in the outskirts of Madinah, and he would go out, and we with him, and enter the house, and it was smoky, and his foster father was a blacksmith, so he would take him and kiss him, then return. Amr said: When Ibrahim died, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ibrahim is my son, and he died in infancy, and he has two foster mothers who complete his suckling in Paradise."
"12127","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin informed us from Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jarud from Anas ibn Malik, he said: One of my uncles made food for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love that you eat in my house and pray in it. He said: So he came to him, and in the house was a stallion of those stallions, so he ordered a side of it, so it was swept and sprinkled, then he prayed, and we prayed with him."
"12128","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Said from Qatadah that Anas narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes in their prayer? His speech about that became severe until he said: They will stop from that or their eyes will be snatched away."
"12129","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, and Ibn Jafar: Shubah narrated to us from Abdallah ibn Abdallah ibn Jabr, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a woman of his wives used to wash from one vessel, and he used to wash with five makakiyy and perform ablution with a makkuk."
"12130","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman followed him, and the mountain shook with them, so he said: Be still, upon you is a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs."
"12131","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we believed in you and in what you came with, so do you fear for us? He said: So he said: Yes, indeed hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He turns them."
"12132","Abu Usamah narrated to us from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah from Thabit from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah came on the day of Hunayn making the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laugh about Umm Sulaym. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Umm Sulaym, with her is a dagger? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: What do you do with it, O Umm Sulaym? She said: I intended, if anyone of them comes near me, I stab him with it."
"12133","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Bushayr ibn Yasar, he said: We said to Anas ibn Malik: What do you find objectionable of our condition in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I find objectionable that you do not straighten the rows."
"12134","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12135","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Mishaj al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, he said: When we were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and we said: The sun has declined or has not declined, he prayed Zuhr then departed."
"12136","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day and he was sitting grieved, stained with blood, some of the people of Makkah had beaten him. He said: So he said to him: What is with you? He said: So he said to him: These did to me and did. He said: So Jibril, upon him peace, said to him: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes. He said: So he looked at a tree from beyond the valley and said: Call that tree. So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. So he said: Order it to return. So he ordered it, and it returned to its place. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Enough for me."
"12137","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, old age, miserliness, and the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"12138","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Humayd ibn Hilal from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed, so he said: Zayd took the banner and was struck, then Jafar took it and was struck, then Abdallah ibn Rawahah took it and was struck, and his eyes were shedding tears, then Khalid took it without command, and Allah gave victory upon him, and it would not please me that they are with us, or he said: it would not please them that they are with us."
"12139","Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us from Humayd ibn Zadhawayh, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: We were forbidden, or he said: We were commanded that we do not add to the People of the Book beyond: And upon you."
"12140","Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, he said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was close together, and the prayer of Abu Bakr, until Umar lengthened in the Fajr prayer."
"12141","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Ibn Sirin, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform qunut? He said: Yes, after bowing. Then he was asked after that another time: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform qunut in the Subh prayer? He said: Yes, briefly after bowing."
"12142","Ismail narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us from Anas, he said: The hair of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was to the halves of his ears."
"12143","Ismail narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the time of the Subh prayer. He said: So he ordered Bilal when dawn broke, so he established the prayer, then he delayed brightness the next day until it was bright, then he said: Where is the asker about the time of the morning prayer? What is between these two, or he said: these two, is time."
"12144","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Muhammad from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of sacrifice: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is desired, and he mentioned need of his neighbors, as if the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, believed him. He said: And with me is a jadhaah, it is more beloved to me than two sheep of meat. He said: So he permitted him, and I do not know whether his permission reached others besides him or not. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to two rams and slaughtered them, and the people stood to a small flock of sheep and distributed them, or he said: divided them. Thus Ayyub said."
"12145","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank, and on his right was a Bedouin and on his left Abu Bakr, so he handed to him and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"12146","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Nawfal ibn Masud, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik, so we said: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Three, whoever has them in him, he is made forbidden to the Fire and the Fire is made forbidden to him: faith in Allah, love of Allah, and that to be thrown into the Fire and burned is more beloved to him than to return to disbelief."
"12147","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Humayd, Anas ibn Malik informed us, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a wall belonging to Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound from a grave, so he said: When did the owner of this grave die? They said: He died in Jahiliyyah. So he said: If it were not that you would not bury one another, I would have supplicated Allah to let you hear the torment of the grave."
"12148","Yahya narrated to us from Uqbah ibn Ubayd al-Tai, Bushayr ibn Yasar narrated to me, he said: Anas came to Madinah, so we said to him: What do you find objectionable of us since the time of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So he said: I find nothing objectionable of you except that you do not straighten your rows."
"12149","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"12150","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Listen and obey, even if an Abyssinian is put in charge over you as if his head is a raisin."
"12151","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Thabit from Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man being supported between his two sons. They said: He vowed to walk. He said: Indeed Allah is in no need of this one torturing himself, so he ordered him to ride."
"12152","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, he said: The prayer was established and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in private conversation with a man until some of the people dozed or almost dozed."
"12153","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd, he said: Anas was asked about the night prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: We never wished to see him praying except we saw him, nor sleeping except we saw him."
"12154","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Humayd from Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at al-Baqi, so a man called: O Abu al-Qasim. So he turned to him, so he said: I did not mean you. He said: Name yourselves by my name and do not use my kunyah."
"12155","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah, Ishaq ibn Abdallah narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils are his. He said: So Abu Talhah killed twenty."
"12156","Yahya ibn Said ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said meaning al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A Bedouin entered the mosque in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and urinated, so they forbade him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave him, and he ordered that water be poured over it or spilled over it."
"12157","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us from Thumamah ibn Abdallah from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to breathe in his vessel three times, and Anas used to breathe three times."
"12158","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik that a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and complained to him of need, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do you have nothing? So he brought him a cloak and a cup, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who buys this? So a man said: I take them for a dirham. He said: Who increases over a dirham? So the people fell silent. So he said: Who increases over a dirham? So a man said: I take them for two dirhams. He said: They are yours. Then he said: Begging is not lawful except for one of three: one with painful blood-money, or crushing debt, or grinding poverty."
"12159","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to open recitation with All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"12160","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then one of us would come to Banu Salamah while he sees the places of his arrows."
"12161","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah had a son called Abu Umayr, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to joke with him. He said: So he saw him sad, so he said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"
"12162","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd, he said: Anas was asked about selling fruit, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling the fruit of palm trees until it ripens. It was said to Anas: What is ripening? He said: It reddens."
"12163","Yahya and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, and Abu Nuaym said: from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals, and Abu Bakr flogged, Yahya said in his hadith: forty. When it was Umar, people came close from the countryside and villages, so he said to his companions: What do you see? So Abd al-Rahman said: Make it like the lightest of the prescribed punishments. So Umar flogged eighty."
"12164","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham ibn Hassan, Muhammad narrated to us from Anas that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Khaybar and said: I ate donkeys twice. He said: Then he came and said: I finished the donkeys. He said: So he called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you from the meat of donkeys, for it is filth."
"12165","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah from Anas, he said: The companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so they said: Indeed the People of the Book greet us, so how do we respond to them? He said: So say: And upon you. And Hajjaj likewise. Shubah said: I did not ask Qatadah about this hadith whether he heard it from Anas."
"12166","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Son of Adam grows old and two remain of him: greed and hope."
"12167","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, al-Taymi narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Badr: Who looks at what happened to Abu Jahl? So Ibn Masud went, and found the two sons of Afra had struck him until he was cold, so he took his beard and said: Are you Abu Jahl? So he said: And is there above a man you killed, or his people killed him?"
"12168","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, he said: When: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, and: Who is it that lends Allah a good loan, was revealed, Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, and my wall which was in such and such place, by Allah, if I could conceal it I would not make it public. He said: Put it among your poor kin."
"12169","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed the Dajjal is blind in the left eye, upon it is a thick membrane, written between his eyes is disbeliever. He said: And kufr."
"12170","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? His speech about that became severe until he said: They will stop from that or their eyes will be snatched away."
"12171","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams, I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides, and mentioning the name and magnifying."
"12172","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete bowing and prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind me, and perhaps he said: from behind my back, when you bow and when you prostrate."
"12173","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like the spreading of the dog."
"12174","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against a tribe of the Arab tribes, then left it."
"12175","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I entered Paradise, and there I was by a river whose banks were tents of pearl, so I struck with my hand in the course of the water, and there was strongly scented musk. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah gave you, or your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, gave you."
"12176","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us from Abu Mijlaz from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against Ril and Dhakwan, and he said: Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"12177","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The believers will gather on the Day of Resurrection and will be inspired with that, so they will say: If we seek intercession with our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, so He relieves us from this place of ours. So they will come to Adam, upon him peace, and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created you with His hand, and made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things, so intercede for us with our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, He relieves us from this place of ours. So Adam will say to them: I am not there, and he will mention his sin which he committed, and he will be shy of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and will say: But go to Nuh, for he is the first messenger Allah sent to the earth. So they will come to Nuh, and he will say: I am not there, and he will mention to them his mistake and his asking his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, what he has no knowledge of, and he will be shy of his Lord with that, but go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. So they will come, and he will say: I am not there, but go to Musa, upon him peace, a servant Allah spoke to and gave him the Torah. So they will come to Musa, and he will say: I am not there, and he will mention to them the soul which he killed without a soul, and he will be shy of his Lord from that, but go to Isa, the servant of Allah and His messenger and His word and His spirit. So they will come to Isa, and he will say: I am not there, but go to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a servant Allah forgave him what preceded of his sin and what followed. So they will come to me, al-Hasan said this word, so I will stand and walk between two rows of the believers, Anas said, until I seek permission upon my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and permission is given to me. When I see my Lord I fall, or fall down, prostrating to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He leaves me as long as Allah wills to leave me. He said: Then it is said: Raise, Muhammad, say, you will be heard, and ask, you will be given, and intercede, you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and praise with a praise He teaches me, then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to Him the second time, and when I see my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, I fall, or fall down, prostrating to my Lord, and He leaves me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it is said: Raise, Muhammad, say, you will be heard, and ask, you will be given, and intercede, you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and praise Him with a praise He teaches me, then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to Him the third time, and when I see my Lord I fall, or fall down, prostrating to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He leaves me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it is said: Raise, Muhammad, and say, you will be heard, and ask, you will be given, and intercede, you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and praise Him with a praise He teaches me, then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will admit them into Paradise. Then I will return the fourth time and say: O Lord, none remains except whom the Quran has held. Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and in his heart was of good what weighs a barley grain, then there will come out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and in his heart was of good what weighs a wheat grain, then there will come out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and in his heart was of good what weighs an atom."
"12178","Yahya narrated to us from al-Taymi, he said: I heard Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. He said it twice, and he said once: Whoever lies upon me deliberately."
"12179","Yahya narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah that Anas narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes in their prayer? He said: So he was severe about that until he said: They will stop from that or their eyes will be snatched away."
"12180","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Abdallah ibn Abdallah ibn Jabr narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a woman of his wives used to wash from one vessel, and he used to wash with five makakiyy and perform ablution with a makkuk."
"12181","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, entrusted to the womb an angel. He says: O Lord, a drop, O Lord, a clot, O Lord, a lump. When the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, decrees its creation, he says: O Lord, wretched or happy, male or female, what is the provision and what is the term? He said: So it is written thus in the belly of his mother."
"12182","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us in Makkah, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas Abu Muadh narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"12183","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas that Barirah was given charity, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is for her charity and for us a gift."
"12184","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, he said: al-Qasim ibn Shurayh narrated to me from Thalabah, he said: I heard Anas saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I am amazed at the believer, indeed Allah does not decree a decree except it is good for him."
"12185","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that animals be tied up as targets."
"12186","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik meaning Ibn Mighwal informed us from al-Zubayr ibn Adi from Anas ibn Malik, he said: No time comes upon you except it is worse than the time that was before it. We heard that from your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, twice."
"12187","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ismail informed us, and Yala ibn Ubayd said: Ismail narrated to us from Nafi from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no one on the Day of Resurrection, rich or poor, except he wishes he was given of the world only sustenance. Yala said: In the world."
"12188","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed me from Asim al-Ahwal from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O possessor of two ears."
"12189","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us from Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym was with the women of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a driver was driving them, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon them, he said: Ah, or: O Anjashah, your driving with the glass vessels."
"12190","Yahya narrated to us from al-Taymi from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, old age, miserliness, cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and he mentioned in it life and death."
"12191","Yahya narrated to us from al-Taymi from Anas, he said: Two men sneezed at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he invoked mercy for, or invoked for, one of them, so he said: Indeed this one praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and that one did not praise Allah. Yahya said: And perhaps he said this or similar."
"12192","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah informed us from Said ibn Abi Burdah from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is pleased with the servant that he eats the meal or drinks the drink and praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for it."
"12193","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when death came to him was: Prayer and what your right hands possess, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made his chest rattle with it and his tongue could hardly utter it."
"12194","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us from Yunus from Abu Ishaq from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant seeks refuge from the Fire three times except the Fire says: O Allah, protect him from me, and he does not ask Paradise except Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into me."
"12195","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Muhammad from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of sacrifice: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is desired, and he mentioned need of his neighbors, as if the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, believed him. He said: And with me is a jadhaah, it is more beloved to me than two sheep of meat. He said: So he permitted him. He said: So I do not know whether his permission reached others besides him or not. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to two rams and slaughtered them, so the people stood to a small flock of sheep and distributed them, or he said: divided them."
"12196","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Humayd ibn Hilal from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed and said: Zayd took the banner and was struck, then Jafar took it and was struck, then Abdallah ibn Rawahah took it and was struck, then Khalid took it without command, and Allah gave victory upon him, and he said: It would not please them, or he said: It would not please me, that they are with us. He said: And his eyes were shedding tears."
"12197","Waki ibn al-Jarrah al-Ruasi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Yusuf from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted ruqyah for the evil eye, sting, and ant bite."
"12198","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Asim from Yusuf ibn Abdallah ibn al-Harith from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned similar to it."
"12199","Waki and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah, Bahz said in his hadith: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had hair reaching his shoulders, and Bahz said: striking his shoulders."
"12200","Waki narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us from Thumamah ibn Abdallah ibn Anas from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought perfume, he did not refuse it."
"12201","Waki narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, and Ishaq al-Azraq said: al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, broke his fast at a household, he would say: May the fasting people break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."
"12202","Waki narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The site of the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, belonged to Banu al-Najjar, and in it were palm trees and graves of the polytheists, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Set a price for it for me. They said: We will take no price for it. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was building it while they handed things to him, and he was saying: Verily life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray before the mosque was built wherever prayer overtook him."
"12203","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah and al-Dastuwai, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no tiyarah, and al-fal pleases me. He said: And al-fal is the good pleasant word."
"12204","Waki narrated to us: Hammam narrated to me, from Ghalib, thus Waki said Ghalib, though it is really Abu Ghalib, from Anas, that a funeral of a man was brought and he stood at the head of the bier, then a funeral of a woman was brought and he stood lower than that opposite the bier, then when he prayed, al-Ala ibn Ziyad said to him: O Abu Hamzah, was that how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to stand with respect to the man and the woman, about as I saw you do. He said: Yes. He said: Then al-Ala ibn Ziyad turned to us and said: Memorize it."
"12205","Waki narrated to us: Salamah ibn Wardan narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions one day: Who among you witnessed a funeral today. Umar said: I did. He said: Who among you visited a sick person. Umar said: I did. He said: Who gave charity. Umar said: I did. He said: Who woke up fasting. Umar said: I did. He said: It has become due, it has become due."
"12206","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: We startled a hare at Marr al-Zahran. He said: The boys chased it until they grew tired. He said: So I caught it and brought it to Abu Talhah, and he slaughtered it, then he sent its haunch with me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he accepted it."
"12207","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtering his sacrifice with his own hand."
"12208","Waki narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Bilal ibn Abi Musa, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever seeks judgeship is left to it, and whoever is forced into it, an angel descends upon him and guides him rightly."
"12209","Waki narrated to us: al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to drink standing."
"12210","Waki narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu Isam, from Anas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to breathe in the vessel three times, and he would say: This is more wholesome and more pleasant and more healing."
"12211","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I said to Muawiyah ibn Qurrah: Did you hear Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to al-Numan ibn Muqarrin: The son of the sister of a people is from them. He said: Yes."
"12212","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, he said: The son of the daughter of Anas ibn Malik informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Umm Sulaym, and in the house was a hanging waterskin, so he drank from its mouth while standing. He said: So Umm Sulaym cut off the mouth of the waterskin, and it is with us."
"12213","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Hubayrah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Talhah asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about orphans who inherited wine. He said: Pour it out. He said: Shall we not make it vinegar. He said: No."
"12214","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Talhah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found a date and said: Were you not from charity, I would have eaten you."
"12215","Waki narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped on the two jugular veins and on the upper back."
"12216","Waki narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: A man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Where is my father. He said: In the Fire. He said: Then when he saw what was on his face, he said: Verily my father and your father are in the Fire."
"12217","Waki narrated to us: Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us: Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"12218","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Yusuf, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted ruqyah for the evil eye and the ant bite and the venomous sting."
"12219","Waki narrated to us, from Yahya, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm: I heard Anas say: Verily Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to complete the takbir, they would say takbir when they prostrated and when they rose. Yahya said: Or lowered. He said: They said takbir."
"12220","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful say: I asked Anas ibn Malik about drinking in vessels. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the pitched vessel, and he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"12221","Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a woman met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a road of the roads of Madinah, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need for you. He said: O mother of so-and-so, sit in whichever side of the streets you wish and I will sit with you. He said: So she sat, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat with her until she fulfilled her need."
"12222","Waki narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about the recitation of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He used to prolong his voice with it, prolonging."
"12223","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to mix with us until he would say to a little brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did al-Nughayr do, a bird he used to play with. He said: And a mat of ours was sprinkled with water. He said: So he prayed upon it and lined us up behind him."
"12224","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Iyas, meaning Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah."
"12225","Waki narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come down from the minbar on Friday, and a man would speak to him about a need, and he would speak with him, then he would go forward to his prayer place and pray."
"12226","Waki narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Jafar, both said: Shubah narrated to us. Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: I heard Qatadah, from Anas, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The son of Adam grows old, and two things of him remain: greed and hope."
"12227","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Attab, freedman of Ibn Hurmuz, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to hear and obey, and he said: As much as you are able."
"12228","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, camped at a stopping place, he would not depart until he prayed Zuhr. He said: Then Muhammad ibn Umar said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, even if it were midday. He said: Even if it were midday."
"12229","Waki narrated to us: Abu Khuzaymah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask You as praise belongs to You, there is no god but You, alone, with no partner for You, the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Majesty and Honor. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have asked Allah by the Greatest Name of Allah, by which when He is invoked He answers, and when He is asked by it He gives."
"12230","Waki narrated to us, from Misar, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped, and he would wrong no one his wage."
"12231","Waki narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words I may supplicate with. He said: You glorify Allah, mighty and majestic, ten times, and praise Him ten times, and magnify Him ten times, then ask your need, for He says: I have done it, I have done it."
"12232","Waki narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Majishun, narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily the Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, and you will split into the like of them, all of them in the Fire except one party."
"12233","Waki narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I shall tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, none will tell you after me, I heard him say: The Hour will not come until there is for fifty women a single caretaker, and women become many and men become few."
"12234","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I passed on the night I was taken by night upon Musa, and I saw him standing praying in his grave."
"12235","Waki narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I passed on the night I was taken by night upon a people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. He said: I said: Who are these. They said: Preachers of the people of the world, they used to command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book, will they not reason."
"12236","Waki narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was harmed for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic, as none is harmed, and I was frightened for the sake of Allah as none is frightened, and there came upon me three between day and night when I and my family had no food that any living being eats except what the armpit of Bilal covers."
"12237","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said, in this hadith: There came upon me thirty between day and night."
"12238","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not feel free to admire anyone until you see how he is sealed, for a worker works for a time of his life, or a period of his age, with a righteous deed, such that if he died upon it he would enter Paradise, then he turns and works an evil deed, and a servant works a period of his age with an evil deed, such that if he died upon it he would enter the Fire, then he turns and works a righteous deed, and when Allah wants good for a servant, He employs him before his death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him. He said: He enables him to do a righteous deed, then takes him upon it."
"12239","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas, that a man used to write for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he had read al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and when a man read al-Baqarah and Al Imran he became prominent among us, meaning he became great, and the Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, would dictate to him Most Forgiving, Most Merciful, and he would write Most Knowing, Most Wise, and the Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, would say to him: Write such and such, write as you wish, and he would dictate to him Most Knowing, Most Wise, and he would say: I write All-Hearing, All-Seeing, and he would say: Write, write as you wish. Then that man apostatized from Islam and joined the polytheists, and said: I am the most knowledgeable of you about Muhammad, I used to write whatever I wished. Then that man died, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily the earth did not accept him. And Anas said: Then Abu Talhah told me that he came to the land in which that man died and found him cast out. Abu Talhah said: What is the matter with this man. They said: We buried him repeatedly, and the earth did not accept him."
"12240","Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man used to write before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he had read al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and when a man read al-Baqarah and Al Imran he was regarded as great among us. Then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Yazid."
"12241","Yazid narrated to us: Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Abu Talhah in the campaign of Khaybar to call out: Verily Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is filth. He said: So the pots were overturned."
"12242","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd informed us, and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at al-Baqi, and a man called to a man: O Abu al-Qasim. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned, and the man said: I did not mean you, O Messenger of Allah, I meant so-and-so. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Name yourselves with my name, and do not use my kunyah."
"12243","Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us, in his hadith: Name yourselves with my name."
"12244","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the time of the dawn prayer, so he ordered Bilal and he called the adhan when dawn rose, then he made the iqamah and he prayed. Then when it was the next day, he delayed until it was bright, then he ordered him to make the iqamah and he prayed, then he called the man and said: What is between this and this is the time."
"12245","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: Among the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Hunayn was: O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today."
"12246","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to play with the boys, and a comer came to him and took him and split his chest and took out a clot from it and threw it, and said: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed him in a basin of gold with water of Zamzam, then he joined it. Then the boys came to his foster mother: Muhammad has been killed, Muhammad has been killed. Then she met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his color changed. Anas said: We used to see the trace of the stitching in his chest."
"12247","Yazid narrated to us: Said informed us, and Ibn Jafar said: Said narrated to us, the meaning, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of you women sees that and discharges fluid, let her wash. Umm Salamah said: Can that be, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes. The water of the man is thick and white, and the water of the woman is yellow and thin, so whichever of them precedes or dominates, the child resembles it."
"12248","Yazid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, he said: Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh informed me. Muhammad said: And Waqid was among the most handsome of people and the greatest and tallest of them. He said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik, and he said to me: Who are you. I said: I am Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh. He said: You resemble Sad. Then he wept and wept much, and said: May the mercy of Allah be upon Sad, he was among the greatest of people and the tallest of them. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an army to Ukaydir of Dumah, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a jubbah of brocade woven with gold. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wore it and stood upon the minbar, or sat, and did not speak. Then he came down, and the people began touching the jubbah and looking at it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you marvel at it. They said: We never saw a garment better than it. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than what you see."
"12249","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Al-Ukaydir gave the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a jar of manna. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the prayer, he passed by the people and began giving each man of them a piece, and he gave Jabir a piece. Then he returned to him and gave him another piece, and said: You already gave me once. He said: This is for the daughters of Abd Allah."
"12250","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek refuge from eight: anxiety and sorrow and inability and laziness and miserliness and cowardice and the overwhelming of debt and the overwhelming of the enemy."
"12251","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned from al-Hudaybiyah, this verse came down: Verily We have opened for you a clear opening, that Allah may forgive you what preceded of your sin and what followed, and complete His favor upon you and guide you a straight path. He said: The Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings to you for what Allah gave you, so what is for us. Then there came down: That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein, and expiate their evil deeds from them, and that was with Allah a mighty triumph."
"12252","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: On the day of al-Hudaybiyah, eighty men of the people of Makkah descended upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his Companions, with weapons, from the direction of the mountain of al-Tanim. So he supplicated against them and they were taken. And this verse came down: And He is the One who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah, after He gave you victory over them. He said: Meaning the mountain of al-Tanim near Makkah."
"12253","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: I used to hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, and I do not know whether something came down upon him or something he was saying, while he says: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third for them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"12254","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The sandals of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had two straps."
"12255","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam, meaning Ibn Yahya, informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about lice, so he permitted them to wear silk. Then I saw upon each of them a shirt of silk."
"12256","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Verily part of the excellence of prayer is straightening the row."
"12257","Yazid narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Musa informed us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set for us, for trimming the mustache and clipping the nails and shaving the pubic hair, once every forty days."
"12258","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord, mighty and majestic, said: If My servant draws near Me a span, I draw near him a cubit, and if he draws near Me a cubit, I draw near him a fathom, and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"12259","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, emigrated, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was riding while Abu Bakr was behind him, and Abu Bakr was known on the road for his traveling to Sham, and he would pass by people who would say: Who is this before you, O Abu Bakr. So he would say: A guide guiding me. Then when they neared Madinah, he sent to the people who had embraced Islam of the Ansar, to Abu Umamah and his companions, and they came out to them and said: Enter safe and obeyed. Anas said: I never saw a day brighter nor better than the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr entered Madinah, and I witnessed his death, and I never saw a day darker nor uglier than the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died."
"12260","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, and Affan: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a sword on the day of Uhud and said: Who will take this sword. So some people took it and began looking at it. He said: Who will take it with its right. So the people held back. Then Abu Dujanah Simak said: I will take it with its right. So he took it and split the heads of the polytheists with it."
"12261","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever kills a man, his spoils are his. So Abu Talhah killed twenty men and took their spoils."
"12262","Yazid narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, and Bahz: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah informed us, the meaning, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily Allah does not wrong the believer a good deed, he is given for it in this world and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, He gives him his good deeds in this world, until when he reaches the Hereafter, he has no good deed left to be given good for."
"12263","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, joined his fingers and placed them upon the ground and said: This is the son of Adam. Then he raised them a little behind that and said: This is his term. Then he threw his hand before him and said: And there is his hope."
"12264","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he supplicated, would make the outer sides of his palms toward his face and their inner sides toward the ground."
"12265","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that Safiyyah fell in the share of Dihyah al-Kalbi, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, a beautiful slave girl has fallen in the share of Dihyah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought her for seven heads. Then he placed her with Umm Sulaym until she prepared herself and completed her waiting period, as far as Hammad knows. Then the people said: By Allah, we do not know whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her or took her as a concubine. Then when he carried her, he veiled her and mounted her behind him, so the people knew he had married her. Then when he neared Madinah, the people hastened and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened, and thus they used to do. Then the camel stumbled, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell, and she fell with him, while the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were looking. They said: May Allah distance the Jewess, and may He do to her and do. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and covered her and mounted her behind him."
"12266","Bahz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Safiyyah became for Dihyah in his share. Then he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: Until when he placed her behind him, he descended, then he struck the tent over her."
"12267","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The site of the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, belonged to Banu al-Najjar, and in it were palm trees and ruins and graves from the graves of the Jahiliyyah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Set a price for me. They said: We seek no price for it except with Allah, mighty and majestic. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the palms and they were cut, and the plowed land and it was spoiled, and the graves and they were exhumed. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, before that used to pray in the sheep pens wherever prayer overtook him."
"12268","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a Persian neighbor of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made good broth, so he made some for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he came to him inviting him. He said: And this one, for Aishah. He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No. Then he returned inviting him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And this one. He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And this one. He said: Yes, on the third time. So they stood pushing each other until they came to his house."
"12269","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Madinah, the Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it, so the Dajjal will not enter it, nor the plague, if Allah Almighty wills."
"12270","Yazid narrated to us: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. And he pointed with the index finger and the middle finger."
"12271","Yazid narrated to us: Hammad informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Strive against the polytheists with your wealth and your selves and your tongues."
"12272","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, and once he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Muadh ibn Jabal used to lead his people, and Haram entered while wanting to water his palms, so he entered the mosque to pray with the people, and when he saw Muadh lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. Then when Muadh finished the prayer, it was said to him: Haram entered the mosque, and when he saw you lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. He said: He is a hypocrite, does he hasten from prayer for the sake of watering his palms. He said: So Haram came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while Muadh was with him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted to water palms of mine, so I entered the mosque to pray with the people, and when he lengthened, I shortened my prayer and joined my palms to water them, and he claims I am a hypocrite. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to Muadh and said: Are you a trial, are you a trial. Do not lengthen with them. Recite: Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High, and By the sun and its brightness, and the like of them."
"12273","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wisal at the end of the month, and some people performed wisal. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: If the month were extended for us, I would continue a wisal that those who go to extremes would abandon their extremism. I am not like you. I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"12274","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, that he heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Walid narrate, from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raided or traveled and night overtook him, he would say: O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. I seek refuge in Allah from your evil and the evil of what was created in you and the evil of what is in you and the evil of what creeps upon you. I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the dweller of the town, and from the evil of a father and what he begot, and from the evil of a lion and a black snake and a serpent and a scorpion."
"12275","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: He lived one hundred years less a year."
"12276","Yazid narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Umm Sulaym took my hand upon the arrival of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Madinah, and brought me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my son, and he is a boy who writes. He said: So I served him nine years, and he never said to me for anything I ever did: You did wrong, or: Evil is what you did."
"12277","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that Harithah went out watching, and an arrow came to him and killed him. So his mother said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Harithah with me, so if he is in Paradise I will endure, otherwise you will see what I do. He said: O mother of Harithah, it is not one Paradise, but they are many Paradises, and Harithah is in the best of them. Or he said: In the highest Firdaws. Yazid doubted."
"12278","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When Allah, mighty and majestic, created the earth, it began to sway, so He created the mountains and cast them upon it, and it settled. So the angels marveled at the creation of the mountains and said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than the mountains. He said: Yes, iron. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than iron. He said: Yes, fire. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than fire. He said: Yes, water. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than water. He said: Yes, wind. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than wind. He said: Yes, the son of Adam, who gives charity with his right hand hiding it from his left."
"12279","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that eighty men of the people of Makkah descended upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the mountain of al-Tanim, armed, seeking to take the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his Companions unawares. So he took them peacefully and spared them. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: And He is the One who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah, after He gave you victory over them."
"12280","Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to turn to us with his face before saying takbir, and he would say: Line up closely and stand straight, for I see you from behind my back."
"12281","Yahya narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I entered Paradise and heard a movement before me. I said: What is this. They said: Al-Ghumaysa daughter of Milhan, the mother of Anas ibn Malik."
"12282","Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: A man peeked at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, through a crack, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, aimed an arrowhead at him until it reached his head. Yahya said: I said: Who narrated to you, O Abu Ubaydah, meaning Humayd. He said: Anas."
"12283","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid, and Rawh: Yazid ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, the meaning, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrate, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Some people of my ummah will enter the Fire until when they become charred, they will be admitted into Paradise. Then the people of Paradise will say: Who are these. So it will be said: They are the Jahannamiyyun."
"12284","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, he said: I heard Anas say: Verily the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to complete the takbir, they would say takbir when they prostrated and when they rose. Yahya said: Or lowered."
"12285","Abu al-Muthanna Muadh ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about His Almighty saying: Then when his Lord manifested to the mountain. He said: He said like this, meaning that he brought out the tip of the little finger. My father said: Muadh showed us. He said: Then Humayd al-Tawil said to him: What do you want with this, O Abu Muhammad. He said: Then he struck his chest a severe blow and said: Who are you, O Humayd, and what are you, O Humayd. Anas ibn Malik narrates it to me from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and you say: What do you want with it."
"12286","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that when the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they asked him to send with them a man to teach them. So he sent with them Abu Ubaydah, and said: He is the trustee of this ummah."
"12287","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while one of his wives was with him. So he said: O so-and-so, informing him that she was his wife. Then the man said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do you suspect me. So he said: I feared that Satan would enter upon you."
"12288","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not come to his family by night unexpectedly. He would enter upon them in the morning or in the evening."
"12289","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily Allah, mighty and majestic, does not wrong the believer a good deed, he is rewarded for it with provision in this world and recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given for his good deeds in this world, then when he meets Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection, he has no good deed left to be given good for."
"12290","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his hair would reach to his shoulders."
"12291","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, or from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had large feet and large hands and a handsome face. I never saw anyone like him after him."
"12292","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym sent him to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a basket containing ripe dates. So he began taking a handful and sending it to some of his wives, and taking a handful and sending it to some of his wives. Then he sat and ate the remainder, eating as a man eats of whom it is known that he desires it."
"12293","Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When it was the day of Fitr, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not go out until he ate dates, eating them singly."
"12294","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey in Ramadan, and a vessel was brought and he placed it upon his hand. Then when the people saw him, they broke their fast."
"12295","Rawh narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated, he said: I heard the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the people of Paradise see them, they will say: These are the Jahannamiyyun."
"12296","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, and Yunus: Shayban narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily the servant, when he is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, until he hears the striking of their sandals, two angels come to him and make him sit, and say to him: What did you used to say about this man, about Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. So it is said: Look at your seat from the Fire, Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So he sees them both together. Rawh said in his hadith: Qatadah said: Then it was mentioned to us that his grave is widened for him seventy cubits, and it is filled over him with greenery until the day they are raised. Then he returned to the hadith of Anas ibn Malik. He said: As for the disbeliever and the hypocrite, it is said to him: What did you used to say about this man. So he says: I do not know, I used to say what the people said. So it is said to him: You neither knew nor followed. Then he is struck with a hammer of iron, a blow between his ears, and he screams a scream heard by those next to him except the two weighty beings. And some of them said: His grave tightens upon him until his ribs differ."
"12297","Rawh narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The good dream of a righteous man is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"12298","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no soul that dies, having good with Allah, that is pleased to return to this world except the martyr, for he is pleased to return to this world and be killed another time, for what he sees of the merit of martyrdom."
"12299","Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not an insulter nor a curser nor obscene. He used to say to one of us when rebuking: What is with him, may his forehead be dusted."
"12300","Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas, who said: We attended a daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting upon the grave. Then I saw his eyes shedding tears. He said: Is there among you a man who did not commit last night. Abu Talhah said: Yes, I. He said: Then descend. He said: So he descended into her grave."
"12301","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you saw what I saw you would laugh little and weep much. They said: What did you see? He said: I saw Paradise and Hell. And he urged them to pray, and forbade them to precede him when he was their imam in bowing and prostration, and to leave before his leaving the prayer, and he said to them: I see you from in front of me and from behind me. And I asked Anas about the prayer of the sick person, and he said: He bows and prostrates sitting in the obligatory prayer."
"12302","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Mahan narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his she-camel voluntarily while traveling, facing other than the qiblah."
"12303","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Shumayt narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah al-Hanafi narrating that he heard Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Begging is not lawful except for three: one of grinding poverty, or one of crushing debt, or one of painful blood-money."
"12304","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl al-Uqayli narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has a household among people. It was said: Who are the household of Allah among them? He said: The people of the Quran, they are the household of Allah and His special ones."
"12305","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik while he was praying in a single garment, wrapped up, and his cloak was laid aside. He said: So I said to him: Do you pray in a single garment? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray like this."
"12306","Rawh narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadhin narrated to us, Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he ascended a hill or an elevation, said: O Allah, to You belongs eminence above every eminence, and to You belongs praise above every praise."
"12307","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted ruqyah for the evil eye, venomous sting, and scabies."
"12308","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The recitation of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was prolonged; he would prolong it with elongation."
"12309","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be spoken to about a need after he came down from the pulpit."
"12310","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, and Abu Usamah said: Sharik informed me, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O possessor of two ears."
"12311","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr or Khaythamah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me the kunyah after a herb I used to gather."
"12312","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit, and when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom, and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him hurrying."
"12313","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Permission was granted, or the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that was in them."
"12314","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It will be said to the man of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection: What do you think, if you had all that is on the earth, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. He will say: I wanted from you easier than that; I took a covenant from you in the back of Adam that you not associate anything with Me, but you refused except to associate with Me."
"12315","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"12316","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which supplication is best? He said: You ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Then he came to him the next day and said: O Messenger of Allah, which supplication is best? He said: You ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Then he came to him on the third day and said: O Messenger of Allah, which supplication is best? He said: You ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter, for if you are given them in this world and then given them in the Hereafter, you have succeeded."
"12317","Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has a household among people. He said: It was said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The people of the Quran, they are the household of Allah and His special ones."
"12318","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye is made in prayer."
"12319","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir al-Qari narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye is made in prayer."
"12320","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, when he drank, would breathe twice and thrice, and Anas would breathe three times."
"12321","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, he said: We used to come to Anas while his baker was standing. He said: So he said to us one day: Eat, for I do not know the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ever saw a thin loaf with his eye, nor ever ate a roasted sheep with skin intact."
"12322","Abu Amir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali, from Musa ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik while he was praying in a single garment, wrapped in it, and his cloak was laid aside. When he finished, we said to him: You pray while your cloak is laid aside? He said: Thus I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray."
"12323","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd narrated to me, from his father, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Khaybar, and a companion of ours entered a ruin to relieve himself, and took a brick to clean himself with, and it collapsed upon him as gold dust. So he took it and brought it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of that. He said: Weigh it. So he weighed it, and it was two hundred dirhams. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is buried treasure, and in it is the fifth."
"12324","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi narrated to me, that Anas informed him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Friday when the sun declined, and when he went out to Makkah he prayed Zuhr at al-Shajarah two rak'ahs."
"12325","Safwan ibn Isa and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, they said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Hamzah and stood over him and saw him mutilated. He said: Were it not that Safiyyah would feel it in herself, I would have left him until the wild beasts ate him. And Zayd ibn al-Hubab said: Until the carrion-eaters ate him, until he is resurrected from their bellies. Then he said: He called for a striped garment and shrouded him in it. He said: When it was drawn over his head his feet showed, and when it was drawn over his feet his head showed. He said: The slain were many and clothes were few. He said: And two men, and Zayd doubted, and three would be shrouded, Safwan doubted, in a single garment. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would ask about the one with most Quran and advance him toward the qiblah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, buried them and did not pray over them. And Zayd ibn al-Hubab said: So one man, and two men, and three would be shrouded in a single garment."
"12326","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I ended at the Lote Tree, and its fruits were like jars, and its leaves were like elephant ears. When it was covered by what covered it of the command of Allah, it turned into ruby or emerald or the like."
"12327","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that al-Rubayyi', the paternal aunt of Anas, broke the incisor of a girl. So they asked the people for pardon and they refused. So they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Retaliation. Anas ibn al-Nadr said: O Messenger of Allah, will the incisor of so-and-so be broken? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Anas, the Book of Allah is retaliation. He said: So he said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, the incisor of so-and-so will not be broken. He said: So the people were satisfied and pardoned and left retaliation. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear upon Allah, Allah fulfills it."
"12328","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mundhir ibn Jarud, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: One of my uncles made food and said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I love that you eat in my house and pray in it. He said: So he came, and in the house was a stallion camel among those stallions. He said: So he ordered a side of it, and it was swept and sprinkled, and he prayed, and we prayed."
"12329","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Badr: Who will look into what Abu Jahl did? He said: So Ibn Mas'ud went and found him struck down by the two sons of Afra until he fell to his knees. He said: So he took him by his beard and said: Are you Abu Jahl? He said: And is there above a man killed by his people, or he said: you killed?"
"12330","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham, Affan said: Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A woman from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Affan said: With her was a son of hers. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, and Ibn Ja'far said: He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was alone with her and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are among the most beloved people to me, three times."
"12331","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning the Ansar: You are among the most beloved people to me."
"12332","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sahl Abu al-Asad, he said: Bukayr ibn Wahb al-Jazari narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik said to me: I narrate to you a hadith I do not narrate to everyone: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at the door of the house while we were inside it, and said: The imams are from Quraysh. They have a right over you, and you have a right over them like that, as long as when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, and when they covenant they fulfill, and when they judge they are just. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"12333","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, from Anas, that he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith through which Allah may benefit you? The Messenger of Allah, when he stopped at a place, would not depart until he prayed Zuhr. He said: So Muhammad ibn Amr said: Even if at midday? He said: Even if at midday."
"12334","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hamzah al-Dabbi said: I met Anas ibn Malik at the mouth of the Nile, and he walked, and between me and him was Muhammad ibn Amr, and he mentioned the like of it. He said: So Muhammad ibn Amr said: Even if at midday?"
"12335","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Abu Fazarah, he said: I asked Anas about the two rak'ahs before Maghrib. He said: We used to hasten to them in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Shu'bah said: Then he said afterward, and I asked him more than once, and he said: We used to hasten to them, and he did not say: In the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12336","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Sadaqah, freedman of Anas, he said: I asked Anas about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and Asr between these two prayers of yours, and Maghrib when the sun set, and Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr when dawn rose until sight spread."
"12337","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to the lightest of the people of Hell in punishment: If you had all that is on the earth, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. He will say: I wanted from you what is easier than this, while you were in the loins of Adam, that you not associate with Me, but you refused except to associate with Me."
"12338","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about shortening prayer. He said: I used to go out to Kufah and pray two rak'ahs until I returned. And Anas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went out a distance of three miles or three farsakhs, Shu'bah the doubter, prayed two rak'ahs."
"12339","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, he said: The prayer was established while a man was privately conversing with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he kept conversing with him until his Companions slept. Then he stood and prayed."
"12340","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr, that he heard Anas ibn Malik narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe, he and a woman of his wives, from a single vessel."
"12341","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr, he said: I heard Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sign of faith is love of the Ansar, and the sign of hypocrisy is hatred of them."
"12342","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Patience is at the first shock."
"12343","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over the grave of a woman who had been buried."
"12344","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit, and when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom, and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hurrying."
"12345","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Allah commanded me to recite to you: Those who disbelieved were not. He said: And did He name me to you? He said: Yes. So he wept."
"12346","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, and Yazid said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, Ibn Ja'far said in his hadith: He said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Complete bowing and prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind me, and perhaps he said: from behind my back, when you bow and prostrate."
"12347","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. Shu'bah said: And I heard Qatadah saying in his stories: Like the excellence of one of them over the other. So I do not know whether he mentioned it from Anas or Qatadah said it."
"12348","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no contagion and no bad omen, and the good omen pleases me. It was said: And what is the good omen? He said: A good word."
"12349","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought meat, and it was said to him: It was given in charity to Barirah. So he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"12350","Mu'adh ibn Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yunus, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never ate on a table, nor in a small bowl, nor was thin bread baked for him. He said: I said to Qatadah: Upon what did they eat? He said: Upon leather mats."
"12351","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Rabi'ah narrated to me, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died when he was sixty years old, and there were not on his head and beard twenty white hairs."
"12352","Hasan al-Ashyab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The parable of my nation is the parable of rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"12353","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to give me a kunyah after a herb I used to gather."
"12354","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was a bulky man who could not pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I cannot pray with you; if only you came to my house and prayed, so I follow you. So the man prepared food, then invited the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he sprinkled the edge of a mat of theirs, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed two rak'ahs. So a man of the family of al-Jarud said to Anas: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Duha? He said: I did not see him pray it except that day."
"12355","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man of the Ansar said, and he mentioned its meaning."
"12356","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Abyad, Hajjaj said: A man of Banu Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Asr while the sun was white, high."
"12357","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, our neighbor, narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Mu'adh ibn Jabal: Know that whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"12358","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah informed us, and Hashim said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Make easy and do not make difficult, and give tranquility and do not repel."
"12359","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two, and he extended his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"12360","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, and Hajjaj said: I heard Shu'bah, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray in sheepfolds before the mosque was built."
"12361","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the major sins, or he was asked about the major sins, and said: Associating with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, killing a soul, and disobedience to parents. And he said: Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the major sins? He said: False speech, or he said: False testimony. Shu'bah said: The greater part of my supposition is that he said: False testimony."
"12362","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar, he said: I was walking with Thabit al-Bunani, and he passed by boys and greeted them, and narrated that he used to walk with Anas, and he passed by boys and greeted them, and Anas narrated that he used to walk with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he passed by boys and greeted them."
"12363","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to drink standing. He said: So we said to Anas: And food? He said: That is worse, or more foul. Ibn Bakr said: Or more evil."
"12364","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Mahmud, he said: I prayed with Anas on Friday, and we were pushed toward the pillars, so we moved forward or backward. So Anas said: We used to avoid this in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12365","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that his grandmother Mulaykah invited the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to food she made. So he ate of it, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Stand, so I pray for you. Anas said: So I stood to a mat of ours that had blackened from long use, and sprinkled it with water. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood upon it. So I stood, I and the orphan, behind him, and the old woman behind us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us two rak'ahs, then left."
"12366","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about the recitation of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: He would prolong his voice with elongation."
"12367","Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A man of the people of Paradise will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your dwelling? He will say: O Lord, the best dwelling. He will say: Ask and wish. He will say: I ask and wish only that You return me to this world and I be killed in Your path ten times, for what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom."
"12368","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would see a date, and were it not that he feared it was charity, he would have eaten it."
"12369","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Ibn Umm Maktum twice in charge of Madinah, and I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah with him a black banner."
"12370","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: There was no person more beloved to them than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when they saw him they did not stand, for what they knew of his dislike of that."
"12371","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would perform ablution at every prayer. He said: I said: And you, how did you do? He said: We used to pray the prayers with a single ablution, as long as we did not break it."
"12372","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Zubayr, meaning Ibn Adi, he said: We complained to Anas ibn Malik of what we meet from al-Hajjaj. He said: Be patient, for there comes upon you no year or day except what is after it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord, Mighty and Majestic. I heard it from your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12373","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the Asr prayer came, and people sought water for ablution and did not find it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought his ablution water, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand in that vessel and ordered people to perform ablution from it. So I saw water springing from beneath his fingers, and people performed ablution until they all performed ablution, to the last of them."
"12374","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to complete the takbir when they rose and when they lowered."
"12375","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A morning going in the path of Allah, or an evening going, is better than this world and what is in it."
"12376","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raid at dawn break, and listen. If he heard an adhan, he held back, otherwise he raided. He said: So he listened one day. He said: So he heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. So he said: Upon the fitrah. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. So he said: You have come out of Hell."
"12377","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete the first row, then the one next to it. If there is a deficiency, let it be in the last row."
"12378","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Aban, meaning Ibn Khalid, Ubaydullah ibn Rawahah narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, that he did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray Duha except to go out on a journey or to come from a journey."
"12379","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Jews, when a woman of them menstruated, would not eat with them nor mingle with them in houses. So the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from women in menstruation, and do not approach them until they are pure, until the end of the verse. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do everything except intercourse. That reached the Jews, and they said: This man does not want to leave anything of our affair except he opposes us in it. So Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews said such and such; shall we then mingle with them? So the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed, until we thought he was angry with them. So they left, and a gift of milk to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met them. So he sent after them and gave them to drink, and they knew he was not angry with them. Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Hammad ibn Salamah would not praise or commend anything of his hadith except this hadith, for its excellence."
"12380","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Imran, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to Khosrau, Caesar, and Ukaydir of Dumah, calling them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"12381","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Azrah narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abdullah, that Anas would not refuse perfume. He said: And Anas claimed that the Messenger of Allah would not refuse perfume."
"12382","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: For every nation is a trustworthy one, and Abu Ubaydah is the trustworthy one of this nation."
"12383","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Had Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lived, he would have been a truthful prophet."
"12384","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left the prayer from his right."
"12385","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that he walked to the Prophet with barley bread and rancid melted fat."
"12386","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had mortgaged a shield of his with a Jew in Madinah, and took barley from him for his family."
"12387","He said: And I heard him one day saying: There did not remain in the evening with the family of Muhammad a sa' of grain nor a sa' of wheat, while he had nine wives that day."
"12388","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Some people will be struck by blackness from Hell as punishment for sins they did, then Allah will admit them to Paradise by the excellence of His mercy, and it will be said to them: The Hell-dwellers."
"12389","Abu Amir and Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Like what is between the two sides of my Basin is like what is between Madinah and Sanaa, or like what is between Madinah and Oman. And Azhar said: Like, and he said: Oman."
"12390","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the barber was shaving him, and his Companions had surrounded him; they did not want a hair to fall except in the hand of a man."
"12391","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would perform ablution at every prayer. I said: And you, how do you do? He said: We used to pray the prayers with a single ablution."
"12392","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, Ja'far said: I think it only from Anas, he said: We were rained upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he went out and uncovered his garment until the rain struck it. He said: So it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do this? He said: Because it is newly come from its Lord."
"12393","Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the verse of the veil came down, I came to enter as I used to enter, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Behind you, O my son."
"12394","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw yellowness on a man and disliked it. He said: If only you ordered this one to wash this yellowness. He said: And he would hardly confront anyone to his face with what he disliked."
"12395","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe with a woman of his wives from a single vessel."
"12396","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sign of hypocrisy is hatred of the Ansar, and the sign of faith is love of the Ansar."
"12397","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, once from Thabit, from Anas, and once from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was no one of people more beloved to them in person than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When they saw him, none of them would stand for him, for what they knew of his dislike of that."
"12398","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah informed me, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the major sins, or he mentioned them. He said: Association, disobedience, killing a soul, and false testimony or false speech."
"12399","Bahz and Abd al-Samad, the meaning, narrated to us, they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, I said: How many pilgrimages did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform? He said: One pilgrimage, and he performed Umrah four times: his Umrah at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah, and his Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah from Madinah, and his Umrah from al-Ji'ranah in Dhu al-Qa'dah where he divided the spoils of Hunayn, and his Umrah with his pilgrimage."
"12400","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: We used to come to Anas ibn Malik while his baker was standing. He said: So he said one day: Eat, for I do not know the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ever saw a thin loaf, nor a roasted sheep with skin intact. Affan said in his hadith: Until he met his Lord."
"12401","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that it was sent down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his way back from al-Hudaybiya while his Companions were mingled with grief and gloom and had been barred from their homes and had sacrificed the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiya: Indeed We have granted you a clear conquest, up to His saying, a straight path. He said: Two verses have been sent down upon me that are dearer to me than the whole world. He said: When he recited them a man said: Joyful and wholesome, O Prophet of Allah, Allah has made clear to you what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down the verse after it: That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, until he sealed the verse."
"12402","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada saying in his stories: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will come out of the Fire after the Fire has touched them with scorching, then they will enter Paradise, and the people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamis. He said: And Qatada used to follow this narration, and Allah knows best, but the most deserving whom you believe are the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whom Allah chose for the companionship of His Prophet and the establishment of His religion."
"12403","Bahz and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a supplication he has supplicated with and been answered, and I have held back my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"12404","Bahz and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, he said: I said to Anas: Which clothing was most pleasing, Affan said: or most beloved, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The hibara."
"12405","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping unripe dates and ripe dates together."
"12406","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast over one another about mosques."
"12407","Bahz and Affan said: Aban narrated to us, Bahz, Bahz ibn Yazid al-Attar said: Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hell will keep saying: Is there any more? He said: Then the Lord of the worlds will lower His foot into it. He said: Then part of it will contract to another part, and it will say: Enough, enough, by Your might. And there will remain surplus in Paradise until Allah creates another creation for it and settles them in the surplus of Paradise."
"12408","Bahz narrated to us, Ali ibn Masada narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Islam is outward and faith is in the heart. He said: Then he would point with his hand to his chest three times. He said: Then he would say: Taqwa is here, taqwa is here."
"12409","Bahz narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada, he said: I asked Anas about the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: His hair was wavy, neither very curly nor very straight; it was between his ears and his shoulders."
"12410","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us except that he said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"12411","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Utban complained of his eye, so he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him what had befallen him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, come and pray in my house so that I may take it as a prayer place. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, along with whomsoever Allah willed of his Companions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying while his Companions talked among themselves and began mentioning what they met from the hypocrites, and they attributed the bulk of that to Malik ibn Dukhaysham. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished and said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? A speaker said: Yes, but it is not from his heart. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, the Fire will never taste him, or he said: he will never enter the Fire."
"12412","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the good dream, and he would often say: Has any one of you seen a dream? And if a man saw a dream he would ask about him, and if there was nothing wrong with him his dream would be more pleasing to him. He said: Then a woman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as though I entered Paradise and heard therein a crash at which Paradise shook, and I looked and behold so-and-so son of so-and-so and so-and-so son of so-and-so had been brought, until she counted twelve men, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent an expedition before that. She said: They were brought wearing dusty garments with their jugular veins spurting blood. He said: Then it was said: Take them to the river of al-Baydakh, or he said: to the river of al-Baydag. He said: They were dipped in it and came out of it with their faces like the moon on the night of full moon. He said: Then chairs of gold were brought and they sat upon them, and a platter or a word like it containing unripe dates was brought and they ate from it, and they would not turn it to any side but they ate of whatever fruit they wished, and I ate with them. He said: Then the bearer of glad tidings came from that expedition and said: O Messenger of Allah, such-and-such happened in our affair, and so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted the twelve whom the woman had counted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the woman. She came. He said: Narrate your dream to this man. She narrated it. He said: It is as she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12413","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, the same meaning."
"12414","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined his fingertips and poked them into the earth and said: This is the son of Adam, and he said with his hand behind that: And this is his term, he said: And he gestured before him, he said: And there is his hope, three times."
"12415","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Musa Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in the winter days, and we would not know whether more of the day had passed or what remained."
"12416","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his hair would not go beyond his ears."
"12417","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"12418","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam daughter of Imran, and Khadija daughter of Khuwaylid, and Fatima daughter of Muhammad, and Asiya the wife of Pharaoh."
"12419","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: It reached Safiyya that Hafsa said: I am the daughter of a Jew. So she wept, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was weeping and said: What is the matter with you? She said: Hafsa said to me: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the daughter of a Prophet, and your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsa."
"12420","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed on behalf of Julaybib a woman of the Ansar to her father, and he said: Until I consult her mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then yes, if so. He said: So the man went to his wife and mentioned that to her, and she said: No, by Allah, then, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find none but Julaybib, and we have already refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: And the girl was in her curtain listening. He said: So the man set out intending to inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, and the girl said: Do you want to turn back the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If he has approved him for you, then marry her to him. It was as though she removed doubt from her parents, and they said: You are right. So her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If you have approved him, we have approved him. He said: Then I have approved him. So he married her to him. Then the people of Medina were alarmed, so Julaybib rode out, and they found him killed with people of the polytheists around him whom he had killed. Anas said: I saw her, and she was indeed of the most spending house in Medina."
"12421","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: A man of Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am one of much wealth and of family and children and settled presence, so tell me how I should spend and what I should do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You take out the zakat from your wealth, for it is a purification that purifies you, and you join your kin, and you recognize the right of the beggar and the neighbor and the poor. He said: O Messenger of Allah, make it less for me. He said: Then give the near of kin his right, and the poor, and the wayfarer, and do not squander wastefully. He said: It is enough for me, O Messenger of Allah, if I pay the zakat to your messenger I am quit of it before Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, if you pay it to my messenger you are quit of it, so for you is its reward and its sin is upon whoever alters it."
"12422","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina while it was feverish, so the people suffered fever. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while the people were sitting praying, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. So the people strained themselves to pray standing."
"12423","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and took a midday nap with us, and he sweated, and my mother came with a bottle and began to collect the sweat into it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: O Umm Sulaym, what is this that you are doing? She said: This is your sweat; we put it in our perfume, and it is among the sweetest of perfume."
"12424","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will come to the gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and seek its opening, and the keeper will say: Who are you? He said: So I will say: Muhammad. He said: He will say: For you I was commanded not to open for anyone before you."
"12425","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Busaysa as a scout to see what the caravan of Abu Sufyan had done. He came while there was no one in the house other than me and other than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I do not know what he exempted of some of his women. So he told him the report. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and spoke and said: We have a pursuit, so whoever has his mount present, let him ride with us. Men began to ask his permission for mounts of theirs in the upper part of Medina. He said: No, except whoever has his mount present. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions set out until they outpaced the polytheists to Badr, and the polytheists came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you advance to anything until I am the one who gives him leave. The polytheists drew near, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rise to a Paradise whose width is the heavens and the earth. He said: Umayr ibn al-Humam al-Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, a Paradise whose width is the heavens and the earth? He said: Yes. So he said: Bakh bakh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you say bakh bakh? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, except hope that I may be of its people. He said: Then you are of its people. He said: Then he took out dates from his quiver and began to eat of them, then he said: If I live until I eat these dates of mine, it is indeed a long life. He said: Then he threw away what he had with him of dates, then he fought them until he was killed."
"12426","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When this verse came down: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, up to His saying, while you do not perceive, and Thabit ibn Qays ibn al-Shammas was loud of voice, he said: I am the one who used to raise my voice above the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); my deed is nullified; I am of the people of the Fire. And he sat among his family grieving. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him, so some of the people went to him and said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has missed you; what is the matter with you? He said: I am the one who raises my voice above the voice of the Prophet and speaks out loudly; my deed is nullified and I am of the people of the Fire. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what he said, and he said: No, rather he is of the people of Paradise. Anas said: And we used to see him walking among us while we knew that he was of the people of Paradise. Then on the day of al-Yamama there was among us some retreat, so Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas came having embalmed himself and put on his shroud and said: How evil is what you accustom your peers to. So he fought them until he was killed."
"12427","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the barber shaving him while his Companions surrounded him, not wanting a single hair to fall except into the hand of a man."
"12428","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer, the servants of the people of Medina would come with their vessels containing water, and no vessel would be brought but he would dip his hand into it, and they would often come to him in the cold morning and he would dip his hand into it."
"12429","Hashim and Affan, the meaning, said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: We were with Anas ibn Malik, and he wrote a document between his family and said: Bear witness, O company of reciters. Thabit said: It is as though I disliked that, so I said: O Abu Hamza, if only you had named them by their names. He said: And what is wrong with that, that I say to you reciters? Shall I not narrate to you about your brothers whom we used to call in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the reciters? Then he mentioned that they were seventy, and when night covered them they would go to a teacher of theirs in Medina and study the night until morning, and when morning came whoever had strength would fetch sweet water and gather firewood, and whoever had means, they would gather and buy a sheep and prepare it, so that would become hung at the apartments of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Khubayb was struck, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them, and they came upon a clan of Banu Sulaym, and among them was my uncle Haram. Haram said to their leader: Leave me so I may inform these people that we do not intend them, so that they let our way be, and Affan said: so they let our way be. He said to them, Haram: We do not intend you, so let our way be. A man faced him with a spear and pierced him through with it, and when he felt the spear in his belly he said: Allah is greatest, I have won, by the Lord of the Kaba. He said: Then they closed in upon them, and none of them remained. Anas said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieve over anything ever as he grieved over them. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning prayer raise his hands and supplicate against them. Then after that, behold Abu Talha saying to me: Are you interested in the killer of Haram? He said: I said to him: What of him, may Allah do to him and do. He said: Gently, for he has become Muslim. And Affan said: He raised his hands supplicating against them. And Abu al-Nadr said: He raised his hands."
"12430","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to Ubayy ibn Kab: My Lord the Mighty and Majestic commanded me to recite the Quran to you. Ubayy said: Did He name me to you? He said: Yes. So Ubayy wept."
"12431","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Usayd ibn Hudayr and another man of the Ansar talked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night about a need of theirs until an hour of the night had gone, on a night of intense darkness. Then they left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returning, with a small stick in the hand of each of them. The stick of one of them lit the way for them until they walked in its light, until when the road parted them, the stick of the other lit for him. Each of them walked in the light of his stick until he reached his family."
"12432","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: O son of Adam, if you remember Me within yourself I remember you within Myself, and if you remember Me in a gathering I remember you in a gathering of angels or in a gathering better than them. If you draw near to Me a span I draw near to you a cubit, and if you draw near to Me a cubit I draw near to you a fathom, and if you come to Me walking I come to you hastening. Qatada said: Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic is quicker with forgiveness."
"12433","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas or another, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked permission upon Sad ibn Ubada and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Sad said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah, without letting the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hear, until he greeted three times and Sad answered him three times without letting him hear. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, and Sad followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be for you, you did not greet a greeting but it was in my ear, and I answered you without letting you hear; I loved to increase in your greeting and in blessing. Then he brought him into the house and set before him raisins, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate. When he finished he said: The righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have prayed upon you, and the fasting have broken fast with you."
"12434","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture in prayer."
"12435","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between Zuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha while traveling."
"12436","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Mecca and I have family there, and I want to go to them, so I am absolved if I disparage you or say something. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him leave to say what he wished. He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather for me what you have with you, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth struck. He said: So that spread in Mecca, and the Muslims were suppressed, and the polytheists showed joy and gladness. He said: And the news reached al-Abbas, and he was crippled and could not stand. Mamar said: Uthman al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, he said: So he took a son of his called Qutham, lay back, placed him on his chest, saying: Long live Qutham, long live Qutham, like the one with the proud nose, son of the possessor of favors, may whoever resists be humbled. Thabit said, from Anas: Then he sent a boy to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat: Woe to you, what have you brought and what are you saying, for what Allah has promised is better than what you have brought. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said to his boy: Convey greeting to Abu al-Fadl and say to him: Let him be alone for me in one of his houses so I may come to him, for the news is what will please him. His boy came, and when he reached the door of the house he said: Glad tidings, O Abu al-Fadl. He said: Al-Abbas leapt in joy until he kissed between his eyes. He informed him of what al-Hajjaj said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came to him and informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoil, and the arrows of Allah the Mighty and Majestic had run in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Safiyya daughter of Huyayy for himself and gave her choice that he free her and she be his wife or join her family, and she chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for wealth of mine here I wanted to gather and go with, so I asked leave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave me leave to say what I wished, so conceal from me for three days, then mention what you wish. He said: So his wife gathered what she had of jewelry and goods, gathered it, and handed it to him. Then he went on with it. When after three days, al-Abbas went to the wife of al-Hajjaj and said: What did your husband do? She informed him that he had gone on such-and-such day, and said: May Allah not disgrace you, O Abu al-Fadl, we were grieved by what reached you. He said: Yes, may Allah not disgrace me; there was, by praise of Allah, nothing but what we loved: Allah opened Khaybar for His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the arrows of Allah ran therein, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyya daughter of Huyayy for himself. If you have need of your husband, join him. She said: I think, by Allah, you are truthful. He said: Then I am truthful; the affair is as I informed you. He went until he came to the gatherings of Quraysh, and they were saying when he passed them: Nothing but good befall you, O Abu al-Fadl. He said to them: Nothing but good befell me, by praise of Allah. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat informed me that Allah has opened Khaybar for His Messenger, and the arrows of Allah have run therein, and he chose Safiyya for himself. He asked me to conceal for him for three days, and he only came to take his wealth and what he had of anything here, then go. He said: So Allah turned the gloom that had been upon the Muslims onto the polytheists, and the Muslims came out, and whoever had entered his house gloomy, until they came to al-Abbas and he informed them of the news. The Muslims rejoiced, and Allah turned, meaning what there was of gloom or anger or grief, onto the polytheists."
"12437","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, he said: I saw with Anas the cup of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in it a silver band."
"12438","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: I saw with Anas ibn Malik a cup that had belonged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in it a silver band."
"12439","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I said to Anas: Narrate to us, O Abu Hamza, something of these wonders you witnessed, not narrating it from another than you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Zuhr prayer one day, then went until he sat upon the seats to which Jibril used to come to him. Bilal came and called him to Asr. Everyone who had family in Medina rose to relieve himself and take ablution, and there remained men of the Muhajirin who had no families in Medina. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a wide cup containing water, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in the vessel, but the vessel did not contain the whole palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said with these four into the vessel. Then he said: Draw near and perform ablution, with his hand in the vessel. So they performed ablution until none of them remained but had performed ablution. He said: I said: O Abu Hamza, how many do you see them? He said: Between seventy and eighty."
"12440","Affan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I said to Anas: Narrate to us something of these wonders, not narrating it from another than you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Zuhr prayer, then he mentioned its meaning."
"12441","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Drawing water with camels was hard upon the Ansar, so they gathered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him to make flow for them a flowing river. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Welcome to the Ansar. By Allah, you will not ask me today for anything but I will give it to you, nor will I ask Allah for you for anything but He will give it to me. Some of them said to others: Seize it and seek forgiveness. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah for us for forgiveness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"12442","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he said: There was a man who made a lahd and another who made a darih. They said: We seek the good choice of our Lord. So they sent to them, and whichever of them came first we would leave him. So they sent to them, and the maker of the lahd came first, so they made a lahd for him."
"12443","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: Abu Talha cauterized me while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, and I was not forbidden it."
"12444","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining upon a bed woven with cord, with under his head a pillow of leather stuffed with palm fiber. Some of his Companions entered upon him, and Umar entered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shifted a shifting, and Umar saw no garment between his side and the cord, and the cord had marked the side of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What makes you weep, O Umar? He said: By Allah, only that I know you are more honored with Allah the Mighty and Majestic than Kisra and Caesar, while they revel in the world in what they revel in, and you, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), are in the place I see. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you not pleased that for them be the world and for us the Hereafter? Umar said: Yes. He said: Then it is so."
"12445","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men of those who have accompanied me will come to my Basin, and when I see them raised to me they will be snatched away from me."
"12446","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first intercessor in Paradise."
"12447","Abu Asim narrated to us, Abu Amr Mubarak al-Khayyat, grandfather of the children of Abbad ibn Kathir, informed us, he said: I asked Thumama ibn Abdillah ibn Anas about coitus interruptus, and he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked about coitus interruptus. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were to spill the fluid from which the child comes upon a rock, Allah the Mighty and Majestic would bring forth from it, or there would come forth from it, a child, the doubt is from him, and Allah will surely create a soul He is its Creator."
"12448","Hammad ibn Masada narrated to us, from Qurra ibn Khalid, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Uhud and said: A mountain that loves us and we love it."
"12449","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas and Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering, and whoever plunders is not of us."
"12450","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping dates and raisins together, and steeping dates and unripe dates together."
"12451","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad meaning Ibn Talha narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lower garment is to mid-calf and to the ankles; there is no good in lower than that."
"12452","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman al-Bakri narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A man came until he peered into the apartment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and took a barbed arrowhead, came until he faced the man and brought it to him, so the man shrank back and went away."
"12453","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? He said: Then his speech about that grew stern until he said: They will either stop from that or their eyesight will be snatched away."
"12454","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Jew greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. He said: Bring him back to me. He said: Did you say death be upon you? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."
"12455","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the call of Bilal prevent you from the pre-dawn meal, for in his sight is something."
"12456","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Muadh ibn Harmala al-Azdi narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people are rained upon with a general rain and the earth grows nothing."
"12457","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man passed, and a man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this man. He said: Have you informed him of that? He said: No. He said: Rise and inform him. He said: So he rose to him and said: O you, by Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah. He said: May the One for whose sake you loved me love you."
"12458","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed a man over to Hafsa daughter of Umar and said: Guard him. He said: Hafsa was heedless and the man went off. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: O Hafsa, what did the man do? She said: I was heedless of him, O Messenger of Allah, so he left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah cut your hand. So she raised her hands thus. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: What is the matter with you, O Hafsa? She said: O Messenger of Allah, you said before to me such-and-such. He said to her: Fold your hands, for I asked Allah the Mighty and Majestic that any human of my nation against whom I supplicate Allah the Mighty and Majestic, He make it forgiveness for him."
"12459","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I love this chapter: Say, He is Allah, One. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"12460","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this chapter. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"12461","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: When Fatima said that, meaning when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt of the distress of death what he felt, Fatima said: O distress. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O my little daughter, there has come upon your father what Allah will not leave anyone of in meeting the Day of Resurrection."
"12462","Khalaf narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, Thabit narrated to me, from Anas, he said: When Fatima said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"12463","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the cause of Allah or an evening going is better than the world and what is in it, and the span of the bow of one of you, or the place of his whip, meaning his lash, of Paradise is better than the world and what is in it. If a woman of the women of the people of Paradise were to look down to the earth, she would fill what is between them with fragrance and what is between them would be sweet, and her head-cover upon her head is better than the world and what is in it."
"12464","Al-Hashimi meaning Sulayman narrated to us, from Ismail, from Humayd, from Anas, its meaning."
"12465","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talha, he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Abu Talha was the most wealthy of the Ansar in Medina, and the most beloved of his wealth to him was Bayruha, and it was facing the mosque. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter it and drink of sweet water therein. Anas said: When there came down: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, Abu Talha said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah says: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, and the most beloved of my wealth to me is Bayruha, and it is charity for Allah the Mighty and Majestic, I hope its righteousness and its store with Allah, so place it, O Messenger of Allah, where Allah shows you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bakh, that is profitable wealth, that is profitable wealth. I have heard, and I think you should place it among the nearest kin. Abu Talha said: I will do, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So Abu Talha divided it among his kin and his cousins."
"12466","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man asks Allah for Paradise three times but Paradise says: O Allah, admit him. And no Muslim man seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire three times but the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge."
"12467","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hell will keep saying: Is there any more? Then the Lord of the worlds says, and He places His foot in it, so part of it contracts to another part, and it says: By Your might, enough, enough. And there will remain surplus in Paradise until Allah creates another creation and settles them in the surplus of Paradise."
"12468","Hisham ibn Said al-Talaqani narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Umar a cloak of sundus. He said: Umar met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You sent to me a cloak of sundus, yet you said about it what you said. He said: I did not send it to you to wear it; I only sent it to you to sell it or benefit by it."
"12469","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Suhayl brother of Hazm informed me, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Worthy of piety and worthy of forgiveness. He said: Your Lord said: I am worthy to be feared, so no god is set with Me. Whoever fears to set with Me a god is worthy that I forgive him."
"12470","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For every treacherous one a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known."
"12471","Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the son of Adam, and here is his term, and there is his hope. And Affan put forth his hand."
"12472","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his hair would not go beyond his ears."
"12473","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you dozes while praying, let him leave and sleep until he knows what he says."
"12474","Rawh narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came to Mecca having entered ihram for hajj and umra. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them, after they circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwa, to make it umra and to exit ihram. The people shrank from that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I drove the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. So the people exited ihram and enjoyed."
"12475","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Abu Qudama al-Hanafi, he said: I said to Anas: With what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter ihram? He said: I heard him seven times: With umra and hajj, with umra and hajj."
"12476","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrating from Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joining between fresh dates and melon."
"12477","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad meaning Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that Hilal ibn Umayya accused his wife with Sharik ibn Sahma. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at her; if she brings him curly-haired, dark-eyed, thin-legged, he is for Sharik ibn Sahma, and if she brings him fair, straight-haired, bleary-eyed, he is for Hilal ibn Umayya. She brought him curly-haired, dark-eyed, thin-legged."
"12478","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Maymun al-Marai narrated to us, Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No two Muslims meet and one of them takes the hand of his companion but it is due upon Allah to attend their supplication and not separate their hands until He forgives them."
"12479","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, place in Medina twice what is in Mecca of blessing."
"12480","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Maymun al-Marai informed us, Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No people gather remembering Allah, intending by that nothing but His face, but a caller from heaven calls to them: Rise forgiven for you; your evil deeds have been exchanged for good deeds."
"12481","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that three men of those before among people went out seeking pasture for their families. Rain seized them, so they entered a cave, and a rock falling from above dropped upon them until they saw no opening of it. Some of them said to others: The rock has fallen and the trace is effaced, and none knows your place but Allah, so supplicate Allah with your firmest deeds. He said: A man of them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel and bring them, and when I found them sleeping I would stand over their heads, disliking to disturb their slumber in their heads, until they woke whenever they woke. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. A third of the rock moved away. The other said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a hireling for work he would do, and he came to me seeking his wage while I was angry, so I scolded him, and he went off leaving that wage of his. I gathered it and increased it until all wealth came from it. He came to me seeking his wage, and I handed to him all that. Had I wished I would have given him only his first wage. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: Two thirds of the rock moved away. The third said: O Allah, if You know that a woman pleased him, so he set for her a reward, and when he had power over her and her soul settled for him and he handed to her her reward. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. The rock moved away, and they came out embracing, walking."
"12482","Abdullah said: Abu Bahr narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, Abdullah said: from Anas, then he mentioned the like of it."
"12483","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that three men set out, then he mentioned its meaning. My father said: And he did not raise it."
"12484","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We had been forbidden to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything, so it used to please us that a sensible man of the desert folk come and ask him while we listened. A man of the desert folk came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed to us that you claim that Allah sent you. He said: He spoke truth. He said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah. He said: Who created the earth? He said: Allah. He said: Who set up these mountains and placed therein what He placed? He said: Allah. He said: By the One who created the heaven and created the earth and set up these mountains, did Allah send you? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that upon us are five prayers in our day and our night. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that upon us is zakat in our wealth. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that upon us is fasting the month of Ramadan in our year. He said: Yes, he spoke truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that upon us is pilgrimage to the House, whoever is able to it a way. He said: He spoke truth. He said: Then he turned away and said: By the One who sent you with the truth as Prophet, I will neither add to them anything nor decrease of them anything. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he speaks truth he will surely enter Paradise."
"12485","Abd al-Samad narrated to me, Shuba narrated to us, and Abu Dawud said: Shuba informed us, the meaning, Thabit narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas saying to a woman of his family: Do you know so-and-so? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her while she was weeping over a grave and said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said to him: Away from me, for you do not care about my calamity. He said: And she had not known him. It was said to her: He is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Death-like seizure took her. She came to his door and found no doorkeeper upon it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not know you. He said: Patience is at the first shock."
"12486","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Shuayb meaning Ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have urged you much about the toothstick."
"12487","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrating from Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joining between fresh dates and melon."
"12488","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The likeness of my nation is like the rain; it is not known whether its first is better or its last."
"12489","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd and Yunus, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my nation, then he mentioned it."
"12490","Yunus and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not foul-mouthed, nor obscene, nor cursing. He used to say to one of us at rebuke: What is with him, may his forehead be dusted."
"12491","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth meaning Ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakas, and with Abu Bakr two rakas, and with Umar two rakas, and with Uthman two rakas at the beginning of his rule."
"12492","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Musahiq, from Amir ibn Abdillah meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, from Anas, he said: I never saw an imam more resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this imam of yours, for Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, while he was in Medina that day. And Umar would not lengthen the recitation."
"12493","Yunus narrated to us, Aban meaning Ibn Zayd al-Attar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughter his sacrifice with his hand, and he would magnify Allah over it."
"12494","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: While the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions, a Jew passed them and greeted them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring him back. He said: How did you say? He said: I said death be upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: And upon you, that is what you said."
"12495","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Zayd meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: If My servant is tried with his two beloved ones then is patient, I compensate him for them with Paradise, meaning his two eyes."
"12496","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am the first of people whose skull the earth will split from on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am given the banner of praise, and no boast. I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am the first who will enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I will come to the gate of Paradise and take its ring. They will say: Who is this? He will say: I am Muhammad. They will open for me and I will enter, and behold the Compeller the Mighty and Majestic facing me, so I will prostrate to Him. He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, say and it will be accepted from you, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and say: My nation, my nation, O Lord. He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart the weight of a grain of barley of faith, admit him into Paradise. So I will come; whomever I find in his heart that, I will admit him into Paradise. And behold the Compeller the Mighty and Majestic facing me, so I will prostrate to Him. He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, say and it will be accepted from you, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and say: My nation, my nation, O Lord. He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart half a grain of barley of faith, admit them into Paradise. So I will go; whomever I find in his heart the weight of that, I will admit them into Paradise. And behold the Compeller the Mighty and Majestic facing me, so I will prostrate to Him. He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, say and it will be accepted from you, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and say: My nation, my nation. He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard of faith, admit him into Paradise. So I will go; whomever I find in his heart the weight of that, I will admit them into Paradise. Allah will finish the reckoning of people and admit who remains of my nation into the Fire with the people of the Fire. The people of the Fire will say: What availed you that you used to worship Allah the Mighty and Majestic associating nothing with Him? The Compeller the Mighty and Majestic will say: By My might, I will surely free them from the Fire. He will send to them, and they will come out charred. They will enter the river of life and grow therein as the seed grows in the foam of the torrent. It will be written between their eyes: These are the freed ones of Allah the Mighty and Majestic. They will be taken and enter Paradise. The people of Paradise will say to them: These are the Jahannamis. The Compeller will say: Rather these are the freed ones of the Compeller the Mighty and Majestic."
"12497","Abu Salama al-Khuzai narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am the first of people, then he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: As the seed sprouts."
"12498","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: And Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered some twenty-odd men of the chiefs of Quraysh, and they were cast into a foul defiled well of the wells of Badr. He said: And when he prevailed over a people he would stay at the open ground three nights. He said: When he prevailed at Badr he stayed three nights, until when it was the third he ordered his mount and it was saddled with its saddle. Then he walked and his Companions followed him. They said: We only think he goes to relieve himself. He said: Until he stood on the edge of the well. He said: He began calling them by their names and the names of their fathers: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, would it have pleased you to have obeyed Allah and His Messenger? Have you found what your Lord promised you true? Umar said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you address of bodies with no souls in them? He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are not more hearing of what I say than they. Qatada said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic gave them life for him until they heard his saying as rebuke and belittling and vengeance."
"12499","Ismail ibn Muhammad, and he is Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Abbad meaning Ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar in my house which is in Medina."
"12500","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib narrated it to us, and he was of the best of people, and Abu Abd al-Rahman greatly magnified his standing."
"12501","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in mosques."
"12502","Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abu Ya'qub, meaning Ishaq, narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani, and a man asked him: Did you ask Anas ibn Malik? Thabit said: I asked Anas: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, took His Messenger and did not disgrace him with grey hair; there were on his head and his beard on the day he died not thirty white hairs. And it was said to him: Is it a disgrace? He said: As for you, you count it a disgrace, but as for us, we used to count it an adornment."
"12503","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama, narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in the house of Umm Sulaym on an old mat that had changed with age. He said: And she sprinkled it with some water, and he prostrated on it."
"12504","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire and the people of Paradise? As for the people of Paradise, every weak one, deemed weak, disheveled, with two worn garments, if he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. And as for the people of the Fire, every coarse, swaggering, hoarder, withholder, follower."
"12505","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to sell the stud service of his stallion."
"12506","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prayer at Mina as two rak'as, and Abu Bakr prayed it at Mina as two rak'as, and Umar prayed it at Mina as two rak'as, and Uthman ibn Affan prayed it at Mina as two rak'as for four years, then he prayed it complete afterwards."
"12507","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and seventy sects perished and one sect was saved. And my umma will split into seventy-two sects; seventy-one will perish and one sect will be saved. They said: O Messenger of Allah, which sect is that? He said: The congregation, the congregation."
"12508","Al-Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: When this verse was revealed, O you who believe, do not raise your voices, to the end of the verse, Thabit ibn Qays sat in his house and said: I am of the people of the Fire, and he kept away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, saying: O Abu Amr, what is the matter with Thabit? Has he complained of illness? Sa'd said: He is my neighbor, and I know of no complaint of his. He said: So Sa'd went to him and mentioned to him the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: This verse was revealed, and you know that I am among the loudest of you in voice toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I am of the people of the Fire. Sa'd mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, he is of the people of Paradise."
"12509","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Send with us a man to teach us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah and sent him with them, saying: This is the trustworthy man of this umma."
"12510","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree, and I lay out my garden wall by it, so order him to give it to me so I may straighten my wall with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise. But he refused. Then Abu al-Dahdah came to him and said: Sell me your palm tree for my garden. So he did it. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the palm tree for my garden. He said: So give it to him, for I have given it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a hanging cluster, ready to be gathered, belongs to Abu al-Dahdah in Paradise. He said it repeatedly. He said: Then he went to his wife and said: O Umm al-Dahdah, go out of the garden, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise. She said: Profitable is the bargain, or a word like it."
"12511","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted the barber to shave his head, Abu Talha took the hair of one side of his head in his hand, took his hair, and brought it to Umm Sulaym. He said: And Umm Sulaym used to mix it into her perfume."
"12512","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to us, from Wafa al-Khawlani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: While we were reciting, among us the Arab and the non-Arab, the black and the white, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: You are in good, reciting the Book of Allah, and among you is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And there will come upon people a time when they master it as they straighten an arrow, hastening its wages and not deferring them."
"12513","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me, from Mawhub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Anas ibn Malik, that he used to differ from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Umar said to him: What makes you do this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer; whenever you agree with it I pray with you, and whenever you differ from it I pray and return to my family."
"12514","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, that al-Dahhak ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey pray the forenoon supererogatory prayer as eight rak'as. When he finished he said: I prayed a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, for three things; He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to afflict my umma with years of famine, and He did. And I asked Him not to let their enemy prevail over them, and He did. And I asked Him not to divide them into sects, and He refused me."
"12515","Harun said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun more than once: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, that he heard Qatada ibn Di'ama: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having performed ablution but leaving on his foot a spot the size of a fingernail. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go back and perfect your ablution."
"12516","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Wardan narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say, O disbelievers, is a quarter of the Qur'an, and When the earth is shaken, is a quarter of the Qur'an, and When the help of Allah comes, is a quarter of the Qur'an."
"12517","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will be struck by blackening from the Fire as a punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will admit them into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy, and they will be called the Jahannamiyyun."
"12518","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to drink while standing."
"12519","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, he said: Hammad said, and al-Ja'd mentioned it: Umm Sulaym took half a mudd of barley and ground it, then took a skin bag in which there was some ghee and made from it a dish of khatifa. He said: Then she sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I came to him while he was among his companions, and I said: Umm Sulaym sent me to you, inviting you. He said: I and those with me? He said: So he came, he and those with him. He said: So I entered and said to Abu Talha: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, and those with him. So Abu Talha went out and walked beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And he said: O Messenger of Allah, it is only a khatifa made by Umm Sulaym from half a mudd of barley. He said: So he entered, and it was brought. He said: He put his hand in it, then said: Admit ten. He said: So ten entered and ate until they were full. Then ten entered and ate, then ten, then ten, until forty ate from it, all of them eating until full. He said: And it remained as it was. He said: So we ate."
"12520","Hujayn narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if a woman of the women of the people of Paradise were to look down upon the people of the earth, she would illuminate what is between them and fill what is between them with her fragrance, and her head-cover on her head is better than the world and what is in it."
"12521","Hujayn narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Bakr al-Thaqafi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Arafa; among us were those saying takbir and among us those saying tahlil; neither was the one saying takbir blamed for his takbir nor the one saying tahlil for his tahlil."
"12522","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most handsome of people, and he was the most generous of people, and he was the bravest of people. He said: And the people of Medina were frightened one night, so he set off toward the sound. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, having investigated the sound for them, while he was on a bare horse belonging to Abu Talha with no saddle on it and a sword around his neck, saying to the people: You were not frightened, you were not frightened. And he said of the horse: We found him a sea, or: He is indeed a sea. Anas said: And the horse before that was slow. He said: He was not outrun after that."
"12523","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who sows a crop or plants a planting, and a bird or a man or a beast eats from it, but it is charity for him."
"12524","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Umar ibn al-Khattab a cloak of sundus. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent it to me, though you said about it what you said. He said: I did not send it to you to wear it; I sent it to you only to benefit from its price, or to sell it."
"12525","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water in a wide cup. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his fingers in the cup, and the water began to gush forth, and the people began to perform ablution from it, coming out from between his fingers. He said: And the people began to perform ablution. He said: So I counted the people, and they were between seventy and eighty."
"12526","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas or another, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cares for two daughters, or three daughters, or two sisters, or three sisters, until they die or he dies leaving them, I and he will be like these two. And he gestured with his two fingers, the forefinger and the middle."
"12527","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, raising the hadith, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has entrusted an angel with the womb. He says: O Lord, a drop; O Lord, a clot; O Lord, a lump. And when Allah, mighty and majestic, wills to decree its creation, he says: O Lord, male or female, wretched or happy? What is the provision? What is the term? He said: So it is written likewise in its mother's belly."
"12528","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"12529","Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama, narrated to us, from Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and there were not on his head and beard twenty white hairs."
"12530","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik and Hasan ibn Musa said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Asma al-Sayqal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We went out raising our voices with the Hajj. When we reached Mecca, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it an Umra. He said: Had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would have made it an Umra, but I drove the sacrificial animal and joined the Hajj and the Umra."
"12531","Hasan and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Rabi'a, from Anas, Affan said in his hadith, he said: Abu Rabi'a informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah afflicts the Muslim servant with an affliction in his body, Allah says: Write for him the righteous deed he used to do. If He heals him, He washes him and purifies him, and if He takes him, He forgives him and has mercy on him."
"12532","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Sulayman al-Taymi and Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came upon Musa on the night I was taken on the night journey, at the red dune, while he was standing praying in his grave."
"12533","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq, a white beast above the donkey and below the mule, placing its hoof at the farthest reach of its sight. So I rode it, and it carried me until I came to Bayt al-Maqdis. I tied the beast to the ring to which the prophets tie. Then I entered and prayed in it two rak'as. Then I came out, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me with a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk. I chose the milk. Jibril said: You hit upon the fitra. Then we were taken up to the lowest heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Adam. He welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the second heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. He said: So it was opened for us, and there I was with the two sons of the maternal aunt, Yahya and Isa. They welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the third heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Yusuf, peace be upon him, and he had been given half of beauty. He welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the fourth heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. The door was opened, and there I was with Idris. He welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: And We raised him to a high place. Then we were taken up to the fifth heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been commissioned to him? He said: He has been commissioned to him. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Harun. He welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the sixth heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been commissioned to him? He said: He has been commissioned to him. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Musa, peace be upon him. He welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the seventh heaven. Jibril sought entry. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been commissioned to him? He said: He has been commissioned to him. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was leaning against the Much-Frequented House, into which seventy thousand angels enter every day, never returning to it. Then he took me to the Lote Tree of the Farthest Limit, its leaves like the ears of elephants and its fruits like jars. When there covered it of the command of Allah what covered it, it changed, and no one of Allah's creation can describe it for its beauty. He said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to me what He revealed, and obligated upon me in every day and night fifty prayers. I descended until I reached Musa. He said: What did your Lord obligate upon your umma? He said: I said: Fifty prayers in every day and night. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening, for your umma cannot bear that, and I have tested the Children of Israel and know them well. He said: So I returned to my Lord, mighty and majestic, and said: O Lord, lighten for my umma. So He removed five from me. I returned to Musa and he said: What did you do? I said: He removed five from me. He said: Your umma cannot bear that, so return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening for your umma. He said: I kept going back between my Lord and Musa, with five removed from me each time, until He said: O Muhammad, they are five prayers in every day and night, with ten for each prayer, so those are fifty prayers. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, it is written a good deed; if he does it, it is written tenfold. And whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, nothing is written; if he does it, it is written one evil deed. So I descended until I reached Musa and informed him. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening for your umma, for your umma cannot bear that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have returned to my Lord until I am indeed ashamed."
"12534","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him Jibril while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, and split open his chest. He took out the heart, then split the heart and took out from it a clot. He said: This is Satan's share of you. He said: Then he washed it in a basin of gold with the water of Zamzam, then joined it together, then returned it to its place. He said: And the boys came running to his mother, meaning his foster mother, saying: Muhammad has been killed. He said: They met him while his color had changed. Anas said: And I used to see the trace of the stitching on his chest."
"12535","Ishaq ibn Isa, meaning al-Tabba', narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Anas ibn Malik, that his grandmother Mulayka invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to food she had made. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it, then said: Stand, that I may pray for you. Anas said: So I went to a mat of ours that had blackened from long remaining, sprinkled it with water, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on it. I and the orphan stood behind him, and the old woman behind us. He prayed with us two rak'as, then left."
"12536","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The good dream of a righteous man is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"12537","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from al-Ala, he said: We visited Anas ibn Malik after Zuhr. He stood to pray Asr. When he finished his prayer, we discussed hastening the prayer. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That is the prayer of the hypocrites, three times. One of them sits until, when the sun has yellowed and is between the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks four, remembering Allah in them only a little."
"12538","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, from Anas ibn Malik, that Uhud appeared before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. O Allah, Ibrahim forbade Mecca, and I forbid what is between its two lava tracts."
"12539","Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Zayd ibn Haritha. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his wife Zaynab, as if something entered him, I do not know whether from the saying of Hammad or in the hadith. Then Zayd came complaining of her to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Keep your wife to you and fear Allah. He said: Then there was revealed: And fear Allah, and you hide within yourself what Allah will disclose, up to His saying: We married her to you, meaning Zaynab."
"12540","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this sura: Say, He is Allah, One. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"12541","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from his uncle Anas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) following the pumpkin from the dish, and I shall never cease to love it."
"12542","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I love so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you inform him? He said: No. He said: Then inform him. He said: So he met him afterwards and said: By Allah, I love you for Allah. He said to him: May He love you for Whose sake you loved me."
"12543","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Quraysh, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the Friday prayer with us when the sun declined."
"12544","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Atiyya, meaning al-Hakam, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out to the mosque, in which were the Emigrants and the Helpers, and none of them raised his head from his huddling except Abu Bakr and Umar; he would smile at them and they would smile at him."
"12545","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir, meaning al-Khazzaz, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a black man used to clean the mosque, then he died and was buried at night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and was informed. He said: Go to his grave. So they went to his grave. He said: These graves are filled with darkness over their people, and Allah, mighty and majestic, lights them with my prayer over them. So he came to the grave and prayed over him. A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother died and you did not pray over him. He said: Where is his grave? So he informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with the Ansari."
"12546","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: My father, and he dictated to us, meaning Abu Dawud, with Ali ibn al-Madini, he said: Shu'ba said: Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For every traitor there is a banner, I think he said, on the Day of Resurrection."
"12547","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Hafsa, she said: I asked Anas ibn Malik of what the son of Abu Amra died. They said: Of the plague. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"12548","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes while in prayer, let him leave and sleep until he knows what he says."
"12549","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Talha: Convey peace to your people, for they, as far as I know, are chaste and patient."
"12550","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, my father narrated to me, that Anas informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was met by women and boys and servants coming from a wedding among the Ansar. He greeted them and said: By Allah, I love you."
"12551","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, graze. They said: What are the gardens of Paradise? He said: The circles of remembrance."
"12552","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ammar, meaning Abu Hashim, the keeper of the al-baghut, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Bilal was late for the dawn prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What detained you? He said: I passed by Fatima while she was grinding and the boy was crying. I said to her: If you wish, I will suffice you the millstone and you suffice me the boy, or if you wish, I will suffice you the boy and you suffice me the millstone. She said: I am gentler with my son than you. That detained me. He said: You showed mercy to her, may Allah have mercy on you."
"12553","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Anas narrated to us, that Anas informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine these two prayers on a journey, meaning Maghrib and Isha."
"12554","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come, and there was no person on earth dearer to us than him, yet we would not stand for him, for what we knew of his dislike of that."
"12555","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the signs of the Hour are that knowledge is lifted, ignorance is established, wines are drunk, and fornication appears."
"12556","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyya narrated to us, Abu al-Mukhayyis narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, your freedman so-and-so has been martyred. He said: No indeed; I saw on him a cloak he stole on such-and-such a day."
"12557","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Nafi', Abu Ghalib al-Bahili, narrated to us, he witnessed Anas ibn Malik, he said: Al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi said: O Abu Hamza, of what age of men was the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was commissioned? He said: A man of forty years. He said: Then what was it? He said: He was in Mecca ten years and in Medina ten years, so sixty years were completed for him, then Allah, mighty and majestic, took him to Himself. He said: Of what age of men was he that day? He said: Like the most youthful of men, and the best and most handsome of them, and the most full-fleshed. He said: O Abu Hamza, did you campaign with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I campaigned with him on the day of Hunayn. The polytheists came out in multitude and charged us until we saw our cavalry behind our backs. Among the polytheists was a man charging us, crushing us and smashing us. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he dismounted, and Allah, mighty and majestic, defeated them and they turned. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood when he saw the victory, and captives of them began to be brought to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), man by man, pledging him upon Islam. A man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a vow upon me that if the man who had today been smashing us is brought, I will strike his neck. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. The man was brought, and when he saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: O Prophet of Allah, I repent to Allah; O Prophet of Allah, I repent to Allah. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withheld from him and did not pledge him, so that the other might fulfill his vow. He said: He kept looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to order him to kill him, and kept fearing to kill him before the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw he did nothing, he came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, my vow? He said: I did not withhold from him today except that you might fulfill your vow. He said: O Prophet of Allah, why did you not signal to me? He said: It is not for a prophet to signal treacherously."
"12558","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, he said: While the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in palms belonging to us, belonging to Abu Talha, relieving himself, and Bilal was walking behind him, honoring the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) too much to walk beside him, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and stood until Bilal joined him. He said: Woe to you, O Bilal, do you hear what I hear? He said: I do not hear anything. He said: The owner of the grave is being punished. He said: So he was asked about, and he was found to be a Jew."
"12559","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A'isha had a curtain with which she had screened part of her house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove from us this curtain of yours, for its images keep presenting themselves to me in my prayer."
"12560","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: We visited Anas ibn Malik with Thabit. He said to him: I complained of illness. He said: Shall I not treat you with the ruqya of Abu al-Qasim, blessings and peace be upon him? He said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, Lord of people, Remover of harm, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You; heal with a healing that leaves no illness."
"12561","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sinan Abu Rabi'a narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If those who stay behind from the Isha prayer and the morning prayer knew what is in them, they would come to them even crawling."
"12562","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sinan narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a branch and shook it, and it did not shed. Then he shook it and it did not shed. Then he shook it and it shed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, shed sins as the tree sheds its leaves."
"12563","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik al-Numayri narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man whose three children die before reaching puberty, but Allah, mighty and majestic, admits his parents into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy toward them."
"12564","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be clothed with a garment from the Fire is Iblis; he puts it on his eyebrow and drags it from behind him, and his offspring after him, while he cries: O my ruin, and they cry: O our ruin. Abd al-Samad said it twice, until they stand over the Fire. He says: O my ruin, and they say: O our ruin. It is said to them: Do not call today for one ruin, but call for many ruins. Affan said: And his offspring are behind him, saying: O our ruin. Affan said: His two eyebrows."
"12565","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in mosques."
"12566","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say on the day of Uhud: O Allah, if You will not to be worshipped on earth."
"12567","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, mighty and majestic, created Adam, He left him as long as Allah willed to leave him. Iblis began to circle him, looking at him. When he saw him hollow, he knew he was a creation that does not control itself."
"12568","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Abyssinians used to perform a war dance before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dancing and saying: Muhammad is a righteous servant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are they saying? They said: They are saying: Muhammad is a righteous servant."
"12569","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise enter Paradise, and there remains of it what Allah, mighty and majestic, wills. Then Allah, exalted, originates for it, meaning a creation, until He fills it."
"12570","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given al-Kawthar, and it is a river flowing thus on the face of the earth, its banks domes of pearl, not dammed. I struck with my hand to its soil, and it was a fragrant musk, and its pebbles were pearl."
"12571","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of Banu al-Najjar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O maternal uncle, say: There is no god but Allah. He said: Am I a maternal uncle or a paternal uncle? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather a maternal uncle. He said to him: Is saying: There is no god but Allah better for me? He said: Yes."
"12572","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard sounds. He said: What is this? They said: They are pollinating the palms. He said: Had they left it without pollinating, it would have been good. So they left it without pollinating, and it came out poor. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with you? They said: You left it because of what you said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is a matter of your worldly affair, you know better of it; and when it is of the affair of your religion, then to me."
"12573","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah and Abu Talha."
"12574","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Kathir, narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked al-faghiya, and the most liked food to him was pumpkin."
"12575","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be in prayer and recite a light sura because of the woman and the crying of the boy."
"12576","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wearing a Najrani cloak with a thick border. A bedouin caught up with him and yanked him so that I saw the side of the neck of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked by the border of the cloak from the violence of his yank. He said: O Muhammad, give me from the wealth of Allah that is with you. He turned to him and laughed, then ordered for him a gift."
"12577","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi informed us, he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Asadi informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the supplication of the wronged, even if he is a disbeliever, for there is no veil before it."
"12578","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt."
"12579","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Muhammad, our master and son of our master, and our best and son of our best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, upon you is your piety, and let not Satan allure you. I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the servant of Allah and His Messenger. By Allah, I do not like that you raise me above the station Allah, mighty and majestic, gave me."
"12580","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would say: Praise be to Allah Who fed us and gave us drink and sufficed us and sheltered us, and how many are those who have none to suffice them nor to shelter them."
"12581","Hasan, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a grey mule. He passed by a garden wall belonging to Banu al-Najjar, and there was a grave whose owner was being punished. The mule shied. He said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave."
"12582","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain, pointing with the backs of his hands toward the sky."
"12583","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strive against the polytheists with your tongues and yourselves and your wealth and your hands."
"12584","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going forth in the path of Allah, or an evening, is better than the world and what is in it. And the space of the bow of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"12585","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul that dies, having good with Allah, that wishes to return to the world, except the martyr; the martyr wishes to return to the world to be killed, for what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom."
"12586","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Much-Frequented House is in the seventh heaven; seventy thousand angels enter it every day, then never return to it."
"12587","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"12588","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be clothed with a garment from the Fire is Iblis; he puts it on his two eyebrows while dragging it from behind him, and his offspring behind him, saying: O our ruin, until he stands over the Fire. He says: O my ruin, and they cry: O our ruin. It is said: Do not call today for one ruin, but call for many ruins."
"12589","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Yunus ibn Ubayd and Humayd, from Anas, meaning Ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is he whom people trust, and the Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is he who abandons evil. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant enters Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"12590","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Yunus and Humayd, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is he whom people trust. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"12591","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar. He said: O maternal uncle, say: There is no god but Allah. He said: Maternal uncle or paternal uncle? He said: No, rather maternal uncle. He said: Is it good for me to say: There is no god but Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"12592","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no bad omen, and the good omen pleases me. They said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: The good word."
"12593","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We asked him about ablution for every prayer. He said: As for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to perform ablution for every prayer, but as for us, we used to pray the prayers with one ablution."
"12594","Hasan narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, he said: My father mentioned that, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam never met anything, since Allah created him, harder upon him than death. Then death is indeed easier than what is after it."
"12595","Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: Seldom did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address us without saying: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"12596","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, he said: I asked Anas about the vessels for nabidh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade whatever is pitched of anything. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It is the pitched one."
"12597","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing. I see you from before me and from behind me. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, had you seen what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you see? He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire."
"12598","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thumama, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them in Ramadan and lightened for them, then entered and lengthened. Then he came out and lightened for them, then entered and lengthened. In the morning we said: O Prophet of Allah, we sat last night; you came out to us and lightened, then entered and lengthened. He said: Because of you."
"12599","Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was a tree in the path of people harming people. A man came to it and removed it from the path of people. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw him tossing about in its shade in Paradise."
"12600","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Ja'far, meaning al-Ahmar, informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, for the devils stand in the gaps."
"12601","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man came in to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wearing yellow perfume, and he disliked it. When the man stood up, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to some of his Companions: If only you would order this man to leave off this yellow, saying it two or three times. Anas said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rarely confronted a man face to face with something he disliked about him."
"12602","Aswad narrated to us, Umarah al-Saydalani narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: A beggar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered a date for him, but he did not take it, or he turned up his nose at it. He said: Another came to him and he ordered a date for him, and he said: Glory be to Allah, a date from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he said to the slave girl: Go to Umm Salamah and give him the forty dirhams that are with her."
"12603","Aswad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Farz, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily muzzat is unlawful, and muzzat is mixing ripe dates and unripe dates."
"12604","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd who said: I saw with Anas a drinking cup that had belonged to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in which was a silver patch."
"12605","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, the like of it."
"12606","Hashim ibn al-Qasim said, Jasr narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Glad tidings to whoever believed in me and saw me once, and glad tidings to whoever believed in me and did not see me seven times."
"12607","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Jasr narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I wish I could meet my brothers. The Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Are we not your brothers? He said: You are my Companions, but my brothers are those who believed in me and did not see me."
"12608","Abd Allah ibn Bakr Abu Wahb narrated to us, Sinan ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Hadrami, from Anas ibn Malik that a woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, a daughter of mine, such and such, mentioning her beauty and loveliness, and I have preferred you with her. He said: I have accepted her. She kept praising her until she mentioned that she had never suffered headache nor complained of anything at all. He said: I have no need of your daughter."
"12609","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Wafa al-Khawlani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he came out to us and said: Among you is one better than you, meaning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and you recite the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; among you are the red and the white and the Arab and the non-Arab. There will come a time when they will recite the Quran, mastering it as the arrow shaft is straightened, hastening its rewards and not deferring them."
"12610","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tomorrow there will come to you people who are more tender-hearted toward Islam than you. He said: Then the Asharis came, among them Abu Musa al-Ashari. When they drew near Madinah they began to chant, saying: Tomorrow we meet the loved ones, Muhammad and his party. When they arrived they shook hands, and they were the first to introduce handshaking."
"12611","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah said, and I myself heard it from al-Hakam ibn Musa: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Nubayt ibn Umar, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever prays forty prayers in my mosque, not missing a prayer, there will be written for him exemption from the Fire and salvation from punishment and innocence of hypocrisy."
"12612","Aswad and Husayn ibn Muhammad both said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"12613","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Yunus meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim man asks Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for Paradise three times except Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and no one seeking refuge from the Fire seeks refuge three times except the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire."
"12614","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Khaythamah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I went in with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to visit Zayd ibn Arqam while he was complaining of his eyes, and he said to him: O Zayd, if your sight were taken for what it suffers, what would you do? He said: Then I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your sight were taken for what it suffers, then you were patient and sought reward, you would meet Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, with no sin upon you."
"12615","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would hear a boy crying with his mother while he was in prayer, and would recite a light surah. Jafar said: Or a short surah."
"12616","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muslim meaning Ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki al-Muqri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is pleased that Allah magnify his provision and extend his term, let him join his kinship ties."
"12617","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Bukayr, from al-Dahhak al-Qurashi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey pray the forenoon supererogatory prayer eight rakahs. When he finished he said: I prayed a prayer of desire and fear; I asked my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to test my ummah with years of famine nor to make their enemy prevail over them, and He did so, and I asked Him not to divide them into sects, but He refused me."
"12618","Husayn and Khalaf ibn al-Walid both said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik told me that a man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I love so-and-so for the sake of Allah. He said: Did you tell him? He said: No. He said: Then tell him. Then he met him and said: Know that I love you for the sake of Allah. He said to him: May the One for whose sake you loved me love you. And Khalaf said in his hadith: Then he met him."
"12619","Surayj and Muammal both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would fix prices. He said: Indeed Allah is the Creator, the Withholder, the Expander, the Provider, the Fixer of prices, and I hope to meet Allah with no one demanding of me an injustice I wronged him in blood or wealth."
"12620","Surayj and Yunus ibn Muhammad both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was with one of his wives when a man passed by, so he said: O so-and-so, this is my wife. He said: O Messenger of Allah, whom would I suspect, I would never suspect you. He said: Indeed Satan flows through the son of Adam as blood flows."
"12621","Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrate from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has three daughters or three sisters, fears Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and stands over them in care, will be with me in Paradise like this, and he gestured with his four fingers."
"12622","Yunus narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the wives of the Ansar and the offspring of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner confidants and keepers; if people took a mountain path and the Ansar took a mountain path, I would take the mountain path of the Ansar; were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar."
"12623","Yunus narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: When I take the sight of My servant and he is patient and seeks reward, his recompense with Me is Paradise."
"12624","Yunus narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, he said: I heard Imran al-Ammi, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, when He created disease created cure, so seek treatment."
"12625","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over the rest of food."
"12626","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade plunder, and said: Whoever plunders is not of us. Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade steeping dates and raisins together, and dates and unripe dates together."
"12627","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, from Abu Hafs, he narrated to him that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The likeness of scholars on earth is like the likeness of stars in the sky, guided by in the darknesses of land and sea; when the stars fade, the guides are about to go astray."
"12628","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not go beyond his ears."
"12629","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A morning going forth in the path of Allah or an evening going forth is better than the world and what is in it."
"12630","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub told us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The space of the bow of one of you is better than the world and what is in it; if a woman of the people of Paradise looked down to the world she would fill what is between them with the scent of musk and what is between them would be perfumed, and her head cover on her head is better than the world and what is in it."
"12631","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: You do deeds that are finer in your eyes than hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among the destructive sins."
"12632","Arim narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Umar ibn al-Khattab a cloak of sundus. Umar said: Do you send it to me when you said about it what you said? He said: I did not send it to you to wear it; I only sent it to you to sell it and benefit from its price."
"12633","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that it was mentioned to him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Muadh: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him will enter Paradise. He said: O Prophet of Allah, shall I not give glad tidings to the people? He said: No, I fear they will rely upon it, or as he said."
"12634","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate that Anas said: It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If only you would visit Abd Allah ibn Ubayy. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out riding a donkey, and the Muslims went walking, and it was marshy land. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to him, he said: Keep away from me, for by Allah the smell of your donkey has harmed me. A man of the Ansar said: By Allah, the donkey of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smells better than you. A man of his tribe became angry for Abd Allah, and the companions of each of them became angry, and there was striking with palm stalks and hands and sandals. We were told that there was revealed concerning them: If two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them."
"12635","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: al-Sumayt al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We conquered Makkah, then we raided Hunayn. The polytheists came with the finest ranks I ever saw; the cavalry were drawn up, then the fighters were drawn up, then the women were drawn up behind that, then the sheep were drawn up, then the camels were drawn up. We were many people, reaching six thousand, and over the flank of our cavalry was Khalid ibn al-Walid. Our horses began to take shelter behind our backs, and before long our cavalry were uncovered and the bedouins and those of the people we know fled. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called out: O for the Muhajirun, O for the Muhajirun, then he said: O for the Ansar, O for the Ansar. Anas said: This is a diffuse hadith. We said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, advanced, and by Allah, we had not reached them before Allah defeated them. We took that wealth, then we went to al-Taif and besieged them forty nights, then we returned to Makkah. We stopped, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began giving a man a hundred and giving a man a hundred. The Ansar spoke among themselves: As for one who fought him, he gives him, and as for one who did not fight him, he does not give him. The talk was raised to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he ordered the chiefs of the Muhajirun and the Ansar to come in to him, then he said: None shall come in to me except my Ansar, or the Ansar. We entered the dome until we filled the dome. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O company of the Ansar, or as he said: What talk has reached me? They said: Nothing has reached you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What talk has reached me? They said: Nothing has reached you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Are you not pleased that people go with wealth and you go with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until you enter your houses? They said: We are pleased, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If people took a mountain path and the Ansar took a mountain path, I would take the mountain path of the Ansar. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased. He said: Then be pleased, or as he said."
"12636","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal meaning Ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not foul-mouthed nor obscene nor given to cursing; he would say to one of us when reproaching: What is wrong with him, may his forehead be dusty."
"12637","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ubayd Allah meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a prayer that if one of you prayed it today you would criticize him for it. Sharik and Muslim ibn Abi Namir said to him: Will you not mention that to our governor, and the governor on that day was Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz? He said: I already did."
"12638","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Affan both said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, from Anas who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the circle while a man was standing praying. When he bowed and prostrated, he sat and testified, then supplicated saying: O Allah, I ask You, as all praise belongs to You, there is no god but You, al-Hannan, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Majesty and Honor, O Living, O Sustainer, I ask You. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know with what he supplicated? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, he supplicated Allah with His greatest name, which when called by is answered and when asked by is given. Affan said: He called with His name."
"12639","Husayn narrated to us, Khalaf narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Umar, from Anas who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sitting in the circle when a man came and greeted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people. The man said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. The Prophet returned upon him, peace and blessings upon him: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. When the man sat he said: Praise be to Allah, much good blessed praise in it, as our Lord loves to be praised and as befits Him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: How did you say? He repeated to him as he had said. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, ten angels raced to it, each of them keen to write it, not knowing how to write it until they raised it to the Possessor of Might, and He said: Write it as My servant said."
"12640","Husayn and Affan both said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command marriage and forbid celibacy with severe prohibition, saying: Marry the loving fertile, for I will boast in numbers over the prophets on the Day of Resurrection."
"12641","Husayn narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Hafs, from his uncle Anas ibn Malik who said: A household of the Ansar had a camel on which they drew water, and the camel became refractory toward them and denied them its back. The Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: We had a camel on which we drew water, and it became refractory against us and denied us its back, and the crops and palm trees have become thirsty. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions: Arise. They arose, and he entered the garden with the camel in a corner. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walked toward it. The Ansar said: O Prophet of Allah, it has become like a rabid dog, and we fear its attack against you. He said: There is no harm to me from it. When the camel looked at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it came toward him until it fell prostrating before him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it by its forelock, the most docile it had ever been, until he put it to work. His Companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, this is a beast that does not reason, prostrating to you, while we reason, so we are more entitled to prostrate to you. He said: It is not right for a human to prostrate to a human; if it were right for a human to prostrate to a human, I would order the woman to prostrate to her husband because of the greatness of his right upon her. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if from his foot to the parting of his head there were a sore bursting with pus and matter, then she faced him and licked it, she would not fulfill his right."
"12642","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Khalaf narrated to us, from Hafs, from Anas ibn Malik that he said: We set out with him to Sham, to Abd al-Malik, we forty men of the Ansar, for him to assign stipends for us. When he returned, while we were at Fajj al-Naqah, he led us in Asr, then saluted and entered his tent, and the people stood adding two more rakahs to his two rakahs. He said: May Allah disgrace faces; by Allah, it neither hit the Sunnah nor accepted the concession. I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There are people who go deep in religion, passing through as the arrow passes through the game."
"12643","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail told us, Amr ibn Abi Amr, mawla of al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abu Talhah: Seek for us a boy of your boys to serve me. Abu Talhah went out with me, mounting me behind him, and I used to serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whenever he stopped, and I used to hear him often say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief and incapacity and laziness and cowardice and miserliness and the burden of debt and the overpowering of men. I kept serving him until we came back from Khaybar, and he came back with Safiyyah bint Huyayy, having taken her. I saw him wrapping behind him with a cloak or a garment, then mounting her behind him, until when we were at al-Sahba he made hays on a leather spread, then sent me and I called men and they ate, and that was his wedding feast with her. Then he came on until when Uhud appeared to him he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When he overlooked Madinah he said: O Allah, I make sacred what is between its two mountains as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. O Allah, bless them in their mudd and their sa."
"12644","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Humayd told me, from Anas that the last prayer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people, he prayed in a single garment wrapped in it behind Abu Bakr."
"12645","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Humayd narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raided a people, would not raid with us by night until morning; if he heard an adhan he refrained from them, and if he did not hear an adhan he attacked them."
"12646","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail told us, Humayd told me, from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came from a journey and saw the walls of Madinah, would hasten his mount, and if he was on a beast he would move it out of love for it."
"12647","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail told us, Humayd told me, from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the wind blew, that would be known in his face."
"12648","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the wind blew, that would be known in his face."
"12649","Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Aban ibn Khalid who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Rawahah say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that he never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray Duha at all except when going out on a journey or returning from a journey."
"12650","Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came from a journey and looked at the walls of Madinah, would hasten his she-camel, and if he was on a beast he would move it out of love for it."
"12651","Abu Kamil, whose name is Muzaffar ibn Mudrik, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast until it was said: He fasted, he fasted, and break fast until it was said: He broke fast, he broke fast."
"12652","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves people but does not reach their deeds. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man is with whom he loves."
"12653","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in a voluntary prayer; Umm Sulaym and Umm Haram stood behind us. Thabit said: I only know he said: And he placed me on his right, and we prayed on a mat."
"12654","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit narrated to us, Abu Labid Lumazah ibn Zabbar narrated to us, he said: Horses were sent forth in the time of al-Hajjaj, and we said: If only we went to the race. We went to it, then we said: If only we went to Anas ibn Malik and asked him: Did you race in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? We went to him and asked him, and he said: Yes, he raced on a horse of his called Subhah, and it outran the people, so he rejoiced at that and it pleased him."
"12655","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Salm al-Alawi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw on a man yellow perfume, or he said a trace of yellow perfume. When he stood up he said: If only you would order this man to wash off this yellow. He rarely confronted anyone face to face with something he disliked."
"12656","Abu Kamil and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us, Humayd told us, from Musa ibn Anas, Affan said in his hadith: Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas ibn Malik, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You left behind in Madinah men; no march you marched nor expense you spent nor valley you crossed except they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can they be with us while they are in Madinah? He said: Excuse kept them back."
"12657","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Salm al-Alawi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A bowl containing pumpkin was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he liked pumpkin, and he began seeking the pumpkin with his finger, or he said with his fingers."
"12658","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim meaning Ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik that he saw on the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a ring of silver one day, so the people made rings of silver. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cast away his ring, and the people cast away their rings."
"12659","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went around all his wives in one day."
"12660","Abu Kamil and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, Affan said in his hadith: Thabit told us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Isha prayer was established, Affan said: or delayed, one night, then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need for you. He stood with him conversing with him until the people dozed, or he said some of the people, then he prayed, and he did not mention ablution."
"12661","Abu Kamil and Affan both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Musa Abu al-Ala, and Affan said in his hadith: Musa Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the Zuhr prayer in the winter days, and we did not know whether more of the day had gone or what remained of it."
"12662","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had hardly turned grey except a little, but Abu Bakr and Umar after him dyed with henna and katam."
"12663","He said: Abu Bakr came with his father Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the conquest of Makkah, carrying him until he placed him before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abu Bakr: If only you had left the old man in his house, we would have come to him, as an honor to Abu Bakr. Then he embraced Islam, his beard and head white like thaghamah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Change them, and avoid black."
"12664","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from Jabir, from Khaythamah, from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came in to Zayd ibn Arqam visiting him while he was complaining of his eyes. He said: How would you be if your eye were taken for what it suffers? He said: Then I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your eye were taken for what it suffers, you would meet Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, with no sin."
"12665","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me a kunyah while I was a boy, with a herb I used to gather."
"12666","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from a shaykh of ours, from Anas who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling palm trees until they color, and grain until it hardens, and fruits until they become edible."
"12667","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas that people came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Ukl, and they found Madinah unhealthy, so he ordered for them some milch she-camels, ordering them to drink from their urine and their milk."
"12668","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar told us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to go around his wives with one washing."
"12669","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar told us, from al-Zuhri who said: Anas ibn Malik told me, he said: Prayers were enjoined upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night he was taken by night, fifty, then reduced until made five. Then it was called: O Muhammad, indeed the Word is not changed with Me, and for you with these five is fifty."
"12670","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar told us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Prayer would be established, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would speak to a man about a need he had, standing between him and the qiblah, remaining standing speaking to him; sometimes I saw some of the people dozing from the length of the standing of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him."
"12671","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri who said: Anas ibn Malik told me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr when the sun declined."
"12672","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar told us, from al-Zuhri who said: Anas ibn Malik told me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Asr, then one would go to al-Awali while the sun was still high. Al-Zuhri said: Al-Awali is two miles from Madinah, and three, I think he said, and four."
"12673","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri who said: Anas ibn Malik told me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When supper is brought near and prayer is called, begin with supper, then pray."
"12674","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Attend to these rows, for I see you from behind me."
"12675","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a ring of silver made, engraving in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Then he said: Do not engrave upon it."
"12676","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas that a desert man whose name was Zahir used to gift the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gifts from the desert, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would equip him when he wanted to leave. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Zahir is our desert and we are his town. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, loved him, and he was an unattractive man. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him one day while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind while he could not see him. The man said: Let me go, who is this? He turned and recognized the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and began to press his back against the chest of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he recognized him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began saying: Who will buy the slave? He said: O Messenger of Allah, then by Allah you will find me unsold. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: But with Allah you are not unsold, or he said: But with Allah you are precious."
"12677","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, the Abyssinians played with their spears for his arrival, rejoicing at that."
"12678","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Ansar are my confidants to whom I resorted; accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrong-doers, for they fulfilled what was upon them and there remains what is for them."
"12679","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"12680","Mamar said: Ayyub told me, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"12681","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the imam says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise."
"12682","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his head from prostration or bowing, he would pause between them until we would say: Has he forgotten, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12683","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: I never prayed after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a prayer lighter than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in completeness of bowing and prostration."
"12684","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated one month in the Fajr prayer against tribes of the Arabs: Usayyah and Dhakwan and Ril or Lihyan."
"12685","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell from a horse and his right side was scraped. They entered upon him and he led them sitting, gesturing to them to sit. When he saluted he said: The imam is only made to be followed; when he says takbir say takbir, when he bows bow, when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise, when he prostrates prostrate, and if he prays sitting pray sitting all together."
"12686","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abu Jafar meaning al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept supplicating in Fajr until he left the world."
"12687","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no shighar in Islam, no oath-alliance in Islam, no jalab and no janab."
"12688","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar told us, from al-Zuhri who said: Anas ibn Malik told me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out when the sun declined and prayed Zuhr. When he saluted he stood upon the minbar and mentioned the Hour and mentioned that before it are great matters. Then he said: Whoever loves to ask about something, let him ask about it; by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except I will tell you of it as long as I am in this station of mine. Anas said: The people wept much when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, often said: Ask me. Anas said: A man stood and said: Where is my entrance, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Fire. Abdullah ibn Hudhafah stood and said: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Then he often said: Ask me. Umar knelt upon his knees and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord and with Islam as religion and with Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as messenger. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell silent when Umar said that. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were shown to me just now in the breadth of this wall while I was praying, and I never saw like today in good and evil."
"12689","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come upon anyone saying: Allah, Allah."
"12690","Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us, my father told me, from Wahb ibn Manus, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I never saw anyone resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more than this boy, meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. He said: We estimated in bowing ten glorifications and in prostration ten glorifications."
"12691","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah and Thabit, from Anas that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are people who will come out of the Fire, having been touched by scorching of the Fire as punishment for sins they did, so Allah will bring them out by the grace of His mercy, and they will enter Paradise."
"12692","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The people of Madinah panicked once, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode a horse as if cross-bred, galloping after them in their tracks. When he returned he said: We found him a sea."
"12693","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should wish for death."
"12694","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abd al-Malik said to me that Anas ibn Malik said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The people should be led by the most reciting of them of the Quran."
"12695","Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj told us, Ibn Shihab told me, from Anas ibn Malik that he said: The last look I looked at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was that he complained of illness, and ordered Abu Bakr, who led the people in prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, uncovered the curtain of the chamber of Aishah and looked at the people; I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf, until Abu Bakr stepped back on his heels to join the row, thinking the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to lead the people in prayer. He smiled when he saw them in rows, gestured with his hand to them to complete their prayer, and lowered the curtain between him and them, and died that very day."
"12696","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik that a Jewish man killed an Ansari girl for her jewelry, then threw her in a well and crushed her head with stones. He was seized and brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who ordered that he be stoned until he died, and he was stoned until he died."
"12697","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas that a group of Ukl and Uraynah professed Islam and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, telling him they were people of udders and were not people of countryside, and complaining of the fever of Madinah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered for them some milch she-camels, ordering them to go out of Madinah and drink from their milk and their urine. They went and stayed in the vicinity of al-Harrah, then disbelieved after their Islam, killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and drove away the she-camels. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he sent seekers after them, and they were brought. He blinded their eyes and cut off their hands and their feet, and they were left in the vicinity of al-Harrah biting its stones until they died. Qatadah said: We were told that this verse came down concerning them: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger."
"12698","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Anas who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Zaynab, Umm Sulaym gifted him hays in a stone bowl. Anas said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go and invite whomever you meet. They kept entering, eating, and leaving, with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placing his hand on the food and supplicating in it and saying what Allah willed him to say. I did not leave anyone I met except I invited him; they ate until full and left, and a group of them remained, prolonging talk upon him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, felt shy of them to say anything to them, so he went out leaving them in the house. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you to food, not looking for its readiness, but when you are invited enter, up to His saying: for your hearts and their hearts."
"12699","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attacked Khaybar early morning, they having come out with spades. When they looked at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they said: Muhammad and the army. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hands and said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned."
"12700","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Khaybar, he found them as they went out to their crops with their spades. When they saw him with the army they drew back, returning to their fortress. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned."
"12701","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq on the night he was taken by night, saddled and bridled, for him to ride it, but it became refractory toward him, and Jibril said to it, What carries you to do this, for by Allah none more noble to Allah, Almighty and Majestic, than him ever rode you, he said, Then it broke out in sweat."
"12702","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for me in the seventh heaven, its lote fruit like the earthen water jars of Hajar and its leaves like the ears of elephants, there come out of its trunk two outward rivers and two inward rivers, so I said, O Jibril, what are these two, he said, As for the two inward ones, they are in Paradise, and as for the two outward ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates."
"12703","Abdul-Razzaq said, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said, Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said, No one resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than al-Hasan ibn Ali and Fatimah, may Allah's blessings be upon them all."
"12704","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, concerning His saying, Almighty and Majestic, Indeed We have given you al-Kawthar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, It is a river in Paradise, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I saw a river in Paradise whose banks were domes of pearl, so I said, What is this, O Jibril, he said, This is al-Kawthar which Allah, Almighty and Majestic, has given you."
"12705","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to break his fast upon fresh dates before he prayed, and if there were no fresh dates, then dry dates, and if there were no dry dates, he sipped some sips of water."
"12706","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, concerning His saying, Almighty and Majestic, And extended shade, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"12707","Ma'mar said, And Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Hurayrah says, Recite if you wish, And extended shade."
"12708","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said, I was riding behind Abu Talhah while he was traveling alongside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said, My foot indeed touches the stirrup of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him pronouncing the Talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together."
"12709","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, that the crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out, Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you from eating the meat of domestic donkeys, for it is filth."
"12710","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that his grandmother Mulaykah invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to food she had made for him, he said, So he ate, then he said, Stand up so I may pray for you, he said, So I stood toward a mat of ours that had become black from long use, and I sprinkled it with water, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and I and the orphan lined up behind him, and the old woman behind us, and he prayed for us two rak'ahs, then he left."
"12711","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, he said, Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the conquest wearing a helmet, then a man came and said, This is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Kill him."
"12712","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram on the back of the foot because of a pain he had."
"12713","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Your deeds are shown to your dead relatives and kinsfolk, so if it is good they rejoice at it, and if it is other than that they say, O Allah, do not cause them to die until You guide them as You have guided us."
"12714","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, and Abdul-A'la, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat."
"12715","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf with a trace of khaluq perfume on him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, What is this, O Abdur-Rahman, he said, I have married a woman of the Ansar, he said, How much did you give her as dowry, he said, The weight of a date stone of gold, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Give a wedding feast even with a sheep, Anas said, I saw him apportion to each wife of his wives after his death one hundred thousand dinars."
"12716","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit and Aban and more than one, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, There is no shighar in Islam."
"12717","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"12718","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a sign, so the moon split in Makkah twice, then he said, The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split, and if they see a sign they turn away and say, Continuous magic."
"12719","Abdul-Razzaq said, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Obscenity was never in anything except that it disgraced it, and modesty was never in anything except that it adorned it."
"12720","Abdul-Razzaq said, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said, I counted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his beard only fourteen white hairs."
"12721","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Do not envy one another, and do not sever ties, and do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"12722","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, And what have you prepared for it, so the Bedouin said, I have not prepared for it much for which I praise myself except that I love Allah and His Messenger, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, And you are with whom you loved."
"12723","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached to the halves of his ears."
"12724","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said, Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked for water for ablution but did not find it, he said, So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Here is water, he said, So I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his hand in the vessel in which there was water, then he said, Perform ablution in the name of Allah, and I saw the water gushing, meaning between his fingers, while the people performed ablution until they all performed ablution to the last of them, Thabit said, I said to Anas, How many do you think they were, he said, About seventy."
"12725","Abdul-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, or from an-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed Allah, Almighty and Majestic, has promised me to admit into Paradise four hundred thousand of my nation, so Abu Bakr said, Increase us, O Messenger of Allah, he said, And like this, and he joined his palm, he said, Increase us, O Messenger of Allah, he said, And like this, so Umar said, It is enough, O Abu Bakr, so Abu Bakr said, Leave me, O Umar, what harm is it to you that Allah, Almighty and Majestic, admits us all into Paradise, so Umar said, Indeed Allah, Almighty and Majestic, if He wills, admits His creation into Paradise with a single handful, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Umar has spoken the truth."
"12726","Abdul-Razzaq said, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said, Anas ibn Malik informed me, that some people of the Ansar said on the day of Hunayn, when Allah granted to His Messenger the wealth of Hawazin and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began giving some men of Quraysh a hundred camels to each man, They said, May Allah forgive the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords drip from their blood, Anas said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of their saying, so he sent to the Ansar and gathered them in a tent of leather and did not invite anyone other than them, and when they had gathered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and said, What is this report that reached me about you, so the Ansar said, As for our men of judgment, they said nothing, and as for people young in age, they said such and such, of what they said, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I give men newly accustomed to disbelief to reconcile them, or he said, to win them over, will you not be pleased that the people go with wealth and you return with the Messenger of Allah to your dwellings, for by Allah what you return with is better than what they return with, they said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, You will find after me severe favoritism, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger, for I am your forerunner at the Pond, Anas said, But we did not endure."
"12727","Abdul-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said, Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said, We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, There shall now come upon you a man of the people of Paradise, so a man of the Ansar came up with his beard dripping from his ablution, having hung his sandals in his left hand, and when it was the next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of that, so that man came up like the first time, and when it was the third day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of his saying also, so that man came up in the like of his first state, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As followed him and said, I quarreled with my father and swore that I would not enter upon him for three days, so if you see fit to shelter me with you until they pass, do so, he said, Yes, Anas said, And Abdullah used to narrate that he spent those three nights with him but did not see him stand in the night for anything except that when he stirred and turned on his bed he remembered Allah, Almighty and Majestic, and said Allah is Most Great until he stood for the dawn prayer, Abdullah said, Except that I did not hear him say but good, and when the three nights had passed and I almost belittled his deed, I said, O Abdullah, there was no anger nor desertion between me and my father at all, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about you three times, There shall now come upon you a man of the people of Paradise, and you came up the three times, so I wanted to stay with you to look at your deed and follow it, but I did not see you doing much deed, so what is it that raised you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, so he said, It is nothing but what you saw, he said, Then when I turned away he called me and said, It is nothing but what you saw except that I find in myself no deceit toward any of the Muslims, nor do I envy anyone for any good Allah has given him, so Abdullah said, This is what raised you, and it is what we cannot bear."
"12728","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan ibn Hilal ibn Abi Zaynab narrated to us, from Khalid, meaning al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, he said, I asked Anas ibn Malik, Did Umar recite Qunut, he said, Yes, and one better than Umar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), after bowing."
"12729","Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah, narrated to us, he said, I asked Anas, Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in sandals, he said, Yes."
"12730","Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah, narrated to us, he said, I asked Anas, Did the Prophet recite In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Gracious, or Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, so he said, You are asking me about something I do not remember, or no one asked me before you."
"12731","Abdul-Aziz ibn Abdus-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in a single night."
"12732","Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, he said, I heard Anas saying, The Prophet said, Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12733","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said, Sa'id, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and warned the people, then a man stood and said, When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) frowned in his face, so we said to him, Sit down, for you have asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he dislikes, he said, Then he stood a second time and said, O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) frowned in his face more severely than the first, so we seated him, he said, Then he stood a third time and said, O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, Woe to you, and what have you prepared for it, he said, I have prepared for it love of Allah and His Messenger, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, Sit down, for you are with whom you loved."
"12734","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Humayd at-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that ar-Rubayyi bint an-Nadr, the paternal aunt of Anas ibn Malik, broke the incisor tooth of a slave girl, so they offered them blood money but they refused, and they sought pardon but they refused, then they refused, they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ordered retaliation, then her brother Anas ibn an-Nadr, the paternal uncle of Anas ibn Malik, came and said, O Messenger of Allah, will the incisor tooth of ar-Rubayyi be broken, no, by the One Who sent you with the truth, her incisor shall not be broken, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Anas, the Book of Allah is retaliation, he said, Then the people pardoned, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Indeed among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear upon Allah, He fulfills them."
"12735","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Anas, he said, I asked him about Qunut, is it before bowing or after bowing, so he said, Before bowing, he said, I said, For they claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Qunut after bowing, so he said, They have lied, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only recited Qunut for a month supplicating against people who killed some of his companions called the Reciters."
"12736","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited us to assign for us in Bahrain an allotment, he said, So we said, No, unless you assign for our brothers of the Muhajirun the like of it, so he said, You will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me, they said, Then we shall endure."
"12737","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Ismail, narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Asim, he said, I entered upon Anas ibn Malik at Kufah and asked him about nabidh, so he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat."
"12738","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nufay', he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik, it was said, O Messenger of Allah, how will people be gathered upon their faces, he said, Indeed the One Who made them walk upon their feet is able to make them walk upon their faces."
"12739","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and relieved his need, then he stood to the side of the mosque, he said, So some of the people shouted at him, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restrained them, then he ordered a bucket of water and it was poured over his urine."
"12740","Ya'la narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Nufay', from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, There is no one, rich or poor, but will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he had been given in this world mere sustenance."
"12741","Ya'la narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, A sacrificial camel or a sacrificial offering was passed with before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to its owner, Ride it, so he said, It is a sacrificial camel or a sacrificial offering, he said, Even so."
"12742","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said, When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he said, Praise be to Allah Who fed us and gave us drink and sufficed us and sheltered us, for how many have none to suffice them nor to shelter them."
"12743","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Qatadah and Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man came while breathless and said, Allah is Most Great, praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said, Which of you spoke the words, for he said no harm, so the man said, I, O Messenger of Allah, I sat breathless and said them, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I saw twelve angels racing as to which of them would raise them."
"12744","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad informed us, he said, Qatadah and Thabit and Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to open the Qur'an with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"12745","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the establishment of the Hour while the prayer was established, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said, Where is the asker about the Hour, so the man said, Here I am, O Messenger of Allah, so he said, And what have you prepared for it, for it is imminent, he said, I have not prepared for it much deed except that I love Allah and His Messenger, he said, Then you are with whom you loved, he said, So the Muslims never rejoiced at anything after Islam more severely than they rejoiced at it."
"12746","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said, Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari narrated to me, that he was ten years old when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, he said, And my mothers used to urge me to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I was the most knowledgeable of the people about the matter of the veil when it was revealed, and the first of what was revealed was when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Zaynab bint Jahsh, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke with her as a bridegroom, then he invited the people and they partook of the food, then they went out while a group of them remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prolonged their stay, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and went out, and I went out with him so that they would leave, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked and we walked with him until he came to the threshold of the chamber of Aishah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thought that they had gone out, so he returned and I returned with him, and behold they had gone out, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a curtain between him and them, and Allah, Almighty and Majestic, revealed the veil."
"12747","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another valley, and nothing fills his mouth but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"12748","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said, Bukayr narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said, I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rak'ahs, and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman two rak'ahs in the early part of his rule."
"12749","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying, While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, a man entered upon a camel and made it kneel in the mosque and tied it, then he said, Which of you is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining among them, he said, So we said, This white reclining man, so the man said, O son of Abdul-Muttalib, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, I have answered you, so the man said, I, O Muhammad, am asking you and will be severe upon you in asking, so do not take offense at me in yourself, so he said, Ask whatever comes to you, so the man said, I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you, did Allah send you to all people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Allah, yes, he said, So I adjure you by Allah, did Allah command you to pray the five prayers in the day and night, he said, O Allah, yes, he said, So I adjure you by Allah, did Allah command you to fast this month of the year, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Allah, yes, he said, I adjure you by Allah, did Allah command you to take this charity from our rich and divide it among our poor, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Allah, yes, the man said, I have believed in what you have brought, and I am the messenger of those behind me of my people, he said, And I am Dimam ibn Tha'labah, the brother of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr."
"12750","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said, When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the Romans, they said, They do not read a letter unless sealed, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, as if I am looking at its whiteness in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its engraving was Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"12751","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, The son of Adam grows old while two of him remain, greed and hope."
"12752","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said, I heard Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say, Indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, or he said, O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah, Shu'bah said, So Qatadah used to say this in his stories."
"12753","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Abu Sadaqah, the freedman of Anas, and Shu'bah praised him well, he said, I asked Anas about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun had declined, and Asr between these two prayers of yours, and Maghrib when the sun had set, and Isha when the twilight had disappeared, and Fajr when the dawn had risen until sight clears."
"12754","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon boys while they were playing and greeted them."
"12755","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said, Shu'bah informed us of it, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, he said, I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was branding sheep, Hisham said, I think he said, In their ears, he said, Then he said afterwards, In their ears, without doubting."
"12756","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Abyad, a man of Banu Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was white and lofty."
"12757","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, I said, Narrate to us something of these wonders you witnessed, do not narrate to us from others, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and sat upon the seats upon which Jibril, peace be upon him, used to come to him, he said, So Bilal came and announced to him the Asr prayer, so he said, Whoever has distant family in Madinah, let him relieve his need and get some ablution, while some people of the Muhajirun remained who had no families in Madinah, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a wide cup with something of water at its bottom, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in the cup, but his palm was too wide for it, so he placed these four fingers of his, then he said, Draw near and perform ablution, he said, So they performed ablution until none of them remained but performed ablution, so we said, O Abu Hamzah, how many do you think they were, he said, Between seventy and eighty."
"12758","Abdus-Samad narrated to us, Umarah, meaning Ibn Zadham, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin."
"12759","Abdus-Samad narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, he said, I was told from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, The longest of people in necks on the Day of Resurrection are the muezzins."
"12760","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, When Makkah was opened, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the spoils among Quraysh, so the Ansar said, This is indeed wonder, our swords drip from their blood while our spoils are returned to them, so it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them and said, What is this that reached me about you, so they said, It is what reached you, and they would not lie, so he said, Are you not pleased that the people return with this world and you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses, if the people took a valley or a mountain pass and the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar or the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"12761","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Humayd, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, A man called a man in the market and said, O Abu al-Qasim, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, so the man said, I only meant a man, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Name with my name but do not use my kunyah."
"12762","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Ansar said, We are those who pledged Muhammad to jihad as long as we remain forever, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered them, O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"12763","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Muhammad ibn Bakr said, Shu'bah narrated to us, and al-Khaffaf, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Complete bowing and prostration, for by Allah I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"12764","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Asbat said, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while complete."
"12765","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said, Ride it, he said, It is a sacrificial camel, he said, Ride it, he said, Shall I ride it, he said, Ride it."
"12766","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black and white rams, slaughtering them with his hand and placing his foot upon their sides and mentioning Allah, Almighty and Majestic."
"12767","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a group of Ukl or Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, we were people of udders and were not people of countryside, so Madinah was unhealthy for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered for them some milch camels and ordered them to go out with them and drink of their milk and urine, then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drove off the camels and disbelieved after their Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought, so he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes and left them in the Harrah until they died."
"12768","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr said, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to some of these non-Arabs, it was said to him, They do not accept a letter except with a seal, he said, So he took a ring of silver, its engraving, and Ibn Bakr said, and its engraving was Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, as if I am looking at its gleam or its whiteness in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12769","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Thabit took the pre-dawn meal, and when they had finished their meal, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to prayer and prayed, so we said to Anas, How long was between their finishing and their meal and their entering into prayer, he said, As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"12770","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Rawh said, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Do not practice continuous fasting, so it was said, You practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah, he said, I am not like any of you, indeed my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"12771","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Jew killed a slave girl for her silver ornaments, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed him."
"12772","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Zawra and was brought a vessel with water not covering his fingers, so he ordered his companions to perform ablution, so he placed his palm in the water, and the water began to spring from between his fingers and the tips of his fingers until the people performed ablution, he said, So I said to Anas, How many were you, he said, We were three hundred."
"12773","Abdullah ibn Bakr and Muhammad ibn Ja'far said, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah bint Huyayy and made her freedom her dowry."
"12774","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said, There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse of ours called Mandub, he said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, We saw no alarm, and we found him swift, Hajjaj said, Meaning the horse."
"12775","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qaza'ah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, I was riding behind Abu Talhah, he said, And the knee of Abu Talhah almost touched the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pronounce the Talbiyah for both of them."
"12776","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, I heard Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas ibn Malik, he said, I entered with my grandfather Anas ibn Malik the house of al-Hakam ibn Ayyub, and behold a people had set up a chicken shooting at it, so Anas said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up animals as targets."
"12777","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said, We passed and startled a hare at Marr al-Zahran, so they chased it and grew tired, so I ran until I caught it, then I brought it to Abu Talhah and he slaughtered it, then he sent its haunch or its thigh to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he accepted it, Hajjaj said, I said to Shu'bah, So I said, Did he eat it, he said, Yes, he ate it, he said to me afterwards, He accepted it."
"12778","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Ansar, You will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me, and your appointment is the Pond."
"12779","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Ansar, You will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me, and your appointment is the Pond."
"12780","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that his mother, when she gave birth, they took the boy to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to do tahnik for him, he said, And behold the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in an animal enclosure branding sheep, Shu'bah said, And to the best of my knowledge he said, In their ears."
"12781","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd narrating that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"12782","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr, Hear and obey even for an Abyssinian whose head is like a raisin."
"12783","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mix with us so that he would say to a little brother of mine, O Abu Umayr, what did al-Nughayr do, he said, And when prayer came we sprinkled for him the edge of a mat, then he led us and lined us behind him, Shu'bah said, Then Abu al-Tayyah after he grew old said, Then he stood and prayed, and he did not say, He lined us behind him, nor he led us."
"12784","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the lavatory, so I and a boy like me would carry a skin of water and a spear, and he would cleanse himself with water."
"12785","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, I heard Ali ibn Zayd saying, I heard Anas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, The believer should not wish for death, or he said, one of you, but if he must do so, let him say, O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die as long as death is better for me."
"12786","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, The son of the sister of a people is of them."
"12787","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, O Allah, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, Shu'bah said, Or he said, O Allah, indeed life is the life of the Hereafter, so rectify the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"12788","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik saying, When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits was seen, or I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"12789","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdul-Aziz ibn Suhayb, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never gave a wedding feast for any of his wives greater or better than what he gave for Zaynab, so Thabit al-Bunani said, So what did he serve, he said, He fed them bread and meat until they left it."
"12790","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, He used to describe for us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would stand and pray, and when he raised his head from bowing we said, He has forgotten, from the length of his standing."
"12791","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling with a camel driver chanting for his women, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, and behold he had turned aside with them, he said, So he said, O Anjashah, woe to you, be gentle with the glass vessels."
"12792","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), When is the Hour, so he said, What have you prepared for it, so he said, I have not prepared for it much prayer nor fasting nor charity except that I love Allah and His Messenger, so he said, You are with whom you loved."
"12793","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said, I heard Attab, the freedman of Ibn Hurmuz, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, I pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine, meaning the right, to hear and obey as much as I could."
"12794","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, and Hashim said, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Attab, and Hashim said, the freedman of Banu Hurmuz, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, Were I not afraid to err, I would narrate to you things I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he said, Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire, Hashim said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, or I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12795","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Three, whoever has them finds the taste of faith, whoever loves a man loving him only for Allah, and whoever Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything besides them, and whoever being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah, Almighty and Majestic, saved him from it."
"12796","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, he said, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said, Is there among you anyone from others, they said, No, except a sister's son of ours, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The sister's son of a people is of them, Hajjaj said, Or of themselves, so he said, Indeed Quraysh are recent in Jahiliyyah and calamity, and I wanted to console them and win them over, will you not be pleased that the people return with this world and you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses, if the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"12797","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning except that he said, So I wanted to win them over and console them."
"12798","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say, O Allah, indeed life is the life of the Hereafter, Shu'bah said, Or he said, O Allah, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so honor the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"12799","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Qatadah, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, When is the Hour, he said, What have you prepared for it, he said, Love of Allah, Almighty and Majestic, and His Messenger, he said, You are with whom you loved."
"12800","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, he said, I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, There is no prophet but warned his nation of the one-eyed liar, indeed he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed, written between his eyes is kafara, Hajjaj said, Kafir."
"12801","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no one who enters Paradise who would love to return to this world even if he had everything on earth, except the martyr, for he wishes to return and be killed ten times because of the honor he sees."
"12802","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, whoever had in his heart good weighing a barley grain. Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, whoever had in his heart good weighing an atom. Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, whoever had in his heart good weighing a wheat grain."
"12803","Hajjaj and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, they both said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while making it complete."
"12804","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, and Aswad, meaning Shadhan, said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man driving a sacrificial camel: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, on the third time."
"12805","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah narrating, he said: I said to Qatadah: Did you hear Anas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: Spittle in the mosque is a sin? He said: Yes, and its expiation is to bury it."
"12806","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: You practice continuous fasting. He said: You are not like me in that; I spend the day, or he said: I spend the night, being fed and given drink."
"12807","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, he informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gathered the Ansar, said: Is there among you anyone from other than you? They said: No, except a son of our sister. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of the sister of a people is from themselves, or he said: from the people."
"12808","He said: So I mentioned that to Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, and he narrated to me from Anas."
"12809","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed me that he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no evil omen. He said: And the good omen pleases me. So I said: What is the good omen? He said: The good word."
"12810","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, that he said: When this verse was revealed: Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins, then he says: He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congratulations, pleasant and wholesome, to you, O Messenger of Allah, so what is for us? Then this verse was revealed: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein, and expiate their evil deeds from them. And Shubah said: Qatadah used to mention this hadith in his stories from Anas ibn Malik, he said: This verse was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from al-Hudaybiyah: Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins, then he says: He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congratulations to you, this hadith. He said: So I thought that all of it was from Anas, so I came to Kufah and narrated from Qatadah from Anas, then I returned and met Qatadah at Wasit, and he was saying: Its beginning is from Anas and its end is from Ikrimah. He said: So I came to them in Kufah and informed them of that."
"12811","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, Ibn Jafar said in his hadith: I heard Ali ibn Zayd, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: A young slave girl from among the slave girls of the people of Madinah would come and take the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not withdraw his hand from her hand until she took him wherever she wished."
"12812","Muhammad ibn Abdullah, meaning al-Ansari, narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When this verse was revealed: You will never attain righteousness until you spend from what you love, or he said: Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, Abu Talhah ibn Sahl al-Ansari came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my walled garden which is in such-and-such place, and if I could, O Messenger of Allah, I would conceal it and not make it public. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it among your poor relatives, or he said: among the poor of your family."
"12813","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Abi Dawud al-Habati Abu Hisham, he said: My brother Harun ibn Abi Dawud narrated to me, he said: I came to Anas ibn Malik and said: O Abu Hamzah, the place is far and we would like to visit you. So he raised his head and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any man who visits a sick person only wades into mercy, and when he sits with the sick person mercy covers him. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for the healthy one who visits the sick, so what is for the sick? He said: His sins are dropped from him."
"12814","Al-Muammal ibn Ismail and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three qualities, whoever has them finds through them the sweetness of faith: that Allah the Mighty and Majestic and His Messenger be more beloved to him than all besides them, that the servant hate to return from Islam as he hates to be thrown into the Fire, and that the servant love a servant loving him only for the sake of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"12815","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when I was nine years old, so Umm Sulaym took me to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my son, employ him as a servant. So I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years, and he never said to me about something I did: Why did you do such-and-such, nor did he say to me about something I did not do: Why did you not do such-and-such. And he came to me one day while I was playing with the boys, or he said: with the children, and he greeted us and called me and sent me on an errand, and when I returned he said: Do not inform anyone. And I stayed long with my mother, and when I came to her she said: O my son, what kept you? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand of his. She said: What is it? I said: He said: Do not inform anyone about it. She said: O my son, then conceal the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12816","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered for him a sa of dates and spoke to his family, and they reduced part of his dues."
"12817","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Ask me. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah, for the one to whom he used to be attributed. So his mother said to him: O my son, you have put your mother in a grave position. He said: I wanted to clear my chest of what was being said, and things had been said about him."
"12818","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin, so when broth containing pumpkin was brought, the pumpkin was placed on the side next to him."
"12819","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Itban ibn Malik lost his eyesight, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would come and pray in my house, or he said: in my home, so I would take your prayer place as a mosque. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and prayed in his house, or he said: in his home, and the people of Itban gathered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So they mentioned Malik ibn al-Dukhshum and said: O Messenger of Allah, he and he, insinuating hypocrisy about him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant says it truthfully except that the Fire is forbidden for him."
"12820","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a delegation from the people of Yemen came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wanted to send a man with them, so they said: Send a man with us. So he said: I will send with you the trustworthy man of this nation. So he sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. My father said: And in another place: They said: O Messenger of Allah, send with us a man to teach us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and said: Every nation has a trustworthy man, and this is the trustworthy man of this nation."
"12821","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him sheep filling the area between two mountains. So the man came to his people and said: O my people, embrace Islam, for by Allah, Muhammad gives the gift of a man who does not fear poverty, or he said: destitution. He said: And Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas said: A man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepting Islam wanting nothing but to gain some worldly goods, or he said: worldly gain he would gain, and before that day of his ended his religion would become more beloved to him, or he said: weightier to him, than this world and all in it."
"12822","Muammal and Hasan al-Ashyab narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, Hasan said: from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on his grey mule by a walled garden of Banu al-Najjar and heard the voices of people being punished in their graves, so the mule shied. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah the Mighty and Majestic to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"12823","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a Jewish boy used to place the ablution water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and hand him his sandals, then he fell ill. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and entered upon him while his father was sitting at his head. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O boy, say: There is no god but Allah. So he looked at his father and his father was silent. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated to him, and he looked at his father, so his father said: Obey Aba al-Qasim. So the boy said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out saying: Praise be to Allah Who rescued him through me from the Fire."
"12824","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, the like thereof."
"12825","Muammal and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The prayer time came, so the neighbors of the mosque stood up to their homes to perform ablution, and there remained in the mosque some people from the Muhajirun, between seventy and eighty. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, and a stone vessel containing water was brought. So he placed the fingers of his right hand in the vessel and began pouring upon them while they performed ablution, saying: Perform ablution, come to ablution, until they all performed ablution, and there remained in it about as much as had been in it."
"12826","Muammal and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I set out with Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was born. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a cloak smearing tar on a camel of his. So he said to me: Do you have dates with you? I said: Yes. So he took some dates and threw them into his mouth and chewed them in his palate. So the boy opened his mouth wide, and he fed him. So the boy began moving his tongue. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar cannot but love dates. And he named him Abdullah."
"12827","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When we are with you and you narrate to us our hearts soften, but when we leave you we mix with women and children and do such-and-such. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If that hour continued with you, the angels would shake hands with you."
"12828","Ismail, meaning Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Suhayb, narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw children and women coming forward, Abd al-Aziz said: I think he said: from a wedding, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up showing joy and said: O Allah, you are among the most beloved of people to me. O Allah, you are among the most beloved of people to me. O Allah, you are among the most beloved of people to me, meaning the Ansar."
"12829","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, he said: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he invoked Allah's mercy for one of them, or he said: he blessed one of them, and left the other. So it was said: They are two men who sneezed, and you invoked mercy for, or he said: blessed, one of them and left the other. So he said: This one praised Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and this one did not praise Allah. Sulayman said: I see it is something like this."
"12830","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Umm Sulaym was with the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a driver was driving them, so he said to him: O Anjashah, gently with the glass vessels."
"12831","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire. Let him take his seat in the Fire, thus twice. And he narrated it another time and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12832","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother, or for his neighbor, what he loves for himself. And Hajjaj did not doubt."
"12833","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner circle and my repository, and people will increase and they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their evil-doers. And Hajjaj said: from their evil-doers."
"12834","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, and I do not know whether something was revealed or he used to say it: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would wish for, or would seek, a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"12835","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, and I do not know whether something was revealed to him, then he mentioned it."
"12836","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk wine, so he flogged him with two palm stalks about forty times. He said: And Abu Bakr did so. Then when Umar came he consulted the people, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The lightest of the prescribed punishments is eighty. He said: So Umar ordered it."
"12837","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shubah informed us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), no one will narrate to you after me having heard it from him: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, adultery will spread, wine will be drunk, men will go and women will remain until there will be for fifty women one caretaker."
"12838","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I shall certainly narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like thereof, except that he said: Men will go and women will remain."
"12839","Muhammad said: Shubah narrated to us, and Yazid said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have invoked Allah the Mighty and Majestic to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"12840","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer he converses privately with his Lord the Mighty and Majestic, so let him not spit, Hajjaj said: let him not expectorate, in front of him nor on his right, but on his left and under his foot."
"12841","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and I did not hear any of them reciting: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Hajjaj said: Shubah said: Qatadah said: I asked Anas ibn Malik with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open the recitation. So he said: You are asking me about something no one has asked me about."
"12842","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved pumpkin. Hajjaj said: gourd. He said: So food was brought to him or he was invited to it. Anas said: So I kept following it and placing it before him because I knew he loved it."
"12843","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as a dog spreads."
"12844","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of the perfection of prayer."
"12845","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his father and his son and all mankind."
"12846","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lick his three fingers when he ate, and said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the harm from it and eat it and not leave it for Satan, and let one of you lick the dish clean, for you do not know in which of your food the blessing lies."
"12847","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped, and he would not wrong anyone his wage."
"12848","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Zubayr, meaning Ibn Adi, he said: We complained to Anas ibn Malik about what we meet from al-Hajjaj. So he said: Be patient, for no year or day will come upon you but the one after it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord the Mighty and Majestic. I heard it from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12849","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four units and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two units."
"12850","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah Sanbar al-Jahdari narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that some people came to Madinah and found Madinah unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered for them camels and their herdsman and ordered them to drink from their urine and milk. He said: So they killed the herdsman and drove away the camels. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought. So he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes and threw them in the sun until they died."
"12851","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they pressed him with questioning. So he ascended the minbar one day and said: You will not ask me about anything but I will clarify it for you. Anas said: So I began looking right and left, and every person had wrapped his head in his garment weeping. He said: And a man who, when he quarreled, was attributed to other than his father, began and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Abu Amir said, and I think he said: So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, in Paradise or in the Fire? He said: In the Fire. He said: Then Umar began and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. We seek refuge with Allah from the evil of trials. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have never seen in good and evil like today at all. Paradise and the Fire were pictured until I saw them below the wall."
"12852","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"12853","Abd al-Malik and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab said: Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no evil omen, and the good omen pleases me. He said: It was said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: The good word. Abu Amir said, or he said: The fine word."
"12854","Hisham narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: A man, or a Bedouin, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have prepared nothing for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So he said: You are with whom you love. Anas said: I never saw the Muslims rejoice at anything after Islam more intensely than they rejoiced on that day."
"12855","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun Abu al-Khattab al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me: I will be standing waiting for my nation to cross over the bridge when Isa came to me and said: These prophets have come to you, O Muhammad, asking, or he said: gathering to you, and calling upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic to disperse the crowds of nations to where Allah wills because of the distress they are in, while creation are bridled in sweat. As for the believer, it is upon him like a cold, and as for the disbeliever, death will overwhelm him. He said: He said to Isa: Wait until I return to you. He said: So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went until he stood beneath the Throne and met what no chosen angel and no sent prophet had met. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed to Jibril: Go to Muhammad and say to him: Raise your head, ask and you will be given, and intercede and your intercession will be accepted. He said: So I was granted intercession for my nation, to bring out one person from every ninety-nine people. He said: I kept going back and forth to my Lord the Mighty and Majestic, and I did not stand in a station but I was granted intercession, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic granted me thereof that He said: O Muhammad, admit from your nation, from the creation of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, whoever testified one day sincerely that there is no god but Allah and died upon that."
"12856","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: I asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. He said: He said: I will do so for them. He said: So where shall I seek you on the Day of Resurrection, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Seek me the first time you seek me on the bridge. He said: I said: If I do not meet you on the bridge? He said: Then I am at the Balance. He said: I said: If I do not meet you at the Balance? He said: Then I am at the Pond, I will not miss these three places on the Day of Resurrection."
"12857","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mukhtar ibn Fulful, he said: I heard Anas, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O best of creation. So he said: That is Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"12858","Sahl ibn Yusuf, meaning al-Mismai, narrated to us, from Humayd, and Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while the people of Madinah had two days in which they played. So he said: You came to you while you had two days in which you play, but Allah has replaced for you two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice."
"12859","Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: No, grey hair did not disfigure him. He said: So it was said: O Abu Hamzah, is grey hair a disfigurement? He said: It is said: All of you dislike it. And Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and Umar dyed with henna."
"12860","Sahl informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that a man looked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a crack, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) aimed at him with an arrowhead, and the man pulled out his head."
"12861","Sahl narrated to us, from Humayd, and Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams. Ibn Bakr said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams. My father said: Both of them narrated it as a chain from Thabit from Anas."
"12862","Sahl narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded on the day of Uhud and they broke his incisor tooth, so he began wiping blood from his face saying: How will a people succeed who stain the face of their prophet with blood while he calls them to their Lord the Mighty and Majestic. So there was revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"12863","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: Anas was asked about the voluntary fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He used to fast until we would say: He does not break fast, and he would break fast until we would say: He does not fast."
"12864","Yahya narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from laziness and miserliness and the punishment of the grave."
"12865","Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this palace? They said: For a young man from Quraysh. So I thought that I was he. They said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"12866","Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for mounts and met him busy. He said: By Allah, I will not carry you. Then when he turned away he called him and said: I swore not to carry you. He said: And I swear I shall surely carry you. So he carried them."
"12867","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: I heard Anas, that Abu Musa said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for mounts, so he swore he would not carry us, then he carried us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not carry us. He said: And I swear I shall surely carry you."
"12868","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that a funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and good was said of it and tongues followed it with good. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It became due. Then another funeral passed, and they spoke evil of it and tongues followed it with evil. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It became due. You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"12869","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Al-Zubayr ibn Adi narrated to me, he said: We came to Anas ibn Malik complaining to him about al-Hajjaj. So he said: No day or time will come upon you but the one after it is worse than it. I heard it from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12870","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Ibn Jabr ibn Atik, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two ratls of water suffice for ablution."
"12871","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as a beast of prey spreads."
"12872","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish your rows, for proper establishment of the row is part of the excellence of prayer."
"12873","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while making it complete."
"12874","Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abdullah ibn Jabr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a vessel holding two ratls and perform ritual bath with a sa."
"12875","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on a mat."
"12876","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and behind Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and they would not recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"12877","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to me, from al-Suddi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to leave to his right."
"12878","Waki narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the minbar."
"12879","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman would not omit the takbir."
"12880","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only performed qunut for a month, supplicating after bowing."
"12881","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abi al-Tayyah al-Dubai, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while handing to his companions while they were building the mosque: Indeed life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"12882","Waki and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse of Abu Talhah called Mandub and rode it, then he came and said: We saw no alarm, and indeed we found him to be a sea."
"12883","Waki narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the Conquest wearing a helmet."
"12884","Waki narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyah narrated to us, from Abi al-Mukhis al-Yashkuri, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, your freedman so-and-so has been martyred. He said: No, I saw upon him a cloak he had pilfered on such-and-such day."
"12885","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, that Abu Talhah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about orphans under his care who had inherited wine, whether to make it vinegar. So he disliked that. And Waki once said: Why does he not make it."
"12886","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to discipline for wine with sandals and palm stalks. He said: Then Abu Bakr lashed forty. Then when it was the time of Umar and people drew near from the countryside and villages and he consulted the people about that and that became widespread among the people, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I see that you make it like the lightest of the prescribed punishments. So Umar lashed eighty."
"12887","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night, I passed by people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these? He said: These are the preachers of your nation from the people of this world; they used to command people to righteousness and forget themselves while reciting the Book, will they not reason."
"12888","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of the sister of a people is from them."
"12889","Waki and Ibn Jafar, meaning Ghundar, narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat given as charity to Barirah. So he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"12890","Waki narrated to us, Abu al-Umays narrated to us, from Abu Talhah al-Asadi, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know you would laugh little and weep much."
"12891","Waki narrated to us, Musab ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, and I came while he was eating dates squatting on his heels."
"12892","Waki narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a tailor invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to food, so he brought him food made with rancid fat and pumpkin. So I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) following the pumpkin in the dish. Anas said: Since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liking it, pumpkin has always pleased me."
"12893","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up an animal to kill it."
"12894","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf were permitted to wear silk because of an itch they had. Shubah said: And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them."
"12895","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah, the meaning, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write a letter to the Romans, so it was said to him: If it is not sealed your letter will not be read. So he took a ring of silver and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. So it is as if I am looking at its whiteness in his palm."
"12896","He narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I read this hadith to my father, finding it, so he acknowledged it, and he narrated part of it to us in another place, he said: Musa ibn Hilal al-Abdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abu Talhah married Umm Sulaym, and she is the mother of Anas and al-Bara. He said: So she bore him a son. He said: And he used to love him intensely. He said: So the boy fell severely ill. Abu Talhah used to rise for the dawn prayer, perform ablution, come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pray with him, stay with him until near midday, come back, rest at midday and eat, and when he prayed Zuhr he would get ready and go and not come back until the night prayer. He said: So he went one evening and the boy died. He said: And Abu Talhah came. He said: She spread a cloth over him and left him. He said: So Abu Talhah said to her: O Umm Sulaym, how did my son spend tonight? She said: O Abu Talhah, your son has not been calmer since he complained than tonight. He said: Then she brought him food and he ate and felt content. He said: Then he stood to his bed and laid his head. She said: And I stood and touched some perfume, then I came until I entered the bed with him, and as soon as he found the scent of perfume there occurred what occurs between a man and his wife. He said: Then Abu Talhah woke in the morning getting ready as he used to get ready every day. He said: So she said to him: O Abu Talhah, tell me, if a man entrusted you with a deposit and you enjoyed it, then he sought it and took it from you, would you grieve over that? He said: No. She said: Then your son has died. Anas said: So he grieved intensely over him and told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what she had done regarding food and perfume and what had occurred between him and her. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So you spent the night as newlyweds while he was beside you both? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you both in your night. He said: So Umm Sulaym became pregnant that night. He said: So she gave birth to a boy. He said: When morning came Abu Talhah said to me: Carry him in a cloth until you bring him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and carry with you some ajwah dates. He said: So I carried him in a cloth. He said: And he had not been rubbed in the palate nor tasted food or anything. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym has given birth. He said: Allah is Most Great, what did she bear? I said: A boy. He said: Praise be to Allah. So he said: Bring him to me. So I handed him to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rubbed his palate, then said to him: Do you have ajwah dates with you? I said: Yes. So I took out some dates, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a date and threw it into his mouth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept chewing it until it mixed with his saliva, then he handed the boy back, and as soon as the boy found the sweetness of the dates he began sucking some of the sweetness of the dates and the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the first to open the bowels of that boy was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The love of the Ansar is dates. So he was named Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah. He said: So many men descended from him. He said: And Abdullah was martyred in Persia."
"12897","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, Shuayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry, or her bridal gift. Yahya said: Or he gave her freedom as her dowry."
"12898","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Anas narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in anything of his supplication, and Yahya once said: of supplication, except in seeking rain, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"12899","Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Embrace Islam. He said: I find myself reluctant. He said: Even if you are reluctant."
"12900","Yahya narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I used to serve Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Ubayy ibn Kab and Suhayl ibn Bayda and a group of his companions at Abu Talhah's, serving them drink until the drink had almost taken effect in them, when a comer from the Muslims came and said: Do you not know that wine has been prohibited. So they did not say: Let us wait and ask. So they said: O Anas, pour out what remains in your vessel. He said: By Allah, they never returned to it, and it was only dates and unripe dates, and that was their wine on that day."
"12901","Yahya narrated from Humayd, he said: I heard Anas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj."
"12902","Yahya narrated from Shubah, Qatadah narrated from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing. I said: What about eating? He said: That is worse."
"12903","Yahya narrated from Humayd, and Yazid informed us, Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: There will come to you peoples softer in heart than you. Then the Asharis came, among them Abu Musa, and when they arrived at Madinah they began chanting: Tomorrow we meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party."
"12904","Yahya ibn Said narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: The Muslims heard at Badr while he was calling, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Shaybah ibn Rabiah, O Utbah ibn Rabiah, O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, have you found true what your Lord promised? For I have found true what my Lord promised me. They said: How do you speak to a people who have decayed or who cannot answer? He said: You do not hear what I say better than they do."
"12905","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: When we returned from the expedition of Tabuk, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Madinah there are peoples, you did not cross a valley nor travel a journey except they shared with you in it. They said: While they are in Madinah? He said: Excuse detained them."
"12906","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the time of the Fajr prayer, so he prayed when dawn rose, then he prayed the morning prayer the next day after it had become bright, then he said: Where is the questioner about the time of the Fajr prayer? What is between these two."
"12907","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas that Banu Salimah wanted to move from their homes to near the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that the mosque be left empty, so he said: O Banu Salimah, will you not count your footsteps? So they stayed. My father said: Yahya ibn Said erred in it, it is only that they would leave Madinah empty, but Yahya said the mosque, and my father struck it out here, and he had narrated it to us in the book of Yahya ibn Said."
"12908","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the crying of a child in prayer, so he shortened it, and we thought he shortened it for the sake of his mother, out of mercy for the child."
"12909","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: I never saw anyone more complete in prayer than the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor briefer."
"12910","Yahya narrated, Ashath narrated from al-Hasan from Anas, similar to it, the same."
"12911","Yahya narrated from Humayd, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a ring? He said: Yes, he delayed the Isha prayer one night until half the night, then he said: The people have prayed and slept, and you remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. As if I now look at the shine of his ring."
"12912","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: The prayer was established while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in private conversation with a man, until some of the people dozed or nearly dozed."
"12913","Yahya ibn Said narrated from Humayd, he said: Anas was asked about the night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: We never wished to see him praying except we saw him, nor sleeping except we saw him."
"12914","Yahya ibn Said narrated from Humayd, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about the earnings of the cupper. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, Abu Taybah cupped him, so he ordered for him a saa of barley, and he spoke to his masters to lighten his tax, and he said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and sea costus."
"12915","Yahya ibn Said narrated from Humayd from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to his companions and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"12916","Yahya ibn Said narrated, Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write for some people of the Ansar to Bahrain, so they said: Not unless you write the same for our brothers among the Muhajirun. So he called them but they refused. He said: Indeed you will see after me preference, so be patient until you meet me."
"12917","Yahya narrated from al-Taymi from Anas, he said: It was mentioned to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and I did not hear it from him: Indeed among you are a people who worship and strive until people admire them and their own souls admire them, they pass out of religion as the arrow passes out of the prey."
"12918","Yahya narrated, Hisham narrated, Qatadah narrated from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, used to open the recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"12919","Yahya said, al-Taymi narrated from Anas, he said: I was standing serving the tribe with date-wine made from dates, then a man came and said: Wine has been forbidden. They said: Pour it out, O Anas. So I poured it out. I said: What was their drink? He said: Unripe dates and ripe dates. And Abu Bakr ibn Anas said: That was their wine that day, while Anas was listening, and he did not deny it. And some of those who were with us said: Anas said: That was their wine that day."
"12920","Yahya narrated from Humayd from Thabit from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man being supported between his two sons. They said: He vowed to walk. He said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is in no need of this one tormenting himself. So he ordered him to ride."
"12921","Yahya ibn Said narrated from Hisham, Qatadah narrated, and Waki narrated, Hisham narrated from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is to cover it."
"12922","Ismail narrated, Hisham informed us, the same, and he said: Its expiation is burying it."
"12923","Waki narrated, Misar narrated from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A sacrificial animal or a sacrificial camel was brought past the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial offering or a sacrificial camel. He said: Even so."
"12924","Waki narrated, Shubah narrated from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered, and he mentioned the name of Allah and magnified Him."
"12925","Waki narrated from Shubah from Qatadah, and Ibn Jafar, Shubah narrated, he said: I heard Qatadah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams. He said: It was said: And you saw him slaughter them with his hand? He said: And I saw him placing his foot on their sides. He said: And he mentioned the name of Allah and magnified Him."
"12926","Waki narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik that a Jew crushed the head of a woman between two stones and killed her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crushed his head between two stones."
"12927","Waki narrated from Habib from Qays from Thabit from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were playing, and he said: Peace be upon you, O boys."
"12928","Waki narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Salih narrated, and he was a tanner, and he was of good appearance, with him were four hadiths. He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will enter Hell until when they have become charred they will be taken out and admitted to Paradise, so the people of Paradise will say: These are the Hell-dwellers."
"12929","Waki narrated from Ibn Abi Layla from Thabit from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Here I am with Hajj and Umrah together."
"12930","Waki narrated, Musab ibn Sulaym narrated, he said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with Hajj and Umrah."
"12931","Waki narrated, al-Amash narrated from Sahl Abi al-Asad from Bukayr al-Jazari from Anas, he said: We were in the house of a man of the Ansar, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he stood, and he took hold of the doorpost, and he said: The leaders are from Quraysh, and they have a right over you, and you have the like of that over them, as long as when they are asked for mercy they show mercy, and when they judge they are just, and when they covenant they fulfill. So whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"12932","Waki narrated from Sufyan from one who heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Sad while he was supplicating with two fingers, so he said: Make it one, O Sad."
"12933","Waki narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Hisham from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Hour comes upon one of you while in his hand is a seedling, let him plant it."
"12934","Waki narrated, he said: Shubah said: I heard Thabit from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"12935","Waki narrated from Sufyan from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abi Qilabah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my nation is Abu Bakr, and the strongest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar, and the truest of them in modesty is Uthman, and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and the unlawful is Muadh ibn Jabal, and the best reciter of them of the Book of Allah is Ubayy, and the most knowledgeable of them in the laws of inheritance is Zayd ibn Thabit. And for every nation there is a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"12936","Waki narrated from Hammam from Qatadah, he said: I said to Anas: Which clothing was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Hibarah."
"12937","Waki narrated from Sufyan from al-Qasim ibn Shurayh from Abi Bahr from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wonder at the believer, indeed Allah does not decree for the believer a decree except it is good for him. Abu Bahr, his name is Thalabah."
"12938","Abd al-Rahman narrated from Sufyan from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O best of creation. He said: That is Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"12939","Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful from Anas, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O best of creation. He said: That is Ibrahim, my father."
"12940","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sleeps through prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Establish prayer for My remembrance. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raided, used to say: O Allah, You are my support and You are my helper, and with You I fight."
"12941","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Shubah narrated from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A mat was sprinkled with water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he prayed on it. He said: Then a man said to him: I saw him pray the forenoon prayer. He said: I did not see him except that day."
"12942","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Anas ibn Sirin from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing."
"12943","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Sufyan narrated from Mansur from Ribi from Abi al-Abyad from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was white and high, then I would return to my family and tribe in the outskirts of Madinah and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prayed, so stand and pray."
"12944","Abd al-Rahman narrated from Hammad from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come upon a date and say: Were it not that I fear it is from charity, I would have eaten it."
"12945","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Hammad narrated from Thabit from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the house of Umm Haram on a mat."
"12946","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Thabit from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a rope stretched between two pillars, so he said: Whose is this? They said: It belongs to Hamnah bint Jahsh, when she becomes unable she clings to it. So he said: Let her pray what she is able, and when she becomes unable, let her sit."
"12947","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Hammad narrated from Humayd from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"12948","Bahz narrated, Shubah narrated, Anas ibn Sirin informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: There was a bulky man of the Ansar who could not pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I cannot pray with you. So he prepared food for him and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they spread a mat for him and sprinkled it, so he prayed on it two rakahs. Then a man of the family of al-Jarud said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the forenoon prayer? He said: I never saw him pray it except that day."
"12949","Bahz ibn Asad narrated, Hammad narrated, Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas informed us from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his companions came to him one night, so he went out and prayed with them and shortened it, then he entered his house and prolonged it, then he went out and prayed with them and shortened it, then he entered his house and prolonged it. When morning came they said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed, and you prolonged when you entered and shortened when you went out. He said: Because of you is what I did."
"12950","Abd al-Rahman narrated from Hammam, and Bahz, Hammam narrated from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy: Indeed Allah commanded me to recite to you. Ubayy said: Did Allah name me to you? He said: Allah named you to me. He said: Bahz said in his hadith: So he began to weep."
"12951","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Sufyan narrated from Rabiah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: There were not twenty white hairs in the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12952","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Shubah narrated from Attab, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I pledged the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey as much as I could."
"12953","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Hammad ibn Zayd from Thabit from Anas, and Abu Kamil, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Thabit narrated from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the best of people, the bravest of people, and the most generous of people. There was an alarm in Madinah, so the people went out toward the sound, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them, having preceded them, having investigated the alarm, on a bare horse of Abi Talhah with no saddle on it, with the sword on his neck. So he said: You need not fear. And he said to the horse: We found it swift, indeed it is swift."
"12954","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Hisham narrated from Abi Isam from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times, and say: It is more pleasant, more wholesome, and healthier."
"12955","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas that Anas used to breathe in the vessel two or three times. He said: And Anas claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"12956","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from Sufyan from Mamar from Qatadah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives with one washing."
"12957","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Thabit from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives in one night with one washing."
"12958","Bahz narrated, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated, he said: I heard Marwan al-Asghar narrate from Anas that Ali came from Yemen, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with. So he said: Had I not had the sacrificial animal with me, I would have exited ihram."
"12959","Abd al-Rahman narrated, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there is a tree, a rider travels in its shade a hundred years without crossing it. He said: So I narrated it to my father. He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrate it."
"12960","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik after Zuhr, so he stood to pray Asr, and when he finished his prayer we mentioned hastening the prayer, or he mentioned it, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them sits until when the sun has yellowed and is between the two horns of Satan, or on the horn of Satan, he stands and pecks four, remembering Allah in them only a little."
"12961","Abd al-Rahman narrated from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dream of the believer, or the Muslim, is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"12962","Abd al-Rahman narrated from Shubah from Thabit from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"12963","Abd al-Rahman narrated: Malik from Ibn Shihab from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest with a helmet on his head, and when he removed it a man came to him and said: Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kabah. So he said: Kill him. Malik said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not in ihram that day, and Allah knows best."
"12964","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and married her. He said: Then Thabit said to him: What did he give her as dowry? He said: Herself, he freed her and married her."
"12965","Ismail narrated, Ayyub narrated from Abi Qilabah from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"12966","Ismail narrated, Ayyub narrated from Abi Qilabah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon his wives while a driver was driving them, called Anjashah, so he said: Woe to you, O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels. Abu Qilabah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke a word which, had some of you spoken it, you would have blamed him for it, meaning his saying: Your driving with the glass vessels."
"12967","Ismail narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated, Abu Raja, the freedman of Abi Qilabah, narrated to me, he said: I narrate to you the hadith of Anas ibn Malik to me. Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that a group of eight men from Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged him upon Islam, then the land did not suit them and their bodies fell sick, so they complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Will you not go out with our herdsman among his camels and obtain from their urine and milk? They said: Yes. So they went out and drank from their urine and milk and recovered, then they killed the herdsman and drove away the cattle. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent after them, and they were caught and brought, so he ordered concerning them, and their hands and feet were cut off and their eyes were branded, then they were left in the sun until they died."
"12968","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about garlic, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats anything from this tree, let him not come near us, or let him not pray with us."
"12969","Ismail narrated, Abd al-Aziz narrated from Anas, he said: They passed with a funeral and praised it with good, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Incumbent, incumbent, incumbent. And they passed with a funeral and praised it with evil, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Incumbent, incumbent, incumbent. Then Umar said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, a funeral was passed with and it was praised with good, so you said: Incumbent, incumbent, incumbent, and a funeral was passed with and it was praised with evil, so you said: Incumbent, incumbent, incumbent. So he said: Whomever you praise with good, Paradise is incumbent for him, and whomever you praise with evil, the Fire is incumbent for him. You are the witnesses of Allah on earth, you are the witnesses of Allah on earth, you are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"12970","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated from Thabit from Anas, he said: A funeral was passed with and the people praised it with good, so he said: Incumbent. Then another funeral was passed with and it was praised with evil, so he said: Incumbent. So they said: You said for this: Incumbent, and for this: Incumbent. He said: The testimony of the people, and the believers are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"12971","Yunus narrated, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated from Thabit and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr in darkness, then he said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined. Indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. He said: So they came out hastening in the streets, saying: Muhammad and the army. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevailed over them, and he killed their fighters and took their offspring captive, and Safiyyah became for Dihyah al-Kalbi, then she became for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) afterwards, so he married her and made her freedom her dowry. He said: Then Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb said to him: O Abu Muhammad, did you ask Anas what he gave her as dowry? Then Anas said to you: He gave her herself as dowry. So Thabit laughed and said: Yes."
"12972","Yunus narrated, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken a ring of silver and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, so do not engrave upon it."
"12973","Yunus narrated, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated from Abd al-Aziz from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade men from saffron-dyed garments."
"12974","Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated, Abu Muid narrated, Makhul narrated from Anas ibn Malik, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when do we abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil? He said: When there appears among you what appeared among the Children of Israel, when indecency is among your elders, and rule is among your young, and knowledge is among your lowly."
"12975","Hajjaj narrated, he said: Shubah narrated from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and there was a singer chanting for his wives, or a driver. He said: And his wives would go ahead before him, so he said: O Anjashah, woe to you, be gentle with the glass vessels."
"12976","Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah, and he kept praying two by two until he returned. Yahya said: So I said to Anas: How long did he stay? He said: Ten."
"12977","Abd al-Ala narrated from Yahya from Anas, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Makkah, so I heard him say: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj."
"12978","From Abd al-Ala, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated from Anas, he said: We came from Khaybar, I and Abu Talhah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Safiyyah riding behind him. He said: Then the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stumbled, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell and Safiyyah fell. He said: So Abu Talhah leapt forward and said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you. I doubt, he said that or: Are you hurt? He said: You need not worry about me, attend to the woman. He said: So Abu Talhah threw the garment over his face and went to her and spread his garment over her, then he fixed her saddle for her, so we rode, then we surrounded him, one of us on his right and the other on his left. When we overlooked Madinah, or we were at the back of the Harrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Returning, worshipping, repenting, to our Lord praising. He kept saying them until we entered Madinah."
"12979","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Hajjaj ibn Hassan narrated, he said: We were with Anas ibn Malik, so he called for a vessel with three iron clasps and an iron ring in it, taken from a black case, smaller than a quarter and larger than half a quarter, so Anas ibn Malik ordered and water was put in it for us, so it was brought to us, and we drank and poured over our heads and faces, and we invoked blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12980","Ubaydah narrated from Humayd al-Tawil, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about raising the hands, so he said: Some of the Muslims stood up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday and said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has failed and the land is barren, wealth has perished. He said: So he prayed for rain and raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, while we saw no cloud in the sky. Then he stood and prayed until one near in house began to intend returning to his family due to the severity of the rain. He said: So we remained seven days, then on Friday they said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and riders have been detained. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: So it cleared away from Madinah."
"12981","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated from Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and the Ansar met him among them, so he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, indeed I love you. Indeed the Ansar have fulfilled what is upon them, and there remains what is upon you, so do good to their doer of good and overlook their doer of evil."
"12982","Ubaydah narrated from Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a cold morning, and the Muhajirun and Ansar were digging the trench, so he said: O Allah, indeed good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun. So they answered him: We are those who pledged Muhammad to jihad as long as we remain."
"12983","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated from Humayd from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave from the spoils of Hunayn to Uyaynah and al-Aqra and others, so the Ansar said: Does he give our spoils to those whose swords drip from their blood, or their blood drips from our swords? That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called the Ansar and said: O company of Ansar, are you not pleased that people go with worldly things and you go with Muhammad to your homes? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, had people taken a valley and the Ansar taken a ravine, I would take the ravine of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner garment and my repository, and were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar."
"12984","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated from Humayd from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Umm Sulaym, so she offered him ghee and dates. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return your ghee to its skin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting. Then he stood and prayed in a corner of the house, so we prayed with his prayer, then he supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Then Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a special little one. He said: And what is she? She said: Anas. He said: So he left no good of the Hereafter or this world that day except he supplicated with it, from his saying: O Allah, grant him wealth and children and bless them for him. He said: Then Anas said: My daughter told me that over a hundred and twenty of my loins were buried, and I am among the richest of the Ansar in wealth."
"12985","Ubaydah narrated from Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted about going out to Badr, so Abu Bakr advised him, then he consulted Umar, so Umar advised him, then he consulted them, so some of the Ansar said: It is you whom the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) means, O company of Ansar. So the speaker of the Ansar said: Do you consult us, O Prophet of Allah? Indeed we do not say to you as the Children of Israel said to Musa, peace be upon him: Go you and your Lord and fight, indeed we sit here. But by the One Who sent you with truth, had you struck its flanks to Bark, Ibn Abi Adi said: To Bark al-Ghimad, we would follow you."
"12986","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, meaning al-Ansari, narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the call of a child while in prayer, so he shortened it, and we thought he only did that out of mercy for the child, as he knew his mother was with him in prayer."
"12987","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas that he was asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: Gray hair had not disfigured him."
"12988","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd al-Tawil narrated from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter upon Umm Sulaym, and she had a son from Abi Talhah nicknamed Abu Umayr, and he used to joke with him. So he entered upon him and saw him sad, so he said: Why do I see Abu Umayr sad? So they said: His little bird with which he used to play has died. He said: So he began to say: O Abu Umayr, what did the little bird do?"
"12989","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas that Umm Sulaym bore a boy from Abi Talhah, so she sent him with her son Anas to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he did tahnik for him."
"12990","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: He saw spit in the qibla of the mosque, and it distressed him until that was known in his face, so he scraped it off, and he said: Indeed one of you, or a man, when he stands to prayer, converses with his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, or his Lord is between him and the qibla, so when he spits let him spit to his left or under his foot. And he gestured like this, as if into his garment. He said: And we would say to Humayd, and he would say: Glory be to Allah, who is he, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not add to us beyond it."
"12991","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, he said: Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: A man came hurrying, reaching the people while out of breath, then when he stood in prayer he said: Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer, he said: Who is the speaker, or who is the sayer? He said: So the people fell silent. So he said: Who is the speaker, or who is the sayer? For he said good, or he said no harm. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, I reached the row while out of breath, or breath hurried me. He said, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it. Then he said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly, let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"12992","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: A man called: O Abu al-Qasim. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not mean you, I only called so-and-so. He said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"12993","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a ring? He said: Yes, one night he delayed the last Isha prayer until near half the night, then when he prayed he turned to us with his face and said: The people have prayed and slept, and you remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. Anas said: As if I now look at the shine of his ring."
"12994","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the time of the morning prayer, so he prayed when dawn rose, then he brightened with them until it was bright, then he said: Where is the questioner about the time of the morning prayer? He said: What is between these two is the time."
"12995","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas, he said: We used to pray Maghrib, then one of us would go to Banu Salimah while seeing the places of his arrows."
"12996","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated from Said ibn Yazid, and he is Abu Salamah, he said: I said to Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in his sandals? He said: Yes."
"12997","Ismail narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated from Abi Qilabah, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed for every nation there is a trustee, and our trustee, O nation, is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"12998","Ismail narrated, Humayd narrated from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives in one night with one washing."
"12999","Ismail narrated, Said narrated from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned rams, stepping on their sides, slaughtering them with his hand, mentioning the name of Allah and magnifying Him."
"13000","Ismail narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: Anas said: I came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and Abu Talhah, with Safiyyah riding behind him on his camel. While we were traveling, the camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stumbled, so he fell and the woman fell. So Abu Talhah leapt from his camel, he said: Then he said: O Prophet of Allah, did anything harm you? He said: No, attend to the woman. So Abu Talhah threw his garment over his face, then he went to the woman and draped the garment over her, then she stood, and he tied for them on their mount, so they rode, and we rode traveling until when we were at the back of Madinah, he said: Returning, repenting, to our Lord praising. He kept saying that until we arrived at Madinah."
"13001","Ismail narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that Abdullah ibn Salam heard of the arrival of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, so he came to him and asked him about things. He said: I shall ask you about things which none knows except a prophet. He said: What is the first of the signs of the Hour, and what is the first food the people of Paradise will eat, and why does the child resemble his father and why does the child resemble his mother? He said: Jibril informed me of them just now. Ibn Salam said: Then he is the enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: As for the first of the signs of the Hour, it is a fire that will gather them from the east to the west. And the first food the people of Paradise will eat is the extra lobe of the fish liver. And as for the child, if the water of the man precedes the water of the woman, the child resembles him, and if the water of the woman precedes the water of the man, the child resembles her."
"13002","Ismail narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, Anas said: Bilal was ordered to make the adhan even and to make the iqamah odd. So I narrated it to Ayyub, and he said: Except the iqamah."
"13003","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: It was mentioned to me that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and I did not hear it from him: Among you there are a people who worship and exert themselves, meaning they impress the people and their own selves impress them, they pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game."
"13004","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: I was standing serving the tribe a fadikh drink of theirs when a man came and said: Wine has been made unlawful. So they said: Pour it out, O Anas. So I poured it out. So I said to Anas: What was it? He said: Unripe dates and ripe dates. He said: Then Abu Bakr ibn Anas said: That was their wine on that day. He said: And a man narrated to me from Anas that he said that also."
"13005","Ismail narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid informed us, he said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) open the recitation with In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, or with All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds? So he said: You are asking me about something no one has asked me about."
"13006","Ismail narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about shortening the prayer. So he said: We traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah to Makkah, and he led us in prayer two rakahs until we returned. So I asked him: Did he stay? So he said: Yes, we stayed in Makkah ten days."
"13007","Ismail narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to Madinah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi. So he said: I will share my wealth with you in two halves, and I have two wives, so I will divorce one of them, and when her waiting period ends, marry her. So he said: May Allah bless for you your family and your wealth; show me the market. So they showed him, and he went, and he did not return except with some dried yogurt and clarified butter which he had gained. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him after that with a trace of yellow perfume on him, so he said: What is this? He said: I married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dowry? He said: A date-stone weight of gold. Humayd said: Or the weight of a date-stone of gold. So he said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."
"13008","Bahz ibn Asad Abu al-Aswad al-Ammi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with children, women, camels and cattle, and they arranged them in rows to outnumber the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they met, the Muslims turned back in flight, as Allah Almighty said. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servants of Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. O company of the Ansar, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. So Allah defeated the polytheists. Affan said: And they did not strike with a sword nor thrust with a spear. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on that day: Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils belong to him. So Abu Talhah killed twenty men on that day and took their spoils. He said: And Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder joint while he wore armor, but I was turned away from him, so look who took it. So a man stood and said: I took it, so make him accept compensation from it and give it to me. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything but he gave it or remained silent. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. So Umar said: No, by Allah, Allah will not return it upon a lion of His lions and give it to you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Umar has spoken the truth. He said: And Umm Sulaym had a dagger with her. So Abu Talhah said: What is this with you? She said: I took it so that if any of the polytheists comes near me, I will rip open his belly with it. So Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us of the freed ones who fled from you. He said: Indeed Allah has sufficed us and done good, O Umm Sulaym."
"13009","Affan narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas narrated to me, from Anas: When it was the day of Hunayn, and Hawazin and Ghatafan gathered for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a large gathering, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with ten thousand or more, and with him were the freed ones, they came with cattle and offspring, then he mentioned the hadith."
"13010","Bahz narrated to us, Musa ibn Said narrated to me, from Abi al-Tayyah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Umm Sulaym, and she had a small son called Abu Umayr, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr? He said: A small bird he used to play with. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Umm Sulaym at times and talk at her place, then the prayer would overtake him, so he would pray on a mat, which was a palm mat that he would sprinkle with water."
"13011","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark, intensely black night. He said: When they left him, the staff of one of them lit up, so they walked by its light. Then when they parted, the staff of this one and the staff of that one lit up."
"13012","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Hour comes while in the hand of one of you is a palm shoot, if he is able not to stand until he plants it, let him do so."
"13013","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: I entered with my grandfather the governor's house, and there was a tied-up hen being shot at; whenever an arrow hit it, it cried out. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up animals as targets."
"13014","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni and Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. So I said: Whose is this? They said: For a young man of Quraysh. So I thought it was mine, but it was for Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing prevented me, O Abu Hafs, from entering it except what I know of your jealousy. He said: He said: O Messenger of Allah, of whom would I be jealous, for I would never be jealous of you."
"13015","Bahz narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his uncle Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque with his Companions when a Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque. So his Companions said: Stop, stop. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not cut him off; leave him. Then he called him and said to him: These mosques are not fit for anything of filth, urine and relieving oneself, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; they are only for reciting the Quran, remembering Allah, and prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of the people: Stand and bring us a bucket of water and pour it over it. So he brought a bucket of water and poured it over it."
"13016","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying in his house when a man came and peered into the house, and Affan said: into his house. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an arrow from his quiver and aimed it toward his eyes until he left."
"13017","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will come and tread the earth except Makkah and Madinah. He will come to Madinah and find at every pass of its passes rows of angels. Then he will come to the salty plain of al-Jurf and pitch his tent, then Madinah will shake three tremors, and every hypocrite, male and female, will go out to him."
"13018","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah and Thabit informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar."
"13019","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, and said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you said such and such? He said: Then the people fell silent. So he repeated it three times. Then a man said: I said it, and I meant by it only good. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve angels hastened to it, and they did not know how to write it until they asked their Lord Almighty. He said: Write it as My servant said."
"13020","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was traveling in Paradise, I came upon a river whose banks were domes of hollow pearls. He said: So I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord Almighty gave you. He said: Then I struck with my hand, and its clay was pungent musk. And Affan said: Hollow."
"13021","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, then left it."
"13022","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog does, and let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, for he is only conversing privately with his Lord; but to his left or under his foot."
"13023","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Qatadah narrated to us, that Anas informed him that al-Zubayr and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, and they sought permission during a campaign of theirs, so he permitted them to wear silk shirts. Bahz said: Anas said: So I saw on each one of them a shirt of silk."
"13024","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam informed us, Affan said: He narrated to us, and Bahz said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that a man of the desert people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When is the Hour? He said: Woe to you, and what have you prepared for the Hour? He said: I have not prepared anything for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you are with whom you love. He said: His Companions said: Are we likewise? He said: Yes, and you are likewise. He said: So they rejoiced on that day with great joy. He said: Then a boy of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah passed by; Anas said: And he was of my age-mates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this one is kept alive, old age will not overtake him before the Hour comes. And Affan said: So we rejoiced at it on that day with great joy."
"13025","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: It did not reach that; there was only something at his temples. But Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, dyed with henna and katam."
"13026","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that a Jew passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions and said: Death be upon you. So the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it upon him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He only said: Death be upon you. So the Jew was seized and brought, and he confessed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return upon them what they said."
"13027","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. Affan said: Then Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13028","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys, then he mentioned the like of it."
"13029","Affan narrated to us, and Bahz narrated to me, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, and Affan said: From Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The son of Adam grows old, but two things of him grow young: greed for wealth and greed for age."
"13030","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a palm grove of Umm Mubashshir, a woman of the Ansar, and said: Who planted this planting, a Muslim or a disbeliever? They said: A Muslim. He said: No Muslim plants a planting from which a human, an animal or a bird eats, except it is charity for him."
"13031","Bahz narrated to us, Abu al-Awwam al-Qattan narrated to us, my father said, and he is Imran ibn Dawar, and he is blind: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah twice to lead them in prayer, while he was blind."
"13032","Bahz narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped three times: once on his upper back and twice on the two jugular veins."
"13033","Bahz narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah say: I said to Anas: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to prolong his voice with prolongation."
"13034","Bahz narrated to us, and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from speech that is not heard, and a deed that is not raised, and a heart that does not humble itself, and knowledge that does not benefit."
"13035","Bahz narrated to us, and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, madness, elephantiasis, and from evil diseases."
"13036","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by a date, and nothing would prevent him from taking it except fear that it might be charity."
"13037","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that a slave girl was found with her head between two stones. So she was asked: Who did this to you, such-and-such, such-and-such, until the Jew was named. So she nodded with her head: Yes. So the Jew was seized and confessed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding him, and his head was crushed with stones."
"13038","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord Almighty promised me to admit one hundred thousand of my community into Paradise. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, increase us. He said to him: And like this, and he gestured with his hand. He said: O Prophet of Allah, increase us. So he said: And like this, and he gestured with his hand. He said: O Prophet of Allah, increase us. So he said: And like this. So Umar said: Enough of you, O Abu Bakr. He said: What is it to you, O Ibn al-Khattab? Umar said to him: Indeed Allah Almighty is able to admit all people into Paradise with a single handful. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar has spoken the truth."
"13039","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in good so long as he does not hasten. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how does he hasten? He said: He says: I supplicated my Lord but He did not answer me."
"13040","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"13041","Bahz narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two, and he raised his two fingers, the index and the middle, preferring one of them over the other."
"13042","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, Affan said: Thabit narrated to us, Anas said: We were forbidden in the Quran to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything. He said: And it used to please us that a sensible man of the desert people would come and ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So a man came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed for us that you claim that Allah Almighty sent you. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then who created the heaven? He said: Allah. He said: Then who created the earth? He said: Allah. He said: Then who set up these mountains? He said: Allah. He said: Then by the One who created the heaven, created the earth and set up the mountains, did Allah send you? He said: Yes. He said: And your messenger claimed that five prayers in our day and night are upon us. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: And your messenger claimed that charity in our wealth is upon us. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: And your messenger claimed that fasting the month of Ramadan in our year is upon us. Affan said: He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. And your messenger claimed that pilgrimage is upon us for whoever is able to find a way to it. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then by the One who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. Affan said: Then he turned away, then said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall neither add to them nor subtract from them anything. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he speaks the truth, he will surely enter Paradise."
"13043","Bahz narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us with the meaning, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in Ramadan, so I came and stood behind him. He said: And a man came and stood beside me, then another came, until we were a group. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perceived that we were behind him, he shortened the prayer, then stood and entered his dwelling, and prayed a prayer he did not pray with us. He said: When morning came, we said: O Messenger of Allah, did you notice us last night? He said: Yes, and that is what prompted me to do what I did. He said: Then he began continuous fasting, and that was at the end of the month. He said: Then some men of his Companions began continuous fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with men who fast continuously? You are not like me. By Allah, if the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a manner that would make the deeply strict abandon their strictness."
"13044","Bahz narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and there was none but me, my mother and Umm Haram, my maternal aunt. He said: So he said: Stand, so I may pray for you outside the time of prayer. Hajjaj said: He said: So he led us in prayer. A man of the people said to Thabit: Where did he place Anas? He said: He placed him on his right. He said: Then he supplicated for us, the people of the house, with every good of the good of this world and the Hereafter. He said: My mother said: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant, supplicate Allah for him. Then he said: So he supplicated for me with every good. Bahz said: And among the last of what he supplicated with was: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children and bless for him in it."
"13045","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Sulayman narrated to us, and Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah informed us, Affan said: Thabit narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A boy was born to me tonight, so I named him by the name of my father Ibrahim. He said: Then he handed him to Umm Sayf, the wife of a blacksmith called Abu Sayf, in Madinah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to visit him, and I went with him. We reached Abu Sayf while he was blowing his bellows, and the house had filled with smoke. He said: So I hastened walking ahead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I said: O Abu Sayf, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come. He said: So he stopped. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and called for the boy and embraced him. Anas said: I saw him in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was struggling with himself. So the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eye weeps, and the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord Almighty. By Allah, indeed we are grieved for you, O Ibrahim."
"13046","Bahz narrated to us, and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas said: My uncle, Hashim said: Anas ibn al-Nadr, after whom I was named, did not witness with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the day of Badr. He said: It weighed upon him, and he said: In the first battle witnessed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I was absent from him. If Allah shows me a battle afterwards with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah will surely see what I do. He said: He feared to say other than it. He said: So he witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the day of Uhud. He said: Then he met Sad ibn Muadh. So Anas said to him: O Abu Amr, where? He said: Ah, for the scent of Paradise; I find it below Uhud. He said: So he fought them until he was killed. And there were found on his body more than eighty wounds of striking, thrusting and shooting. He said: So his sister, my paternal aunt al-Rubayyi bint al-Nadr, said: I did not recognize my brother except by his fingertip. And this verse was revealed: Men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah; of them is he who fulfilled his vow, and of them is he who waits, and they did not change with alteration. He said: And they used to think it was revealed concerning him and his companions."
"13047","Bahz narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas said: I was sitting by the pulpit on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, when one of the people of the mosque said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has been withheld, livestock have perished; supplicate Allah to give us water. Anas said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands, while I saw no cloud in the sky. Then the clouds were joined together. Hajjaj said: So Allah joined the clouds, and we went. Hajjaj said: We hastened until I saw the strong man whose own self concerned him to reach his family. So we were rained upon for seven days. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out delivering the sermon on the next Friday, when one of the people of the mosque said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed, travelers have been detained; supplicate Allah Almighty to lift it from us. He said: So he raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: Then what was above our heads cleared away, until we were as if in a crown, raining around us while we were not rained upon."
"13048","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup of water, and he performed ablution. He said: So I said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution for every prayer? He said: Yes. He said: I said: And you? He said: We used to pray the prayers with a single ablution. He said: Then I asked him after that, and he said: So long as we did not break ablution."
"13049","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah narrating from Abi al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before building the mosque used to pray in sheepfolds."
"13050","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Musa ibn Anas narrating from Anas, that he, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his mother and his maternal aunt were together, so he led them in prayer. Anas was placed on his right, and his mother and his maternal aunt behind them both. Shubah said: Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar was younger than me."
"13051","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that befell him. If he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive so long as life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me."
"13052","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years, and not all my affairs were as my companion would like them to be. He never said to me in them: Uff, nor did he say to me: Why did you do this, and why did you not do this."
"13053","Hajjaj and Hashim narrated to us with the meaning, they said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day until, when I thought I had finished serving him, I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will take a midday rest. So I went out to boys playing. He said: So I came looking at their play. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and greeted the boys while they were playing. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and sent me for a need of his. So I went for it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in the shade until I came to him. And I was kept from my mother from the coming I used to come to her. When I came to her, she said: What kept you? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for a need of his. She said: And what is it? I said: It is a secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Then guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: Anas said to me: Had I narrated it to anyone of the people, or had I been one to narrate it, I would have narrated it to you, O Thabit."
"13054","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, Anas narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah fell to Dihyah in his share, and they praised her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And they said: We have not seen among the captives the like of her. He said: So he sent to Dihyah and gave him for her what he wanted, then handed her to my mother and said: Prepare her. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Khaybar until, when he placed it behind his back, he alighted, then pitched a tent over her. In the morning he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever has extra provisions, let him bring it to us. He said: So a man began bringing extra dates, extra sawiq and extra clarified butter, until they made of that a heap of hays. So they ate of that hays and drank from pools beside them of rainwater. He said: So Anas said: That was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for her. And we went until, when we saw the walls of Madinah, we rejoiced at them and raised our mounts, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his mount. He said: And Safiyyah was behind him, he had mounted her behind him. He said: Then the mount of the Messenger of Allah stumbled, and he fell and she fell. He said: And none of the people looked at him nor at her until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and covered her. He said: So we came to him, and he said: You are not harmed. He said: Then he entered Madinah, and the slave girls of his women came out to look at her and gloat over her fall."
"13055","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I saw a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there was neither bread nor meat, when Safiyyah fell to Dihyah al-Kalbi in his share. They praised her, then he mentioned its meaning."
"13056","Bahz narrated to us, and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the waiting period of Zaynab ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd: Go and mention her to me. He said: So he went until he came to her. He said: And she was leavening her dough. When I saw her, she became great in my chest so that I could not look at her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned her. So I turned my back to her and ran back on my heels. So I said: O Zaynab, rejoice; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to mention you. She said: I shall do nothing until I consult my Lord Almighty. So she stood to her prayer place, and it was revealed, meaning the Quran. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered upon her without permission. He said: And we saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed us bread and meat. Hashim said: When I knew that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had proposed to her. Hashim said in his hadith: We saw when she was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we were fed bread and meat. Then the people left, and men remained talking in the house after the food. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and I followed him. He began visiting the chambers of his women, greeting them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you find your wife? He said: I do not know whether I informed him that the people had left or he was informed. He said: So he went until he entered the house, and I went to enter with him, but he cast the curtain between me and him, and the veil was revealed. He said: And the people were admonished with what they were admonished with. Hashim said in his hadith: Do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permission is given to you for food, without waiting for its preparation, nor seeking familiar talk; indeed that used to harm the Prophet and he was shy of you, but Allah is not shy of the truth."
"13057","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A son of Abu Talhah by Umm Sulaym died. So she said to her family: Do not inform Abu Talhah of his son until I inform him. He said: So he came, and she brought dinner near to him, so he ate and drank. He said: Then she adorned herself for him with the best she used to adorn before that, and he had intercourse with her. When she saw that he was full and had attained from her, she said: O Abu Talhah, tell me, if a people lent their loan to a household and then sought their loan, do they have the right to withhold it from them? He said: No. She said: Then reckon your son as reward. So he went until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what happened. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless for you both in the rest of your night. He said: So she conceived. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and she was with him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Madinah from a journey, would not enter it by night. They drew near Madinah, and labor seized her, and Abu Talhah was detained with her, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on. So Abu Talhah said: O Lord, You know that it pleases me to go out with Your Messenger when he goes out and to enter with him when he enters, and I have been detained by what You see. Umm Sulaym said: O Abu Talhah, I do not feel what I felt; so let us go. He said: And labor seized her when they arrived, and she gave birth to a boy. So my mother said to me: O Anas, let none suckle him until you bring him in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: In the morning I carried him and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I found him with a branding iron. When he saw me, he said: Perhaps Umm Sulaym has given birth. I said: Yes. He said: So he put down the branding iron. He said: So I came with him and placed him in his lap. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for an Ajwah date of the Ajwah of Madinah, chewed it in his mouth until it dissolved, then cast it into the mouth of the boy. The boy began smacking his lips. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at the love of the Ansar for dates. He said: Then he wiped his face and named him Abdullah."
"13058","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, he said: Asim ibn Sulayman informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieve over anything as he grieved over the companions of Bir Maunah, the companions of the expedition of al-Mundhir ibn Amr. He remained a month supplicating against those who struck them in the qunut of the dawn prayer, supplicating against Ril, Dhakwan, Usayyah and Lihyan, and they are of Banu Sulaym."
"13059","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, he said: Al-Zuhri said, and Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: When it was Monday, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered the curtain of the chamber and saw Abu Bakr praying with the people. He said: So I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf, while he was smiling. He said: And we almost became distracted in our prayer out of joy at seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Abu Bakr wanted to step back, but he signaled to him to remain as you are. Then he let down the curtain, and he passed away on that very day. So Umar stood and said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has not died, but his Lord sent to him as He sent to Musa, who stayed away from his people forty nights. By Allah, I hope the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will live until he cuts the hands of men of the hypocrites and their tongues who claim, or he said: who say, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died."
"13060","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, and he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), served him and accompanied him, that Abu Bakr used to lead them in prayer during the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he died, until when it was Monday, then he mentioned the hadith."
"13061","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that Abu Bakr used to lead them in prayer during the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he died. It was Monday, and they were in rows for prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered the curtain of the chamber, then he mentioned its meaning."
"13062","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that Fatimah wept for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O my father, how near to his Lord he is; O my father, to Jibril we announce his death; O my father, the garden of al-Firdaws is his abode."
"13063","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from the women when they pledged to him not to wail. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, women helped us in the Jahiliyyah; shall we help them in Islam? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no helping in wailing in Islam, nor shighar, nor sacrificial slaughter at graves in Islam, nor bringing animals for zakah collection in Islam, nor keeping apart, and whoever plunders is not of us."
"13064","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and that was at dawn: O Anas, I intend to fast, so feed me something. He said: So I brought him dates and a vessel with water after Bilal had called the adhan. So he said: O Anas, look for a person to eat with me. He said: So I called Zayd ibn Thabit. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, I drank a drink of sawiq, and I intend to fast. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I intend to fast. So he took sahur with him, prayed two rakahs, then went out, and the prayer was established."
"13065","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years. No, by Allah, he never reviled me with a reviling, nor ever said to me: Uff, nor said to me for something I did: Why did you do it, nor for something I did not do: Why did you not do it."
"13066","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: There was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Allah may forgive you your sin, what preceded and what followed, on our return from al-Hudaybiyah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A verse has been revealed to me dearer to me than what is on the earth. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it to them. So they said: Congratulations, O Messenger of Allah; Allah Almighty has made clear to you what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then there was revealed to them: That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into gardens, until: a great triumph."
"13067","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my community disagreement and division; there will come out of them a people who recite the Quran, it does not pass their throats. Their mark is shaving and cutting hair short. When you see them, kill them. Al-tasbit means removing the short hair completely."
"13068","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Shall I not pray for you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he led them in a good prayer without prolonging it."
"13069","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in our house, and a domestic animal was milked for him. They mixed its milk with water of the house, then handed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drank, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin on his right. So Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, give Abu Bakr who is with you, fearing he would give it to the Bedouin. He said: So he gave it to the Bedouin, then said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"13070","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Praise it. So they said: So far as we knew, he loved Allah and His Messenger, and they praised him with good. So he said: It has become due. Then another funeral was passed with him, so he said: Praise it. So they said: An evil man he was in the religion of Allah. So he said: It has become due. You are the witnesses of Allah on the earth."
"13071","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, and Rawh, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Marwan, the freed slave of Hind bint al-Muhallab, Rawh said: Hind sent me to Anas ibn Malik, and he did not say: the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for a need, and I heard him narrating to his companions that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid continuous fasting."
"13072","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever alone sheds the blood of a man and kills him, his spoils belong to him. He said: So Abu Talhah came with the spoils of twenty-one men."
"13073","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah came on the day of Hunayn making the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh about Umm Sulaym. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see Umm Sulaym wearing a dagger? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What are you doing with it, O Umm Sulaym? She said: I intended that if anyone of them comes near me, I would stab him with it."
"13074","Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Suwayd Abu Muala informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Three birds were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he fed his servant a bird. When the next day came, she brought it to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Did I not forbid you to put anything aside, for indeed Allah Almighty brings the provision of every morrow."
"13075","Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us meets his friend; should he bow to him? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. He said: Then should he embrace him and kiss him? He said: No. He said: Then should he shake his hand? He said: Yes, if he wishes."
"13076","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Abu Qilabah al-Jarmi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Eight men of Ukl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam, but they found Madinah unhealthy. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to go to the charity camels and drink of their urine and milk. So they did so and recovered. Then they apostatized, killed its herdsmen, drove them away. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent trackers in pursuit of them. They were brought, so he cut their hands and feet and did not cauterize them until they died, and he blinded their eyes."
"13077","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the non-Arabs, so it was said: They do not accept a letter except with a seal. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"13078","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you sent ahead for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13079","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Masadah al-Bahili informed me, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The faith of a servant is not upright until his heart is upright, and his heart is not upright until his tongue is upright. And no man will enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms."
"13080","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Masadah al-Bahili informed me, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam errs, and the best of those who err are the repentant. And if the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third for them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"13081","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim al-Azdi Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with prolongation."
"13082","Hisham ibn Said, and he is Abu Ahmad al-Talaqani, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I heard Makhul narrating from Musa ibn Anas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reach of gray hair what requires dyeing, but Abu Bakr used to dye with henna and katam until his hair became dark red."
"13083","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hamzah informed me, Khalaf Abu al-Rabi, the imam of the mosque of Said ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed this religion is firm, so enter deeply into it with gentleness."
"13084","Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, nor cut off from one another, nor turn your backs on one another, nor envy one another. And be, servants of Allah, brothers. And it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"13085","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali was the most resembling of them in face to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13086","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Does a woman see in her dream what a man sees? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she sees what a man sees, meaning fluid, let her wash. Umm Salamah said: Can that be? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; the fluid of the man is thick and white, and the fluid of the woman is thin and yellow. From whichever of them precedes or prevails, Said said: We doubt, comes the resemblance."
"13087","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been ordered to fight the people until they testify that there is no god except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. When they testify, face our qiblah, eat our slaughtered animals and pray our prayer, their blood and wealth have become unlawful to us except by its right. For them is what belongs to the Muslims, and upon them is what is upon them."
"13088","Abd al-Wahid Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Sallam Abi al-Mundhir, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer."
"13089","Abd al-Wahid Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn Jabir, meaning al-Luqayti, narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from his father, he said: When the caller stood and called the Maghrib prayer in a mosque in Madinah, whoever wished stood and prayed until the prayer was established, and whoever wished bowed two rakahs then sat. And that was before the eyes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13090","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a man would go to Banu Salamah while he could still see the spot of his arrow."
"13091","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The prayer was established, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, then a man met him and kept him until some of the people almost dozed."
"13092","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O my little son."
"13093","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing. He said: So it was said to Anas: And eating? He said: That is more severe, or more evil."
"13094","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim informed us, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declare Madinah sacred? He said: Yes, it is sacred; Allah and His Messenger made it sacred. Its grass shall not be cut. Whoever does that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people."
"13095","Yazid informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be next to him in prayer, so they would learn from him."
"13096","Yazid informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one night praying in his chamber, then some people of his Companions came and prayed with his prayer. So he lightened, then entered the house, then came out and did that repeatedly, each time praying and leaving. In the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed with you last night, and we would like you to prolong your prayer. So he said: I knew of your place, and I did that deliberately."
"13097","Yazid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off, and the severity of that upon him was seen in his face. So he said: When the servant stands praying, he is only conversing privately with his Lord Almighty between him and the qiblah. When one of you spits, let him spit to his left or under his left foot, or do like this. And he took the edge of his cloak, spat in it, then rubbed part of it with part."
"13098","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym took his hand upon the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Anas, my son, and he is a boy who writes. Anas said: So I served him nine years, and he never said to me for anything I did: You did wrong, or: How evil what you did."
"13099","Yazid narrated to us, Humayd and al-Ansari informed us, he said: Humayd narrated to us with the meaning, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man of the desert people coming and asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to please us. He said: So a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And the prayer was established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose and prayed. When he finished the prayer, he said: Where is the asker about the Hour? So the man stood and said: I am. So he said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much prayer nor fasting, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves. He said: I never saw the Muslims rejoice at anything after Islam as their rejoicing at that. And al-Ansari said: Much deed, prayer nor fast."
"13100","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: He was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a ring? He said: Yes; one night he delayed the prayer, the Isha prayer, until midnight. Then he prayed, and when he prayed, he turned with his face and said: The people have prayed and slept, and you have not ceased to be in prayer since you waited for the prayer. He said: As if I look now at the glitter of his ring."
"13101","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed uninterrupted fasting at the end of the month, so some people performed uninterrupted fasting, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If the month were extended for us, I would have performed an uninterrupted fast that would make the overzealous abandon their overzealousness. I am not like you. I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"13102","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) injured his foot and it became dislocated, so he stayed in an upper chamber of his whose stairs were of palm trunks, and he took an oath of abstention from his wives for a month, so his Companions came to visit him, and he prayed with them sitting while they were standing, and when the next prayer came he said to them: Follow your imam; if he prays standing then pray standing, and if he prays sitting then pray sitting with him. He said: And he came down after twenty-nine. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you had taken an oath for a month. He said: The month is twenty-nine."
"13103","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Zaynab and fed the Muslims to their fill with bread and meat, then he went out as he used to do when he married, visiting the chambers of the Mothers of the Believers, greeting them and supplicating for them, and they would greet him and supplicate for him, then he returned, and I was with him, and when he reached the door, there were two men conversing in a corner of the house, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them he turned away, and when the two men saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had turned back, they jumped up in alarm and left, and I do not know whether I informed him or who informed him, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned."
"13104","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and of Abu Bakr were close in length, until Umar came, and he lengthened the dawn prayer."
"13105","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: I never smelled any scent, musk or ambergris, more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never touched brocade or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13106","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen the like of a people we have come to, better in comforting with little nor better in giving generously with much. They have sufficed us the burden of work and shared with us the pleasant livelihood, so much that we feared they would take all the reward. He said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate Allah, mighty and majestic, for them."
"13107","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: My father — and al-Ansari narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, extreme old age, cowardice, miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave."
"13108","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that a small son of Umm Sulaym called Abu Umayr had a small bird called a nughayr, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to him he would joke with him, then he saw him sad and said: What is the matter with Abu Umayr? They said: O Messenger of Allah, his nughayr has died. He said: So he began to say: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"
"13109","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid informed us, he said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: Gray hair did not disfigure him. It was said: Is it a blemish? He said: You all dislike it. There were only a few hairs at the front of his beard."
"13110","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother whether oppressor or oppressed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, we help him when oppressed, but how do we help him when oppressing? He said: You prevent him from oppression."
"13111","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by date-palms belonging to Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound, so he said: What is this? They said: The grave of a man buried in the Jahiliyyah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would stop burying one another, I would have supplicated Allah, mighty and majestic, to make you hear the punishment of the grave."
"13112","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal has his left eye effaced, over it a thick membrane, and written between his eyes is disbeliever."
"13113","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until no one on earth says Allah, Allah."
"13114","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded in his face on the day of Uhud, his front tooth was broken, and he was struck with a throw upon his shoulders, so blood began to flow upon his face while he wiped it from his face, saying: How can a people prosper who did this to their Prophet while he calls them to Allah, mighty and majestic? Then there was revealed: Not yours is any part of the affair, whether He turns to them, to the end of the verse."
"13115","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave from the spoils of Hunayn to al-Aqra ibn Habis one hundred camels and to Uyayna ibn Hisn one hundred camels, so some men of the Ansar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gives our spoils to men whose swords drip with our blood, or our swords drip with their blood. That reached him, so he sent for the Ansar and said: Is there among you anyone other than you? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister's son of a people is from them. Did you say such-and-such? Are you not pleased that people should go with worldly goods while you go with Muhammad to your homes? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if people took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar or their mountain pass. The Ansar are my inner garment and my repository, and were it not for the Hijrah I would have been a man of the Ansar."
"13116","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, that his uncle missed the fighting at Badr, so he said: I missed the first fighting which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought against the polytheists. If Allah witnesses a battle for me against the polytheists, Allah will surely see what I do. Then on the day of Uhud the Muslims were exposed, so he said: O Allah, I apologize to You for what these did, meaning his Companions, and I disavow to You what these brought, meaning the polytheists. Then he advanced and Sa'd met him short of Uhud — and Yazid said in Baghdad: short of Uhud — and Sa'd said: I am with you. Anas said: Sa'd said: I could not do what he did. He was found with more than eighty wounds, between a sword strike, a spear thrust, and an arrow shot. He said: So we used to say about him and his companions was revealed: Among them is he who fulfilled his vow, and among them is he who waits."
"13117","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he broke his fast with some people, would say: May fasting people break their fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you."
"13118","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The People of the Book greet us, so how should we reply to them? He said: Say: And upon you."
"13119","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not perform uninterrupted fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you perform uninterrupted fasting. He said: I am not like any of you. I spend the night fed and given drink."
"13120","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Madinah — the Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it, so neither the Dajjal nor the plague will approach it, if Allah wills."
"13121","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"13122","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you be balanced in his prayer and not spread his forearms like a dog."
"13123","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Kathir ibn Khunays, from Anas ibn Malik, that he narrated to them that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was preaching and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for the Hour? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13124","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, so he said after twice: O Bilal, you have conveyed, so whoever wishes let him pray and whoever wishes let him leave. Bilal returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, who will pray with the people? He said: Order Abu Bakr to pray with the people. When Abu Bakr stepped forward, the curtains were lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So we looked at him as if he were a white sheet, wearing a striped cloak. Abu Bakr started to step back, thinking he wanted to come out to the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to Abu Bakr to stand and pray. So Abu Bakr prayed with the people. Then we did not see him afterwards."
"13125","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best houses of the Ansar? They said: Yes. He said: The houses of Banu al-Najjar. He said: Shall I not inform you of those who come after them? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The houses of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. Shall I not inform you of those who come after them? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The houses of Banu Sa'ida. He said: Then he raised his voice and said: In all the houses of the Ansar there is good."
"13126","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith which no one after me will narrate to you. I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, adultery will appear, men will decrease and women will increase, until one man will be the caretaker of fifty women."
"13127","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys, and there was a camel-driver chanting for his wives, or a driver. His wives would go ahead before him. He said: O Anjasha, woe to you, be gentle with the glass vessels. Shu'ba said: This is in the hadith from something like his statement."
"13128","Yazid ibn Harun and Rawh both said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us — Rawh said: from Ubaydullah ibn Dihqan, and Yazid said: from Ubaydullah ibn Dihqan — from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand. Rawh said in his hadith: and drink with his left hand."
"13129","Affan narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to eat with his left hand."
"13130","Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyya bint Huyayy and made that her dowry."
"13131","Yazid and Abu Qatan both said: Shu'ba informed us, from Hammad, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And Abu Qatan did not say deliberately."
"13132","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti, who is al-Muzani, narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Dates were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began to distribute them with a single basket, and I was his messenger with them until he finished them. He said: Then he began to eat while sitting on his heels, eating voraciously, and I recognized hunger in his eating."
"13133","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two straps on his sandals."
"13134","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Qatada and Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to open the recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"13135","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing, he would stand until we would say he has become confused, and when he raised his head from prostration, he would sit between the two prostrations until we would say he has become confused."
"13136","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talha in the army is harder upon the polytheists than a troop."
"13137","Yazid narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, informed us, from Qatada, he said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: How was the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: It was wavy hair, neither lank nor curly, between his ears and his shoulders."
"13138","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that a slave girl went out wearing silver ornaments, so a Jew seized her, crushed her head, and took what was upon her. She was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while life remained in her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Who killed you? So-and-so? She said with her head: No. He said: So-and-so? She said with her head: No. He said: So-and-so, the Jew? She said with her head: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized him and crushed his head between two stones."
"13139","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Shu'ba, except that Qatada said in his hadith: So the Jew confessed."
"13140","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ribi ibn al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabra al-Tamimi informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabra, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to pray voluntarily upon his mount, he would face the qiblah, say the takbir for prayer, then leave his mount free and pray wherever it turned with him."
"13141","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymuna, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself, I and a boy would bring him a water skin and a short spear, and he would clean himself."
"13142","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Musa informed us, Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set a time for us in trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and shaving the pubic hair, once every forty days."
"13143","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most blissful of the people of this world among the people of the Fire will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and dipped in the Fire once, then it will be said to him: O son of Adam, did you ever see any good? Did any bliss ever pass you? He will say: No, by Allah, my Lord. And the most miserable of people in this world among the people of Paradise will be brought and dipped in Paradise once, then it will be said to him: O son of Adam, did you ever see any misery? Did any hardship ever pass you? He will say: No, by Allah, my Lord, no misery ever passed me nor did I ever see hardship."
"13144","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: We met Anas ibn Malik when he came from Syria, meeting him at Ayn al-Tamr, while he was praying upon his mount facing other than the qiblah. We said to him: You are praying facing other than the qiblah. He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing that, I would not have done it."
"13145","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Ghalib al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Anas ibn Malik pray over the funeral of a man, standing at his head, then when it was lifted, the funeral of a woman of Quraysh or of the Ansar was brought, and it was said to him: O Abu Hamza, this is the funeral of so-and-so, daughter of so-and-so, so pray over her. So he prayed over her, standing at her middle, and among us was al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi. When he saw the difference of his standing for the man and the woman, he said: O Abu Hamza, is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for a man where you stood and for a woman where you stood? He said: Yes. He said: So al-Ala turned to us and said: Memorize this."
"13146","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Salm al-Alawi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Pumpkin was among the most beloved foods to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or: pumpkin used to please the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Yazid doubted. A bowl containing pumpkin was brought, and I saw him inserting his fingers into the broth, following the pumpkin with them, the forefinger and the middle finger. He separated them then joined them."
"13147","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, he said: I heard Attab, the freedman of Ibn Hurmuz, say: I accompanied Anas ibn Malik on a ship, and I heard him say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine — and he gestured with his hand — to hear and obey as much as I could."
"13148","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, he said: Anas said: When we buried the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and returned, Fatima said: O Anas, did your souls feel good burying the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the dust and returning?"
"13149","Zayd narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Umm Haram, and he placed me on his right, with Umm Haram behind us."
"13150","Yazid and Affan both said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha — Affan and Hammam said: Ishaq, the nephew of Anas ibn Malik, informed us — from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not come to his family at night unannounced. He would arrive in the morning or in the evening."
"13151","Muadh ibn Muadh Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against Ril, Dhakwan, and Usayya."
"13152","Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Humaid al-Tawil narrated to us, and Ibn Abi Adi from Humaid al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between two pillars — Ibn Abi Adi said: in the mosque — so he asked about it, and they said: So-and-so woman prays, and when she is overcome she holds to it. He said: Let her pray as long as she is conscious, and when she is overcome let her sleep."
"13153","Muadh narrated to us, Humaid al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not seen the like of a people we have come to, better in giving generously from much nor better in comforting with little. They have sufficed us the burden of work and shared with us the pleasant livelihood, and we have feared they will take all the reward. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, as long as you praise them for it and supplicate Allah, mighty and majestic, for them."
"13154","Muadh narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came as an emigrant, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi, so Sa'd said to him: I have wealth, half of it is yours, and I have two wives, so look at the dearer of them to you so I may divorce her, and when her waiting period ends you may marry her. He said: Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth. Show me the market. He said: He did not return that day until he returned with something he had gained from the market. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him for some days, then he came to him with a trace of yellow perfume upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? He said: I married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What dowry did you give her? He said: A date-stone weight of gold, or he said: the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"13155","Muadh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: When Anas ibn Malik narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and finished it, he would say: Or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"13156","Muadh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to open their recitation in their prayer with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"13157","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest, or the most complete, of people in prayer, and the briefest."
"13158","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out while the Muhajirun were digging the trench on a cold morning. Anas said: And they had no servants. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, true good is only the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. He said: So they answered him: We are those who pledged to Muhammad for jihad as long as we live, never fleeing, never fleeing, never fleeing."
"13159","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: Some people of Urayna embraced Islam but found Madinah unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: If you went out to our milch camels and drank from their milk — Humaid said: And Qatada said, from Anas: and their urine — so they did, and when they recovered they disbelieved after their Islam, killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a believer, or a Muslim, drove away the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and fled as warriors. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, they were seized, he cut their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the Harrah until they died."
"13160","Yazid narrated to us, Humaid informed us, from Anas, he said: A group of Urayna came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but found Madinah unhealthy, so he mentioned its meaning, and he also mentioned in his hadith, he said: Humaid said: Qatada narrated in this hadith: and their urine."
"13161","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the prayer of Abu Bakr were close in length, until Umar extended the dawn prayer."
"13162","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: We used to pray Maghrib in the house of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would go to Banu Salima with one of us seeing the places where his arrows land."
"13163","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he heard a boy crying, so he shortened his prayer. We thought he only lightened it because of the boy, whose mother was in the prayer."
"13164","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, he said: Anas was asked about the punishment of the grave, so he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, extreme old age, cowardice, miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave."
"13165","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The prayer was commenced and a man intercepted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him, detaining him after the prayer was commenced until some of the people dozed."
"13166","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be next to him in prayer so they would retain from him."
"13167","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The prayer was commenced and there was something between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his wives, so he kept turning some of them back upon others. Abu Bakr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, throw dust in their mouths and go out to the prayer."
"13168","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day with his head bandaged. He said: The Ansar and their women and children met him, and seeing the faces of the Ansar, he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I love you. And he said: The Ansar have fulfilled what was upon them, and what is upon you remains. So do good to their good-doer and overlook their wrongdoer."
"13169","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: On the day of Uhud the front tooth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was broken and he was wounded in his face. He said: Blood began to flow upon his face, and he began to wipe the blood from his face, saying: How can a people prosper who dyed the face of their Prophet with blood while he calls them to Allah, mighty and majestic? He said: Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Not yours is any part of the affair, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"13170","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: Abu Talha was in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his head from behind him, looking at the places of his arrows, while Abu Talha would stretch his chest to shield the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it. He said: And he would say: O Messenger of Allah, my throat before your throat."
"13171","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched to Khaybar and reached it at night. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon them at night, he would not raid them until morning. If he heard the call to prayer he held back, and if they were not praying he raided them. He said: When morning came, he rode and the Muslims rode. He said: The people of the village went out to their fields with their baskets and spades, and when they saw the Messenger of Allah and the Muslims they said: Muhammad, by Allah, and the army. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined. When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. Anas said: And I was riding behind Abu Talha, with my foot touching the foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13172","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sa'd, informed me, that Ibn Shihab informed him, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, that he saw a silver ring on the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, then the people made silver rings and wore them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."
"13173","Rawh narrated to us, Zurara ibn Abi al-Halal al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating with broth containing pumpkin before him, and he kept following it, eating it."
"13174","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He had seen of gray only a little, meaning. And Abu Bakr and Umar had dyed, I think with henna and katam."
"13175","Rawh narrated to us, Zurara ibn Abi al-Halal al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anjasha, such is your driving with the glass vessels."
"13176","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that a speaker among the people said: O Prophet of Allah, will the Dajjal enter Madinah? He said: He will indeed head toward it, but he will find the angels arrayed at its passes and its gates, guarding it from the Dajjal. He said:"
"13177","Abd al-Wahhab said in his hadith: Qatada said: And Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Written between his eyes is: he disbelieved, spelled out; every believer reads it, illiterate or literate."
"13178","Rawh narrated to us, Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."
"13179","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Anas informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is so-and-so. Then was revealed: O you who believe, ask not about things which, if disclosed to you, would grieve you, to the end of the verse."
"13180","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that Ukaydir of Duma gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cloak of sundus or dibaj — Sa'id doubted — before silk was prohibited. He wore it and the people admired it, so he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than it."
"13181","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, that Anas ibn Malik informed them, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between his eyes is written k f r, meaning disbeliever; the believer reads it, illiterate and literate."
"13182","Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a briefer prayer, nor more complete, than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13183","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you believes until Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than others, and until being cast into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it, and none of you believes until I am dearer to him than his child, his parent, and all people."
"13184","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur, he said: I heard Talq ibn Habib narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"13185","Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, then mounted his mount, and when he ascended the mountain of al-Bayda he called out the talbiyah."
"13186","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show them a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."
"13187","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for one hundred years without crossing it."
"13188","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was traveling in Paradise, a river appeared before me, its banks domes of hollow pearl, so I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord gave you. He said: Then the angel dipped his hand and brought forth from its clay a strong-smelling musk."
"13189","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking until he reached near the mosque. He said: An old man, or a man, came to him and said: When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And what have you prepared for it? The man said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I have not prepared for it much prayer or fasting, but I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13190","Aswad narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Humaid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for twenty days."
"13191","Rawh and Muhammad ibn Ja'far both said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out both together, or said the talbiyah for both together."
"13192","Rawh and Affan, the meaning, both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that a youth of the Ansar — Affan said: A youth of Aslam — said: O Messenger of Allah, I want jihad but I have no wealth to equip myself with. He said: Go to so-and-so al-Ansari, for he had equipped himself but fallen ill. Say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveys peace to you and says to you: Hand over to me what you equipped yourself with. He said that to him, so he said: O so-and-so, hand over to him what you equipped me with, and withhold nothing from him, for by Allah, if you withhold anything from him Allah will not bless you in it."
"13193","Rawh and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A morning outing or an evening outing in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the bow-length of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"13194","Rawh and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will be brought and it will be said to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O Lord, the best abode. He will say: Ask and wish. He will say: I ask and wish only that You return me to this world and I be killed in Your path ten times, for what he sees of the merit of martyrdom. And a man of the people of the Fire will be brought and it will be said to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O Lord, the worst abode. He will say to him: Would you ransom yourself from it with an earth-full of gold? He will say: O Lord, yes. He will say: You lie. I asked you for less than that and easier, but you did not do it. Then he will be returned to the Fire."
"13195","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say in his supplication: O Allah, give us good in this world, good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shu'ba said: So I said to Thabit: Did he hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"13196","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamrah, then sacrificed the camels while the cupper was sitting, then he said to the cupper — and Hisham described that — and he placed his hand upon his forelock, shaved one side, the right, distributed it among the people, shaved the other, and gave it to Abu Talha."
"13197","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: None of you should wish for death due to harm that befell him. If he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."
"13198","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, both said: We heard Anas ibn Malik narrate the like of it, except that he said: due to harm that descended upon him."
"13199","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much fasting, prayer, or charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13200","Rawh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I do not recognize anything of what I knew with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) today. Abu Rafi said: O Abu Hamza, not even the prayer? He said: Have you not known what al-Hajjaj has done with the prayer?"
"13201","Rawh and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they both said: Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he walked to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he had mortgaged his armor with a Jew and taken barley for his family, and I heard him one day saying - Abd al-Samad said: he would say that repeatedly - there never remained by evening with the family of Muhammad a sa of wheat nor a sa of grain, while he had nine wives at that time."
"13202","Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he has already supplicated for his nation, and I have held back my supplication as intercession for my nation."
"13203","Rawh narrated to us: Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Some people will be struck by scorching from the Fire as punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will admit them into Paradise by the bounty of His mercy; they will be called al-Jahannamiyyun."
"13204","Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say in his supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, extreme old age, and the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and the trial of death."
"13205","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge in Allah from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire."
"13206","Rawh narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would fast until it would be said he has fasted, and would break his fast until it would be said he has broken his fast."
"13207","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us: I heard Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Make things easy and do not make them difficult, and give comfort and do not drive people away."
"13208","Rawh narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I would enter upon him without permission, then one day I came and entered upon him, and he said: O my son, a new matter has come up, so do not enter upon me except with permission."
"13209","Rawh and Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, they both said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: If a trotter were gifted to me I would accept it, and if I were invited - Abd al-Wahhab said: to it, and Rawh said: to attend it - I would respond."
"13210","Rawh narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic is He: Then when his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, he said: He gestured with his little finger, he said: and it crumbled down."
"13211","Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sever ties with one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"13212","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj and Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sever ties, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights."
"13213","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: We visited Anas ibn Malik in a group of the people of Medina, he said: Have you prayed, meaning Asr? They said: Yes. We said: Inform us, may Allah set you right, when would the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray this prayer? He said: He would pray it while the sun was still white and clear."
"13214","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is to bury it."
"13215","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of silver with an Abyssinian stone, and he engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"13216","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jabr, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bathe with a woman of his wives from a single vessel."
"13217","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid, meaning al-Hadhda', from Muhammad, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did Umar observe qunut? He said: Yes, and one better than Umar did, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after bowing."
"13218","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Thabit, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would supplicate often, saying: O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"13219","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Thabit: He heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, so I mentioned that to Ali ibn Zayd, and he said: That is only in the prayer for rain. He said: I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to Allah. He said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Glory be to Allah."
"13220","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a garment of silk, and they began touching it and looking at it, and he said: Are you astonished at this? The handkerchiefs of Sa'd - or the handkerchief of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh - in Paradise are better than this, or softer than this."
"13221","Sulayman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hammad and Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay' and Attab, the freedman of Ibn Hurmuz, and Rabi' as well: They heard Anas narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever deliberately lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This is how he said it to us; he erred in it, for it is rather Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb."
"13222","Sulayman and Abu Sa'id, meaning the freedman of Banu Hashim, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Anas narrated to us: He heard Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"13223","Sulayman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while they were digging the Trench: O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so set right the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"13224","Sulayman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: I am at the expectation My servant has of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"13225","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, he said: I heard Anas saying: A man from the People of the Book came and greeted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Death be upon you. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck? He said: No; when they greet you, say: And upon you."
"13226","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Ishaq narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I was walking with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was wearing a Najrani cloak with a thick hem, and a bedouin from the desert folk was asking him, until he reached one of his rooms, and he pulled it with such a pull that the cloak tore and its hem sank into the neck of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the response of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was that he ordered something for him and he was given it."
"13227","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Ishaq narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sent Haram, his maternal uncle, the brother of Umm Sulaym, with seventy men, they were killed on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah, and the chief of the polytheists that day was Amir ibn al-Tufayl, and he was the one who had come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Choose for me one of three traits: the settled folk shall be yours and the desert folk mine, or I shall be your successor after you, or I shall raid you with a thousand dusky horses of Ghatafan and a thousand dusky mares. He said: Then he was pierced by plague in the house of a woman of Banu so-and-so, and he said: A swelling like the swelling of a camel in the house of a woman of Banu so-and-so; bring me my horse. It was brought to him and he mounted it, and he died on its back. Then Haram, the brother of Umm Sulaym, set out with two men with him, a man of Banu Umayyah and a lame man, and he said to them: Stay near me until I go to them; if they grant me security, well and good, otherwise stay near, and if they kill me, inform your companions. He said: Haram came to them and said: Do you grant me security so that I may convey to you the message of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? They said: Yes. He began speaking to them, and they signaled to a man of them behind him, and he stabbed him until he pierced him through with the spear. He said: Allah is Greatest; I have succeeded, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: Then they killed them all except the lame man, who was on top of a mountain. Anas said: Then there was revealed to us - and it was of what used to be recited, then it was abrogated -: Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and has made us pleased. He said: Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them for forty mornings, against Ri'l and Dhakwan and Banu Lihyan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"13228","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade soaking unripe dates and ripe dates together."
"13229","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"13230","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The servant remains in good so long as he does not hasten. They said: And how does he hasten? He said: He says: I have supplicated my Lord and He has not answered me."
"13231","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa both said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never addressed us except that he said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"13232","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that Umm Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, if Harithah has attained good, well and good, otherwise I shall weep much. He said: O Umm Harithah, there are many gardens, and he is in the highest Firdaws."
"13233","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that a Jew invited the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he accepted."
"13234","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, slaughtering them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides, pronouncing the name of Allah and magnifying Him."
"13235","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A funeral passed by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was praised with good, and he said: It has become due. And a funeral passed by and it was praised with evil, and he said: It has become due."
"13236","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not come out to us for three days, and the prayer was announced, and Abu Bakr went forward to lead, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lifted the curtain with his hand, and when the face of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became clear to us, we never looked upon a sight more pleasing to us than the face of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when it became clear to us, and he gestured with his hand, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Abu Bakr to go forward, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, let down the curtain, and he was never able to come out again until he died."
"13237","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came toward Medina while he had Abu Bakr riding behind him, and Abu Bakr was an elder who was known, while the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was young and unknown. He said: A man would meet Abu Bakr and say: O Abu Bakr, who is this man in front of you? And he would say: This is a man guiding me to the way. The reckoner would think he meant only guiding him along the road, while he meant the way of good. Then Abu Bakr turned and saw a horseman catching up with them, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, here is a horseman catching up with us. He said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned and said: O Allah, throw him down. His horse threw him, then stood whinnying. He said: Then he said: O Prophet of Allah, command me as you wish. He said: Stay in your place; do not let anyone catch up with us. He said: In the morning he had striven against the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and by the end of the day he was a guard for him. He said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, alighted at the side of the lava field, then sent for the Ansar, and they came to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, greeted them both, and said: Ride safe and secure. He said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr rode, and they surrounded them with weapons. He said: It was announced in Medina: The Prophet of Allah has come. They looked out for the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gazing at him and saying: The Prophet of Allah has come. He came riding until he reached the side of the house of Abu Ayyub. They said: He was speaking to its people when Abd Allah ibn Salam heard of him while he was among palms belonging to his family, gathering ripe dates for them, and he hastened to put down that in which he was gathering and came with it, and he heard from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then returned to his family. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Which of the houses of our family is nearest? He said: Abu Ayyub said: I, O Prophet of Allah; this is my house and this is my door. He said: Go and prepare a midday resting place for us. He said: So he went and prepared a resting place for them, then came and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have prepared a resting place for you, so arise with the blessing of Allah. And they took their midday rest. When the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had come, Abd Allah ibn Salam came and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah in truth, and that you have come with the truth, and the Jews know that I am their chief and the son of their chief, and their most learned and the son of their most learned, so call them and ask them. They came to him, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: O company of Jews, woe to you, fear Allah, for by Him besides whom there is no god, you know that I am the Messenger of Allah in truth, and that I have come to you with the truth; submit. They said: We do not know that - three times."
"13238","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal is blind in one eye, with k f r written between his eyes; he spells it out: every Muslim reads it, k f r."
"13239","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abu Isam narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would breathe in his drink three times, and say: It is more wholesome, more healing, and more pleasant. Anas said: And I breathe three times."
"13240","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived, he alighted in the upper part of Medina in a quarter called Banu Amr ibn Awf, and stayed among them fourteen nights, then he sent for the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar. He said: They came with their swords slung. He said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on his mount, with Abu Bakr riding behind him and the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar around him, until he stopped at the courtyard of Abu Ayyub. He said: He would pray wherever the prayer overtook him, and would pray in sheepfolds, then he ordered the mosque to be built, and sent for the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar, and they came, and he said: O Banu al-Najjar, name a price for this walled plot of yours. They said: By Allah, we seek its price only from Allah. He said: And in it was what I tell you: there were graves of the polytheists, and there was tilth, and there were palm trees. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the graves of the polytheists to be dug up, the tilth to be leveled, and the palms to be cut. He said: They lined the palms toward the qibla of the mosque and made its doorposts of stone. He said: They began carrying those stones while chanting, with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them, saying: O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so aid the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"13241","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Tayyah informed us: Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the best of people in character, and I had a brother called Abu Umayr. He said: I think he said: newly weaned. He said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and saw him, he would say: O Abu Umayr, what has the Nughayr done? He said: A small bird he used to play with. He said: Sometimes the prayer would come while he was in our house, and he would order the mat beneath him to be swept, then sprinkled with water, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would stand and we would stand behind him, and he would pray with us. He said: And their mat was of palm stalks."
"13242","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I brought Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was born, while he was smearing tar on a camel of his and wearing a cloak, and he said: Do you have dates with you? So I handed him some dates, and he threw them into his mouth and chewed them, then opened his mouth, then fed them to him, and the child began smacking his lips, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The love of the Ansar is dates. And he named him Abd Allah."
"13243","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and al-Qasim together, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: Upon you. And the other said: And upon you."
"13244","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Yemen have come to you, and they are more tender-hearted than you, and they are the first who brought handshaking."
"13245","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him one night in Ramadan, and he prayed for them and shortened it, then went inside and prolonged the prayer, then came out and prayed with them, then went inside and prolonged the prayer, and he did that repeatedly, and in the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to you and you did such and such. And he said: I did that for your sake."
"13246","Abd al-Samad and Affan both said: Hammad narrated to us - the meaning is one - from Simak, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Bara'ah with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and when he reached Dhu al-Hulayfah - Affan said -: None shall convey it but I or a man of my household. So he sent it with Ali."
"13247","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Umm Ayman wept when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and it was said to her: What makes you weep for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? And she said: I knew that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would die, but I weep only for the revelation that has been lifted from us."
"13248","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw mucus in the qibla of the mosque and scraped it off with his hand."
"13249","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the people of Yemen came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they said: Send with us a man to teach us the Book of our Lord and the Sunnah. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took Abu Ubaydah by the hand and handed him to them, saying: This is the trustee of this nation."
"13250","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he wanted to shave his head, Abu Talhah grasped one side of his head, and when the barber shaved it, he took it and brought it to Umm Sulaym, and she began putting it in her perfume."
"13251","Abd al-Samad and Hasan both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw as if tonight I were in the house of Rafi' ibn Uqbah - Hasan said: in the house of Uqbah ibn Rafi' - and we were brought dates of Ibn Tab, and I interpreted that we shall have eminence in this world and a good end in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good."
"13252","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Abi Bakr al-Muzani, narrated to us: Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, he said: I know it only from Anas, he said: No case involving retaliation was ever raised to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except that he enjoined pardon in it."
"13253","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he spoke a word would repeat it three times, and when he came to a people and greeted them, he would greet them three times."
"13254","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Bistam ibn Hurayth narrated to us, from Ash'ath al-Harrani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my nation."
"13255","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Ammar Abu Hashim, the dealer in saffron, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Fatimah handed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a piece of barley bread, and he said: This is the first food your father has eaten in three days."
"13256","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas, that a bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the coming of the Hour, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: What have you prepared for it? He said: Nothing, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: A man shall be with whom he loves. Then he said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? He said: And there was a boy there, and he said: If this one lives, he will not reach old age before the Hour comes."
"13257","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Harb ibn Shaddad, a Basran, narrated to us: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Zunayb al-Anbari reported that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him that Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, what if there are rulers over us who do not follow your sunnah nor take your command, what do you command concerning them? And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no obedience to one who does not obey Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"13258","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Anas narrating from his father that drawing water with camels became hard for the Ansar, so they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for him to supplicate for them or dig a river for them, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told of that, and he said: They will not ask me for anything today but that they shall be given it. The Ansar were told of that, and when they heard what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, they said: Supplicate Allah for forgiveness for us. And he said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."
"13259","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you finding his camel after losing it in a desert land."
"13260","And Shahr narrated that from Abu Hurayrah."
"13261","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be met by a man on Friday after he came down from the pulpit, and he would speak to him, then enter into the prayer."
"13262","Wahb narrated to us: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal narrating from Anas ibn Malik that he said: It is as if I am looking at the dust of the procession of Jibril, peace be upon him, rising in the lane of Banu Ghanm when he marched to Banu Qurayzah."
"13263","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Hisham, meaning Ibn Sanbar Abu Abd Allah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith that none will narrate to you after me; I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge shall be lifted, ignorance shall appear, wine shall be drunk, fornication shall appear, men shall become few and women many, until there shall be among fifty women a single caretaker."
"13264","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to drink standing."
"13265","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you prostrate spreading his forearms as a dog does."
"13266","Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, extreme old age, from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of life and death. Abd al-Wahhab said: miserliness and cowardice."
"13267","Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams, slaughtering them with his own hand, pronouncing the name of Allah and magnifying Him, and placing his foot on their sides."
"13268","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray Asr while the sun was white and alive, then one going to al-Awali would reach them while the sun was still high."
"13269","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to people who were praying sitting due to illness, and he said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"13270","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Musa ibn Anas ibn Malik, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have left men in Medina; you have traveled no journey, spent no expense, nor crossed any valley, but that they are with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can they be with us while they are in Medina? He said: Excuse has detained them."
"13271","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, that Anas was asked about the hair of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I never saw hair more like the hair of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than the hair of Qatadah. And Qatadah rejoiced that day."
"13272","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Kharijah ibn Abd Allah, of the descendants of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to us, from his father, he said: We returned from Zuhr with Kharijah ibn Zayd, and we visited Anas ibn Malik, and he said: O slave girl, see if the time has come. He said: She said: Yes. So we said to him: We have only just returned from Zuhr with the imam. He said: Then he stood and prayed Asr, then said: This is how we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13273","Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a Jew came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was with his Companions, and said: Death be upon you. The people answered him, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know what he said? They said: Yes, he said: Death be upon you. He said: Bring the man back to me. So they brought him back, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did you say such and such? He said: Yes. Then the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: Upon you, meaning: upon you what you said."
"13274","Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a road with some of his Companions when a woman met him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you. He said: O mother of so-and-so, sit in whichever side of the streets you wish and I shall sit with you. So she did, and he sat with her until she fulfilled her need."
"13275","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he shaved, began with the right side of his head and shaved it, then handed it to Abu Talhah. He said: Then he shaved the left side of his head and divided it among the people."
"13276","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, for he is conversing with his Lord; rather let him spit to his left or under his foot."
"13277","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a vessel with water only enough to cover his fingers, or not covering his fingers - Sa'id doubted - and they began performing ablution, with water springing from between his fingers. He said: We said to Anas: How many were you? He said: Three hundred."
"13278","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"13279","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, and Abd al-Wahhab from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins, upon his return from al-Hudaybiyah while they were overcome with grief and gloom, and he had sacrificed the offering at al-Hudaybiyah, he said: A verse has been revealed that is dearer to me than the whole world. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know what shall be done for you, so what shall be done for us? Then there was revealed: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein, and expiate their evil deeds from them, and that is with Allah a mighty triumph. Abd al-Wahhab said in his narration: while his Companions were overcome with grief and gloom, and he said in it: A speaker said: Joyful and wholesome to you, O Messenger of Allah; Allah, mighty and majestic is He, has made clear what He shall do with you."
"13280","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete the first row and the one after it, and if there is any deficiency, let it be in the last row."
"13281","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear shirts of silk on a journey because of an itch they had."
"13282","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Abu Ali ibn Yazid, the brother of Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited it: And We ordained for them therein a life for a life, and an eye for an eye, putting nafs in the accusative and ayn in the nominative."
"13283","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Harithah ibn Suraqah went out to look around, not out to fight, and an arrow struck him and killed him, and his mother came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah: if he is in Paradise I shall endure and seek reward, and he said: O Umm Harithah, there are many gardens, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaws."
"13284","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Shurahbil narrated to me, from A'yan al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves debt, it is upon Allah, mighty and majestic is He, and upon His Messenger."
"13285","Asbat narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf to wear silk on a journey because of an itch they had."
"13286","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be cupped and would not wrong anyone his wage."
"13287","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us: Malik narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, let his forelock hang down as long as Allah willed him to let it hang, then he parted it afterwards."
"13288","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against those who killed the people of Bi'r Ma'unah for thirty mornings, against Ri'l and Dhakwan and Lihyan and Banu Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, and concerning that a Quranic passage was revealed which we recited: Convey from us to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and has made us pleased."
"13289","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A servant girl of the people of Medina, though a slave, would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would not pull his hand from hers until she took him wherever she wished."
"13290","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, so I mentioned that to Ali ibn Zayd, and he said: That is only in the prayer for rain. He said: I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to Allah."
"13291","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while on his mount: Here I am, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah, humbling himself on his mount."
"13292","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhda', from Abu Na'amah al-Hanafi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar would not recite, meaning they would not recite aloud."
"13293","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The last prayer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, he wore a cloak wrapped around him, while sitting."
"13294","Azhar ibn al-Qasim and Abd al-Wahhab both said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The distance between the two sides of my Basin is like that between Sanaa and Medina, or like that between Medina and Amman. Abd al-Wahhab said: Hisham doubted."
"13295","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a man who sleeps through the prayer or is heedless of it. He said: Let him pray it when he remembers it."
"13296","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never dyed his hair at all; the whiteness was only in the front of his beard, on the lower lip, on the head, and on the temples, hardly visible. And Abu Bakr dyed with henna."
"13297","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Ma'bad, the nephew of Humayd ibn Abd Allah al-Himyari, narrated to us, he said: I went with Humayd to Anas ibn Malik, and he said: When the people pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - or: when we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he would dictate to us to say: As much as you are able. My father said: He is not Humayd al-Tawil."
"13298","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, observed qunut for a month, supplicating against Ri'l and Dhakwan and Banu Lihyan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"13299","Yunus narrated to us: Hazm narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out one day for one of his excursions with some of his Companions, and they set out walking, and the prayer came and the people found no water with which to perform ablution, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah we find nothing with which to perform ablution. And he saw dislike in the faces of his Companions, so a man of the people went and brought a small cup with a little water, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it and performed ablution from it, then spread his four fingers over the cup, then said: Come, perform ablution. So the people performed ablution until they fulfilled what they wanted. He said: It was asked: How many did they reach? He said: Seventy or thereabouts."
"13300","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas saying: Hardly a night comes upon me except that I see in it my dear friend, peace be upon him. And Anas would say that while his eyes shed tears."
"13301","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Talhah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a body and said: How long shall we draw from these wells, if only we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he supplicated Allah for us and caused springs to gush for us from these mountains. So they came in a body to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he saw them he said: Welcome, you have indeed been brought to us by a need. They said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You will not ask me for anything today except that you will be given it, and I will not ask Allah for anything except that He gives it to me. So some of them turned to others and said: You want this world, so seek the Hereafter. So they said in a body: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah for us that He forgive us. So he said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and our children from others than us. He said: And the children of the Ansar. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and our freedmen. He said: And the freedmen of the Ansar. He said: And my mother narrated to me from Umm al-Hakam bint al-Nu'man ibn Suhban that she heard Anas reporting from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of this, except that he added in it: and the daughters-in-law of the Ansar."
"13302","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came in to us, I and my mother and my maternal aunt being present, and said: Stand, I shall pray with you at other than a prayer time. He said: A man from the people said to Thabit: Where did he place Anas in relation to himself. He said: On his right, and the women behind him."
"13303","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning al-Umari, narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Yahya saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A son of Abu Talhah died, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over him. Abu Talhah stood behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Umm Sulaym behind Abu Talhah, as if they were the comb of a rooster, and he gestured with his hand."
"13304","Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman informed me, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us, I being with him, and Umm Sulaym, and he placed me on his right and Umm Sulaym behind us."
"13305","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Asr while the sun was white and alive, then one going would go to al-Awali and come to it while the sun was still elevated."
"13306","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Patience is at the first shock. I think he said: The first. Abu Qatan doubted."
"13307","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against some tribes of the Arabs, then he left it."
"13308","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit and Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When wine was forbidden, he said: I was on that day serving it to them, serving eleven men. They commanded me and I poured it out, and the people poured out their vessels with what was in them until the streets were almost blocked by its smell. Anas said: And their wine on that day was only unripe dates and ripe dates mixed together. He said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: There was with me an orphan's property, so I bought wine with it, will you permit me to sell it and return to the orphan his property. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah fought the Jews, fat was forbidden to them so they sold it and consumed its price. And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not permit him to sell wine."
"13309","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to buy and sell, and there was weakness in his mind, meaning his intellect. His family came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, place such-and-such under interdiction, for he buys and sells and there is weakness in his mind. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him and forbade him from selling. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I cannot be patient without selling. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you will not give up selling, then say: Here it is, and no deceit, no, no deceit."
"13310","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ru'asi narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, he said: I asked Anas about turning away after prayer, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turning away to his right."
"13311","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Za'idah informed us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you saw what I have seen you would weep much and laugh little. They said: What have you seen, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I have seen Paradise and Hell. And he forbade them to precede him when he led them in bowing and prostration, and to leave before his leaving the prayer. He said: I see you from in front of me and from behind me."
"13312","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Abi Dharrah al-Ansari narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no long-lived one who lives long in Islam to forty years except that Allah averts from him three kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty years Allah makes the reckoning easy for him. When he reaches sixty Allah grants him turning to Him with what He loves. When he reaches seventy years Allah loves him and the people of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty Allah accepts his good deeds and overlooks his evil deeds. When he reaches ninety Allah forgives him what came before of his sin and what comes after, and he is named the prisoner of Allah on His earth, and he intercedes for the people of his household."
"13313","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Qunut for a month."
"13314","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every Prophet has an invocation with which he invoked for his nation, and I have stored my invocation as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"13315","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: He said, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: But you practice continuous fasting. He said: I am not like one of you, I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"13316","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Sa'd, informed us, he said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to invite him, having made food for him. I came, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, being with the people. He said: He looked at me and I felt shy, and I said: Answer Abu Talhah. He said to the people: Stand. Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, I only made something for you. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, touched it and invoked blessing in it, then said: Admit a group of my Companions, ten. He said: Eat. They ate until they were full and went out. He said: Admit ten. They ate until they were full. He kept admitting ten and sending out ten until none of them remained except he entered and ate until full. Then he prepared it, and it was as it had been when they ate from it."
"13317","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that a Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Death be upon you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And upon you. Do you know what he said. He said: Death be upon you. They said: Shall we not kill him. He said: No, but when the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."
"13318","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating that a Jewess put poison in meat then brought it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate from it. He said: She put poison in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill her. He said: No. He said: I kept recognizing that in the uvula of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13319","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded me to have you recite the Quran, or to recite the Quran to you. He said: Has Allah named me to you. He said: Yes. He said: Have I been mentioned with the Lord of the worlds. He said: Yes. He said: Then his eyes shed tears."
"13320","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would raise his middle finger and the one next to it, then say: I was only sent, I and the Hour, like these two. He did not give one of them precedence over the other."
"13321","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The disbeliever will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: What do you think, if you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it. He will say: Yes, my Lord. He said: Then it will be said: You were asked for easier than that. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Those who disbelieved and died while they were disbelievers, never will be accepted from one of them the earth full of gold though he ransom himself with it."
"13322","Amir narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: And my father said: Anas narrated to us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw Paradise and Hell depicted in this wall, and I have never seen, like today, good and evil, or as he said."
"13323","Arim narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Anas that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every Prophet has asked a request, or he said: Every Prophet has an invocation with which he invoked, and I have stored my invocation as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection, or as he said."
"13324","Arim and Affan narrated to us, they said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man had assigned for him, Affan said: assigning for him from his property some palm trees, or as Allah willed, until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered. He said: Then he began to return after that. My family commanded me to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him for what his family had given him, or some of it. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had given him Umm Ayman, or as Allah willed. He said: So I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came and put the garment on my neck and began to say: No, by Allah besides Whom there is no god, he shall not give them to you when he has given them to me, or as he said. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For you is such-and-such, and she says: No, by Allah. He said: And he says: For you is such-and-such. He said: Until he gave her. I thought he said ten times the like of them, or he said: near ten times the like of them, or as he said."
"13325","Arim narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating that Anas said: It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If only you came to Abdullah ibn Ubayy. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out to him riding a donkey, the Muslims setting out walking, it being marshy land. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him, he said: Keep away from me, the smell of your donkey has harmed me. A man from the Ansar said: By Allah, the smell of the donkey of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is sweeter in smell than you. He said: A man of his people became angry on behalf of Abdullah. He said: The companions of each one of them became angry. He said: There was between them striking with palm stalks and with hands and sandals. He said: It reached us that there was revealed concerning them: If two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them."
"13326","Arim narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, confided a secret to me, and I have not told it to anyone after him. Umm Sulaym asked me about it, and I did not tell her of it."
"13327","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between the two sides of my Basin is as between Sanaa and Madinah, or what is between Madinah and Amman. Hisham doubted."
"13328","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to describe for sciatica the rump of an Arab black ram, neither large nor small, divided into three parts, melted, a part drunk each day."
"13329","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, consulted the people on the day of Badr. Abu Bakr spoke and he turned away from him. Then Umar spoke and he turned away from him. The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, is it us you mean. Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you commanded us to plunge it into the sea we would plunge it, and if you commanded us to strike its flanks to Bark al-Ghimad we would do it. Your affair, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called upon his Companions and set out until he camped at Badr. The water-carrying camels of Quraysh came, among them a black boy belonging to Banu al-Hajjaj. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seized him and asked him about Abu Sufyan and his companions. He said: As for Abu Sufyan, I have no knowledge of him, but these are Quraysh and Abu Jahl and Umayyah ibn Khalaf who have come. They would beat him, and when they beat him he would say: Yes, this is Abu Sufyan. When they left him and asked him about Abu Sufyan, he said: I have no knowledge of Abu Sufyan, but these are Quraysh who have come. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, then finished and said: You beat him when he tells you the truth and leave him when he lies to you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke with his hand and placed it and said: This is the place of death of so-and-so tomorrow, and this is the place of death of so-and-so tomorrow, if Allah, Exalted is He, wills. They met and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, defeated them. By Allah, not one man of them deviated from the place of the two hands of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to them after three days when they had stunk and said: O Abu Jahl, O Utbah, O Shaybah, O Umayyah, you have found what your Lord promised you true, for I have found what my Lord promised me true. Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you call them after three days when they have stunk. He said: You do not hear what I say better than they do, except that they cannot answer. He commanded concerning them and they were dragged by their legs and thrown into the well of Badr."
"13330","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when news of the approach of Abu Sufyan reached him, he said: Abu Bakr spoke and he turned away from him. Then Umar spoke and he turned away. Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: Is it us you mean, O Messenger of Allah. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you commanded us to plunge it into the seas we would plunge it, and if you commanded us to strike its flanks to Bark al-Ghimad. He said: Affan mentioned the like of the hadith of Abd al-Samad up to his saying: Not one of them deviated from the place of the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13331","Abu Ja'far al-Mada'ini, and he is Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Before the Dajjal there are deceitful years in which the truthful will be belied and the liar will be believed, the trustworthy will be deemed treacherous and the treacherous will be trusted, and al-Ruwaybidah will speak in them. It was said: What is al-Ruwaybidah. He said: The despicable sinner speaking concerning the affair of the public."
"13332","Abu Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like gravy. Abbad said: meaning broth."
"13333","Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and I heard it myself from Uthman, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Before the Hour there are deceitful years. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"13334","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Talhah, from Anas, he said: I passed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a road of the roads of Madinah, and he saw a dome of unbaked brick. He said: Whose is this. I said: So-and-so's. He said: Indeed every building is a loss upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection except what was in a mosque or in the building of a mosque. Aswad doubted, or, or. Then he passed and did not meet it. He said: What happened to the dome. I said: What you said reached its owner, so he demolished it. He said: Then he said: May Allah have mercy on him."
"13335","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Bilal ibn Abi Musa, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Al-Hajjaj wanted to place his son over the judiciary of Basra. He said: Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever seeks judgeship and seeks help for it will be entrusted to it, and whoever does not seek it and does not seek help for it, Allah will send down an angel to guide him."
"13336","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to show them a sign. He said: So he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."
"13337","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, often supplicating with these supplications: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt and the dominance of men."
"13338","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"13339","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Layth informed us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Bakr, from Abdullah ibn Muslim, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about al-Kawthar and said: A river my Lord has given me, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, in it are birds like the necks of camels. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, those are soft birds. He said: Their eaters are softer than them, O Umar."
"13340","Fazarah ibn Umar and Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Musahiq, from Amir ibn Abdullah, from Anas, he said: I have not seen an imam more resembling in prayer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than your imam here, meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. He said: And Umar did not prolong the recitation."
"13341","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: I heard Thumamah ibn Anas mentioning that Anas, when he spoke, spoke thrice, and mentioning that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he spoke, spoke thrice, and would seek permission thrice. Abu Sa'id said: And he narrated to us after that with this hadith that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would seek permission thrice."
"13342","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Wardan narrated to me that Anas ibn Malik, the Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked a man of his Companions and said: O so-and-so, have you married. He said: No, and I have nothing with which to marry. He said: Is there not with you: Say, He is Allah, One. He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Quran. He said: Is there not with you: Say, O disbelievers. He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Quran. He said: Is there not with you: When the earth is shaken. He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Quran. He said: Is there not with you: When the help of Allah comes. He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Quran. He said: Is there not with you the Verse of the Kursi: Allah, there is no god but He. He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Quran. He said: Marry, marry, marry, three times."
"13343","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would enter the house of Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed when she was not in it. He said: He came one day and slept on her bed, and she was told: This is the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sleeping in your house on your bed. He said: She came, he having sweated, his sweat having pooled on a piece of leather on the bed. He said: She opened her chest. He said: She began to dry that sweat and squeeze it into her bottles. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, started and said: What are you doing, O Umm Sulaym. She said: O Messenger of Allah, we hope for its blessing for our boys. He said: You are right."
"13344","Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The birds of Paradise are like the Bukht camels, grazing in the trees of Paradise. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, those are soft birds. He said: Their eaters are softer than them. He said it three times. I hope you will be among those who eat from it, O Abu Bakr."
"13345","Sayyar narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When it was the day in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Madinah, everything of Madinah was lit up. When it was the day in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, everything of Madinah was darkened. No sooner had we finished his burial than we felt our hearts estranged."
"13346","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Abi Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Four will come out of the Fire and be presented to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and He will command them to the Fire. One of them will turn and say: My Lord, I had hoped, if You brought me out of it, that You would not return me to it. He will say: Then We shall not return you to it."
"13347","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fruit to be sold until it ripens, and grapes until they blacken, and grain until it hardens."
"13348","Hasan narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the king of Dhu Yazan gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a suit which he had taken for thirty-three camels, or thirty-three she-camels."
"13349","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a man but cannot do as he does. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A person is with whom he loves. Anas said: I never saw the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rejoice at anything at all, except Islam be, as they rejoiced at this saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Anas said: We love the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, though we cannot do as he does. If we are with him, that suffices us."
"13350","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, he said: Anas said: I never smelled anything, ambergris or musk or anything at all, sweeter than the smell of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I never touched anything, brocade or silk, softer to touch than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Thabit said: I said: O Abu Hamzah, is it as if you are looking at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and as if you are listening to his tone. He said: Yes, by Allah, I hope to meet him on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant. He said: I served him ten years in Madinah, a boy, not all my conduct being as my master would like it to be. He never said to me in them: Uff, nor said to me: Why did you do this, and why did you not do this."
"13351","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was running among the boys, they saying: Muhammad has come. I would run and see nothing. Then they would say: Muhammad has come. I would run and see nothing. He said: Until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and his companion Abu Bakr. We were in some lava tracts of Madinah. Then a man of the people of Madinah sent us to announce them to the Ansar. About five hundred of the Ansar met them until they reached them. The Ansar said: Proceed safe and obeyed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came forward, his companion among them. The people of Madinah came out until even the maidens were above the houses watching him, saying: Which of them is he, which of them is he. He said: We never saw a sight resembling it on that day. Anas ibn Malik said: I saw him on the day he entered among us and on the day he died, and I never saw two days resembling them."
"13352","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abi al-Tayyah and Qatadah and Hamzah al-Dabbi, that they heard Anas ibn Malik saying from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I was sent, I and the Hour, thus. And he pointed with the index finger and the middle finger. Qatadah would say: Like the superiority of one of them over the other."
"13353","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book greet us, how shall we respond to them. He said: Say: And upon you."
"13354","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah Abi Iyas, he said: I said to him: Did you hear Anas narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin: The son of the sister of a people is among them or from themselves. He said: Yes."
"13355","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to the Ansar: Is there among you anyone from other than you. They said: A son of a sister of ours. He said: The son of the sister of a people is among them or from themselves."
"13356","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: I said: Did you hear it yourself. He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, mentioning Allah's name and magnifying Him. I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot on their sides."
"13357","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was among us a man of Banu al-Najjar who had read al-Baqarah and Al Imran and used to write for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He went fleeing until he joined the People of the Book. He said: They raised him and said: This one used to write for Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They were impressed with him. It was not long before Allah broke his neck among them. They dug for him and buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out upon its surface. Then they returned and dug for him and buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out upon its surface. Then they returned and dug for him and buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out upon its surface. So they left him exposed."
"13358","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A son of Abu Talhah had a small bird he played with. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Umayr, what has the little bird done."
"13359","Hashim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas ibn Malik described to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then stood praying with us. He bowed then stood straight until some of us thought he had forgotten. Then he prostrated then sat straight until some of us thought he had forgotten. Then he sat straight."
"13360","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to write to the Romans, it was said to him: Your letter will not be read until it is sealed. So he took a ring of silver and engraved it, or engraved: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. He said: It is as if I am looking at its whiteness in his hand."
"13361","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to write to the Romans. Then he mentioned its meaning."
"13362","Hashim and Husayn narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, from Musa ibn Anas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not reach of gray hair what he would dye, but Abu Bakr would dye his head and beard with henna and katam. Hashim said: until they redden their hair."
"13363","Hashim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Anas ibn Malik that he saw in the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a ring of silver one day. The people made rings of silver and wore them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."
"13364","Ishaq ibn Isa and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that he told him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray Asr while the sun was elevated and alive. One going would go to al-Awali and come to al-Awali while the sun was elevated."
"13365","Ishaq narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever lies upon me, I think he said: deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"13366","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: Anas said: You need not marvel at the deed of a man until you know what he is sealed with. A man may do for a period of his time or a span of his life an evil deed, if he died upon it he would die upon evil, then turn to a righteous deed and be sealed with it. And a servant may do for a period of his time or a span of his life a righteous deed, if he died upon it he would die upon good, then turn to an evil deed and be sealed with it. He said: Humayd raised it in isnad once, then refrained from it."
"13367","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come to you a people softer of hearts toward Islam than you. He said: The Ash'aris came, among them Abu Musa al-Ash'ari. When they neared Madinah they began to chant and began to say: Tomorrow we meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party. He said: They were the first to introduce handshaking."
"13368","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, Hafsah bint Sirin narrated to me, she said: Anas ibn Malik said to me: Of what did Yahya ibn Abi Amrah die. I said: Of the plague. Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"13369","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik came to al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik, and he asked him: What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah mentioning the Hour. He said: I heard the Messenger saying: You and the Hour are like these two."
"13370","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Qatadah wrote to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and they would open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, not mentioning: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, at the beginning of the recitation nor at its end."
"13371","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik and Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, and Abu al-Mughirah had narrated it to us from Anas from Abi Sa'id, then it returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There will be in my nation dissension and division, a people who speak well and do evil, reciting the Quran not passing their throats. One of you will belittle his prayer compared to their prayer and his fasting compared to their fasting. They will pass through religion as the arrow passes through the game. They will not return until they return to the bowstring. They are the worst of creation. Blessed is he who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah yet are nothing of it. Whoever fights them is worthier of Allah than they are. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark. He said: Shaving."
"13372","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the mosque wearing a thick-made Najrani cloak. A Bedouin came from behind him and pulled the edge of his cloak with a severe pull until the make affected the side of the neck of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: O Muhammad, give us from the wealth of Allah that is with you. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to him and smiled, then said: Order a gift for him."
"13373","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Rashid ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When my Lord took me up, I passed by a people with nails of copper scratching their faces and chests. I said: Who are these, O Jibril. He said: These are those who eat the flesh of people and attack their honors."
"13374","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Jabir, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: War is deceit."
"13375","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Jabir, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: War is deceit."
"13376","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah al-Ansari, that he heard Humayd ibn Ubayd, freedman of Banu al-Mu'alla, saying: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said to Jibril, peace be upon him: Why have I not seen Mika'il laughing at all. He said: Mika'il has not laughed since the Fire was created."
"13377","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal will come out from the Jewry of Asbahan, with him seventy thousand of the Jews, upon them crowns."
"13378","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Makkah in the year of the Conquest with a helmet on his head."
"13379","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, he said: Anas ibn Malik came to Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan while he was in Damascus. He said: He entered upon him, and Mu'awiyah said to him: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with no one between you and him in it. He said: Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Faith is Yemeni, thus toward Lakhm and Judham."
"13380","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the Ansar: You will find severe preference given over you, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger, for I am at the Basin. They said: We shall be patient. Abdullah said: If Allah wills, and he concealed it, and I thought it is not in the hadith."
"13381","Ali ibn Ishaq and al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. When they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, face our qiblah, eat our slaughtered meat, and pray our prayer, their blood and wealth have become forbidden to us except by its right. For them is what is for the Muslims, and upon them is what is upon them."
"13382","Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Abdullah ibn Umayr, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I was at the calloused knees of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he said: Here I am for Hajj and Umrah together. That was in the Farewell Hajj."
"13383","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht al-Makki narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears this saying of mine and conveys it. Many a carrier of understanding in whom there is no understanding, and many a carrier of understanding to one more understanding than him. Three over which the heart of a Muslim does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sincere advice to those in authority, and adherence to the community of the Muslims, for their supplication encompasses behind them."
"13384","Issam ibn Khalid and Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: We prayed Zuhr with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, then we went to Anas ibn Malik asking about him, he being ill. When we entered upon him we greeted. He said: Have you prayed. We said: Yes. He said: O slave girl, bring me ablution water. I never prayed behind an imam after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more resembling in prayer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than this imam of yours. Issam said in his hadith: Thus my father said. Zayd said: He does not mention in that Abu Bakr nor Umar. He said: Zayd said: Umar would complete the bowing and prostration and lighten the sitting and standing."
"13385","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, he said: Muhammad, meaning al-Zuhri, Anas ibn Malik informed me that he saw on the finger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a ring of silver one day. Then the people made rings of silver and wore them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."
"13386","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In my Basin are pitchers numbering the stars of the sky."
"13387","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to desert his brother for more than three nights. They meet, this one turning away and this one turning away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"13388","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would go around his wives with one washing."
"13389","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abi Iqal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Asqalan is one of the two brides. Seventy thousand will be raised from it on the Day of Resurrection with no reckoning upon them, and fifty thousand martyrs will be raised from it as delegations to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. In it are rows of martyrs with their heads cut off in their hands, their jugular veins spurting blood, saying: Our Lord, give us what You promised us upon Your messengers, indeed You do not break the promise. He will say: My servants have spoken the truth, wash them in the river of al-Baydah. They will come out of it pure and white, roaming in Paradise wherever they wish."
"13390","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"13391","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a ring of silver whose stone was Abyssinian."
"13392","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man invited the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he went and I went with him. He said: Broth was brought in which was pumpkin. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began to eat that pumpkin, liking it. When I saw that I began to offer it to him and not eat any of it myself. Anas said: I have kept loving it ever since. Sulayman said: I narrated this hadith to Sulayman al-Taymi, and he said: We never came to Anas ibn Malik at all in pumpkin season except we found it in his food."
"13393","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ammi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The wine addict will not enter the wall of al-Quds, nor one disobedient to his parents, nor one who reminds of his giving."
"13394","Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas, he said: Zaynab bint Jahsh would boast over the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, married me from heaven. Bread and meat were served on that day. The people were sitting as they were in the house. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and went out, staying as long as Allah willed him to stay, then returned, the people sitting as they were. That distressed him and was recognized in his face. The verse of the Hijab was revealed."
"13395","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his house, and a man asked him: When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It is coming, what have you prepared for it. He said: By Allah, I have not prepared much deed except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love, and for you is what you counted."
"13396","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he preached on Friday, would lean his back against a piece of wood. When the people became many, he said: Build for me a pulpit, wanting to make them hear. They built for him two steps. He moved from the wood to the pulpit. He said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that he heard the wood moaning the moaning of a parent. He said: It kept moaning until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended from the pulpit, walked to it, and embraced it, and it quieted."
"13397","Hashim narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: No perfume was ever offered to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he rejected it."
"13398","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt and the dominance of men."
"13399","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would enter the house of Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed when she was not in her house. He said: She was told one day: This is the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sleeping on your bed. She said: I came, that being in summer, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, having sweated until his sweat pooled on a piece of leather on the bed. I began to dry that sweat and squeeze it into a bottle. He started while I was doing that and said: What are you doing, O Umm Sulaym. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we hope for its blessing for our boys. He said: You are right."
"13400","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us in the house of Umm Sulaym on a mat changed by age, sprinkled with some water, and he prostrated on it."
"13401","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, I only know it from Anas, that a Bedouin came to the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and urinated in it, so the people stood up to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Leave him, do not interrupt him, then he called for water and poured it over it."
"13402","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I do not spare any effort to pray with you as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray with us. He said: Anas used to do something I do not see you doing; when he raised his head from bowing he would stand upright until one would say he has forgotten, and when he raised his head from prostration he would sit until one would say he has forgotten."
"13403","Yunus and Surayj said: Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a trace of yellow perfume on Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and said: What is this? He said: I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold. He said: May Allah bless you, give a wedding feast even with a sheep."
"13404","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: Nothing, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those you love. Anas said: We were never as happy with anything after Islam as we were happy with the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: You are with those you love. He said: So I love the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, and I hope to be with them because of my love for them even though I do not do deeds like theirs."
"13405","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, that Anas was asked: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dye his hair? He said: The gray hair of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not reach such that he would dye it; if I wished I could count the white hairs that were in his beard, but Abu Bakr used to dye with henna and katam, and Umar used to dye with henna."
"13406","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I served the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for ten years; by Allah, he never said to me Uff, nor did he say about anything I did: Why did you do so and so, nor: Why did you not do so and so."
"13407","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I never touched with my hands any brocade or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor did I smell any scent that was sweeter than the scent of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13408","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said, and I only know it from Anas, that a Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he fell ill, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to visit him while he was dying, and invited him to Islam. The boy looked at his father who was by his head, and his father said to him: Obey Abu al-Qasim. So he accepted Islam, then he died. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out from him saying: Praise be to Allah who saved him through me from the Fire."
"13409","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I was serving drink to the people on the day wine was forbidden. Abu Talhah had gathered some of his companions, then a man came and said: Wine has indeed been forbidden. Abu Talhah said to me: Go out and see. He said: So I went out and looked, and I heard a caller calling: Wine has indeed been forbidden. He said: So I informed him. He said: Go and spill it. He said: So I came and spilled it. Some of them said: Suhayl Ibn Bayda was killed while it was in his stomach. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, to the end of the verse. Their wine on that day was fadikh made from unripe and ripe dates."
"13410","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey, and with him was a black boy called Anjashah who was chanting to the camels. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Woe to you, O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels, be gentle with the glass vessels. And in the hadith of Abu Qilabah, meaning women."
"13411","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, give a wedding feast for any of his wives as he gave for Zaynab bint Jahsh; he gave a feast with a sheep, or he slaughtered a sheep."
"13412","Yunus and Muammal said: Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, Salm al-Alawi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: When the verse of the veil was revealed, I went to enter as I used to enter, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Stay behind, O my son."
"13413","Yunus narrated to us, Habib ibn Hajar narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I went out from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heading to my family, and I passed by boys playing, and their play pleased me, so I stood watching the boys. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me while I was standing with the boys, and greeted the boys, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand for him. I returned and went out to my family after the time I used to return to them, and my mother said to me: What kept you today, O my son? I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand for him. She said: What errand, O my son? I said: O mother, it is a secret. She said: O my son, keep the secret of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Thabit said: I said: O Abu Hamzah, do you remember that errand today? He said: Yes, by Allah, and I do not mention it; if I were to tell anyone among the people about it, I would have told you, O Thabit."
"13414","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was of a bright color; his sweat was like pearls; when he walked he leaned forward. I never touched brocade or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor did I smell the scent of musk or amber sweeter in scent than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Hasan said: miskah and anbarah."
"13415","Yunus and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed a prayer, and Surayj said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us one day a prayer, then he ascended the pulpit and spoke about prayer and bowing, then he said: I indeed see you from behind me as I see you from in front of me."
"13416","Yunus and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali ibn Usamah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We attended the burial of a daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting at the grave, and I saw his eyes shedding tears. Then he said: Is there any man among you who did not commit sin last night? Surayj said, meaning a sin. Abu Talhah said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then go down. So he went down into her grave."
"13417","Yunus and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Anas ibn Malik informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Asr in the time it takes one going to Banu Harithah ibn al-Harith to go and return before sunset, and in the time it takes a man to slaughter a camel and divide it before sunset, and he used to pray Friday when the sun declined, and when he went out to Makkah he prayed Zuhr at al-Shajarah two rakahs."
"13418","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd and Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is Kafir, which every believer will read, literate and illiterate."
"13419","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the Hour will be established, and with him was a boy of the Ansar called Muhammad. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: If this boy lives, perhaps old age will not overtake him before the Hour comes."
"13420","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the establishment of the Hour, and the prayer was established. When he finished his prayer he said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? The man said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And what have you prepared for it, for it is coming? He said: I have not prepared for it much deeds, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are with those you love. He said: The Muslims were never happier with anything after Islam than they were with that."
"13421","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves the people but has not reached their deeds. The Messenger of Allah said: A person is with those he loves. Hasan said: their deeds. He said: A person is with those he loves. Thabit said: When Anas narrated this hadith he would say: O Allah, we love You and we love Your Messenger."
"13422","Yunus said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who plants a plant or sows a crop, and a bird or a human or an animal eats from it, except that it is charity for him."
"13423","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"13424","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah fashioned Adam in Paradise, He left him as long as He willed to leave him, and Iblis began to go around him and look at what he was. When he saw him hollow, he knew that he was created as a creation that would not control itself."
"13425","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that a man said: O Prophet of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered on his face on the Day of Resurrection? The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The One who made him walk on his legs is able to make him walk on his face in the Fire."
"13426","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said, and Anas ibn Malik narrated that a man among the people said: O Prophet of Allah, does he not intend Madinah? He said: Yes, he works toward it, but he will find the angels at its passes and gates guarding it from the Dajjal."
"13427","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said, and Anas ibn Malik narrated that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between his eyes is written K F R, spelled out disbelief, saying Kafir, which every believer will read, illiterate and literate."
"13428","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said, and Anas ibn Malik narrated that a cloak of sundus was gifted to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he used to forbid silk, so the people wondered at it. He said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than this."
"13429","Sulayman ibn Hayyan, who is Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to turn to us with his face before saying takbir, and say: Keep close together and straighten the rows, for I see you from behind my back."
"13430","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly; what he catches he prays, and what he misses he completes."
"13431","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that when Ruqayyah, may Allah be pleased with her, died, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man who has had intercourse with his wife should enter the grave. So Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, did not enter the grave."
"13432","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raid at the time of Fajr prayer, listening for the adhan; if he heard the adhan he refrained, otherwise he raided. One day he listened and heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon the fitrah. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: You have come out of the Fire."
"13433","Yunus and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: The king of the Romans gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a mustaqah of sundus, and he wore it, and I can still see its sleeves shaking from their length. The people began to say: O Messenger of Allah, has this been sent down to you from heaven? He said: What amazes you about it? By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a handkerchief of the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is better than it. Then he sent it to Jafar ibn Abi Talib, who wore it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I did not give it to you to wear. He said: What should I do with it? He said: Send it to your brother the Negus."
"13434","Yunus narrated to us, Hazm narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves that his life be extended and his provision increased, let him be dutiful to his parents and maintain his kinship."
"13435","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, and he mentioned something of exegesis. He said, His saying: On the Day We say to Hell: Are you filled? He said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hell will continue to say: Is there more, until the Lord of Might places His foot in it, and it says: Enough, enough, by Your might, and parts of it will be drawn together."
"13436","Yunus narrated to us, Uthman ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to me, he said: We came to Anas ibn Malik on a Thursday, and he called for his table and invited them to lunch; some of the people ate and some refrained. Then they came to him on a Monday and he did the same, calling for his table and inviting them to lunch; some ate and some refrained. Anas ibn Malik said to them: Perhaps you are Monday fasters, perhaps you are Thursday fasters. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast and not break his fast until we would say there is no intention in the soul of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to break fast this year, then he would break fast and not fast until we would say there is no intention in him to fast this year. The most beloved fasting to him was in Shaban."
"13437","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come until people boast about mosques."
"13438","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that some people mentioned the Hawd in the presence of Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, and he denied it and said: What is the Hawd? That reached Anas ibn Malik, and he said: Of course, by Allah, I will surely do it. So he came to him and said: You mentioned the Hawd. Ubayd Allah said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention it? He said: Yes, saying more than such and such times: What is between its two ends is like what is between Aylah and Makkah, or between Sanaa and Makkah, and its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky. Hasan said: And its vessels are indeed more numerous than the number of the stars of the sky."
"13439","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Hawd was mentioned in the presence of Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: By Allah, I will surely do so and so to him."
"13440","Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three qualities, whoever has them finds through them the sweetness of faith: one to whom Allah and His Messenger are more beloved than anything else, a man who loves a man and loves him only for Allah, and a man to whom being thrown into the Fire is more beloved than returning to being a Jew or a Christian. Hasan said: or a Christian."
"13441","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If Allah intends good for someone, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is His employing him? He said: He enables him to do a righteous deed before his death."
"13442","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to the house of Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed while Umm Sulaym was not in her house. She would come and find him sleeping, and he, upon him prayer and peace, when he slept would sweat profusely, so she would take his sweat with cotton in a bottle and put it in her perfume."
"13443","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a tree was on the path of the people and harmed them, so a man came and removed it from the path of the people. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw him turning about in its shade in Paradise."
"13444","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Sallam meaning Ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Abu Zilal, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: A servant in Hell will call for a thousand years: O Hannan, O Mannan. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to Jibril, upon him peace: Go and bring Me this servant of Mine. Jibril will go and find the people of the Fire fallen weeping, and return to his Lord and inform Him. He will say: Bring him to Me, for he is in such and such place. So he brings him and makes him stand before his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He says to him: O My servant, how did you find your place and your resting place? He says: O Lord, the worst place and the worst resting place. He says: Return My servant. He says: O Lord, I never hoped, when You brought me out of it, that You would return me to it. He says: Leave My servant."
"13445","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd informed us, from Simak meaning Ibn Atiyyah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, in a raised report, he said: When supper is present and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"13446","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik narrating from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with a helmet on his head. When he removed it, a man came to him and said: Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kabah. He said: Kill him."
"13447","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"13448","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, or woe unto you."
"13449","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The son of the sister of a people is from them, or from themselves."
"13450","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek refuge from incapacity, cowardice, miserliness, laziness, old age, and the punishment of the grave."
"13451","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, Imran al-Basri al-Qasir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I served the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for ten years; he never ordered me with a command and I was slow about it or neglected it and he blamed me; if anyone of his household blamed me, he would say: Leave him, for if it had been decreed, or he said: if it had been ordained to be, it would have been."
"13452","Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to me, from Imran al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for ten years, and he mentioned the like of it."
"13453","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ayyub meaning al-Qassab Abu al-Ala, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Let none of you spread his forearms in prayer like a dog."
"13454","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When I was taken by night, I passed by men whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are preachers from your nation who command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book; will they not understand?"
"13455","Abu Salamah Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Majishun narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited us in our house, and we milked for him a domestic ewe of ours and mixed its milk with water from the house. On the right of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was a Bedouin man, and behind the man was Umar ibn al-Khattab, and on the left of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank until, when he removed the cup from his mouth, or was about to remove it, Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, give Abu Bakr. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave the cup to the Bedouin, then he said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"13456","Ishaq ibn Mansur meaning al-Saluli narrated to us, Umarah meaning Ibn ZadHan narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take a midday rest at Umm Sulaym, and he was among the most sweating of people. She made for him a leather mat, and he used to rest on it, and she drew a line between his feet, and she used to dry the sweat and take it. He said: What is this, O Umm Sulaym? She said: Your sweat, O Messenger of Allah, I put it in my perfume. So he supplicated for her with a good supplication."
"13457","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Umm Sulaym to look at a slave girl, and said: Smell her sides of the mouth and look at her ankles."
"13458","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata Abu Nasr al-Ijli al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he informed them from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: While I was walking in Paradise, a river was shown to me whose banks were domes of hollow pearls. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, gave you. He said: I struck with my hands in it, and its clay was strong-smelling musk, and its pebbles were pearls."
"13459","My father said, and Abd al-Wahhab said from his book, I read: The angel who was with me said: Do you know what this is? This is al-Kawthar which your Lord gave you. So he struck with his hands toward its ground and brought out musk from its clay."
"13460","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never went out on the day of breaking fast without eating dates. Anas used to eat three before going out; if he wanted to increase he ate five, and if he wanted to increase he ate an odd number."
"13461","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Talhah brought two mudds of barley, and ordered that food be made from it. Then he said to me: O Anas, go, bring the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and invite him, and you know what we have. I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while his companions were with him, and said: Abu Talhah invites you to his food. He stood and said to the people: Stand. They stood, and I walked in front of him until I entered to Abu Talhah and informed him. He said: You have disgraced us. I said: I could not refuse the command of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reached the door, he said to them: Sit, and ten entered with him. When he entered, food was brought, he took and ate, and the people ate with him until they were full. Then he said to them: Stand, and let ten enter in your place, until all the people entered and ate. I said: How many were they? He said: They were a little over eighty. And there remained for the household enough to satisfy them."
"13462","Ali informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: Bilal established the prayer, then a man intercepted the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and kept him standing until some of the people dozed, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and prayed with the people."
"13463","Ali narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, traveled in Ramadan; he mounted his riding camel and called for water in his hand, then sent it forth, and when it stood upright he drank while the people looked at him."
"13464","Ali narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A hare started up, and the people followed it, and I was among the first to reach it, so I caught it and brought it to Abu Talhah. He ordered that it be slaughtered, then it was cooked. Then he took its hind part and said: Take it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I brought it to him and said: Abu Talhah has sent to you the hind part of this hare. He accepted it from me."
"13465","Ali narrated to us, from Hanzalah al-Sadusi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated in qunut for a month after bowing in the dawn prayer."
"13466","Abd Allah ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Abu Nasr, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave me the kunyah by a vegetable I used to gather."
"13467","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai and Shubah together, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"13468","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, Abu al-Abyad narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Asr with us while the sun was white and high, then I would return to my people in the outskirts of Madinah and find them sitting, and I would say to them: Stand and pray, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has prayed."
"13469","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with barley bread and rancid melted fat."
"13470","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that Anas ibn Malik informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Makkah with a helmet on his head. It was said to him: Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kabah. He said: Kill him."
"13471","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade squatting on the heels and spreading the feet in prayer. Abd Allah said: My father had abandoned this hadith."
"13472","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No prophet before me was sent except that he warned his people of the lying Dajjal, so beware of him; he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed."
"13473","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete the front row, then the one after it; whatever deficiency there is, let it be in the last row."
"13474","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, and he mentioned a hadith, and Qatadah said, he used to say: Complete the front row, then the one after it; if there is deficiency, let it be in the last row."
"13475","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: Four men, all of the Ansar, collected the Quran in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh ibn Jabal, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu Zayd."
"13476","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said to Ubayy: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded me to recite the Quran to you. He said: Did Allah name me to you? He said: Yes. So he began to weep."
"13477","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a group from Ukl and Uraynah came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were people of livestock and were not people of countryside; Madinah did not suit us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered for them some camels and a herdsman, and ordered them to go out with them and drink from their milk and urine. They went until, when they were in the area of al-Harrah, they killed the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drove off the camels, and disbelieved after their Islam. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought; he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the area of al-Harrah until they died in that state. Qatadah said: It was mentioned to us that this verse was revealed about them."
"13478","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment while sitting."
"13479","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Sharik, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was lighter than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor more complete; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would hear the crying of a child and lighten the prayer for fear that his mother would be distressed."
"13480","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When a servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the striking of their sandals; two angels come to him and say to him: What did you say about this man, meaning Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. It is said to him: Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise. So he sees both of them."
"13481","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered a palm grove of Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound and was startled. He said: Who are the occupants of these graves? They said: O Prophet of Allah, people who died in the pre-Islamic period. He said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of the Fire and the trial of the Dajjal. They said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This nation is tested in its graves; when the believer is placed in his grave, an angel comes to him and asks him: What did you worship? If Allah guided him, he says: I used to worship Allah. It is said to him: What did you say about this man? He says: He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. He is not asked about anything after that. He is taken to a house he had in the Fire, and it is said: This was your house in the Fire, but Allah protected you and had mercy on you, and replaced it for you with a house in Paradise. He says: Let me go to give glad tidings to my family. It is said to him: Stay. And when the disbeliever is placed in his grave, an angel comes to him and says to him: What did you say about this man? He says: I used to say what the people said. So he strikes him with a hammer of iron between his ears, and he cries out with a cry heard by all creation except the two heavy ones."
"13482","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"13483","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"13484","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Phlegm in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"13485","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, for he is conversing with his Lord, Mighty and Majestic; rather let him spit to his left or under his foot."
"13486","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Said was asked about the Night of Decree, so he informed us from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek it in the last ten, on the ninth and seventh and fifth."
"13487","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete bowing and prostration; by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"13488","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, and Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, while the bier of Sad was placed: The Throne of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, shook for it."
"13489","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Ukaydir of Dumah gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a silk cloak, and that was before the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade silk. He wore it, and the people wondered at it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sad in Paradise are better than this."
"13490","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, or woe unto you, ride it. Hisham doubted."
"13491","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Hell will continue to have cast into it, and it says: Is there more, until the Lord of Might places His foot in it, and parts of it draw together, and it says: Enough, enough, by Your might and Your generosity. And there will remain space in Paradise until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, creates for it a creation and settles them in the remaining space of Paradise."
"13492","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"13493","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions, and said: Death be upon you. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know what this one said? They said: He greeted, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, but he said such and such. Then he said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back to him, and he said: Did you say death be upon you? He said: Yes. The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said at that: When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: And upon you, meaning, and upon you what you said."
"13494","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Zayd ibn Thabit took the pre-dawn meal together; when they finished their meal, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood for prayer. We said to Anas: How long was it between their finishing their meal and their entering prayer? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"13495","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Said was asked about continuous fasting, so he informed us from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not practice continuous fasting. It was said to him: You practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like any of you; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"13496","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: There were seventy young men of the Ansar called the Reciters. They would be in the mosque; in the evening they would withdraw to an area of Madinah and study and pray; their families thought they were in the mosque, and the people of the mosque thought they were with their families, until when dawn approached they would fetch sweet water and gather firewood, and bring it and lean it against the chamber of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent them all, and they were struck on the day of Bir Maunah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against their killers for fifteen days in the dawn prayer."
"13497","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, who said: There were youths in Madinah called the Reciters, and he mentioned its meaning."
"13498","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, who said: When Anas narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and finished it, he would say: Or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"13499","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail informed us, Humayd informed me, from Anas, who said: There were youths of the Ansar called the Reciters, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Abu Bakr."
"13500","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was close together, and the prayer of Abu Bakr was moderate, and Umar extended the recitation in the dawn prayer."
"13501","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas who said: There was a small boy on the road, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by with some of his Companions. When the boy's mother saw the people, she feared her son would be trampled, so she hastened and carried him, saying: My son, my son. He said: The people said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman would not throw her son into the Fire. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, nor will Allah cast His beloved into the Fire."
"13502","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas said: An old man being supported between his two sons was brought past. He said: He said: What is the matter with this one? They said: He vowed, O Messenger of Allah, to walk. He said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need of this one's tormenting himself. So he ordered him to ride, and he rode."
"13503","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while I was among boys, and he greeted us, then he took my hands and sent me on an errand, and he sat in the shade of a wall, or in a wall, until I returned to him. When I came to Umm Sulaym, she said: What kept you? He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand. She said: And what is it? I said: It is a secret. She said: Keep the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I never told it to anyone after that at all."
"13504","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came to Madinah, and the people of Madinah had two days in which they played during the Jahiliyyah, and he said: I have come to you, and you have two days in which you play. Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has replaced them for you with better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Nahr."
"13505","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Abu Musa al-Ashari came asking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount, and found him busy, so he said: By Allah, I will not carry you. When he turned away, he called him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not carry me. He said: And I swear I shall surely carry you."
"13506","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas who said: Anas was asked about the punishment of the grave and about the Dajjal, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, cowardice, miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave."
"13507","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that he was asked about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his voluntary fasting. He said: He would fast part of the month until we would say he does not intend to break any of it, and he would break fast until we would say he does not intend to fast any of it. And we never wished to see him at night praying but we saw him, nor to see him sleeping but we saw him."
"13508","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: al-Zuhri mentioned, from Uways ibn Abi Uways, from Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Ramadan has come; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, in it the gates of the Fire are closed, and in it the devils are chained."
"13509","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muslim, the nephew of Ibn Shihab, narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about al-Kawthar, and he said: It is a river Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave me in Paradise; its soil is musk, its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; birds with necks like the necks of camels come to it. He said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, they are soft. He said: Those who eat them are softer than them."
"13510","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih. Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would love to have a third valley, and nothing fills his mouth but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13511","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Who will look into what Abu Jahl did? He said: So Abd Allah ibn Masud went and found the two sons of Afra had struck him until he fell down. He said: So Ibn Masud took him by his beard and said: Are you Abu Jahl? Are you the misguided old man? He said: So Abu Jahl said: Is there above a man you killed, or he said: his people killed."
"13512","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih. Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about the Hijab; Ubayy ibn Kab used to ask me about it. Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke as a bridegroom with Zaynab bint Jahsh. He said: And he had married her in Madinah, and he invited the people to food after midmorning. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, and men sat with him after the people had risen, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and walked, and I walked with him until he reached the chamber of Aisha. Then he thought they had left, so he returned, and I returned with him. He said: And there they were, sitting in their place. So he returned, and I returned with him a second time, until he reached the chamber of Aisha, and he returned, and I returned with him, and there they had stood. So he drew the curtain between me and him, and the Hijab was revealed."
"13513","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Salih. Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent revelation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continuously before his death, until he died when revelation was most abundant on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died."
"13514","Yaqub narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me that his brother informed that Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari informed him that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is al-Kawthar? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a river Allah gave me in Paradise, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; in it are birds whose necks are like the necks of camels. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: They are soft, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who eat them are softer than them."
"13515","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came upon a village at night for a raid, would not attack until morning; if he heard a call to prayer, he held back, and if he did not hear a call to prayer, he attacked."
"13516","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada al-Ansari, then al-Zafari, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari who said: I heard him say: No one hastened the Asr prayer more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Even the two men of the Ansar whose houses were farthest from the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Lubaba ibn Abd al-Mundhir, the brother of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and Abu Abs ibn Jabr, the brother of Banu Haritha, the house of Abu Lubaba in Quba, or the house of Abu Abs ibn Jabr among Banu Haritha, yet they would pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to their people, and they had not yet prayed it, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it so early."
"13517","Yaqub narrated to us: My father informed us, from Ibn Ishaq: Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, he said: I left the Zuhr prayer, I and Umar, when Hisham ibn Ismail led the people in it while he was over Madinah, going to Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha to visit him in an illness of his, and we sat only briefly; we asked about him only standing. He said: Then we left and entered upon Anas ibn Malik in his house, which was beside the house of Abu Talha. He said: When we sat, the slave girl came to him and said: The prayer, O Abu Hamza. He said: We said: Which prayer, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: Asr. He said: So we said: We only just prayed Zuhr now. He said: So he said: You left the prayer until you forgot it, or he said: you were made to forget it, until you left it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two, and he stretched his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"13518","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from his brother Abd Allah ibn Muslim, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about al-Kawthar, and he mentioned it, except that he said: Those who eat them are softer than them."
"13519","Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muslim, the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about al-Kawthar, like the hadith of al-Zuhri exactly."
"13520","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad said: Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Jabir narrated to me, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came upon a village at night for a raid, would not attack until morning; if he did not hear a call to prayer, he attacked."
"13521","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Jabir narrated to me, from Abd al-Warith, the freedman of Anas ibn Malik, and Amr ibn Amir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade visiting graves, and sacrificial meats after three days, and nabidh in the gourd, the hollowed trunk, the green jar, and the pitched vessel. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after that: Indeed I had forbidden you three things, then it occurred to me about them. I forbade you visiting graves, then it occurred to me that they soften the heart, bring tears to the eye, and remind of the Hereafter, so visit them, but do not say foul speech. And I forbade you sacrificial meats, that you eat them beyond three nights; then it occurred to me that people honor their guest with them and store for their absent one, so keep whatever you wish. And I forbade you nabidh in these vessels, so drink in whatever you wish, but do not drink an intoxicant. Whoever wishes ties his waterskin upon sin."
"13522","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir al-Taymi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr in his mosque in Madinah, four rakahs, then he led us in Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, two rakahs, safe and not fearing, in the Farewell Hajj."
"13523","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We used to pray Jumuah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return to the midday rest and nap."
"13524","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer was called in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there had been something between the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept holding some of them back from others. He said: So Abu Bakr came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, throw dust in their mouths and go out to the prayer."
"13525","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer comes and supper is served, begin with supper."
"13526","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Qaba of Ukaydir when it was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Muslims began touching it with their hands and marveling at it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you marvel at this? By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than this."
"13527","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Abu Ubayda, meaning Abd al-Mumin ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sadusi, narrated to us: Akhshan al-Sadusi narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, or he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you sinned until your sins filled what is between heaven and earth, then you sought forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He would forgive you. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, or: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you did not sin, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would bring a people who sin, then they seek forgiveness from Allah, and He forgives them."
"13528","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, from Anas who said: When the verse of the Hijab was revealed, I came to enter as I used to enter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Behind you, O my son."
"13529","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will descend, when he descends, in the outskirts of Madinah, and it will shake three tremors, and every disbeliever and hypocrite will go out to him."
"13530","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatada. Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be seen therein jugs of gold and silver, as many as the stars of the sky, or more than the number of the stars of the sky."
"13531","Hasan narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was once invited to barley bread and rancid melted fat. He said: And I heard him many times saying: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there did not remain with the family of Muhammad a sa of grain nor a sa of dates, while he had nine wives that day. And he had pawned a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madinah, taking food from him, and he found nothing with which to redeem it."
"13532","Hasan narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13533","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is sacred, from here to here. Whoever innovates an event in it, or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Its trees are not to be cut. And al-Hasan said: Except for camel fodder."
"13534","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qibla of the mosque and scraped it off with his hand."
"13535","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Rabia, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, afflicts with an affliction in his body but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to the angel: Write for him his righteous deeds he used to do. If Allah heals him, He washes him and purifies him, and if He takes him, He forgives him and has mercy on him."
"13536","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Bayan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman and invited men to food."
"13537","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Umara, meaning Ibn Zadham, narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the muadhdhin, or Bilal, would call the iqamah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter, and a man would meet him with a need, and he would stand with him until most of them nodded their heads."
"13538","Hasan narrated to us: Umara narrated to us: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ascended a high place on earth, would say: O Allah, to You is loftiness above all loftiness, and to You is praise in every state."
"13539","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us: Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would visit nine wives in the forenoon."
"13540","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyya and made her freedom her dowry."
"13541","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, that a man looked into one of the rooms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood toward him and took a broad arrowhead, or arrowheads, Ubayd Allah doubted, then he walked toward him, trying to catch him unawares, and it is as if I look at him about to stab him with it."
"13542","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah wanted the barber to shave his head, Abu Talha took the hair of one side of his head in his hand, and he took his hair and brought it to Umm Sulaym. He said: So Umm Sulaym would mix it into her perfume."
"13543","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the house of Umm Sulaym, and Umm Sulaym and Umm Haram were behind us, and I know only that he said: He placed me on his right."
"13544","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas and al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out leaning on Usama ibn Zayd, wearing a cotton garment with its ends crossed, and he led them in prayer."
"13545","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your dwelling? And he will say: O my Lord, the best dwelling. And He will say to him: Ask and wish. And he will say: I ask and wish only that You return me to the world and I be killed, because of what he saw of the virtue of martyrdom. He said: Then a man of the people of the Fire will be brought, and He will say to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your dwelling? And he will say: O my Lord, the worst dwelling. And He will say: Would you ransom yourself from it with the earth full of gold? And he will say: Yes, O my Lord. And He will say: You lied; I asked you for less than that, and you did not do it. So he will be returned to the Fire."
"13546","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out, with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar, and some Bedouins, until he entered our house. A sheep was milked for him, and water from our well was poured over it, I think he said, and he drank, with Abu Bakr on his left, Umar facing him, and a Bedouin on his right. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr. So he gave it to the Bedouin. He said: Those on the right. He said: So Anas said to us: It is Sunnah, it is Sunnah."
"13547","Al-Hashimi narrated to us: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar ibn Hazm narrated to us that he heard Anas ibn Malik, and he mentioned its meaning."
"13548","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a footstep. I said: What is this footstep? It was said: This is al-Rumaysa bint Milhan, the mother of Anas ibn Malik."
"13549","Hasan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw, on the night I was taken up, men whose lips were cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are preachers from your ummah who command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book; do they not understand?"
"13550","Hasan and Affan, in meaning, said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fashioned Adam, He left him as long as Allah willed to leave him. So Iblis began circling him, and when he saw him hollow, he knew he was a creation that cannot control itself."
"13551","Abu Said narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar, meaning al-Makhzumi, narrated to us, and Ismail ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"13552","Abu Salama al-Khuzai narrated to us: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the Conquest wearing a helmet. He said: So it was said to him: Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kaba. He said: Kill him."
"13553","Abu Salama al-Khuzai narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed us, he said: Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Malik describe the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with whatever description he wished to describe him. He said: Then I heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of medium build among the people, neither short nor conspicuously tall, radiant, neither dark nor white nor pale, with wavy hair, neither lank nor very curly. He was sent at the head of forty; he stayed in Mecca ten years and in Madinah ten years, and he died at the head of sixty years, with not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"13554","Abu Salama narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of my ummah will ride the surface of the sea, or the surface of this sea; they are kings on thrones, or like kings on thrones."
"13555","Abu Salama narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, that he asked Anas ibn Malik, while they were going to Arafah: How did you do on this day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: One of us would utter the talbiyah, and it was not denied him, and the takbir-maker would utter takbir, and it was not denied him."
"13556","Abu Salama narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: I witnessed him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day he entered Madinah upon us, and I never saw a day brighter than it nor better than it. And I witnessed him on the day he died, and I never saw a day uglier than it."
"13557","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us: Sharik, meaning Ibn Abi Namir, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I never prayed behind any imam with a lighter prayer than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor more complete. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear the crying of the child behind him and lighten, fearing hardship for his mother."
"13558","Abu Said narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry, grief, miserliness, cowardice, laziness, old age, the burden of debt, and the domination of the enemy."
"13559","Abu Said narrated to us: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar, and when he saw Uhud, he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When he overlooked Madinah, he said: O Allah, I declare sacred what is between its two lava plains, as Ibrahim declared Mecca sacred."
"13560","Abu Said narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not come to his family at night by surprise; he would enter in the morning or in the evening."
"13561","Abu Said narrated to us: Zaida narrated to us: al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: And what did you see, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire. And he urged them to prayer, and forbade them to precede him in bowing and prostration, and forbade them to leave before he leaves the prayer, and he said: I see you from in front of me and from behind me."
"13562","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Something about the headman of the Ansar reached Musab ibn al-Zubayr, and he intended him. So Anas ibn Malik entered upon him and said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Treat the Ansar well, or he said: kindly; accept from their good-doer and overlook their offender. So Musab threw himself off his couch and stuck his cheek to the carpet and said: The command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is upon the head and the eyes. So he left him."
"13563","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O our master and son of our master, and O our best and son of our best. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, say your saying, and let not Satan allure you. I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah and the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I do not love that you raise me above what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, raised me."
"13564","Al-Ashyab narrated it to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, and Affan: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us: And let not Satan make you venture."
"13565","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Jews entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: al-Sam upon you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Sam upon you. So Aisha said: al-Sam upon you, O brothers of apes and pigs, and the curse of Allah and His wrath. He said: O Aisha, gently. She said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said? He said: Did you not hear what I returned to them? O Aisha, gentleness never entered anything but it beautified it, and it was never removed from anything but it disgraced it."
"13566","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, he heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitrah. He said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one has come out of the Fire."
"13567","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by a date, and nothing would prevent him from taking it and eating it except fear that it might be from the dates of charity."
"13568","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): one of them said: I will not marry, and one of them said: I will pray and not sleep, and one of them said: I will fast and not break. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with people who said so-and-so? But I fast and break, and I pray and sleep, and I marry women. So whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not from me."
"13569","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a man sitting. The man said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I love this one for Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you tell him that? He said: No. He said: Stand and tell him; love will be firm between you. So he stood toward him and told him. He said: I love you for Allah, or he said: I love you for the sake of Allah. So the man said: May He for Whose sake you loved me love you."
"13570","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying for rain, stretching his hands with their backs toward the sky."
"13571","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would meet a man and say: O so-and-so, how are you? And he would say: Well, I praise Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to him: May Allah keep you well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him one day and said: How are you, O so-and-so? And he said: Well, if I am grateful. So he fell silent toward him. He said: O Prophet of Allah, you used to ask me and say: May Allah keep you well, but today you fell silent toward me. So he said to him: I used to ask you and you would say: Well, I praise Allah, so I would say: May Allah keep you well. But today you said: If I am grateful, so you doubted, and I fell silent toward you."
"13572","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us: Ayyub informed us, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas who said: I am the most knowledgeable of people, or among the most knowledgeable of people, about the verse of the Hijab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he slaughtered a sheep and invited his Companions. So they ate and sat talking, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began going out and coming in while they were sitting. Then he would go out and stay as long as Allah willed, and return while they were sitting, with Zaynab sitting in a corner of the house. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was too shy before them to say anything to them. Then was revealed: O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permission is given to you for food, without waiting for its preparation, but when you are invited, enter, the verses, to the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Then ask them from behind a hijab. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a veil at once, and it was set up."
"13573","Muammal narrated to us: Umara ibn Zadham narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the angel of rain asked his Lord to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and He permitted him. So he said to Umm Salama: Guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us. He said: And al-Husayn came to enter, and she prevented him, so he jumped and entered, and began sitting on the back of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on his shoulder and on his back. He said: So the angel said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you love him? He said: Yes. He said: Indeed your ummah will kill him, and if you wish, I will show you the place where he will be killed. So he struck with his hand and brought red clay. So Umm Salama took it and wrapped it in her veil. He said: Thabit said: We were told it is Karbala."
"13574","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, and Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is sacred, from here to here. Whoever innovates an event in it, or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him any exchange nor requital. Hammad said: And Humayd added therein: No weapon is carried in it for fighting."
"13575","Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim dies and four of the people of the houses of his nearest neighbors testify for him but He said: I have accepted your knowledge of him, and I have forgiven him what you do not know."
"13576","Muammal narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl ibn Maysara al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has people among mankind; and the people of the Quran are the people of Allah and His elite."
"13577","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, that a man looked into one of the rooms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood toward him with a broad arrowhead, or arrowheads, and it is as if I look at him sneaking to stab him."
"13578","Ishaq narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O possessor of two ears."
"13579","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyya and made her freedom her dowry."
"13580","Surayj narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with him, and Umm Sulaym and Umm Haram were behind us, on a mat."
"13581","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Umm Sulaym said: Go to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: If you see fit to lunch with us, do so. He said: So I came to him and told him. So he said: And who is with me? I said: Yes. So he said: Arise. He said: So I came and entered upon Umm Sulaym, dismayed at who came with the Messenger of Allah. He said: So Umm Sulaym said: What did you do, O Anas? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered after that. He said: Have you any ghee? She said: Yes; I had a skin with some ghee in it. He said: So bring it. She said: So I brought it to him, and he opened its tie, then he said: In the name of Allah; O Allah, magnify the blessing in it. He said: So he said: Turn it over. So I turned it over, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) squeezed it while naming Allah. He said: So I took the bottom of a pot, and some eighty men ate from it, and a remainder remained in it. So he gave it to Umm Sulaym and said: Eat, and feed your neighbors."
"13582","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a journey, from one of his journeys, and when Uhud appeared to us, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When he overlooked Madinah, he said: O Allah, I declare sacred what is between its two lava plains, as Ibrahim declared Mecca sacred. O Allah, bless their mudd and their sa."
"13583","Surayj narrated to us: Suhayl, the brother of Ibn Abi Hazm al-Qutai, narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite this verse: And you do not will except that Allah wills; He is worthy of piety and worthy of forgiveness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am worthy to be feared, that another god be set up with Me; and whoever fears to set up another god with Me, he is worthy for Me to forgive him."
"13584","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the suhur, for in the suhur is blessing."
"13585","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it."
"13586","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13587","And with this isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim plants a plant or sows a crop, and a bird, a man, or a beast eats from it, but it is charity for him."
"13588","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim, and he mentioned the like of it."
"13589","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No Muslim plants a plant or sows a crop, and a beast or a man eats from it, but it is charity for him."
"13590","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, and he mentioned a man, from al-Hasan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted the people about the captives on the day of Badr, and he said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has enabled you over them. He said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, strike their necks. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and said: O people, indeed Allah has enabled you over them, and they were but your brothers yesterday. He said: So Umar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, strike their necks. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and said the like of that to the people. So Abu Bakr stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to pardon them and accept ransom from them. He said: So what was on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of grief went away. He said: So he pardoned them and accepted ransom from them. He said: And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, you would have been touched for what you took, to the end of the verse."
"13591","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in a garment wrapped around himself."
"13592","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani who said: We were told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in his illness in which he died, sitting, wrapped in a garment, I think he said: a cloak. Then he called Usama and leaned his back against his chest, then he said: O Usama, lift me to you. Yazid said: It was in the book with me from Anas, but he did not say from Anas, so he denied it and affirmed Thabit."
"13593","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, and Khalid, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes and the prayer has been established, let him walk calmly, let him pray what he catches, and let him make up what he missed."
"13594","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us: Abu Salama, the food merchant, narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Yazid, and he is not Jabir al-Jufi, informed me, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Hulayq the Christian, to send him garments on credit. So I came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to you, to send him garments on credit. He said: And what is credit, and when is credit? By Allah, Muhammad has neither herd nor shepherd. So I returned and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he saw me, he said: The enemy of Allah lied. I am the best to be dealt with on credit. For one of you to wear a garment of patched rags is better for him than to take by his trust, or in his trust, what he does not have. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting."
"13595","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh ibn Jabal: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him enters Paradise."
"13596","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The site of the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) belonged to Banu al-Najjar, and in it were tilth, palms, and graves of the polytheists. So he said: O Banu al-Najjar, name a price for it for me. They said: We seek no price for it but with Allah. He said: So he cut the palms, leveled the tilth, and exhumed the graves of the polytheists. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), before he built the mosque, would pray wherever the prayer caught him, and in sheepfolds. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say, while they carried rocks for building the mosque: O Allah, indeed good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"13597","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatada narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be held on the Day of Resurrection and will grieve over that, and they will say: If we sought intercession with our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, He would relieve us from our place. So they will come to Adam and say: You are our father; Allah created you with His hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things, so intercede for us with your Lord. He said: So he will say: I am not there for you, and he will mention his sin he committed, his eating from the tree, though he was forbidden it. But go to Nuh, the first prophet Allah sent to the people of the earth. He said: So they will come to Nuh, and he will say: I am not there for you, and he will mention his sin, his asking Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without knowledge. But go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. So they will come to Ibrahim, and he will say: I am not there for you, and he will mention his sin he committed, the three lies he told: his saying: I am sick, his saying: Rather, the biggest of them did this, and he came upon a mighty tyrant with his wife and said: Tell him I am your brother, for I will tell him you are my sister. But go to Musa, a servant to whom Allah spoke directly and gave the Torah. He said: So they will come to Musa, and he will say: I am not there for you, and he will mention his sin he committed, his killing the man. But go to Isa, the servant of Allah and His messenger, His word and His spirit. So they will come to Isa, and he will say: I am not there for you, but go to Muhammad, the servant of Allah and His messenger, forgiven for what went before of his sin and what comes after. He said: So they will come to me, and I will ask permission of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, in His house, and I will be permitted to Him. When I see Him, I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak, you will be heard, intercede, you will be granted intercession, ask, you will be given. He said: So I will raise my head and praise my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with praise and glorification He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out and enter them into Paradise. And I heard him say: So I will bring them out of the Fire and enter them into Paradise. Then I will ask permission of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, a second time, and I will be permitted to Him. When I see Him, I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak, you will be heard, intercede, you will be granted intercession, ask, you will be given. He said: So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praise and glorification He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out and enter them into Paradise. Hammam said: And I also heard him say: So I will bring them out of the Fire and enter them into Paradise. He said: Then I will ask permission of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, a third time, and when I see my Lord, I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: Rise, Muhammad; speak, you will be heard, intercede, you will be granted intercession, ask, you will be given. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praise and glorification He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out and enter them into Paradise. Hammam said: And I heard him say: So I will bring them out of the Fire and enter them into Paradise. So none will remain in the Fire but those held by the Quran, that is, those upon whom eternity is due. Then Qatada recited: It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station. He said: It is the praised station which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, promised His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13598","Affan narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed me, from Abu Qilaba, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah."
"13599","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had hair reaching his shoulders."
"13600","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada who said: I asked Anas: How many Umrahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform? He said: Four: his Umrah in which the polytheists barred him, in Dhu al-Qada, his Umrah also in the next year, in Dhu al-Qada, his Umrah when he divided the spoils of Hunayn, from al-Jirana, in Dhu al-Qada, and his Umrah with his Hajj."
"13601","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the minbar and said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to give us rain. He said: So he prayed for rain, and we did not see any patch of cloud in the sky. He said: Then we were rained upon, and it would hardly stop. Then when Friday came, that man, or another man, stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to remove it from us. He said: So he supplicated, and I began looking at the clouds dispersing right and left, and not a drop of rain fell from its midst."
"13602","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When one of you spits, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"13603","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sandals with two straps."
"13604","Affan narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us. My father said: And I had seen Khalaf ibn Khalifah, and a man had said to him: O Abu Ahmad, did Muharib ibn Dithar narrate to you? My father said: But I did not understand his speech, for he had grown old, so I left him. Hafs narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command marriage and strongly forbid celibacy, and he said: Marry loving, fertile women, for I will outnumber the prophets through you on the Day of Resurrection."
"13605","Affan narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us: Hafs, the nephew of Anas, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a circle, and a man was standing praying. When he bowed and prostrated and recited the tashahhud, then he said in his supplication: O Allah, I ask You, for to You belongs praise, there is no god but You, the Bestower, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, O Living, O Sustainer, indeed I ask You. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know by what he supplicated to Allah? He said: So they said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he has supplicated to Allah by His Greatest Name, by which when He is called upon He answers, and when He is asked thereby He gives."
"13606","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what have you seen? He said: I have seen Paradise and Hell."
"13607","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they praised it with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is due. Then another funeral was passed by him, and they spoke ill of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is due. Then he said: You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"13608","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that a man used to write for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he dictated to him All-Hearing, he would say: I wrote All-Hearing, All-Seeing. He said: Leave it. And when he dictated to him All-Knowing, All-Wise, he wrote All-Knowing, Forbearing. Hammad said: something like that. He said: And he had read al-Baqarah and Aal Imran, and whoever read them had read much of the Quran. Then he went and became Christian, and said: I used to write for Muhammad whatever I wished, and he would say: Leave it. Then he died and was buried, and the earth cast him out two or three times. Abu Talhah said: And I saw him cast out upon the earth."
"13609","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Abu Sufyan and Uyaynah and al-Aqra and Suhayl ibn Amr among the last on the day of Hunayn. The Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, our swords drip from their blood while they go off with the spoils. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them in a dome of his until it overflowed. He said: Is there anyone among you from other than you? They said: No, except the son of our sister. He said: The son of the sister of a people is from them. Then he said: Did you say such and such? They said: Yes. He said: You are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment. Are you not pleased that the people go with sheep and camels while you go with the Messenger of Allah to your homes? They said: Yes indeed. He said: The Ansar are my belly and my chest. If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take their mountain pass. And were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. And Hammad said: He gave one hundred camels, naming each one of these."
"13610","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah on the day of Khaybar, and my foot touched the foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We came to them when the sun rose, and they had brought out their livestock and come out with their axes and baskets and carriers. They said: Muhammad and the army. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greater, Khaybar is ruined. Indeed when we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, defeated them. He said: And a beautiful slave girl fell in the share of Dihyah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought her for seven heads, then handed her to Umm Sulaym to groom and prepare her, and she was Safiyyah bint Huyayy. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his wedding feast of dates and dried yogurt and clarified butter. He said: The ground was cleared into small pits. He said: Leather mats were brought and laid out, then dried yogurt and dates and clarified butter were brought, and the people ate their fill. He said: The people said: We do not know whether he has married her or taken her as a concubine. They said: If he veils her, she is his wife, and if he does not veil her, she is a concubine. When he wanted to mount, he veiled her until she sat on the back of the camel, so they knew he had married her. When they drew near Madinah, he urged on and we urged on. He said: The she-camel al-Adba stumbled. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell off and she fell off. He stood and covered her. The women looked down and said: May Allah keep the Jewess away. I said: O Abu Hamzah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummate? He said: Yes indeed, by Allah, he did consummate. And I witnessed the wedding feast of Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he fed the people bread and meat to their fill. He used to send me to invite the people. When he finished, he stood and I followed him, and two men lingered, enjoying conversation, and did not go out. He began passing by his wives, greeting each one: Peace be upon you, O people of the house, how are you this morning? They said: Well, O Messenger of Allah, how did you find your wife? He said: Well. When he returned, and I returned with him, and he reached the door, there were the two men still enjoying conversation. When they saw him return, they stood and went out. He said: By Allah, I do not know whether I informed him or revelation came down to him that they had gone out. He returned, and I returned with him. When he placed his foot on the threshold of the door, he drew the curtain between me and him, and Allah sent down the verses of the veil: Do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permission is given to you for a meal, without waiting for its preparation, until he finished them."
"13611","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that when a Jewish woman menstruated, the Jews would expel her from the house, and would not eat with her nor mingle with her. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about that, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: And they ask you about menstruation, say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation, until he finished the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to do everything except intercourse. The Jews said: This man does not want to leave anything of our affair except that he opposes us in it. Abbad ibn Bishr and Usayd ibn Hudayr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews said such and such, so should we not have intercourse with them? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed until we thought he was angry with them. They left him, and a gift of milk for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them, so he sent after them and gave them to drink. We thought he was not angry with them."
"13612","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that he said: I never prayed behind a man whose prayer was briefer than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet well-proportioned. The prayer of Abu Bakr was well-proportioned. When it was Umar, he lengthened the Fajr prayer. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he would stand until we said he had forgotten. And he would sit between the two prostrations until we said he had forgotten."
"13613","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that he recited this verse: Indeed We have given you al-Kawthar. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given al-Kawthar, and behold it is a river flowing, not dug in a trench. Its banks are domes of pearls. I struck my hand to its soil, and behold it was strong-smelling musk, and its pebbles were pearls."
"13614","Affan narrated to us: Hammad informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that has befallen him, but let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me."
"13615","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say often: O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"13616","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: He said: I gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink from this cup of mine all kinds of drink: honey and water and milk."
"13617","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. He said: It was said: But you fast continuously. He said: I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"13618","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drunk, so he commanded nearly twenty men, and they lashed him, each man two lashes, with palm stalks and sandals."
"13619","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out before the sun declined, he would delay Zuhr until the time of Asr, then alight and combine them. If the sun had declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr, then mount."
"13620","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Qurrah, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that Allah expand his provision for him and extend his lifespan, let him maintain his kinship ties."
"13621","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Qurrah and Uqayl and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would seek another valley with it. Nothing will fill his mouth but dust. Then Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13622","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Uqayl informed me, and he mentioned it."
"13623","Qutaybah narrated to us: He said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change gray hair, and do not go near black dye."
"13624","Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb said: And Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas narrated to him: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He delays Asr until when it is between the two horns of Satan, or upon the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks it like the pecking of a rooster. He does not remember Allah in it except a little."
"13625","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Day of Resurrection will be long for the people, so some of them will say to others: Let us go to Adam, the father of mankind, so he may intercede for us with our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and judge between us. They will come to Adam and say: O Adam, you whom Allah created with His Hand and settled in His Paradise, intercede for us with your Lord and judge between us. He will say: I am not for that, but go to Nuh, the chief of the prophets. They will come to him and say: O Nuh, intercede for us with your Lord and judge between us. He will say: I am not for that, but go to Ibrahim, the intimate friend of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. They will come to him and say: O Ibrahim, intercede for us with your Lord and judge between us. He will say: I am not for that, but go to Musa, whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose with His messages and His speech. He said: They will come to him and say: O Musa, intercede for us with your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and judge between us. He will say: I am not for that, but go to Isa, the Spirit of Allah and His Word. They will come to Isa and say: O Isa, intercede for us with your Lord and judge between us. He will say: I am not for that, but go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he is the Seal of the Prophets, and today he is present and he has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed. Isa will say: Have you seen, if there were goods in a vessel sealed over, could what is in the vessel be reached until the seal is broken? They will say: No. He said: Indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the Seal of the Prophets. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then they will come to me and say: O Muhammad, intercede for us with your Lord and judge between us. He said: I will say: Yes. I will come to the gate of Paradise and take hold of the ring of the gate and seek opening. It will be said: Who are you? I will say: Muhammad. It will be opened for me. I will fall prostrate, praising my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with praises no one before me praised Him with, nor will anyone after me praise Him with. He will say: Raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. He will say: O my Lord, my nation, my nation. It will be said: Bring out whoever had in his heart the weight of a grain of barley of faith. He said: I will bring them out. Then I will fall prostrate, praising Him with praises no one before me praised Him with, nor will anyone after me praise Him with. It will be said to me: Raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will say: O my Lord, my nation, my nation. It will be said: Bring out whoever had in his heart the weight of a grain of wheat of faith. He said: I will bring them out. He said: Then I will fall prostrate and say the like of that. It will be said: Whoever had in his heart the weight of a speck of faith. He said: I will bring them out."
"13626","Affan narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that Umm Ayman wept when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died. It was said to her: Are you weeping? She said: By Allah, I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would die, but I weep only for the revelation cut off from us from heaven."
"13627","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: Three things, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be dearer to him than all else, and that he love a slave only for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and that being cast into the Fire be dearer to him than being returned to disbelief."
"13628","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit and Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken by night, I passed by Musa while he was standing praying in his grave at the red dune."
"13629","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Umm Haram, and we brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: Return this to its vessel and this to its skin, for I am fasting. He said: Then he stood and prayed two voluntary rakahs with us. He placed Umm Haram and Umm Sulaym behind us, and placed me at his right, as Thabit thought. He said: He prayed a voluntary prayer with us on a mat. When he finished his prayer, Umm Sulaym said: I have a little one, your little servant Anas, supplicate to Allah for him. He left no good of the good of this world nor the Hereafter that day except that he supplicated for me with it. Then he said: O Allah, increase his wealth and children and bless him in them. Anas said: My daughter informed me that I buried from my loins over ninety, and no man among the Ansar has more wealth than me. Then Anas said: O Thabit, I own neither gold nor silver except my ring."
"13630","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: Prayer came, and the neighbors of the mosque stood to perform ablution, while between seventy and eighty remained, and their homes were far. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a basin with water in it, not full. He placed his fingers in it and began pouring over them, saying: Perform ablution, until they all performed ablution, while there remained in the basin about what had been in it, and they were about seventy to a hundred."
"13631","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man said: O Muhammad, O our best and son of our best, O our master and son of our master. He said: Say your saying, and let not Satan, or the devils, draw you on. He said one of the two words: I am Muhammad ibn Abdillah and His Messenger. I am Muhammad, the slave of Allah and His Messenger. I do not like that you raise me above the station Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave me."
"13632","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a woman of his wives used to wash from one vessel."
"13633","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Shuayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have urged you much regarding the tooth-stick."
"13634","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in one eye, with kafir written between his eyes. He said: Then he spelled it: kaf, fa, ra. Every Muslim reads it."
"13635","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: When supper is laid and prayer comes, begin with supper."
"13636","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, then left it."
"13637","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing."
"13638","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be clothed with a garment of Fire is Iblis. He will place it on his eyebrow and drag it, saying: O my ruin. His offspring will be behind him, saying: O our ruin, until he stands over the Fire and says: O my ruin, and they say: O our ruin. It will be said: Do not call today for one ruin, but call for many ruins."
"13639","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us: He said, I think it is from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah is harder upon the polytheists than a troop."
"13640","Affan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment is to mid-calf. When he saw how hard that was upon the Muslims, he said: To the ankles. There is no good in what is below that."
"13641","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not let his hair pass the lobes of his ears."
"13642","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: He said: Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr informed me: He said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of hypocrisy is hatred of the Ansar, and the sign of faith is love of the Ansar."
"13643","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When Makkah was conquered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the spoils among Quraysh. The Ansar said: This is indeed strange. Our swords drip from their blood, yet our spoils are returned to them. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them and said: What is this I have heard about you? They said: It is what reached you, and they would not lie. He said: Are you not pleased that the people return with this world while you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses? If the people took a valley or a mountain pass and the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar or the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"13644","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah: He said: I heard Anas say: The Ansar said on the day of the conquest of Makkah, when he gave to Quraysh: Indeed this is strange. And he mentioned its meaning."
"13645","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: He said: We used to come to Anas while his baker was standing. He said: One day he said: Eat. By Allah, I do not know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever saw a thin loaf nor a roasted sheep until he joined his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"13646","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes while in prayer, let him leave and sleep."
"13647","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection."
"13648","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens, and selling grapes until they blacken, and selling grain until it hardens."
"13649","Affan narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: He said: I never heard him narrate a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that he said: Or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"13650","Affan narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three things: visiting graves, and the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, and these fermented drinks in vessels. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after that: Indeed I had forbidden you three things. I forbade you visiting graves, then it occurred to me that they soften hearts and bring tears to eyes, so visit them, but do not say foul speech. I forbade you the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, then it occurred to me that people seek their condiments and gift to their guests and store for their absent ones, so eat and keep whatever you wish. I forbade you these vessels, so drink in whatever you wish. Whoever wishes, as if his skin is upon sin."
"13651","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abu Rabiah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a Bedouin who was ill with fever and said: An expiation and a purification. The Bedouin said: Rather a fever boiling over an old man, hurrying him to the graves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and left him."
"13652","Affan narrated to us: al-Mubarak narrated to us: He said: Ismail ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari informed me: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever refuse perfume presented to him."
"13653","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked drinking while standing. He said: I said: And eating? He said: It is worse and more wicked."
"13654","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and a vessel of water was brought, and he drank in Ramadan while the people looked on."
"13655","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abu Musa said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for mounts, and he swore he would not mount us, then he mounted us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not mount us, then you mounted us. He said: And I swear by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, I will indeed mount you."
"13656","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Humayd and Shuayb ibn al-Habhab informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, and your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed. Between his eyes are kaf, fa, ra. Every believer reads it, reader and non-reader. Hammad also said: Written between his eyes."
"13657","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd informed us: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when they had two days in which they played. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are these two days? They said: We used to play in them in the pre-Islamic age. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has replaced them for you with better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice."
"13658","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: No person was dearer to them to see than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they saw him, they would not stand, knowing his dislike for that."
"13659","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Humayd informed us, from Anas: that he said: When the people of Yemen came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you. They are softer in hearts than you. Anas said: And they were the first to bring handshaking."
"13660","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: He said: Qatadah informed us: He said: I said to Anas: Which clothing was dearest, or most pleasing, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Hibarah."
"13661","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the king of Rome gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a long outer garment of brocade, and it is as if I look at its sleeves dangling from their length. The people began touching it and saying: Has this been sent down to you, O Messenger of Allah, from heaven? He said: And what pleases you about it? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, a handkerchief of the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is better than this. Then he sent it to Jafar. He said: Jafar wore it, then came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not send it to you to wear it. He said: What shall I do with it? He said: Send it to your brother, the Negus."
"13662","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping dates and unripe dates together."
"13663","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Anas narrated to us. Bahz said in his hadith: He said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of the people of Paradise is pleased to return, and Bahz said: to return to this world, though he have ten times its like, except the martyr, for he wishes, Bahz said: to return to this world and be martyred, for what he saw of merit."
"13664","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: No slave believes until he loves for his Muslim brother what he loves for himself of good."
"13665","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: He said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye? He said: He did not reach that. There was only something at his temples. But Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam."
"13666","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik informed us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"13667","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, ride it."
"13668","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us. Bahz said in his hadith: He said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion and no bad omen, and the good omen pleases me: the good word and the righteous word."
"13669","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"13670","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Abu Isam narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in drink three times, saying: It is more quenching and more wholesome and more healing. Anas said: And I breathe in drink three times."
"13671","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm narrated to us: He said: Anas was asked about the takbir in prayer, while I listened. He said: He says takbir when he bows and when he prostrates and when he raises his head from prostration and when he stands between the two rakahs. He said: Hakim said to him: From whom do you retain this? He said: From the Messenger of Allah and Abu Bakr and Umar. Then he fell silent. He said: Hakim said to him: And Uthman? He said: And Uthman."
"13672","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us: He heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."
"13673","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strive against the polytheists with your wealth and yourselves and your tongues."
"13674","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: He said: There was sent down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, to the end of the verse, on his return from al-Hudaybiyah, while his companions were mingled with grief and gloom. He said: There has been sent down upon me a verse dearer to me than the world and all it contains. He said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, a man of the people said: Congratulations, it has been made clear to you what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down the verse after it: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, until he sealed the verse."
"13675","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: that Anas ibn Malik informed him: that al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, so he permitted them silk shirts on a campaign of theirs."
"13676","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, then left it."
"13677","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us: He said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a camel-driver of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called Anjashah. He said: He had a beautiful voice. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Anjashah, do not break the glass vessels. Qatadah said: Meaning the weak women."
"13678","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah: He said: Anas informed me that a tailor in Madinah invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his food. He said: There was barley bread with rancid fat, and in it was pumpkin. He said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like pumpkin. Anas said: Pumpkin has not ceased to please me since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like it."
"13679","Affan narrated to us: Abdillah ibn Bakr, meaning al-Muzani, narrated to us: He said: I heard Ata, meaning Ibn Abi Maymunah, narrate, and I know it only from Anas: that no retaliation case was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that he commanded pardon. Ibn Bakr said: I used to narrate it from Anas, and they said to him: From Anas, no doubt in it. I said: I know it only from Anas."
"13680","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Qatadah and Thabit and Humayd informed us, from Anas: that a man came and entered the row while out of breath, and said: Praise be to Allah, much good blessed praise. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: Which of you spoke the words? The people fell silent. He said: Which of you spoke them? For he said nothing but good. The man said: I came while out of breath, so I said them. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to them, which of them would raise them. Humayd added, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes, let him walk as he was walking, pray what he catches, and make up what he missed. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-irmam is silence."
"13681","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say while digging the trench: We are those who pledged to Muhammad for Islam as long as we live. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, indeed good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. Barley bread with rancid fat upon it was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they ate from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed good is the good of the Hereafter."
"13682","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off with his hand."
"13683","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed me, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited all his wives in one night together. Hammad perhaps said: In one day."
"13684","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud: O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth."
"13685","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed me, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until it was said: He has fasted, and break fast until it was said: He has broken fast. Once he said: He broke fast, he broke fast, he broke fast."
"13686","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the like of this."
"13687","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raid at Fajr prayer. He would listen. If he heard an adhan, he held back, otherwise he raided. One day he listened and heard a man say: Allah is Greater, Allah is Greater. He said: Upon the fitrah. He said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah. He said: You have come out of the Fire."
"13688","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, said: Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink and sufficed us and sheltered us. How many have none to suffice them nor shelter them."
"13689","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed me, from Anas: He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I played with boys, and greeted us. Then he called me and sent me on an errand of his. I came, having delayed from my mother. She said: What kept you? Where were you? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand. She said: O my son, what was it? I said: It is a secret. She said: Do not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to anyone. Then he said: By Allah, O Thabit, had I disclosed it to anyone, I would have disclosed it to you."
"13690","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, did I not come to you astray and Allah guided you through me, and enemies and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, joined your hearts through me? Then he said to them: Will you not say: You came to us expelled and we sheltered you, frightened and we secured you, forsaken and we aided you? They said: Rather favor belongs to Allah and His Messenger over us."
"13691","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted continuously in Ramadan, and men of his companions fasted continuously. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of that, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously such that the extremists would abandon their extremism. I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"13692","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud while wiping blood from his face, saying: How shall a people prosper who wounded their Prophet and broke his tooth while he calls them to Allah? Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: You have nothing of the affair, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"13693","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that Anas ibn al-Nadr was absent from the fighting at Badr and said: I was absent from the first battle witnessed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If I see fighting, Allah shall see what I do. When the day of Uhud came, the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fled. Anas advanced and saw Sad ibn Muadh fleeing and said: O Abu Amr, where, where? Rise. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I smell the scent of Paradise beyond Uhud. He charged until he was killed. Sad ibn Muadh said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I could not do what he did. His sister said: I recognized my brother only by his fingertip. There were in him over eighty wounds, between sword strike and arrow shot and spear thrust. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down about him: Men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah, to His saying: and they did not change at all."
"13694","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that al-Adba was never beaten. A Bedouin came on a young camel of his and raced her and beat her. It was as if that weighed upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that He raises nothing of this world except that He lowers it."
"13695","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: He said: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most afflicted man in this world among the people of Paradise will be brought and it will be said: Dip him once in Paradise. They will dip him in it once. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see misery or anything you dislike? He will say: No, by Your Might, I never saw anything I dislike. Then the most pampered man in this world among the people of Hell will be brought and it will be said: Dip him once in it. He will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see good or comfort ever? He will say: No, by Your Might, I never saw good ever nor comfort ever."
"13696","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam and fashioned him, then left him in Paradise as long as Allah willed to leave him, Iblis began circling him. When he saw him hollow, he knew he was a creation without self-control."
"13697","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit: He said: It was said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grow gray? He said: Allah did not blemish him with gray hair. There were in his head and beard only seventeen or eighteen hairs."
"13698","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: I brought a brother of mine to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for tahnik in the livestock pen. He said: I saw him branding sheep, I think he said: on their ears."
"13699","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: He said: Qatadah informed me, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of completing prayer. Abdillah said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I think I dropped it."
"13700","Affan narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Dihqan, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man eating with his left hand."
"13701","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that they asked the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day until they exhausted him with questioning, so he came out one day and ascended the minbar and said: You do not ask me today about anything except I will inform you of it. So the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, feared that some matter had come before them. He said: So I kept not turning right nor left except I found every man wrapping his head in his garment, weeping. Then a man arose who used to be reproached and attributed to other than his father, and said: O Prophet of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. He said: Then Umar stood, or he said, then Umar arose, and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, seeking refuge with Allah from the evil of tribulations. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I never saw the like of today in good and evil ever; Paradise and Hellfire were depicted to me until I saw them below this wall."
"13702","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, with the like of it. He said: And Qatadah used to mention this hadith when he was asked about this verse: Ask not about things which, if made manifest to you, will distress you."
"13703","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"13704","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il informed us, Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, who said: We sought knowledge of the wooden staff that is in the standing place of the imam, and we could not find anyone to mention anything about it to us. Mus'ab said: So Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Khabbab, the keeper of the chamber, informed me and said: Anas ibn Malik sat with me one day and said: Do you know why this was made, and I did not ask him about it. So I said: No, by Allah, I do not know why it was made. So Anas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to place his right hand upon it, then turn to us and say: Straighten yourselves and make your rows even."
"13705","Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that al-Bara ibn Malik used to chant for the men, and Anjashah used to chant for the women, and he was good of voice; so he chanted and the camels quickened their pace. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels."
"13706","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and Hellfire is surrounded by desires."
"13707","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, who said: Umayyah ibn Shibl informed me, from Uthman ibn Yazdawayh, who said: I went out to Madinah with Umar ibn Yazid, while Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz was governor over it before he was made caliph. He said: So I heard Anas ibn Malik, and he had severe vitiligo. He said: And Umar used to lead us in prayer. So Anas said: I never saw anyone whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than this youth; he used to lighten while completing it."
"13708","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Dawud, meaning al-Habati Abu Hisham, narrated to us, who said: My brother Harun ibn Abi Dawud: I came to Anas ibn Malik and said: O Abu Hamzah, the place is distant, and we like to visit you. So he raised his head and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Any man who visits a sick person only wades in mercy, and when he sits with the sick person, mercy covers him. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the healthy one who visits the sick, so what is for the sick? He said: His sins are dropped from him."
"13709","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit, and a deed that is not raised, and a heart that does not fear, and a saying that is not heard."
"13710","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Sallam, meaning Ibn Miskin, narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I served the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for ten years, and he never said to me uff ever, nor did he say: Why did you do such-and-such."
"13711","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ma'dan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attended a wedding feast in which there was neither bread nor meat."
"13712","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sadaqah the flour merchant narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set for us a time limit of forty days for trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and shaving the pubic hair."
"13713","Rawh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: People will enter Hellfire until, when they have become charcoal, they will be admitted into Paradise. Then the people of Paradise will say: Who are these? So it will be said: These are the Jahannamiyyun."
"13714","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the people of Paradise see them, they will say: These are the Jahannamiyyun."
"13715","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, who said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to open the recitation with: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"13716","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, and would say the takbir; and I indeed saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
"13717","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted, or granted a concession to, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that was in them."
"13718","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us from dictation, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Ri'l and Usayyah and Dhakwan and Banu Lihyan came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him that they had accepted Islam, and sought reinforcements against their people. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reinforced them with seventy of the Ansar. He said: We used to call them the Qurra in their time; they used to gather firewood by day and pray by night, until when they were at Bi'r Ma'unah, they treacherously killed them. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month, supplicating against these tribes: Usayyah and Ri'l and Dhakwan and Banu Lihyan. And Anas narrated to us: We recited concerning them a Qur'an: Convey from us to our people that we have met our Lord, mighty and majestic is He, and He is pleased with us and has pleased us. Then it was abrogated, or raised."
"13719","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came walking until he reached the mosque, or near it. An old man, or a man, came to him and said: When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And what have you prepared for it? The man said: By the One Who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, I have not prepared for it much deed of prayer nor fasting, but I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13720","Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shaved his head at Mina, he took the right side of his head with his hand, and when he finished, he handed it to me and said: O Anas, go with this to Umm Sulaym. So when the people saw what he had singled her out with of that, they competed for the other side, this one taking a thing and this one taking a thing. Muhammad said: So I narrated it to Abidah al-Salmani, and he said: For a single hair of it to be with me is more beloved to me than every yellow and white thing that has come to be on the face of the earth and in its belly."
"13721","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdillah informed us, who said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for nine years, and he never said to me ever, for anything I did ever: You did badly, nor: How evil is what you did."
"13722","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I asked Anas: How many umrahs did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform? He said: He performed four: his umrah in which the polytheists barred him from it, in Dhu al-Qa'dah; and his umrah also of the next year, in Dhu al-Qa'dah; and his umrah when he distributed the spoils of Hunayn, from al-Ji'ranah, in Dhu al-Qa'dah; and his umrah with his Hajj."
"13723","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Anas, that Abu Talhah came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was upon the minbar, and said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What do you see, this verse has come down. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, said: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love. And there is no wealth of mine more beloved to me than my land of Bayruha, and I seek nearness to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, through it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Excellent, excellent; Bayruha is profitable good. So he divided it among them as gardens."
"13724","Affan narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, who said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to me, from Abu Labid, who said: Horses were sent out in the time of al-Hajjaj, while al-Hakam ibn Ayyub was governor over Basra. He said: So we came to the racecourse, and when the horses came, we said: If only we inclined toward Anas ibn Malik and asked him: Did you hold races in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So we came to him while he was in his palace in al-Zawiyah, and we asked him, and said: O Abu Hamzah, did you hold races in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hold a race? He said: Yes, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, indeed raced upon a horse of his called Sabhah, and it outran the people, so he rejoiced at that and it pleased him."
"13725","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, who said: Thabit informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw in the mosque a rope stretched between two pillars, and said: What is this rope? So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, it is for Hamnah bint Jahsh; she prays, and when she becomes weary she holds onto it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let her pray as long as she is able; when she becomes weary, let her sit."
"13726","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of it."
"13727","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdillah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: He said, as if meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The lower garment is to the middle of the shin. So it was hard upon them, so he said: Or to the ankles, and there is no good in lower than that."
"13728","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdillah informed us, al-Awza'i informed us, who said: Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari narrated to me, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: The people suffered a year of drought in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering the sermon on Friday, a Bedouin stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished and families have hungered, so supplicate Allah to give us rain. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hands, while no wisp of cloud was to be seen in the sky. Then a cloud arose like mountains. Then he did not come down from his minbar until we saw the rain streaming down upon his beard. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"13729","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The son of Adam grows old, while two things of him grow young: greed for wealth and greed for life."
"13730","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, who said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man may do for a period of his life the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered Paradise; then, before his death, he changes and does the deed of the people of Hellfire, then dies and enters Hellfire. And a man may do for a period of his life the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered Hellfire; then, before his death, he changes and does the deed of the people of Paradise, then dies and enters Paradise."
"13731","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. So his Companions and his family said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us, while we have believed in you and in what you came with? He said: Hearts are in the Hand of Allah, mighty and majestic is He; He turns them."
"13732","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, then he mentioned a hadith. He said: And I am Ubaydillah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: This is the son of Adam, and this is his appointed term, and there is his hope."
"13733","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like the good dream, and perhaps he would say: Has any one of you seen a dream. And when a man whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not know saw a dream, he would ask about him; if there was nothing wrong with him, his dream would be more pleasing to him. Then a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as though I entered Paradise, and I heard a thud at which Paradise shook: So-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so son of so-and-so, until she counted twelve men. Then they were brought, wearing dusty garments, their jugular veins spurting blood. So it was said: Take them to the river of al-Baydakh, or al-Baydaj. So they were dipped in it, then they came out of it with their faces like the moon on the night of full moon. Then chairs of gold were brought and they sat upon them, and a platter was brought and they ate from it; they did not turn it to any side except they ate whatever fruit they wished. And the bearer of glad tidings came from that detachment and said: Among our affair was such-and-such, and so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted twelve men, whom the woman had counted. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring me the woman; recount your dream to this one. So she recounted it, and he said: It is as she said."
"13734","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm narrated to us, who said: Anas was asked about the takbir in prayer, while I was listening. So he said: He says the takbir when he bows, and when he prostrates, and when he raises his head from prostration, and when he stands between the two rak'ahs. He said: So Hakim said to him: From whom do you retain this? He said: From the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar. Then he fell silent. So Hakim said to him: And Uthman? He said: And Uthman."
"13735","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, who said: Abdillah informed us, who said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man stood up to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was delivering the sermon, then he mentioned it. So he raised his hands, and Abd al-Aziz gestured, placing the backs of them toward his face."
"13736","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, who said: Ali ibn Zayd and Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shortened one day in the Fajr prayer. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you shorten? He said: I heard the weeping of a boy, and I thought his mother was with us praying, so I wanted to free his mother for him. And Hammad also said: I thought his mother was praying with us, so I wanted to free his mother for him."
"13737","Affan said: So I found it with me in another place, from Ali ibn Zayd and Humayd and Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik."
"13738","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, who said: Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, and from Anas, as Humayd thinks, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wrapped in a cotton garment whose ends he had crossed over, and led the people in prayer."
"13739","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, consulted when news of the advance of Abu Sufyan reached him. So Abu Bakr spoke, and he turned away from him. Then Umar spoke, and he turned away from him. So Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: It is us you mean, O Messenger of Allah. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you commanded us to plunge it into the seas, we would plunge it, and if you commanded us to strike its flanks to Bark al-Ghimad, we would do it. Hammad said: Sulaym said, from Ibn Awn, from Amr ibn Sa'id: al-Bighmad. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called the people forth, and they went until they halted at Badr. And the water-carriers of Quraysh came to them, among them a black boy belonging to Banu al-Hajjaj. So they seized him, and the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to ask him about Abu Sufyan and his companions. So he would say: I have no knowledge of Abu Sufyan, but this is Abu Jahl ibn Hisham and Utbah ibn Rabi'ah and Shaybah and Umayyah ibn Khalaf. So when he said that, they beat him. When they beat him, he said: Yes, I will inform you; this is Abu Sufyan. Then when they left him and asked him, he said: I have no knowledge of Abu Sufyan, but this is Abu Jahl and Utbah and Shaybah and Umayyah among the people. He said: When he said this also, they beat him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was standing praying. So when he saw that, he left and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you beat him when he tells you the truth, and you leave him when he lies to you. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is the place of death of so-and-so tomorrow, placing his hand upon the ground here and here. So not one of them deviated from the spot of the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13740","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"13741","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every Prophet there is a supplication with which he supplicated and was answered; and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"13742","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pass by a date, and nothing prevented him from taking it except fear that it might be of charity."
"13743","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar: I heard Musa ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led him and a woman of them in prayer; so he placed Anas on his right, and the woman behind that."
"13744","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, who said: Al-Nadr ibn Anas narrated to me, while Anas was alive that day, who said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"13745","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: Hafsah bint Sirin narrated to me, who said: Anas ibn Malik said to me: Of what did Yahya ibn Abi Amrah die? So I said: Of the plague. So Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"13746","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer. So his saying about that was stern, until he said: They shall desist from that, or their eyesight shall surely be snatched away."
"13747","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas informed me, who said: I heard Anas say: A woman of the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of hers. So he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are indeed the most beloved of people to me, three times."
"13748","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah afflicts the Muslim servant with an affliction in his body, He says to the angel: Write for him his righteous deed which he used to do. Then if He heals him, He washes him and purifies him; and if He takes him, He forgives him and has mercy upon him."
"13749","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtering his sacrifice with his own hand, and saying the takbir over it."
"13750","Affan and Bahz said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, placing his foot upon their sides, slaughtering them with his hand, naming Allah and saying the takbir."
"13751","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, who said: Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brown-skinned, and I never smelled musk nor ambergris sweeter in scent than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13752","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution with a makkuk, and used to bathe with five makkuks."
"13753","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Mu'adh, from Ata ibn Abi Maymun, who said: I heard Anas say: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out for his need, I and a boy of us would come with a small vessel of water."
"13754","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer one day, then ascended the minbar and gestured with his hand toward the qiblah of the mosque, then said: O people, since I led you in prayer, I have seen Paradise and Hellfire depicted in the direction of this wall. I never saw the like of today in good and evil; he said it three times."
"13755","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: One whom I do not accuse, of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me that he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Bilal were walking in al-Baqi', the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, do you hear what I hear? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not hear it. He said: Do you not hear the people of these graves being punished, meaning the graves of the pre-Islamic age."
"13756","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Musahiq, from Amir ibn Abdillah, who said: Anas ibn Malik said: I never saw an imam whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than this imam of yours. He said: And Umar, meaning Ibn Abd al-Aziz, did not lengthen the recitation."
"13757","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, who said: I saw with Anas ibn Malik a cup that had belonged to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in which there was a silver band."
"13758","Yahya ibn Adam narrated it to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, then he mentioned it."
"13759","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from Anas, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the sheepfold, while he was branding sheep. Shu'bah said: I think he said: In their ears."
"13760","Aswad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month, supplicating, cursing Ri'l and Dhakwan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"13761","Aswad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month, supplicating, cursing Ri'l and Dhakwan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"13762","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"13763","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that people asked the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about his worship in private. He said: So he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is with people who ask about what I do. As for me, I pray and sleep, and fast and break fast, and marry women. So whoever turns away from my practice is not of me."
"13764","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months when he went out to Fajr, and say: Prayer, O people of the House: Allah only intends to remove defilement from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"13765","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come until Allah, Allah is not said upon the earth."
"13766","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gave him sheep between two mountains. So he came to his people and said: O my people, accept Islam, for Muhammad gives the giving of one who does not fear poverty. And a man would come to him seeking nothing but the world, then evening would not come until his religion was more beloved to him than the world with all in it."
"13767","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: A beggar came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ordered a date for him, and he scorned it. Then another beggar came, so he ordered a date for him, and he said: Glory be to Allah, a date from the Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the maidservant: Go to Umm Salamah and give him the forty dirhams that are with her."
"13768","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, who said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Layth, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, who said: There were orphans in the care of Abu Talhah, so he bought wine for them. Then when wine was forbidden, he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Shall I make it vinegar? He said: No. He said: So he poured it out."
"13769","Aswad ibn Amir and Husayn said: Isra'il narrated to us, Husayn said: From al-Suddi, and Aswad said: Al-Suddi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Hubayrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: There were orphans in the care of Abu Talhah, so he bought wine for them. Then when wine was forbidden, he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Shall I make it vinegar? He said: No. He said: So he poured it out."
"13770","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari narrated to me, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a cup of water, and performed ablution. Amr said: I said to Anas: Did he perform ablution for every prayer? He said: Yes. I said: And you? He said: We used to pray the prayers with one ablution. Then I asked him afterward, and he said: As long as he had not broken it."
"13771","Aswad ibn Amir and Affan said: Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas. Aswad said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Straighten your rows, bring them near together, and align with the necks. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see the devils entering through the gaps in the row as though they are small sheep. And Affan said: I see the devil entering."
"13772","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Isa, from Abdillah ibn Jabr, from Anas, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited a boy who used to serve him, a Jew. So he said to him: Say: There is no god but Allah. So he kept looking toward his father. He said: So he said to him: Say what he says to you. He said: So he said it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his Companions: Pray over your brother. And other than Aswad said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. He said: So he said to him: Say what Muhammad says to you."
"13773","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, and Jabir, from Abu Nadrah, from Anas, who said: He gave me a kunyah by a green I used to gather, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13774","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O possessor of the two ears."
"13775","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was taken up to heaven, said: I came to Idris in the fourth heaven."
"13776","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the people of Paradise see them, they will say: These are the Jahannamiyyun."
"13777","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that al-Rubayyi' came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she is the mother of Harithah ibn Suraqah, and said: O Prophet of Allah, will you not tell me about Harithah, and he had been killed on the day of Badr, struck by a stray arrow. If he is in Paradise, I will be patient, and if he is other than that, I will strive in weeping over him. So he said: O Umm Harithah, they are gardens in Paradise, and your son has attained the highest Firdaws. Qatadah said: And al-Firdaws is the hill of Paradise, and its middle and its best."
"13778","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on one of his journeys, with Mu'adh ibn Jabal riding behind him, with nothing between them but the rear of the saddle, when the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Mu'adh ibn Jabal. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and may you be made happy. Then he traveled an hour, then said: O Mu'adh ibn Jabal. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and may you be made happy. He said: Do you know what is the right of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, upon the servants? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah upon the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. He said: Then do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah, when they do that? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Allah, mighty and majestic is He, is that He not punish them."
"13779","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, who said: And Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that a man called out to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on Friday while he was addressing the people in Madinah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has failed, the land is barren, and the people are in drought, so ask your Lord to give us rain. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked to the sky, while we saw little cloud, and asked for rain. So the cloud grew, part to part, then they were rained upon until the watercourses of Madinah flowed and its roads ran as rivers. And it remained so until the next Friday, not ceasing. Then that man stood, or another, while the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was addressing, and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate Allah to withhold it from us. So the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed, then said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. So he supplicated his Lord, and the cloud began to break away from Madinah, to the right and left, raining around it while not raining in it at all."
"13780","Husayn narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar, who said: I heard Musa ibn Anas, who said: And perhaps I and he sat with him, who said: And he was of our youths, younger than me in age, narrating from Anas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led Anas and a woman in prayer; so he placed Anas on his right, and the woman behind them."
"13781","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Jud'an, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a detachment. He said: And he used to kneel before him in war, then scatter his quiver and say: My face is a shield for your face, and my soul a ransom for your soul."
"13782","Husayn narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: No perfume was ever offered to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he refused."
"13783","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The people were frightened, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode a slow horse belonging to Abu Talhah, then went out galloping alone. So the people rode galloping behind him. So he said: Do not be frightened; it is a sea. He said: By Allah, it was not outrun after that day."
"13784","Husayn narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: Ubaydillah ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, so it was placed in a basin, and he began tapping upon it, and said something about his beauty. So Anas said: He was the most resembling of them to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was dyed with woad."
"13785","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, who said: Thumamah ibn Abdillah ibn Anas narrated to me, that Anas would not refuse perfume, and claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not refuse perfume."
"13786","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, who said: I heard Anas say: A sacrificial camel, or a gift, was brought past the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to the one with it, or to its owner: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel, or a gift. He said: Even so."
"13787","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to be cupped, and he would not wrong anyone his wage."
"13788","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against a tribe of the Arabs, then left it."
"13789","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: No time comes upon you except the time that was before it was more evil than it; I heard that from your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13790","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, who said: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him, and removes ten sins from him."
"13791","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, who said: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, who said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim man ever asks Allah for Paradise three times except Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise; and he does not seek refuge from Hellfire except Hellfire says: O Allah, grant him refuge."
"13792","Husayn narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas narrated to us, that a Jew took some jewelry from a slave girl, then set upon her and crushed her head between two stones. So they reached the slave girl while there was still life in her. So they took the slave girl and began following her through the people: Is this he, or is this he. So they brought her past the man, and she gestured toward him with her head. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered concerning him, and his head was crushed between two stones."
"13793","Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, from Musa ibn Anas, from his father, who said: Gray hair did not reach in the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what would require him to dye it; but Abu Bakr dyed his head and beard until his hair was saturated with henna and katam."
"13794","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I never prayed behind any imam ever lighter and more complete than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"13795","Sulayman informed us, Isma'il informed us, who said: Al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Anas, with the like of it."
"13796","Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays Asr, then sits dictating good until evening, is better than freeing eight of the children of Isma'il."
"13797","Ubaydillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wrapped in a Qitri garment, and led them in prayer, or he said, covered, and led them in prayer."
"13798","Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, with the like of it."
"13799","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wrapped in a Qitri garment, and led them in prayer, or he said, covered, and led them in prayer."
"13800","Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Musa ibn Imran, peace be upon him, when he wanted to enter water, would not cast off his garment until he had concealed his nakedness in the water."
"13801","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman used to complete the takbir when they rose and when they lowered."
"13802","Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions, a Jew passed by them and greeted, and when he had gone on he called him and said: How did you say? He said: I said, death be upon you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: Upon you, meaning what you said."
"13803","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When this verse was revealed, You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, or, Who is it that will lend Allah a goodly loan, he said: Abu Talhah, who had a walled garden, said: O Messenger of Allah, my garden is for Allah, and if I could conceal it I would not make it public. So he said: Put it among your close relatives."
"13804","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come to you a people softer in hearts than you. Then when they drew near Madinah they began to chant: Tomorrow we shall meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party. So the Asharis came, among them Abu Musa al-Ashari."
"13805","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast when he consummated marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he fed the people to their fill with bread and meat. Then he went out to the chambers of the Mothers of the Believers as he used to do on the morning after his marriage, greeting them and supplicating for them, and they greeted him and supplicated for him. Then when he returned to his house he saw two men conversing between them, and when he saw them he turned back from his house, and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn back from his house they leapt up hastening. He said: I do not know whether I informed him of their leaving or he was informed. So he returned until he entered the house, and he let down the curtain between me and him, and the verse of the Hijab was revealed."
"13806","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Banu Salimah wanted to move from their dwellings to near the mosque, but the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that Madinah should become empty, so he said: O Banu Salimah, will you not reckon your footsteps in reward."
"13807","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted regarding Khaybar and we ended up there. When morning came, he rode and the Muslims rode, and I rode behind Abu Talhah, and my foot was touching the foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The people of Khaybar came out with their baskets and spades to their crops and lands, and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims they returned fleeing and said: Muhammad and the army. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Most Great, Khaybar is ruined. Indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"13808","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives, and one of the Mothers of the Believers sent a bowl containing food, and she struck the hand of the servant so the bowl fell and split. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and joined the two pieces and began to gather the food in it, saying: Your mother felt jealous, your mother felt jealous, and saying to the people: Eat. And he detained the messenger until the other one brought her bowl, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed the sound bowl to the one whose bowl was broken, and left the broken one for the one who broke it."
"13809","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Muslims heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling out in the night: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and O Utbah ibn Rabiah, and O Shaybah ibn Rabiah, and O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true, for I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, are you calling out to a people who have decayed. He said: You do not hear what I say any better than they do, except that they are unable to answer."
"13810","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that the Muhajirun and the Ansar be next to him so that they would preserve from him."
"13811","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold, so I said: To whom does this palace belong. They said: To a young man of Quraysh. So I thought that I was he, and I said: Who. They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"13812","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was by a river flowing, its banks tents of pearl, so I struck with my hand into what flows in it, and it was strongly fragrant musk. I said: O Jibril, what is this. He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you."
"13813","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us with his face before uttering the takbir in prayer and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"13814","Muawiyah narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The prayer was established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us with his face and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"13815","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going out in the path of Allah, or an evening. Then he mentioned, meaning he mentioned the hadith of Sulayman ibn Dawud."
"13816","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail meaning Ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed me, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going out in the path of Allah, or an evening, is better than the world and what is in it. The span of the bow of one of you, or the place of his foot, in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it. If a woman of the women of the people of Paradise were to look down to the earth, she would illuminate what is between them and fill what is between them with fragrance, and her head-cover upon her head is better than the world and what is in it."
"13817","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: Whenever we wished to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying we saw him, or sleeping we saw him. He said: He used to fast of the month until we would say, we do not see him intending to break any of it, and he would break fast of the month until we would say, we do not see him intending to fast any of it."
"13818","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, he said: Anas was asked about the punishment of the grave and about the Dajjal, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, cowardice, miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave."
"13819","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym sent with me a basket containing fresh dates, but I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house, for he was with a freedman of his who had made for him tharid, or said tharidah, with meat and pumpkin. He invited me and seated me with him, and I saw that pumpkin pleased him, so I began to leave it toward him. When he had eaten lunch and returned to his house, I placed the basket before him, and he began to eat from it and distribute until he finished the last of it."
"13820","Al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shubah, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr, and with Umar, and they did not recite aloud, In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"13821","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar ibn Hazm, informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over the rest of food."
"13822","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed between Khaybar and Madinah three days consummating marriage with Safiyyah bint Huyayy, so I invited the Muslims to his wedding feast, and there was in it neither bread nor meat. He ordered us with leather mats, which were spread, and dates, dried yogurt, and ghee were put upon them, and that was his wedding feast. The Muslims said: Is she one of the Mothers of the Believers or what his right hand possesses. They said: If he veils her she is of the Mothers of the Believers, and if he does not veil her she is of what his right hand possesses. When he departed he made a place for her behind him and drew the veil between her and the people."
"13823","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail informed us, he said: Humayd informed me, from Anas, he said: The mother of Harithah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Harithah had perished on the day of Badr, struck by a stray arrow, and said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Harithah in my heart. If he is in Paradise I shall not weep over him, otherwise you shall see what I do. He said to her: You are bereaved, is it one Paradise. They are many Gardens, and he is in al-Firdaws, the highest."
"13824","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Isa, he said: Jabr ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A mudd suffices one of you in ablution."
"13825","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah informed us, from al-Amash, he said: It was narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The longest of people in necks on the Day of Resurrection are the muezzins."
"13826","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclined at the daughter of Milhan. He raised his head and laughed, so she said: What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Some people of my Ummah riding this green sea as warriors in the path of Allah, their likeness like kings upon couches. She said: Supplicate Allah, O Messenger of Allah, to make me of them. So he said: O Allah, make her of them. Then she married Ubadah ibn al-Samit. He said: She rode in the sea with her son Qaradhah, until when she returned she mounted a beast of hers at the shore, which threw her off, so she fell and died."
"13827","Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon the daughter of Milhan and reclined at her, then he mentioned its meaning."
"13828","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then says three times: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, entering by whichever he wishes."
"13829","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There remains of Paradise what Allah wills to remain, then Allah creates for it a creation as He wills."
"13830","Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Umarah, meaning Ibn Zadham, informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The angel of rain sought permission to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was permitted. He said to Umm Salamah: Guard the door for us, let no one enter. Then al-Husayn ibn Ali came and leapt until he entered, and began to climb upon the shoulder of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The angel said to him: Do you love him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: Your Ummah will kill him, and if you wish I shall show you the place where he will be killed. He struck with his hand and showed him red soil. Umm Salamah took that soil and tied it in the edge of her garment. He said: We used to hear, he will be killed at Karbala."
"13831","Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us, Umarah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took three pebbles, placed one, then placed another before him, and threw the third, and said: This is the son of Adam, and this is his term, and that is his hope, the one he threw."
"13832","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abdullah ibn Rawahah, when he met a man of his companions, would say: Come, let us believe in our Lord for an hour. One day he said it to a man, and the man became angry and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not see Ibn Rawahah turning away from your faith to the faith of an hour. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Ibn Rawahah, he loves the gatherings over which the angels boast."
"13833","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, from Thabit and Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years, and he never said for a thing I did, why did you do it. I never touched anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor smelled a perfume more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13834","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, from Asim, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu Ayyash Zayd ibn Samit al-Zuraqi while he was praying and saying: O Allah, I ask You, as praise belongs to You, there is no god but You, O Bestower, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has supplicated Allah by His Greatest Name, by which when He is called He answers, and when He is asked by it He gives."
"13835","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he set out before the sun declined, would delay Zuhr to the time of Asr, then alight and combine them, and when the sun had declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr then mount."
"13836","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ishaq ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abu Talhah used to shield himself with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by a single shield, and Abu Talhah was a good archer. When he shot, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would look out to see the landing places of his arrows."
"13837","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"13838","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver, its stone of it."
"13839","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Mawhab informed us, from Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Harithah al-Ansari, that Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who revives a tongue with a truth acted upon after him, except Allah causes his reward to run for him until the Day of Resurrection, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fulfills his reward to him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13840","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, and Attab, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Muti informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah, the foster-son of Aishah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no dead person over whom a community of Muslims reaching a hundred pray and intercede for him, except they are granted intercession for him."
"13841","Sallam said: Shuyb ibn al-Habhab narrated it to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated it to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13842","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning al-Umari, informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I witnessed two wedding feasts of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there was neither bread nor meat. He said: I said: O Abu Hamzah, what was in them. He said: Hays."
"13843","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove many sacrificial camels and said: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj, and I was at the left thigh of his she-camel."
"13844","Yamar narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Iyas, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For every prophet there is a monastic practice, and the monastic practice of this Ummah is striving in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"13845","Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never dyed at all. The whiteness was only in the front of his beard, a little on the chin, and on the head a slight scattering hardly seen. And al-Muthanna said, and the temples. My father said: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated it to us, Abdullah informed us, al-Muthanna informed us, from Qatadah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"13846","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated it to us, Abdullah informed us, al-Muthanna informed us, from Qatadah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"13847","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated to us, Hazm ibn Abi Hazm al-Qutai narrated to us, Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that his lifespan be extended and his provision increased, let him be dutiful to his parents and maintain his kinship ties. He said: And al-Salahini said, be blessed in his provision, and he also said, his parents. And Yunus said, his parents, and he said, his provision be increased."
"13848","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas, he said: There was speech between Khalid ibn al-Walid and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Khalid said to Abd al-Rahman: You exalt yourselves over us by days you preceded us with. It reached us that that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Leave my Companions for me. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you spent the like of Uhud, or the like of the mountains, in gold, you would not reach their deeds."
"13849","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Asma al-Sayqal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We went out raising our voices with Hajj. When we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it Umrah, and said: Had I faced of my affair what I have now seen, I would have made it Umrah, but I drove the sacrificial animal and combined Hajj and Umrah."
"13850","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated to us, Nafi Abu Ghalib al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection while the sky showers upon them."
"13851","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays al-Huddani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what Allah has made obligatory upon me of prayer. He said: Allah has made obligatory upon His servants five prayers. He said: Is there anything before them or after them. He said: Allah has made obligatory upon His servants five prayers. He said it three times. He said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall neither add anything to them nor subtract anything from them. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will enter Paradise if he is truthful."
"13852","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd narrating, he said: Anas was asked about cupping for one in ihram, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped for a pain he had."
"13853","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a mount, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall mount you upon the offspring of a she-camel. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do with the offspring of a she-camel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And do she-camels give birth to except she-camels."
"13854","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brownish, and I never smelled musk nor ambergris more pleasant in scent than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13855","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us that they asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have a ring. He said: Yes. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last Isha one night until nearly half the night had gone, then said: The people have prayed and slept, and you have remained in prayer as long as you awaited the prayer. Anas said: As if I am looking at the glitter of his ring, and he raised his left hand."
"13856","Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Rain befell us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and uncovered his garment until it touched him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do this. He said: It is newly come from its Lord."
"13857","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him his Companions, so he went out to them and prayed with them briefly, then entered his house and prayed at length, then went out to them and prayed with them briefly, then entered and prayed at length. In the morning they said: We came to you last night, O Messenger of Allah, and you prayed with us briefly, then entered your house and prayed at length. He said: I did that for your sake. Hammad said: Thabit had narrated this hadith to us from Thumamah, so I met Thumamah and asked him."
"13858","Affan informed us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Hajjaj al-Ahwal, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, meaning let him pray it. He said: I met Hajjaj al-Ahwal and he narrated it to me."
"13859","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd and Hammad, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he visited the sick, would say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You, heal a healing that leaves no sickness. And Hammad said: There is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"13860","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Messengership and prophethood have ceased, so there is no messenger after me nor prophet. He said: That was hard upon the people. He said: But the bearers of glad tidings. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the bearers of glad tidings. He said: The dream of the Muslim man, and it is a part of the parts of prophethood."
"13861","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in what the sleeper sees, as if I were riding behind a ram, and as if the edge of my sword broke. I interpreted that I shall kill the chief of the force, and that a man of my household will be killed."
"13862","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar and said: O maternal uncle, say, there is no god but Allah. He said: Maternal uncle or paternal uncle. He said: Rather maternal uncle. He said: Is it good for me to say it. He said: Yes."
"13863","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Quraysh made a treaty with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Suhayl ibn Amr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Write, In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Suhayl said: As for, In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, we do not know what, In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, is, but write what we know, In Your Name, O Allah. He said: Write, From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. He said: Had we known you are the Messenger of Allah we would have followed you, but write your name and the name of your father. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write, From Muhammad ibn Abdullah. And they stipulated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever comes to you of us, we shall not return him to you, and whoever comes of us, you shall return him to us. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do you write this. He said: Yes. Whoever goes from us to them, may Allah cast him away."
"13864","Affan and Abu Kamil said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but does not reach their deeds. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"13865","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a footfall, so I said: What is this footfall. It was said: al-Rumaysa bint Milhan."
"13866","Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When the day came in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived at Madinah, everything in it was illuminated, and when the day came in which he died, everything in it darkened. He said: No sooner had we shaken our hands of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than we found our hearts changed."
"13867","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr at Madinah four units, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah two units, and spent the night there until morning. When he prayed Subh he mounted his mount, and when it rose with him he glorified and magnified until it stood straight with him at al-Bayda, then he combined between them. When we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to exit ihram, and when the Day of Tarwiyah came they entered ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered seven camels with his hand standing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams."
"13868","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, he said: The Isha prayer was established one night, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. So he stood conversing with him until the people, or some of the people, dozed, then he prayed and did not mention ablution."
"13869","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not come until there is not said upon the earth, there is no god but Allah."
"13870","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my father. He said: In the Fire. When he turned away he called him and said: My father and your father are in the Fire."
"13871","Affan narrated to us, Marhum narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit saying: I was sitting with Anas, and he had a daughter with him, and Anas said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, have you any need of me. His daughter said: How little was her modesty. He said: She is better than you, she desired the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him."
"13872","Affan informed us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Anas informed me, he said: I heard Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"13873","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew, then he mentioned the like of it."
"13874","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten, straighten. By Allah, I see you from behind me as I see you from before me."
"13875","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a footfall, so I said: What is this footfall. It was said: al-Rumaysa bint Milhan."
"13876","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, that Anas informed him, that a slave girl was found with her head between two stones. It was said to her: Who did this to you, so-and-so, so-and-so, until they named the Jew, and she nodded with her head. He said: The Jew was seized and brought, and he confessed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning him, and his head was crushed with stones."
"13877","Affan and Bahz said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his hair reached his shoulders. Bahz said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had hair reaching between his shoulders."
"13878","Affan and Bahz said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and the prostration, for I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"13879","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym sent with him a basket containing fresh dates to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He took a handful and sent it to one of his wives, and he mentioned it either twice or three times, then he ate the eating of a man known to desire it."
"13880","Bahz and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer and said: Praise be to Allah, much praise, good, blessed in it. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he said: Which of you is the one who said such and such words. He said: The people fell silent. He repeated it three times, and a man said: I said them, and I intended by them only good. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve angels raced for them, not knowing how to write them until they asked their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and He said: Write them as My servant said."
"13881","Affan and Bahz said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, Bahz said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his sandal had two straps."
"13882","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you spits, let him not spit before him nor on his right, but let him spit on his left or under his left foot."
"13883","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Anas narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was walking in Paradise, I came upon a palace, so I said: To whom does this belong, O Jibril, hoping it would be mine. He said: He said, to Umar. He said: Then I walked a while, and I came upon a palace better than the first palace. He said: I said: To whom does this belong, O Jibril, hoping it would be mine. He said: He said, to Umar, and in it are of the wide-eyed maidens. O Abu Hafs, nothing prevented me from entering it except your jealousy. He said: The eyes of Umar filled with tears, then he said: Over you, would I feel jealous."
"13884","Affan and Bahz said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, Affan said in his hadith: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, and there is no expiation for it except that. Bahz said: And Hammam said, I heard him narrating after that, and he added with this speech: Establish prayer for My remembrance."
"13885","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness. The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. Affan said: I asked Hammad, and he narrated it to me, and he went far in its heat."
"13886","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, informed us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come, and with him was a boy of the Ansar called Muhammad. He said: If this one lives, perhaps old age shall not overtake him before the Hour comes."
"13887","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bright in color, his sweat was pearls, and when he walked he leaned forward. I never touched brocade nor silk nor anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor smelled a scent ever, musk nor ambergris, more pleasant than his scent."
"13888","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great. He said: Upon the fitrah. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: You have come out of the Fire."
"13889","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that when Ruqayyah died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man who was intimate with his family last night enter the grave."
"13890","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, he said: Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Send with us men to teach us the Quran and the Sunnah. So he sent to them seventy men of the Ansar called the Reciters, among them my maternal uncle Haram. They recited the Quran and studied it at night, and by day they would bring water and place it in the mosque, gather firewood and sell it, and buy with it food for the people of the Suffah and the poor. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them, and they scattered against them and killed them before they reached the place. They said: O Allah, convey from us to our Prophet that we have met You, and we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us. He said: A man came to Haram, the maternal uncle of Anas, from behind and stabbed him with his spear until it pierced through, and he said: I have won, by the Lord of the Kabah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Your brothers who were killed said to their Lord: Convey from us to our Prophet that we have met You, and we are pleased with You and You are pleased with us."
"13891","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, he said: I heard Anas saying, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The people of Paradise enter Paradise, and there remains of it what Allah wills to remain, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, creates for it a creation of what He wills."
"13892","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the best of people in character."
"13893","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For every treacherous one there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he is known."
"13894","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, that Anas was asked about the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I never saw hair more like the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the hair of Qatadah. So Qatadah rejoiced that day."
"13895","Affan narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never had a lunch nor a supper of bread and meat together except in company."
"13896","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that a Jew invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he accepted. Aban also said: A tailor."
"13897","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas said: I do not recognize among you today anything I knew in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except your saying, there is no god but Allah. He said: I said: O Abu Hamzah, the prayer. He said: You prayed when the sun set. Was that the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He said, though I have not seen a time better for a doer than this time of yours, except a time with a prophet."
"13898","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was the riding companion of Abu Talhah, and Abu Talhah was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I could see my foot touching the foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited for them until the people of crops went out to their crops and the people of livestock to their livestock. He said: He uttered the takbir, then raided them, then said: When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"13899","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit and Humayd informed us, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf arrived at Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari. Sad said to him: O my brother, I am the wealthiest of the people of Madinah in wealth, so look at half my wealth and take it, and beneath me are two wives, so look at whichever of them pleases you more that I divorce her. Abd al-Rahman said: May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth, show me the market. So they showed him the market, and he went, bought and sold and profited, and brought some dried yogurt and ghee. Then he remained as long as Allah willed him to remain, then came with traces of saffron upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married a woman. He said: What did you give her as dowry. He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep. Abd al-Rahman said: I saw myself, had I lifted a stone I would hope to find gold or silver."
"13900","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: So that was permitted."
"13901","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the bravest of people and the finest of people and the most generous of people. He said: The people of Madinah were frightened one night. He said: So the people set out toward the sound, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them, having already outrun them, saying: Do not be frightened. He said: And he was upon a bare horse belonging to Abu Talhah with the sword hung around its neck, and he kept saying to the people: Do not be frightened. He said: And he said: We found him to be a sea, or: He is indeed a sea, meaning the horse."
"13902","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd and Thabit informed us from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons, and he said: What is this? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he vowed to perform Hajj walking. He said: Allah is free of any need of his tormenting himself, so let him ride."
"13903","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us from Anas that the people said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished and we are suffering drought, O Messenger of Allah, so ask for rain for us. So he stood on Friday while upon the minbar and asked for rain, and Hammad described it, spreading his two hands opposite his chest with the insides of his palms toward the ground, while there was not a wisp of cloud in the sky. He did not leave until even the strong young man was concerned about himself getting back to his family. So we were rained upon until the next Friday. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, buildings have collapsed and riders have been cut off, ask Allah to clear it away from us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. So it cleared away until Madinah was as though it were within a wreath."
"13904","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit and Humayd informed us from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, Abdullah ibn Salam was informed of his arrival while he was among his date-palms, so he came to him and said: I will ask you about things which none knows except a prophet, so if you inform me of them I will believe in you, and if you do not know them I will know that you are not a prophet. He said: So he asked him about resemblance and about the first thing the people of Paradise eat and about the first thing that gathers people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril informed me of them just now. He said: That is the enemy of the Jews. He said: As for resemblance, if the fluid of the man precedes the fluid of the woman he takes the resemblance, and if the fluid of the woman precedes the fluid of the man she takes the resemblance. And as for the first thing the people of Paradise eat, it is the extra lobe of the liver of the whale. And as for the first thing that gathers people, it is a fire that comes out from the direction of the east and gathers them toward the west. So he believed and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. Ibn Salam said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a people of slander, and if they hear of my Islam they will slander me, so hide me with you and send for them and ask them about me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hid him and sent for them, and they came. He said: What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you? They said: He is our best and the son of our best, and our chief and the son of our chief, and our scholar and the son of our scholar. He said: What would you think if he became Muslim, would you become Muslim? They said: May Allah protect him from that. He said: O Abdullah ibn Salam, come out to them and inform them. So he came out and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Our most evil and the son of our most evil, and our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one. So Ibn Salam said: I already told you, O Messenger of Allah, that the Jews are a people of slander."
"13905","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thabit from Anas ibn Malik that a Persian man was a neighbor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his broth was the sweetest smelling thing. One day he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gestured to him like this, and Hammad described with his hand, meaning: Come. Then he gestured to him, while Aishah is with me, gesturing with a gesture. The man said with his hand like this, and Hammad described, meaning: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said like this, meaning: No. He said: Then he returned to him to come, and he said the same thing two or three times, saying this and saying that, and Hammad described, meaning: No, and saying that, meaning: No. Then he said like this, meaning: Get up. So they both went."
"13906","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us from Anas that Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark, intensely black night, then they left him, and the staff of one of them lit up, so they walked in its light, and when they parted the staff of the other lit up. And Hammad also said: When they parted, the staff of this one and the staff of that one lit up."
"13907","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us from Anas that Harithah ibn al-Rubayyi came on the day of Badr as an onlooker, and he was a boy, then a stray arrow came and struck the hollow of his throat and killed him. His mother al-Rubayyi came and said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Harithah with me, so if he is among the people of Paradise I will be patient, otherwise Allah will see what I do. He said: So he said: O Umm Harithah, it is not one garden, rather they are many gardens, and he is in al-Firdaws, the highest."
"13908","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, mighty and majestic, said: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan I draw near to him a cubit, and when he draws near to Me a cubit I draw near to him a fathom, and when he comes to Me walking I come to him hastening."
"13909","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I do not know whether something was revealed or he was saying it on his own: If the son of Adam had, and Hajjaj said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would wish for a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"13910","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother, or for his neighbor, what he loves for himself. And Hajjaj did not doubt: Until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"13911","Rawh narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you believes until he loves for people what he loves for himself, and until he loves a person, loving him only for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"13912","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, mentioning the name of Allah, mighty and majestic, and magnifying Him. I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot, meaning upon their sides."
"13913","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, mentioning the name of Allah, mighty and majestic, and magnifying Him. I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot, meaning upon their sides."
"13914","Waki and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, Yahya said: Qatadah informed us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned its meaning."
"13915","Hushaym narrated to us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah, he said: Anas informed us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two rams, then he mentioned its meaning."
"13916","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah informed us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner garment and my repository, and people will increase and decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrongdoers."
"13917","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk wine, so he flogged him about forty. And Abu Bakr did so. Then when it was Umar he consulted the people, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The lightest of the prescribed punishments is eighty. So Umar ordered it, and Hajjaj said: Eighty, and Umar ordered it."
"13918","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and al-Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, my father said: And Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, the meaning being one, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The People of the Book greet us, so how do we reply to them? He said: Say: And upon you. And Hajjaj said: Shubah said: I did not ask Qatadah about this hadith whether he heard it from Anas."
"13919","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which none will narrate to you after me, having heard it from him: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge is taken away and ignorance appears and adultery spreads and wine is drunk and men go away and women remain, until there is one man for fifty women."
"13920","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, raising the hadith, he said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away and ignorance appears and men become few and women become many, until the caretaker of fifty women is one man."
"13921","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, raising the hadith, he said: The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away and ignorance appears and men become few and women become many, until the caretaker of fifty women is one man."
"13922","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Concession was granted, or: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted concession to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that was in them."
"13923","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: Concession was granted to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf to wear silk, meaning because of an ailment that was in them. Shubah said, or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted concession to them."
"13924","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted concession to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr regarding silk."
"13925","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"13926","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer he is conversing with his Lord, mighty and majestic, so let him not spit. He said: Hajjaj said: So let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left under his foot."
"13927","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed me from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to begin the recitation with: All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"13928","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah the same, except that he doubted regarding Uthman."
"13929","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, so I did not hear any of them saying: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"13930","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah said: I asked Anas ibn Malik with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin the recitation. He said: You are asking me about something which no one has asked me about."
"13931","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love pumpkin. He said: So food was brought, or he was invited to it. Anas said: So I kept tracking it and placing it before him, for I knew that he loved it."
"13932","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, and my father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah I see you behind me, and perhaps he said: From behind my back, when you bow and prostrate."
"13933","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads."
"13934","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads."
"13935","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, and my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads."
"13936","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be balanced in prayer, and let none of you spread his forearms like the spreading of the dog. Yazid said it thus: Be balanced in prayer."
"13937","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be balanced in prostration, then he mentioned it."
"13938","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of completing the prayer."
"13939","Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish your rows, for part of the excellence of prayer is the establishing of the row."
"13940","Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah saying from Qatadah: He did not raise it, and I thought that he meant the hadith, so Abdullah ibn Uthman said to me: This is one of them."
"13941","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete your rows, for the straightening of the row, meaning, is part of completing the prayer."
"13942","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold, and that was permitted."
"13943","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, and Sufyan from Humayd from Anas ibn Malik, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold, and that was permitted. He said: And al-Hakam used to act upon this."
"13944","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We saw no fright, yet we found him to be a sea."
"13945","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is its burial."
"13946","Waki and Bahz and Abu al-Nadr said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, Bahz said: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, and Abu al-Nadr said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Jafar."
"13947","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. Hajjaj said in his hadith: Meaning his two fingers, the index and the middle. Shubah said: And I heard Qatadah saying in his stories: Like the excess of one of them over the other, and I do not know whether he mentioned it from Anas or Qatadah said it."
"13948","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me, and Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man driving a sacrificial camel: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, on the third time."
"13949","Muhammad narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"13950","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child and his parent and all people."
"13951","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever has them finds the taste of faith: Whoever loves a person, loving him only for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic, and whoever has Allah and His Messenger more beloved to him than anything besides them, and whoever has being thrown into the Fire more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it."
"13952","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said: Is there among you anyone not of you? They said: No, except a sister’s son of ours. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister’s son of a people is of them. Hajjaj said: Of themselves. He said: Quraysh are fresh in ignorance and calamity, and I wanted to reward them and conciliate them. Are you not pleased that people return with the world and you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your houses? If people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"13953","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that he said regarding this verse: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory: It is al-Hudaybiyah."
"13954","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and behind Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and they would not recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"13955","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write a letter to the Romans, they said: They do not read a letter unless it is sealed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, as though I am looking at its whiteness in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its engraving: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"13956","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13957","And my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The son of Adam grows old, and two things of him remain: greed and hope."
"13958","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The son of Adam grows old, and two things of him remain: greed and hope."
"13959","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah: He heard Anas saying: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13960","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Waki narrated to us from Shubah, and Hisham from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no contagion and no omen and no good omen. It was said: And what is the good omen? He said: The good word. And the wording is that of Muhammad ibn Jafar."
"13961","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Waki narrated to us from Shubah, and Hisham from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no contagion and no omen and no good omen. It was said: And what is the good omen? He said: The good word. And the wording is that of Muhammad ibn Jafar."
"13962","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, life is the life of the Hereafter. And Shubah said, or he said: O Allah, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so honor the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"13963","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, my father said: Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and it was said to him: It was given as charity to Barirah. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"13964","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, my father said: Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and it was said to him: It was given as charity to Barirah. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"13965","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas that Barirah was given charity, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"13966","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"13967","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet but he warned his nation of the one-eyed disbeliever. Verily he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed, written between his eyes: K F R."
"13968","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is none who enters Paradise who loves to return to the world, even if he had everything on earth, except the martyr, for he wishes to return to the world and be killed ten times, because of the honor he sees."
"13969","Hajjaj al-Awar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Shubah informed us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while complete."
"13970","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me: Qatadah narrated to me from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take out of the Fire. And Hajjaj said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Take out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and whoever had in his heart good weighing a speck. Take out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and whoever had in his heart good weighing a barley grain. Take out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and whoever had in his heart good weighing a wheat grain."
"13971","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Take out of the Fire, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Jafar, and he added therein: Take out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah and had in his heart good weighing a worm."
"13972","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us, and Bahz: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not fast continuously. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously. He said: I am not like one of you, I spend the night, and Bahz said: I remain, or spend the night, fed and given drink."
"13973","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, or: Wail upon you, ride it."
"13974","Rawh narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication which he has made for his nation, and I have kept my supplication as intercession for my nation."
"13975","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, informing me, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said: Is there among you anyone not of you? They said: No, except a sister’s son of ours. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister’s son of a people is of themselves. And once he said: Of them. Then he narrated it to me from Anas."
"13976","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us, he said: I heard Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The People of the Book greet us, so how do we reply to them? He said: Say: And upon you."
"13977","Rawh narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Do not sever ties and do not hate one another and do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"13978","Abu Dawud informed us: Shubah informed us from Thabit, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet used to often supplicate: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shubah said: So I mentioned that to Qatadah, and Qatadah said: Anas used to say this."
"13979","Abu Dawud informed us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas about the drink of jars. He said: I did not hear anything about it from the Messenger of Allah. He said: And Anas used to dislike it."
"13980","Abu Dawud informed us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet was brought a garment of silk, and they took to touching it and looking at it. He said: Are you amazed at this? The handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than this and softer than this. Or he said: The handkerchief."
"13981","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas that the Prophet said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I am at the thought of My servant of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"13982","Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Prophet said: The sister’s son of a people is of them."
"13983","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Companions of the Prophet used to sleep then pray and not perform ablution."
"13984","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shubah narrating from Anas, he said: Four gathered the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yahya said: All of them of the Ansar: Ubayy ibn Kab and Muadh ibn Jabal and Zayd ibn Thabit and Abu Zayd. He said: I said: Who is Abu Zayd? He said: One of my paternal uncles."
"13985","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to me from Anas that the Prophet said: Drinking while standing is forbidden. He said: I said: And eating? He said: That is worse."
"13986","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Black Stone is from Paradise."
"13987","Yazid and Abu Nuh said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, Abu Nuh said: And he heard it from him, and my father narrated to me from Hashim and al-Hajjaj, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while complete."
"13988","Yazid and Abu Nuh said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, Abu Nuh said: And he heard it from him, and my father narrated to me from Hashim and al-Hajjaj, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while complete."
"13989","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Men will go away and women will remain."
"13990","Yazid informed us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of Madinah: The Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it, so neither the Dajjal nor the plague will approach it, if Allah the Exalted wills."
"13991","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My father said."
"13992","And al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Makhlad, narrated to me, he said: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13993","And my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us from Hisham al-Dastuwai and Shubah together from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Spittle, and Yazid and al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad said in their hadiths: Mucus in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is its burial."
"13994","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My father said. And al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Makhlad, narrated to me, he said: Shubah informed us from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us from Hisham al-Dastuwai and Shubah together from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Spittle, and Yazid and al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad said in their hadiths: Mucus in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is its burial."
"13995","Hashim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah and Qatadah and Hamzah al-Dabbi that they heard Anas saying from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I was sent, I and the Hour, like this, and he pointed with the index and the middle. And Qatadah used to say: Like the excess of one of them over the other."
"13996","Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, cursing Ril and Dhakwan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"13997","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, supplicating against Ril and Dhakwan and Banu Fulan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. Marwan said, meaning: So I said to Anas: Did Umar perform qunut? He said: Umar, no."
"13998","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer he is conversing with his Lord, mighty and majestic, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, and let him spit to his left or under his foot."
"13999","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Said ibn Amir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to treat us gently very often, so that he said to a little brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did al-Nughayr do?"
"14000","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, good is the good of the Hereafter. Or he said: O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. Shubah said: Qatadah used to say this in his stories."
"14001","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered and mentioned the name of Allah and said the takbir."
"14002","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and behind Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them, and they would not begin the recitation with Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim. Shubah said: I said to Qatadah: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Yes, we asked him about it."
"14003","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to me, from Shubah, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas saying: The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14004","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: None of you believes until Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything besides them, and until being cast into the Fire is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it, and none of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child and his parent and all people."
"14005","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Mansur saying: I heard Talq ibn Habib narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14006","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman and Sulayman al-Taymi informed me, they heard Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"14007","Shabbabah from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married for the weight of a date-pit of gold. He said: And al-Hakam used to act upon it."
"14008","Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"14009","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, and Shubah from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul that dies having good with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that would be pleased to return to this world and have the world and what is in it, except the martyr, who wishes to return and be killed in this world because of what he sees of the merit of martyrdom."
"14010","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while making it complete."
"14011","Abu Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like pumpkin. Anas said: So I used to place it before him."
"14012","Abu Abdillah al-Sulami al-Anbari narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, who said: I asked Anas about the nabidh of the earthen jar, and he said: I did not hear anything about it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Anas used to dislike it."
"14013","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be cast into the Fire and it will say: Is there any more, until He places His foot or His leg upon it, and it will say: Enough, enough."
"14014","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Junaydi narrated to us, a man narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and he was impressed by this hadith, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completeness of prayer."
"14015","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"14016","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Humayd from Anas, who said: We were rained upon with hail while Abu Talhah was fasting, and he began eating from it. It was said to him: Do you eat while you are fasting? He said: This is only a blessing."
"14017","Ubaydullah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri Abu al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Sharik, from Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, mentioning the name of Allah and magnifying, and I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
"14018","Ubaydullah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: My uncle Yaqub narrated to me, from Sharik, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Be moderate in your prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads them. Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind me, or from behind my back, when you bow and when you prostrate."
"14019","Abdullah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to me, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that uncles of his testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the sighting of the crescent, so he ordered the people to break their fast and to go out to their Eid the next day."
"14020","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with women and children and camels and sheep, and made them into rows, and they were numerous against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they met, the Muslims turned away retreating, as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servants of Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: O company of the Ansar, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. He said: So Allah defeated the polytheists, and they did not strike with a sword nor thrust with a spear. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils are his. He said: So Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. And Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder strap while he had a coat of mail, and I was turned away from him, and Hammad also said: I was hurried away from him, so see who took it. He said: So a man stood and said: I took it, so compensate him from it and give it to me. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not be asked for anything except he gave it or remained silent. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. He said: So Umar said: By Allah, Allah will not return it upon a lion among His lions and give it to you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar has spoken the truth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Umar has spoken the truth. And Abu Talhah met Umm Sulaym, and with her was a dagger. Abu Talhah said: What is this with you? She said: I intended that if any of the polytheists came near me, I would rip open his belly with it. Abu Talhah said: Do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us among the freed ones; they fled from you. He said: Indeed Allah has sufficed and done good, O Umm Sulaym."
"14021","Affan narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When it was the day of Hunayn, and Hawazin and Ghatafan gathered against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a great gathering, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day was with ten thousand or more than ten thousand, he said, and with him were the freed ones of Makkah. He said: So they came with livestock and offspring and placed them behind their backs. He said: When they met, the people turned away. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day was upon a white mule. He said: So he dismounted and said: I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. He said: And he called that day two calls between which no speech was mixed. He turned to his right and said: O company of the Ansar. They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings, we are with you. Then he turned to his left and said: O company of the Ansar. They said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, we are with you. Then he came down to the ground and they met, and they were defeated, and they took spoils. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to the freed ones and distributed among them. The Ansar said: We are called at the time of the charge while the spoils are distributed to others. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them and sat in a tent and said: O company of the Ansar, what is this report that reached me about you? They fell silent. Then he said: O company of the Ansar, if the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar. Then he said: Are you not pleased that the people go with the world and you go with the Messenger of Allah, taking him to your houses? They said: We are pleased, O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased. Ibn Awn said: Hisham ibn Zayd said: So I said to Anas: And were you witnessing that? He said: Then where would I be absent from that?"
"14022","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him, and sat at his head and said to him: Accept Islam. He looked at his father, who was at his head, and he said: Obey Abu al-Qasim. So he accepted Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from him saying: Praise be to Allah who saved him through me from the Fire."
"14023","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, and I do not know it except from Anas, that a boy among the Jews used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him while he was dying, and called him to Islam. The boy looked at his father, who was at his head, and his father said to him: Obey Abu al-Qasim. So he accepted Islam, then he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from him saying: Praise be to Allah who saved him through me from the Fire."
"14024","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Isa, meaning Ibn Tahman, narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has a secret with me which I will never inform anyone of until I meet him."
"14025","Hashim narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"14026","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Anas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he combined the Umrah and the Hajj, saying: Here I am for a Hajj and an Umrah together."
"14027","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah informed us, from Mamar, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah daughter of Huyayy and made her freedom her dowry."
"14028","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the caller to prayer gave the call, the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand hastening to the pillars until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, while they were like that, meaning the two units before Maghrib, and there was only a short time between the call and the iqamah."
"14029","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Sad, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, who said: We went out with Ali and came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, and Ali said: I intend to combine the Hajj and the Umrah, so whoever wants that, let him say as I say. Then he raised his voice saying: Here I am for a Hajj and an Umrah together. He said: And Salim said: And Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: By Allah, my foot would touch the foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he raised his voice for both of them together."
"14030","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, he said: I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over his son Ibrahim? He said: I do not know. May Allah have mercy on Ibrahim; had he lived he would have been a truthful prophet. He said: I said: How do I leave when I pray, from my right or from my left? He said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leave to his right."
"14031","Affan narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas, and a speaker said to him: Has it reached you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam? He became angry then said: Yes indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made an alliance between Quraysh and the Ansar in his house."
"14032","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made an alliance between the Emigrants and the Ansar in the house of Anas ibn Malik."
"14033","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, and from Anas, as Hammad thought, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wrapped in a cotton garment whose ends he had crossed, and led the people in prayer."
"14034","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man was accused regarding a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to kill him, and he found him in a well cooling himself in it. He said to him: Give me your hand. He gave him his hand, and behold he was castrated, having no male organ. He came to the Messenger of Allah and informed him. He said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is castrated, he has no male organ."
"14035","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most merciful of my community toward my community is Abu Bakr, and the strongest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar, and Affan once said: in the command of Allah, Umar, and the most truthful of them in modesty is Uthman, and the most knowledgeable of them in inheritance law is Zayd ibn Thabit, and the best of them in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy ibn Kab, and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and the unlawful is Muadh ibn Jabal. Indeed every community has a trustee, and the trustee of this community is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with them all."
"14036","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Men will come to me at the Basin until when I have seen them, they are raised to me, then they are snatched away from me, and I shall surely say: O Lord, my companions, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"14037","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever wears silk in this world will never wear it in the Hereafter."
"14038","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"14039","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, that he heard Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that befell him; if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me."
"14040","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrating from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice them likewise."
"14041","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they spoke well of it, so he said: It has become due, it has become due. And a funeral passed by him and they spoke evil of it, so he said: It has become due, it has become due. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, your first saying: it has become due, and your other saying: it has become due. He said: As for the first, they spoke well of it, so I said: Paradise has become due for him. And as for the other, they spoke evil of it, so I said: The Fire has become due for him. And you are the witnesses of Allah on His earth."
"14042","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make it brief and complete, meaning he would lighten the prayer."
"14043","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah. Thabit said to him: What did he give her as dowry? He said: He gave her herself as dowry; he freed her and married her."
"14044","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the place of relieving himself, would say: I seek refuge with Allah from the male and female devils, or the impurities. Shubah said: And he said both together."
"14045","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Jabr, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash with five makakik and would perform ablution with a makkuk."
"14046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about prayer while traveling, and he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah, and we would pray two units until we returned to Madinah. I asked him: How long did you stay in Makkah? He said: Ten days. I said: For what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his voice in talbiyah? He said: Here I am for an Umrah and a Hajj."
"14047","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed me, from Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Here I am for an Umrah and a Hajj together, or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"14048","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a boy of ours and he cupped him, and gave him his wage, a sa or two sa, and spoke to his masters to lighten his tax from him."
"14049","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked qunut for a month, supplicating against tribes of the Arabs: Ril and Banu Lihyan and Usayyah and Dhakwan, in the dawn prayer."
"14050","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked qunut for a month after bowing."
"14051","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except at the prayer for rain, until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"14052","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"14053","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, who said: I heard Anas saying: The caller to prayer would call in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would think it was the iqamah because of how many would stand and pray the two units before Maghrib."
"14054","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hamzah al-Dabbi saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I never prayed, meaning behind a man, or behind any of the people, a lighter prayer in its completeness than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14055","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that his mother Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: A woman sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees that in her dream, let her wash. Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said, feeling shy: Can this be, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, for whence comes the resemblance? The water of the man is white and thick, and the water of the woman is yellow and thin, so from whichever of them precedes or prevails comes the resemblance."
"14056","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Harithah, son of my maternal aunt, set out on the day of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a young onlooker; he did not set out to fight. He said: An arrow struck him and killed him. He said: So his mother, my maternal aunt, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah, if he is in Paradise I shall be patient and seek reward, otherwise Allah will see what I do. He said: O mother of Harithah, they are many gardens, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaws."
"14057","Affan narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: It is indeed coming, so what have you prepared for it? He said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I have not prepared for it many deeds, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love, and for you is what you intended. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray, and when he finished his prayer he said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? The man was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the house, and behold a boy of Daws, of the kin of Abu Hurayrah, called Sad ibn Malik. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This boy, if his life is prolonged, old age will not reach him before the Hour comes. Al-Hasan said: And Anas informed me that the boy that day was among my peers."
"14058","Affan narrated to us, Ibrahim Abu Ismail al-Qannad narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he narrates it from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, he said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: If My servant meets Me a span, I meet him a cubit, and if he meets Me a cubit, I meet him a fathom, and if he meets Me walking, I meet him hastening."
"14059","Affan narrated to us, Aban, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I and the Hour were sent like these two. And Affan gestured with the index and middle fingers."
"14060","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Harithah was struck on the day of Badr, and the mother of Harithah said: O Prophet of Allah, if my son attained Paradise, otherwise I shall strive in weeping over him. He said: O mother of Harithah, they are many gardens within a garden, and Harithah attained the highest Firdaws."
"14061","My father said, with this chain and wording, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Do not turn away from one another, and do not hate one another, and do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"14062","He narrated to me, he said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Pack your rows together, and bring them near one another, and align the necks. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see the devil entering through the gaps of the row as if it were a small sheep."
"14063","Affan and Bahz said, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not wrong the believer a good deed; he is given provision in this world for it and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. He said: As for the disbeliever, he is fed for his good deeds in this world until when he reaches the Hereafter there is no good deed for him to be given good for."
"14064","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Baraah with Abu Bakr to the people of Makkah. He said: Then he called him and sent Ali with it. He said: None conveys it except a man of my household."
"14065","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast over one another in mosques."
"14066","Affan narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, al-Ashath ibn Jabir al-Huddani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: Whose two precious ones I take away, then he is patient and seeks reward, his reward is Paradise."
"14067","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Aishah had a curtain with which she screened the side of her house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove this curtain of yours from me, for its images keep appearing to me in my prayer."
"14068","Affan narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit, and a heart that does not humble itself, and a supplication that is not heard, and a soul that is not satisfied. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from these four."
"14069","Affan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who had a woman under him and divorced her three times, then she married another man after him, and he divorced her before consummating with her: Is she lawful for her first husband? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, until the other has tasted of her honey and she has tasted of his honey."
"14070","Affan narrated to us, Shubah informed me, Jafar ibn Mabad informed me, he said: I went to Anas ibn Malik, I and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman. He said: So I heard Anas saying: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would dictate to us: As much as you are able."
"14071","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Muadh Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out for his need, I and a boy of ours would come with a small vessel of water."
"14072","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Israil narrated to us, I asked my father about him and he said: A trustworthy shaykh, Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Fazari, informed us, from al-Awzai, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: My mother sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something, and I saw him standing with the branding iron in his hand, branding the charity animals."
"14073","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the sister of al-Rubayyi, Umm Harithah, wounded a person, and they disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Retaliation, retaliation. The mother of al-Rubayyi said: O Messenger of Allah, will retaliation be taken from so-and-so? No, by Allah, retaliation will never be taken from her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, O mother of Rubayyi, the Book of Allah prescribes it. She said: No, by Allah, retaliation will never be taken from her. He said: She kept on until they accepted the blood-money from her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear upon Allah, Allah fulfills it."
"14074","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him sheep between two mountains. He came to his people and said: O my people, accept Islam, for by Allah, Muhammad gives the giving of one who does not fear poverty. A man would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting nothing but this world, and evening would not come before his religion became more beloved to him, or dearer to him, than the world with what is in it."
"14075","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"14076","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit and Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a graveyard of Banu al-Najjar in a garden, upon a gray mule, and behold a grave whose occupant was being punished, and the mule shied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would ask Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"14077","Affan and Bahz said, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ubayy and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to recite to you. He said: Did He name me to you? He said: Allah named you to me. So he began to weep."
"14078","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no living soul that dies having good with Allah that would be pleased to return to this world, except the martyr, for he would be pleased to return to this world and be killed because of what he sees of the merit of martyrdom."
"14079","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis, then was revealed: We see the turning of your face toward heaven, so We shall turn you to a qiblah that pleases you, so turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. A man of Banu Salamah passed while they were bowing in the dawn prayer, having prayed one unit, and called out: Indeed the qiblah has been changed, indeed the qiblah has been changed to the Kabah. He said: So they turned as they were toward the qiblah."
"14080","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise have a market which they come to every Friday, in which are dunes of musk. When they go out to it, the wind blows, Hammad said: I think he said: a northerly one, he said: So it fills their faces and their clothes and their houses with musk, and they increase in beauty and loveliness. He said: They come to their families, who say: You have increased in beauty and loveliness after us. And they say to them: And you have increased in beauty and loveliness after us."
"14081","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When was revealed: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, I see our Lord asking us of our wealth, and I make you witness that I have made my land Bayruha for Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it among your relatives. So he divided it between Hassan ibn Thabit and Ubayy ibn Kab."
"14082","Affan said, and Yazid said, from Humayd, from Anas: Bariha. And Affan said: I asked about it more than one of the people of Madinah, and they claimed it is Bayruha, and that Bayraha is nothing."
"14083","Affan narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye is made in prayer."
"14084","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Jad Abi Uthman, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O my son."
"14085","Affan narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I know today sins which are finer in your eyes than hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the major sins."
"14086","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by the door of Fatimah for six months when he went out to the dawn prayer, saying: Prayer, O people of the house: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly."
"14087","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit and Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four come out of the Fire, Abu Imran said: four; Thabit said: two men, and they are presented to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then they are ordered to the Fire. He said: One of them turns and says: O Lord, I had hoped that when You took me out of it, You would not return me to it. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, saves him from it."
"14088","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with a woman of his wives, a man passed by him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, this is so-and-so, my wife. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, of whom I would think ill, I would never think ill of you. He said: Satan runs through the son of Adam as blood runs."
"14089","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day met by children of the Ansar and slave girls, and he said: By Allah, I love you."
"14090","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a camel-driver with a fine chant, and he was the driver of the men, while Anjashah would drive the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he chanted, the camels quickened, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, O Anjashah, gently driving the glass vessels."
"14091","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his deeds in private. One of them said: I shall not marry women. Another said: I shall not eat meat. Another said: I shall not sleep on a bed. Another said: I fast and do not break. He stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is the matter with peoples saying such and such? But I pray and sleep, and fast and break, and marry women. Whoever turns away from my practice is not of me."
"14092","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a woman who had something in her mind said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He said: O mother of so-and-so, look to whichever road you wish. He stood with her conversing until she fulfilled her need."
"14093","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: We used to say that the Hour will not come until the sky does not rain and the earth does not grow, and until one guardian is for fifty women, and until a woman passes by a man, and he looks at her and says: This one once had a husband. Hammad mentioned it once thus, and he mentioned it from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without doubt about it, and he also said: from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as he thought."
"14094","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the people of Yemen, when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Send with us a man to teach us the practice and Islam. He said: So he took the hand of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and said: This is the trustee of this community."
"14095","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talhah on the day of Hunayn, and behold with Umm Sulaym was a dagger. Abu Talhah said: What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym? Umm Sulaym said: I took it; if any of the disbelievers comes near me, I shall rip open his belly with it. Abu Talhah said: O Prophet of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says, saying such and such? She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us among the freed ones; they fled from you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Umm Sulaym, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sufficed and done good."
"14096","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yusuf, upon him prayer and peace, was given half of beauty."
"14097","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, would begin the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, except that Humayd did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14098","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw as if I were in the house of Uqbah ibn Rafi, and we were brought fresh dates of Ibn Tab, and I interpreted that eminence is ours in this world and the good end in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good."
"14099","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for by Allah, I see you from behind me as I see you from before me."
"14100","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the like of it, except that he said: Straighten and pack together."
"14101","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was frightened for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as no one was frightened, and I was harmed for the sake of Allah as no one was harmed, and there came upon me thirty between day and night when neither I nor Bilal had any food that a living being eats except something that the armpit of Bilal would conceal."
"14102","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit and Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that when the polytheists closed in on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with seven men of the Ansar and two men of Quraysh, he said: Whoever repels them from us will be my companion in Paradise. Then a man of the Ansar came forward and fought until he was killed. When they again pressed him, he said: Whoever repels them from me will be my companion in Paradise, until the seven were killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companion: We have not been fair to our brothers."
"14103","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah and Thabit and Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Prices rose in Madinah in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the people said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen, fix prices for us. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is the Price-Setter, the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider. I hope to meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with none of you seeking from me a wrong in blood or property."
"14104","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas, that Abu Talhah used to shoot before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was behind him shielding himself with him. He was an archer, and when he shot, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his figure to see where his arrow landed. Abu Talhah would raise his chest and say: Like this, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, no arrow shall strike you; my throat is before your throat. Abu Talhah would offer himself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: I am strong, O Messenger of Allah, direct me to your needs and command me with whatever you wish."
"14105","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to shave his head at Mina, Abu Talhah took one side of his head and the barber shaved it, then he brought it to Umm Sulaym. Umm Sulaym used to put it in her musk bag. He used to come and take his midday rest with her on a leather mat, and he used to sweat much. One day he came and she began to wipe the sweat and put it in a bottle of hers. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: What are you doing, O Umm Sulaym? She said: O Prophet of Allah, it is your sweat; I want to mix my perfume with it."
"14106","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When there was revealed: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, Thabit ibn Qays sat in his house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and said to Sad ibn Muadh: O Abu Amr, what is the matter with Thabit ibn Qays that he is not seen? Has he fallen ill? He said: I do not know of any illness for him, and he is my neighbor. So Sad entered upon him and mentioned to him the word of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You know that I was among the loudest of you in voice over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse has been revealed, and I am destroyed; I am among the people of the Fire. Sad mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Rather, he is among the people of Paradise."
"14107","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that people of Uraynah came to Madinah and found its climate unhealthy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them out to the charity camels and said: Drink from their milk and their urine. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. They were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cut off their hands and their feet from opposite sides, branded their eyes, and cast them at the Harrah. Anas said: I used to see one of them biting the earth with his mouth until they died. And perhaps Hammad said: Biting the earth with his mouth until they died."
"14108","Affan narrated to us, Hammad and Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, with a hadith similar to the hadith of Hammad."
"14109","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abu Bakr was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Makkah and Madinah. Abu Bakr used to travel to Sham and was known, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not known. They would say: O Abu Bakr, who is this lad before you? He would say: This one guides me on the way. When they drew near Madinah, they stopped at the Harrah and sent word to the Ansar. They came and said: Arise, safe and obeyed. He said: I witnessed him the day he entered Madinah, and I never saw a day at all that was better or brighter than the day he entered among us, and I witnessed him the day he died, and I never saw a day that was uglier or darker than the day he died (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14110","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the slain of Badr for three days until they decayed, then he came to them and stood over them and said: O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Utbah ibn Rabiah, O Shaybah ibn Rabiah, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. He said: Umar heard his voice and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call them after three days, and do they hear? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: You do not make the dead hear. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you do not hear better than them, but they are not able to answer."
"14111","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that a son of Abu Talhah died, so Umm Sulaym said: Do not inform Abu Talhah until I am the one who informs him. She covered him. When Abu Talhah came, she placed food before him and he ate, then she beautified herself for him and he had intercourse with her, and she conceived a boy. She said: O Abu Talhah, the family of so-and-so borrowed a loan from the family of so-and-so, then they sent to them: Send to us our loan, but they refused to return it. Abu Talhah said: They have no right to that; a loan is to be returned to its owners. She said: Your son was a loan from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has taken him. So he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. Anas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of that and said: May Allah bless them in their night. He said: She conceived a boy and gave birth, and Umm Sulaym sent him with me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I carried dates. I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was wearing a cloak and branding a camel of his. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there dates with you? He said: I said: Yes. He took the dates and cast them in his mouth and chewed them, then gathered his saliva, then opened his mouth and fed him. The boy began to smack his lips. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The love of the Ansar for dates. Then he did tahnik for him and named him Abdullah. There was no young man among the Ansar better than him."
"14112","Affan narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, then he mentioned it."
"14113","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man of his Companions visiting him when he had become like a chick. He said to him: Did you ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for something? He said: I said: O Allah, whatever You would punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have no strength for the punishment of Allah. Why did you not say: O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"14114","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say while digging the Trench: We are those who pledged to Muhammad for Islam as long as we live, ever. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. Barley bread and rancid melted fat were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they ate from it. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: True good is only the good of the Hereafter."
"14115","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by Jibril, peace be upon him, while he was playing with the boys. He seized him and threw him down and opened his chest and took out from it a clot. He said: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then joined it and returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother, meaning his foster mother, and said: Muhammad has been killed. They met him with his color changed. Anas said to me: I used to see the mark of the stitching on his chest. And perhaps Hammad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by a visitor."
"14116","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger be more beloved to him than anything besides them, and that a man loves a man and loves him only for Allah, and that a man would rather be cast into the Fire than return to being a Jew or a Christian."
"14117","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us, and I had a small brother, and he had a small bird he used to play with. His bird with which he played died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered one day and saw him grieved, so he said to him: What is the matter with Abu Umayr that he is grieved? They said: His bird with which he played has died, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the little bird?"
"14118","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud while wiping blood from his face: How can a people prosper who wounded the face of their Prophet and broke his front tooth while he calls them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: You have nothing of the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"14119","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the establishment of the Hour while the prayer was called. When he finished his prayer, he said: Where is the questioner about the Hour? The man said: It is I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What have you prepared for it, for it is coming? He said: I have not prepared much deed for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are with whom you love. He said: The Muslims never rejoiced at anything after Islam as they rejoiced at this hadith. He said: Anas used to say: We love Allah and His Messenger."
"14120","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his maternal uncle Haram, the brother of Umm Sulaym, with seventy men to Banu Amir. When they arrived, my uncle said to them: I will go before you; if they grant me safety so that I convey to them from the Messenger of Allah, well and good, otherwise you will be near me. He said: He went forward and they granted him safety. While he was speaking to them about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they signaled to a man, who stabbed him and pierced him through. He said: Allah is Greatest, I have won, by the Lord of the Kabah. Then they turned upon the rest of his companions and killed them except a lame man among them who had climbed the mountain. Hammam said: I think he mentioned another with the lame man with him on the mountain. He said: Anas narrated to us that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him that they had met their Lord, and He was pleased with them and made them pleased. Anas said: They used to recite: Convey to our people that we have met our Lord and He is pleased with us and has made us pleased. He said: Then that was abrogated afterwards. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against them for thirty mornings: against Ril and Dhakwan and Banu Lihyan and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, or who disobeyed the Most Merciful."
"14121","Bahz narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is to bury it."
"14122","Bahz narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: I said to Anas: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to prolong his voice with prolongation."
"14123","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to open the recitation after the takbir with: All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds, in the prayer. Affan said in his narration: Meaning in the prayer after the takbir."
"14124","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour is, Hammam said: And perhaps he said: The Hour will not come, Hammam said: I heard both: until knowledge is taken away and ignorance appears and wine is drunk and adultery appears and men decrease and women increase, until there is for fifty women one caretaker."
"14125","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was walking in Paradise, I came upon a river whose banks were domes of pearl. He said: I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, gave you. He said: I struck with my hand, and its clay was pungent musk."
"14126","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. It was said to him: You fast continuously. He said: I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"14127","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at midday and his Companions needed water for ablution. He said: A small cup with a little water was brought, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in it, and it began to gush from between his fingers until all the people performed ablution. I said: How many were you? He said: About three hundred."
"14128","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."
"14129","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of the people of Paradise would like to return to this world even if he had ten times its like, except the martyr, for he wishes he would return to this world and be martyred ten times because of what he saw of merit."
"14130","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that a Jew passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions and said: Death be upon you. The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it upon him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He only said: Death be upon you. So the Jew was seized and brought, and he confessed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return upon them what they said."
"14131","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a tailor of the people of Madinah had invited him, and there was barley bread and rancid melted fat, and in it was pumpkin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin. He said: I began to bring it near before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Anas said: Pumpkin has pleased me ever since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liking it."
"14132","Bahz narrated to us, and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Qatadah informed us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, and Bahz said: From Anas ibn Malik, that a group of Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We found Madinah unhealthy; our bellies grew large and our limbs wasted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to join the camel-herd and drink from their milk and their urine. He said: They joined the camel-herd and drank from their milk and their urine until their bellies and their colors became sound. Then they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent in pursuit of them. They were brought, and he cut off their hands and their feet and branded their eyes. Qatadah said, from Muhammad ibn Sirin: This was only before the fixed punishments were revealed."
"14133","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, for I see you from before me and from behind me. He said: Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you see? He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire."
"14134","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A son of Abu Talhah by Umm Sulaym died. He said: Umm Sulaym said to her family: Do not inform Abu Talhah of his son until I am the one who informs him. Then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Bahz, except that he said: My mother said: O Anas, let nothing be fed anything until you go with him in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He spent the night weeping, and I spent the night leaning over him watching him until morning. I went with him in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was a branding iron. When he saw the boy with me, he said: Perhaps Umm Sulaym has given birth. He said: I said: Yes. So he put the branding iron from his hand and sat down."
"14135","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ate food, would lick his three fingers, and said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the harm from it and eat it and not leave it for Satan. And he commanded us to wipe the dish clean, and said: You do not know in which of your food is the blessing."
"14136","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that eighty men of the people of Makkah descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions from Mount al-Tanim at the dawn prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized them peacefully and pardoned them. And the Quran was revealed: And He is the One who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah after He gave you victory over them."
"14137","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and engraved an engraving in it, and said: I have taken a ring and engraved an engraving in it, so let no one engrave upon my engraving."
"14138","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love pumpkin, or he said: gourd. He said: I saw him one day eating it, so I began to place it before him."
"14139","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with five makakik and perform ablution with a makkuk."
"14140","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send a prophet except that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Verily he is the one-eyed liar. Verily he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is: disbelieved."
"14141","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed me, from Anas, that they said: O Messenger of Allah, when the People of the Book greet us, how do we return upon them? He said: Say: And upon you."
"14142","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the rows is part of the perfection of prayer."
"14143","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads."
"14144","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, or: Woe unto you, ride it."
"14145","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, so let him not spit before him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left under his foot."
"14146","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse of Abu Talhah called Mandub. He rode it and said: We saw no fright, and we found him to be a sea."
"14147","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man of the Ansar was bulky and could not pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot pray with you. So he made food for him and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to it. They spread a mat for him and sprinkled it, and he prayed two rakahs upon it. A man of the family of al-Jarud said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? He said: I never saw him pray it except that day."
"14148","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by his Companions one night. He came out and prayed with them briefly, then entered his house and prayed long, then came out and prayed with them briefly, then entered his house and prayed long. In the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed, making it long when you entered and brief when you came out. He said: I did what I did because of you."
"14149","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn al-Habhab and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"14150","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"14151","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked drinking while standing. Qatadah said: We asked Anas about eating. He said: Eating is worse."
"14152","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was a swift boy, and I hunted a rabbit and we roasted it. Abu Talhah sent me with its hind part to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I brought it to him."
"14153","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: What if you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. He said: It will be said to him: You were asked for easier than that."
"14154","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The most beloved clothing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to wear was the hibarah."
"14155","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit his wives in one hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. He said: I said to Anas: Could he bear that? He said: We used to say that he was given the strength of thirty."
"14156","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date and said: Were it not that I fear it is charity, I would eat it."
"14157","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication, and I have kept my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection. Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication, and I have kept my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
